INSERT INTO `ideas_categories` VALUES (1,0,NULL,'Spaces','spaces','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/1/77be445be0464baf0e0facb9b4e1b1cd',0,'2020-08-05 16:34:50',NULL),(2,1,1,'Family rooms','family-rooms','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/2/aaf3c78cf0ac81c8d0ecc5ac63a2e930',1,'2020-08-05 16:35:21','<p>A basement family room is a great addition to any household, adding value to your property and giving your loved ones a place where they will all want to hang out and spend time together – not to mention entertain guests! Whether you are after a traditional basement family room with a fireplace and a casual atmosphere, a contemporary lounging area with chic furniture and dramatic angles, or an idea of a family room for a basement that’s truly original, we have all of the materials and expertise necessary to make your family room ideas come true.</p>\n\n<p>On the other hand, if you have no family room ideas of your own, we will gladly create a basement family room that matches your exact lifestyle. From overstuffed sectional sofas to intimate loveseats, our design experts will choose the right sitting furniture based on your family’s size and individual needs. Watch as coffee table centerpieces and other room accessories transform your downstairs dwelling from drab to fab. No matter what the size of the room, however, one thing always remains the same – a large screen HDTV and a stunning entertainment center for all to enjoy!</p>'),(3,1,1,'Bathrooms','bathrooms','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/3/fa0e9fffc61f1458047e3c18023af04f',2,'2020-08-05 16:35:39',NULL),(4,2,3,'Half','half','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/4/03894119480acd0284be14d412f58039',3,'2020-08-05 16:36:19',NULL),(5,2,3,'Basic','basic','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/5/df9a42c3e68804c432697518b13b4fa8',4,'2020-08-05 16:36:19',NULL),(6,2,3,'Upgraded','upgraded','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/6/1c3655c839045130cbd1235af7a6110d',5,'2020-08-05 16:36:19',NULL),(7,1,1,'Wet Bars','wet-bars','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/7/01e95dd8647d49c1d71f6aefbad64f4a',6,'2020-08-05 16:37:55',NULL),(8,2,7,'Small','small','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/8/08cfd0181b0a5c92f136874dd58a38f8',7,'2020-08-05 16:38:40','<p>When you are brainstorming basement ideas, you want to utilize every corner and side space available. You can astound and entertain close family members and guests alike by converting one of your corner spaces into one of our custom-tailored small wet bars. Small wet bars are a terrific way to show off your downstairs area without taking up too much room. Our design professionals will help you choose from the highest quality cabinets, countertops, built-in wine racks, and stainless steel appliances available on the market to truly bring out the best in your basement ideas.</p>'),(9,2,7,'Medium','medium','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/9/6c30ef2bb1e4275f6d075b7531142d11',8,'2020-08-05 16:38:40','<p>A stylish medium-sized wet bar is the best way to let friends know that they are in for a good time. Let us add color, texture and symmetry to your basement’s medium-sized wet bar with tiled accent walls and floors, LVT planking, overhead lighting, and all the other features needed to make this one of the most amazing gathering spaces that you and your guests have ever seen. With our professional guidance, the only thing you’ll have to worry about is keeping your medium-sized wet bar fully stocked.</p>'),(10,2,7,'Kitchen-Like','kitchen-like','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/10/294eb4db4eb31b5fc05df482297582db',9,'2020-08-05 16:38:40','<p>A full-sized kitchen is a great basement idea, but it is not up to code in most counties. With a few adjustments, however, we can present you with a grandiose dining area in the form of basement kitchenettes that have sectional marble countertops, island centerpieces, diner seating, and the best cooking appliances and refrigerator units on the market. Our stylists will assist you in choosing from the best LVT and tiled flooring options available for the right theme, be it an upscale dining hall or cozy kitchen-like wet bars with a downhome feel.</p>'),(11,2,7,'Full-Size','full-size','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/11/9a095ea96c642e41a8a4132e51a66853',10,'2020-08-05 16:38:40','<p>If you want to focus less on meals and more on serving beverages, full-size wet bars with vanity sinks and wine storage are among the many basement ideas we have available. Let us design the perfect sit-down spot or carve you an intimate walkway so that you and your friends can be immersed in tiled accent walls, wall-to-wall cabinetry, and good conversation. From contemporary to traditional, modern to mellow, our design experts will give you a great space to entertain all!</p>'),(12,1,1,'Kids Playrooms','kids-playrooms','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/12/905d9f407701528ad9e7ccb2d4fb7d17',11,'2020-08-05 16:40:24','<p>Are you tired of picking up toys left in the living room? Has your small child outgrown their bedroom and now needs a larger space to play and grow? With soft lighting, the appropriate flooring (such as LVT planking, faux wood tile, premium carpeting, and more), and other bright and cheery ideas, we can transform your basement into the ultimate kids’ playroom. Whether you want to be able to look over from the family room to make sure they are “playing nice”, or you want to give your kids’ playroom a stenciled mock home entrance for a more secluded space that’s all their own, we can turn you and your children’s basement ideas into a wonderful reality!</p>'),(13,1,1,'Media rooms','media-rooms','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/13/c9e6d15f6d8b9177ecec60e043991910',12,'2020-08-05 16:40:24',NULL),(14,2,13,'Basic Media rooms','basic-media-rooms','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/14/40353208a6a1a522585c2ec8e0b53a1d',13,'2020-08-05 16:41:09','<p>Are you a movie buff or a video game enthusiast? If so, why not transform your downstairs basement into the ultimate media room to enjoy all of your entertainment in class? Our basic media rooms include a home projection unit with screen or mounted HDTV, entertainment cabinets and built-in shelving to hold all of your growing collections, and overstuffed wall-to-wall sitting furniture that will match the atmosphere you are trying to create – casual, sophisticated, or any other basement ideas you can dream of.</p>'),(15,2,13,'Home theaters','home-theaters','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/15/78fda362684b36fb3d7969e7967777e5',14,'2020-08-05 16:41:09','<p>For the ultimate in entertainment, consider installing a premium home theater! With authentic movie seats, theater-style carpet, walls, and a recessed ceiling to hold your deluxe sound system, you and your family will feel like you are out for a night on the town. Or, perhaps you would like to convey a more family-oriented design with soft lighting, modern furniture and casual artwork? Either way, our design experts can make all of your home theater basement ideas come true! Plus, you’ll always have the best seat!</p>'),(16,1,1,'Music rooms','music-rooms','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/16/4ec0f22d482ea623fc4dc068d1aa2238',15,'2020-08-05 16:42:13','<p>Your basement ideas can nurture your creative side as you release your inner-artist in a fully-equipped music room! Basements make for terrific music rooms for a wide variety of reasons – they have plenty of room to hold large instruments such as pianos and drum kits, they provide great acoustics, and the underground location naturally dampens the noise to outsiders. Once you add studio equipment to record your jams and lounging furniture for spectators to sit and enjoy, building a self-propelled music career becomes a breeze. Whether you’d a prefer space that is dark and dramatic, light and open, or something completely different, our design experts can provide you with whatever aesthetic gets you in a creative mindset the most.</p>'),(17,1,1,'Gym','gym','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/17/8c252c901da6da4942fe1d66c0c8e37a',16,'2020-08-05 16:42:13','<p>Do you want to work out, but are tired of gym memberships and crowded equipment stations? Here’s an idea for your basement – turn it into a private gym where you can feel improvement with every movement! From treadmills to punching bags, workout benches, tumbling stations and more, we’ll furnish your gym room with state-of-the-art workout equipment that’s customized for your personal routines. Let us make you feel as comfortable as possible with LVT flooring or gym carpeting that’s designed to absorb the impact of your workout regimes and an entertainment station to keep you fully engaged and never bored as you burn those calories away. Self-improvement becomes an everyday occurrence when you have a terrific basement gym to look forward to! Don’t forget to invite your friends over for a truly “healthy relationship”!</p>'),(18,1,1,'Office','office','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/18/23b460dfd5ee61fdf801393a502ad210',17,'2020-08-05 16:42:13','<p>Are you a serious worker or prefer to work at a casual pace? Your workspace should reflect your personality in your home office, and we have plenty of basement ideas to help! Some people prefer a dramatic den with dark colors and soft lighting to help them concentrate, while others prefer an area that is open, airy and bright. Either way, our design specialists will have you covered with an array of office furniture that will convey the sense of professionalism you are looking for. Director’s chairs, leather seats, and other sitting furniture will send just the right message to clients and business partners – and don’t forget to choose a powerful-looking desk to let others know who’s the boss of this basement.</p>'),(19,1,1,'Laundry','laundry','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/19/0890db2701399b0c811906e5751b013e',18,'2020-08-05 16:42:13','<p>Basement laundry rooms are an integral part of owning a luxury basement. Laundry rooms by BasementRemodeling.com are clean, stylish and practical.</p>'),(20,1,1,'Storage rooms','storage-rooms','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/20/211e9f70a9ccd46900442fe535e67370',19,'2020-08-05 16:42:13','<p>A basement storage room is the perfect idea for safely storing collectibles, children’s toys, family heirlooms, and any other sort of prized possession in the household. These valuable items deserve a clean space to keep them protected, and we are here to create the most stylish and practical storage rooms imaginable. Wheeled wired shelving, wraparound wooden shelves, and mounted mesh holders are among the many choices our design experts have to offer. You can even transform your storage room into a personal wardrobe with vanity wash station or a remarkable wine sampling area with LVT flooring, delightful cabinetry, and – of course – a tasting table!</p>'),(21,1,1,'Wine Cellars','wine-cellars','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/21/8593e673429e64b771296eb613fa8019',20,'2020-08-05 16:42:13','<p>Wine cellars are a great way to prominently showcase your collection and tactfully display your great tastes to all who visit. Bottles from all over the world can be neatly categorized in a variety of wall-mounted, triangulated wine racks that can be as complex or simple as you desire. Dazzle guests with an awe-inspiring marble island (with additional storage space), a centerpiece dining table, or fanciful sit-down sectional counters equipped with sophisticated furniture that’s richly divine. Let our room specialists create a spectacular atmosphere with dramatic chandeliers, perfectly-placed recessed row lights, and a stunning array of LVT, laminate, faux wood tile, and tiled flooring options. We’ve got all of the right ideas to make your basement the place to sample exquisite blends!</p>'),(22,0,NULL,'Features','features','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/22/8623d76e5feebe2c9cda5e7b70bf2f58',22,'2020-08-05 16:44:11',NULL),(23,1,22,'Doors','doors','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/23/6d04295c1cce047aabd4c9d2a0df1231',23,'2020-08-05 16:44:36',NULL),(24,2,23,'Glass','glass','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/24/307b2eccd384c493e2613d46f3bd22b8',24,'2020-08-05 16:46:08','<p>Going with glass doors for the basement is a stylish and practical way to redirect light into darkish hallways, or into any windowless room. When you replace your interior with glass doors, what you are designing is a more open basement with a better flow. Connecting two rooms with glass doors makes them appear larger, and you’ll have more natural light, which means you’ll be flipping that light switch less and saving on the electrical bill.</p>'),(25,2,23,'Pocket','pocket','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/25/1ff89da379489662a6b411ce0ddb8545',25,'2020-08-05 16:46:08','<p>Traditionally, basement pocket doors make the most of limited space by existing in places where swinging doors are not possible. Basement pocket doors slide into place when you need privacy, and slide back open when you want to combine two different rooms into one space again. With that said, many owners of large basements are now requesting pocket doors not to save room, but simply because of their delightful aesthetic. A glass-paned double wide pocket door has the same stylish sophistication as a traditional French door, but with the added novelty of being different and lesser-used. If you are looking for fresh basement door options that are catching on fast, then we have the right pocket door ideas for you.</p>'),(26,2,23,'Barn Doors','barn-doors','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/26/38ebd93e06a2755c5abdc31f5ef2b608',26,'2020-08-05 16:46:08','<p>Like pocket doors, interior sliding barn doors are a rustic alternative to the traditional swinging door format. Interior barn style doors are made of virtually any material you can think of, from iron to steel, but most prefer the timeless look of a weathered set of double barn doors. Barn doors make great focal points by framing the beautiful room behind them on both sides, lending geometrical symmetry to the overall floorplan.</p>'),(27,2,23,'Access Doors','access-doors','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/27/3754dc62aeefee571562d9f8440d19dd',27,'2020-08-05 16:46:08','<p>Basement access doors are great ways for plumbers to easily service fixtures without having to tear apart your beautiful custom walls. The trick is making sure that the access door is not noticeable until it’s needed, and as you can see from these pictures, we are masters of making the access door blend in with the rest of the interior.</p>'),(28,2,23,'Hidden and Mechanical','hidden-and-mechanical','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/28/a7a2e4188acc9f68cf57879664fe0581',28,'2020-08-05 16:46:08','<p>Let’s face it, the mechanical room is the least flattering part of any basement by default. While nobody has tried to decorate a mechanical room yet (and we’d be glad to be the first if someone would only let us try), many customers choose to instead tuck it away from sight by using a basement hidden door. Our basement hidden door ideas will cleverly conceal the unsightly mechanical room from guests and young family members alike by cleverly disguising it as an artsy bookshelf. These trick doors are so popular, that we have even made them for rooms besides the mechanical room.</p>'),(29,1,22,'Wall Treatments','wall-treatments','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/29/18ae2945382541bfc8585d18ffdafe0b',53,'2020-08-05 16:53:03',NULL),(30,2,29,'Wood Wall Panelling','wood-wall-panelling','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/30/d9cde1142c12496776494a44509a714d',56,'2020-08-05 16:54:42','<p>Traditional wooden wall panelling and wainscoting can transform your basement rooms into warm and friendly areas by adding layers of architectural depth and intrigue. The difference between wainscoting and wall paneling simply refers to the height of the wall panel itself. Wainscot panels are typically about the height of the chair, for a sense of casual comfort and uniformity, and include designer flat panels, beaded panels, and texturally raised patterns. Other panels are higher to give a more grandiose appearance that is perfect for dining areas and luxurious family rooms. We excel at providing the very best traditional wood wall paneling and wainscoting ideas to beautifully border your basement’s interior. We can add scintillating color and symmetry to your basement with a wide variety of expert traditional wooden wall paneling and wainscoting ideas.</p>'),(31,2,29,'Contemporary Wall Panelling','contemporary-wall-panelling','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/31/9133e00f03b736c404dfece2c2642fef',54,'2020-08-05 16:54:42','<p>Contemporary wooden walls are completely in style for interior homes, and can make a bold statement in any space. Our contemporary wall paneling ideas will have your basement looking chic and elite without costing a fortune. A contemporary wooden wall can serve as the ultimate accent piece to warm up a room by drawing the eye and embellishing clean line breaks. On top of its visual appeal, it is easy to install and maintain over the years. Appreciative guests will be impressed by your trendy designer basement tastes, and you won’t even have to tell them that our professional team advised you (take all the credit, we don’t mind).</p>'),(32,2,29,'Stacked Stone Wall','stacked-stone-wall','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/32/a15b96b5e64d69df54f6eedfe0ff8b31',55,'2020-08-05 16:54:42','<p>Stacked stone is virtually identical to natural stone, replicating its textures and colors by using molds made from real stones. Stacked stone walls have the same look and feel as organic stone walls at a fraction of the price. Even better, stacked stone walls can be produced in a wide variety of colors and textures&nbsp;modeled after the latest interior design trends for the best look possible. Stacked stone tiling is lightweight, cost-effective, and much easier to install than its organic stone alternative. We have a wide variety of earthy stacked stone tones and sizes that are a great match for any basement fireplace, accent wall, decorative column and other amenities.</p>'),(33,1,22,'Flooring','flooring','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/33/d7b7890423a169a06f6d32f34fde4e1d',29,'2020-08-05 16:55:03',NULL),(34,2,33,'LVT','lvt','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/34/16c0288c84e357a5f923bbdafd59e2ff',30,'2020-08-05 16:55:40','<p>The time has come for you to ditch that drab gray concrete floor and install something that’s more hospitable, and we have all of the basement luxury vinyl tile (LVT) flooring ideas for you and your home to help make it happen. Conventional vinyl tile is thinner and less durable, but our basement LVT flooring is high in style and low in maintenance. It offers the same high-end grainy look of natural floorboards, but with a higher resistance to scuffs and scratches.</p>'),(35,2,33,'Tile','tile','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/35/36982cd9c7c42550aee567b98468e93e',31,'2020-08-05 16:55:40','<p>Ceramic and porcelain tiles are beautiful, long-lasting and fully customizable. Wood, stone, and many other textures are available for a look that is as timeless or contemporary as you desire. Tile flooring is also resistant to water (also called “glazed ceramic flooring”), stains and will not warp from high humidity. This makes them especially ideal for basement bathrooms and kitchenlike areas. Maintenance consists of sweeping, vacuuming and using a heavy duty cleaner for stains. &nbsp;</p>'),(36,2,33,'Laminate','laminate','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/36/82801363facb17a5e44b913cc1f7de6c',32,'2020-08-05 16:55:40','<p>Laminate flooring creates a synthetic wood finish without any of the fuss that natural wood requires. Laminate flooring has a top layer that is specially treated to protect the inner designs from fading, scratching, scuffs, and other forms of wear and tear. As a result, you get an affordable style that stays looking new for years. Our basement laminate flooring ideas take advantage of modern printing technologies, which allow manufacturers to produce laminate floors that look identical to their natural counterparts.</p>'),(37,1,22,'Ceilings','ceilings','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/37/41800dd42e55dbdaf8bc33f8d4f7fed9',34,'2020-08-05 16:56:00',NULL),(38,2,37,'Basic','basic-ceilings','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/38/ad1997f8c8eda274ab2dd7f1e3db2473',35,'2020-08-05 16:57:09','<p>Not many people think about it, but choosing from the best basement ceiling options is just as important as the choosing the right type of flooring. We’ve completed over 500 basements for the Maryland and Virginia regions, and we understand the importance of choosing the right kind of ceiling for your basement, which is why even our most basic basement ceiling options will still stylishly keep your basement’s ductwork out of sight while setting the stage for future groundwork such as LED lighting designs and deluxe sound system setups.</p>'),(39,2,37,'Advanced','advanced','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/39/a330c7b2944e88ff2d13fe26b4a8f15d',36,'2020-08-05 16:57:09','<p>Your basement’s ceiling is like a clean slate that is waiting to accentuate all of the fine accessories underneath it, and we have plenty of advanced basement ceiling options to achieve just that:</p>'),(40,2,37,'Hidden LED lights','hidden-led-lights','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/40/1a80ee14ba0ad475d19da89d653efbd7',37,'2020-08-05 16:57:09','<p>Hidden LED lights can create the perfect atmosphere for your basement while giving the illusion of more space. As nice as they are, however, there are many variables that makes LED strips and downlights difficult to install on your own. With BasementRemodeling.com in charge, you will have a series of pleasingly symmetrical basement lighting ideas to choose from. Our professional expertise means that your hidden LED lights are perfectly spaced apart, use the right type of bulb for the mood you are going for, and, most importantly, are able to pass all of your county’s local ordinances and electrical codes.<br></p>'),(41,2,37,'High-End Ceiling Designs','high-end-ceiling-designs','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/41/eeefb138aa32bc2076c086980962b43b',38,'2020-08-05 16:57:09','<p>We’ve reserved our high-end basement ceiling options for customers who want to completely their charm guests every time they go downstairs, but beware. Our box beam ceilings are of such fine quality, you might find yourself continuously charmed as well. From an aesthetic point of view, the beams guide the eye, giving movement to any floorplan.</p>'),(42,1,22,'Lighting','lighting','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/42/590bd92439ed0e26ded12245a4f8f787',39,'2020-08-05 16:58:51','<p>At BasementRemodeling.com, we have LED lighting ideas that will bask your basement’s interior with a warm and inviting glow. Our LED lighting ideas will create the soft look with dramatic highlights that every style uses, no matter what era. In this sense, our downlights do more than just illuminate basements – they create living, breathing, engaging environments.</p>'),(43,1,22,'Fireplaces','fireplaces','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/43/e76ffcd65580faa52b82c9445c4a1ebf',40,'2020-08-05 16:58:51','<p>Nothing brings a family together like the soft crackle of a basement fireplace, and we want your family to be able to enjoy one in your home. Having a basement fireplace signifies calmness and prosperity, and it is the ultimate accessory to any family room – in fact, family memories just seem all the more pleasant when shrouded in the flickering glow of a warm fire. Winters will be lighter on the wallet as your basement fireplace helps you conserve energy while entertaining envious guests. For the best basement impression, don’t forget to let our custom shelving experts design a basement fireplace mantle, elevated platform, or basement fireplace bookshelf that is right for you and yours. Once you’ve seen your basement fireplace’s custom contours, you’ll know you have made the right decision!</p>'),(44,1,22,'Columns','columns','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/44/b70d979f3f36ad7d8fec703f144da93a',41,'2020-08-05 16:58:51',NULL),(45,2,44,'Stand Alone','stand-alone','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/45/6db5b27d1c6254b20b65ddfd45fb5940',42,'2020-08-05 16:59:52','<p>Regardless of whether they provide structural support or are just for show, decorative columns and stand-alone columns are terrific tools when it comes to adding a refined sense of distinguishment to your basement – and our team knows just how to position them to get the best look. Wood, stone, or steel, our stand-alone and decorative column ideas will bestow a subtle impression of success and good fortune upon your basement by using a wide array of design tactics.</p>'),(46,2,44,'Half Walls and Design','half-walls-and-design','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/46/f3d3f8116d4dd1d60a3260b8bb323909',43,'2020-08-05 16:59:52','<p>If you are looking for room separator ideas for your basement, but still want to have an open floor plan, then half walls with columns are a great compromise. The main purpose of half walls is to compartmentalize larger spaces into neat and tidy areas, but half walls with columns are also perfect for maximizing the amount of light received by each room while providing a cozy dose of privacy, too. Dark interior spaces benefit from half walls, and the columns can cast dramatic shadows and other lighting effects, too – if that’s what you’re after. The right half wall can breathe new style and sophistication into your downstairs area, and we have plenty of sleek half wall ideas for you to choose from!</p>'),(47,1,22,'Built-Ins and Shelving','built-ins-and-shelving','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/47/76199d9022b64cdc7ae9ea818607e3a6',44,'2020-08-05 17:00:17',NULL),(48,2,47,'Entertainment Center','entertainment-center','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/48/c4067e4447475d51325eb7ca5a510598',45,'2020-08-05 17:03:07','<p>A personalized basement entertainment center is one the most stylish ways to please guests and simultaneously showcase a healthy family image. Whether you are heavily into sports, frequently throw social functions, or simply want to foster memories in a warm family environment, our basement design experts have the experience and patience needed to transform your downstairs space into a virtual utopia that meets all of your entertainment goals.</p>'),(49,2,47,'Custom Cabinetry / Shelving','custom-cabinetry-shelving','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/49/a602f635828c5141fd9a08f2d6631771',46,'2020-08-05 17:03:07','<p>At BasementRemodeling.com, we want to create a downstairs area that’s exactly how you envisioned. Custom basement shelving and storage cabinets are the perfect way to give your living space just the right look and feel, adding style, sophistication, warmth, and functionality to any room.&nbsp; With custom basement shelving and storage cabinets that hug every contour just-so, you can rest assured that absolutely no area is going to waste – visually, or otherwise!</p>'),(50,2,47,'Bunk Bed','bunk-bed','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/50/1236882dc71999b8ca91e567b1d62837',47,'2020-08-05 17:03:07','<p>We strive to create basements for the entire family to enjoy, which is why our basement design experts know exactly how to build a great basement for kids. With fun and colorful basement bunk beds in your kids’ playroom, bedtime arguments will quickly become an issue of the past. Add designer themes such as jungle rooms or treehouses, and your child will be the most popular kid at the school when it comes to throwing legendary sleepovers. However, we want to give a fair warning to parents: your children may start to like being grounded!</p>'),(51,2,47,'Basic Shelving','basic-shelving','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/51/6a86a9aa65e0049e498c7fe28325f278',48,'2020-08-05 17:03:07','<p>The main purpose of a basement is for storage, yet many basements do not take advantage of even the most basic shelving ideas. Whether you want basic shelving under your basement entertainment center, sophisticated bookshelves by the fireplace, or simply need extra space for toiletries in the bathroom, we have everything ready for installation.<br></p>'),(52,1,22,'Stairs and Railing','stairs-and-railing','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/52/e1e7eb90de998e052c7a3caa19596c9a',49,'2020-08-05 17:03:30',NULL),(53,2,52,'Stair Railings','stair-railings','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/53/8d59b72cc30b437b5cca61168da9465a',50,'2020-08-05 17:04:25',''),(54,2,52,'Stair Steps','stair-steps','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/54/f9891d6491caba2f33d05a3613e66449',51,'2020-08-05 17:04:25','<p>From a design standpoint, your basement steps are one of the most important features in the entire room, setting the tone for your guests and letting them know what they can expect next. With our incredible array of basement stairs ideas to help inspire you, designing just the right entrance has never been easier – or more fun. Your guests will be delighted as they descend down stairs made of the finest wood and covered with premium carpeting. As you grasp a smoothly polished banister, heels clicking under sturdy wood, you will know that you made the right decision coming to BasementRemodeling.com for all of your stair steps ideas! Try as our competition might, only Basement Masters can design a staircase that is as luxurious as the rest of your home.</p>'),(55,1,22,'Under Stairs Space','under-stairs-space','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/55/48dfadfa135f63d05ba205fd7395b989',52,'2020-08-05 17:04:46','<p>With our expert guidance, no area of your basement will be underutilized, not even your under-the-stairs space! From an extravagant staircase bookshelf to entire wardrobes, we have a litany of astonishing design plans that will give you under stairs storage options the likes of which you have never seen before. For example, if your basement is not large enough for a kids’ playroom, or if you do not feel like devoting a large portion of the basement for this purpose, then let us carefully craft a miniature kids’ playroom area just by utilizing a small portion of space under the stairs. With a mock house stencil on the outside with a working light switch and a small window hole, your kid will truly have a space that they can call all of their own (finally leaving the rest of the downstairs to design as you wish). Call now and let us create simple, practical, and stylishly clean storage spaces under the stairs for your basement for you.</p>'),(56,0,NULL,'Engineering Features','engineering-features','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/56/293899b22f4e54ca98e303986e95cb3b',57,'2020-08-05 17:05:06',NULL),(57,1,56,'Egress Windows','egress-windows','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/57/619c7f3608b9540c9dc82aaee3338b91',58,'2020-08-05 17:06:58','<p>Egress windows and egress window wells are the best ideas for letting natural light into your basement. Situated higher up than normal windows, far away from rocks and dirt, basement egress windows also lets water drain away from the home’s foundation so that water does not build up and warp the infrastructure. Egress window wells fulfill the same purpose, but with the added benefit of giving you easy access in and out of your home.</p>'),(58,1,56,'Walk-Outs','walk-outs','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/58/8a0923be6a467199e7c918de8d957146',59,'2020-08-05 17:06:58','<p>A walkout basement is an innovative architectural design feature that lets in an abundance of natural light, adds overall value to the estate, and gives easy access to your basement from the outside. Having a walkout basement means that you can enter and exit the downstairs area without disturbing anyone else in the home, affording extra privacy that’s ideal for guest situations. Also, when moving large items to and from your home, you can use your walkout basement instead of having to haul them through the main living areas.<br></p>'),(59,1,56,'HVAC','hvac','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/59/17a2c3385622522bb133b47921bcf649',60,'2020-08-05 17:06:58','<p>A basement\'s heating, venting and air conditioning (HVAC) unit is responsible for maintaining a comfortable indoor temperature not only downstairs, but also throughout the entire property. As such, the HVAC system is a critical component in any basement remodeling or basement finishing project.</p>'),(60,1,56,'Waterproofing','waterproofing','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/60/36dbc520f2c474c68c4b421abb7d9619',61,'2020-08-05 17:06:58','<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Waterproofing Your Basement: When, Why, and How</b></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span>You work hard to keep your house looking nice on the outside, but are you doing all that you can to maintain its structural integrity from within? Moisture has many ways of entering your home, where it can go on to cause a wide variety of health problems and damage to infrastructure if left untreated. Fortunately, BasementRemodeling.com are here to waterproof your basement and keep your home in top condition.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Why Does Waterproofing My Basement Matter?</b></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span>Aside from preventing leaks and floods, waterproofing a basement stops the following hazardous conditions from happening:</span></p>\n<ul style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<li><span>Mold and mildew -- this unique form of fungus slowly decomposes all non-living materials, which unfortunately includes many building materials such as carpet, drywall, and lumber. Aside from causing extensive structural damage, mold spores can also spread to other areas of the home and cause upper respiratory complications such as congestion, infections, and severe allergic reactions.</span></li>\n<li><span>Radon – this toxic gas rises from the soil into your home via basement floors or foundational cracks. As more and more radon gas becomes trapped inside of your living space, the levels become dangerously high and can cause cancer. Worse still, it is impossible to detect radon by sight or smell, so you really must rely on the professionals when it comes to this area. </span></li>\n<li><span>Iron bacteria – when water gets into your basement or crawlspace, bacterium in the water produces ferrous oxide, a gummy substance that can clog exterior and interior drain tiles as well as sump pumps. Once the ferrous oxide hardens, nothing will unclog it. Whatever waterproofing system equipment it binds to will need to be completely replaced after a short while.</span></li>\n<li><span>Foundation cracks – water seepage can cause small cracks in the foundation to widen into huge problems. When the cracks get large enough, the foundation becomes compromised and starts to shift. This can lead to the house heavily leaning to one side, or even collapsing altogether.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span>In order to prevent these problems, you need to properly waterproof your basement!</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>How Can I Identify Moisture Problems in My Basement?</b></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span>Not all signs of a basement moisture problem are as easily recognizable as a musty odor or a puddle. Be on the lookout for these common indicators that your basement needs waterproofing:</span></p>\n<ul style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<li><span>High humidity levels</span></li>\n<li><span>Damp patches on the walls or floors</span></li>\n<li><span>Wet insulation</span></li>\n<li><span>Condensation on pipes and ductwork</span></li>\n<li><span>Orange stains (a sign of iron bacteria)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span>Above all else, the only true way to know if your basement is safe is to contact the professionals and allow them to conduct an assessment according to the latest federal guidelines and standards.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>How Does Moisture Get into the Basement?</b></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span>Not all leaky basements are as simple as fixing a broken pipe. There are many ways for moisture to enter your basement or crawlspace and cause devastation. Here are three of the most common ways:</span></p>\n<ul style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<li><span>Cracked foundation – cracks in the foundation are a small problem that can add up. Too much water in your yard, be it from a high water table to improperly placed gutters, will cause your foundation to shift. Conversely, dry soil can create pockets for water to form in as well. </span></li>\n<li><span>High humidity – basement walls and floors are naturally cool, and as warm air enters the home, it can cause condensation to form. As you can see, no leaks have to be present at all for there to be a moisture problem in this instance!</span></li>\n<li><span>Iron bacteria – this special type of bacteria may come from the introduction of contaminated soil, contaminated landscaping tools, or even by way of transplanted plants and flowers.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>How Do You Fix a Basement with Moisture Problems?</b></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span>Eliminating moisture from your basement or crawlspace is a delicate situation that often requires industrial equipment and expert knowledge. After assessing your individual basement’s conditions, the experts at&nbsp;BasementRemodeling.com will be able to handle whatever needs to be done next on a case-by-case basis. Here are some of our general solutions, all proven to work with the highest rates of success:</span></p>\n<ul style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<li><span>Sump pump – if water is threatening your downstairs area, a sump pump will carry water away from the basement and the foundation as well. Not only will we inspect and repair your current sump pump, but we will also replace it, if necessary, with one of our own deluxe models, which includes:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><span>Battery backup in case of power outage.</span></li>\n<li><span>Dual pumping action for maximum efficiency.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><span>Interior and exterior drains – a drainage system captures excessive moisture under your home or in your yard and channels it directly into your sump pump for far-reaching results.</span></li>\n<li><span>Vapor barriers – these protective structures can be built directly into the wall or floor to avoid the formation of moisture from condensation.</span></li>\n<li><span>Foundation repairs – there are many ways for us to fix problems with your foundation:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><span>Epoxy Injections – this special sealant keeps out moisture and repairs basic cracks in floors or walls caused by damage to the foundation.</span></li>\n<li><span>Underpinning Piers – these sturdy steel structures are pushed deep into the earth until they reach a firm layer of soil. Once the piers are properly stress-tested, the house is lifted onto each one for long-lasting re-stabilization.</span></li>\n<li><span>Wall Anchors – rods are inserted through holes in the foundation that extend deep into the earth. Plates are then installed against the interior and exterior wall, and a lug nut squeezes the two plates against the foundation, tightening it back into place.</span></li>\n<li><span>Carbon Fiber Strips – strips of carbon fiber are secured over the cracks in combination with epoxy injections. This method is cost effective, easy to install, and requires no additional maintenance. </span></li>\n<li><span>These repairs also prevent the buildup of radon in your home.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><span>Iron bacteria – from special treatments to custom piping, we can design a waterproofing system that is resistant to the many different strains of iron bacteria.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span>When it comes to crawlspaces,&nbsp;BasementRemodeling.com has developed an all-in-one System Seal plan that eliminates the most common problems associated with moisture control:</span></p>\n<ul style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<li><span>Special steps to eliminate mold, mildew and allergens.</span></li>\n<li><span>Sealant applied to cracks in basement floors, walls, and the foundation to limit radon exposure.</span></li>\n<li><span>Completely insulate the crawlspace to reduce energy costs.</span></li>\n<li><span>In addition to moisture control, no more rodents or other pests will be able to enter your home!</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Why Choose BasementRemodeling.com?</b></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span>We know how daunting it can be to have a leaky basement. You just want to get the problem to go away and never return again. At&nbsp;BasementRemodeling.com, we have the knowledge, the equipment, and the credentials to take care of any basement moisture problem so that you can stop worrying and get back to your normal lifestyle. Let us take a professional waterproofing approach that’s guaranteed to dry up your basement – and keep it that way!<br></span></p>'),(63,2,33,'Carpet','carpet',NULL,33,'2020-10-16 16:56:22',NULL),(64,2,52,'Stair Half-Walls','stair-half-walls','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/categories/64/dd983b2cb5bdd4c4d93307cd77380fd3',34,'2021-08-27 14:10:33','<p>Elegant stair railings and banister ideas create a grand entrance, setting an appropriate tone for the rest of your basement. Whether you want wrought iron railings or traditional wood with stair balusters, we have a wide selection of stair railing ideas guaranteed to make an exquisite debut. Our half walls gently glide to the floor and provide sturdy and decorative banister grips. Let us work with you to create the perfect stair railings and banister ideas for a staircase that can spiral, twist, or otherwise descend into luxury.</p>');
