INSERT INTO `testimonials` VALUES (16,'Loretta Usilton, Mount Airy, MD testimonial','','','loretta-usilton-mount-airy-md','Loretta Usilton','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/16/75984fe393e68cd9b44089bae8d6095e','I found Basement Masters on Angie’s List and, because of the outstanding reviews, decided to get a quote from them in addition to another local company who I’ve had experience with in the past.  From the first meeting with Pavel, I was extremely impressed','<p>I found Basement Masters on Angie&rsquo;s List and, because of the outstanding reviews, decided to get a quote from them in addition to another local company who I&rsquo;ve had experience with in the past. From the first meeting with Pavel, I was extremely impressed with the efficiency and transparency of how he runs his business. He is extremely organized and makes the most of technology via his iPad and various software applications. He sat down with me and, because I knew what I wanted for my finished product, we were able to go through his detailed brochure and develop a proposed initial cost at that very first meeting. As others have stated, you know exactly what each component of your estimate costs and you can choose from various options to make the overall total fit your budget. In addition, if you want to be more hands on and purchase some items (i.e., faucets, vanity, bathroom towel bars, etc.) yourself, Pavel provides an allowance for those items. Not only did this assure I got exactly what I wanted, I was able to save some money by finding things cheaper than the allowance provided by shopping online and/or finding items on sale locally. Once Pavel&rsquo;s team began working, I realized that Pavel&rsquo;s superior customer service and work ethic doesn\'t stop with him. His entire team and the subcontractors he uses share his values. They were on time, communicative and did outstanding work.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Everything was done to code. It is so rare to find this consistent level of caring customer service today. He even provided an interior designer to meet with us to discuss colors and finishes. After selecting paint colors, she got samples and applied them to the walls for us to see in different lights. This was a real asset because what we thought we wanted was not what we finally selected. When we ran into unforeseen issues during the project (which is to be expected), Pavel and/or his team always consulted with me and provided options. I had the final say in how the issue was resolved. I was also amazed at the long hours they kept. It wasn&rsquo;t unusual to see emails from Pavel sent at 12:30 a.m. Also, there were several days when his folks were there for 10-12 hours as well as weekends. This was always done with my advance permission. Not only did they come in on budget and provide a stellar finished project, they completed it one week early.</p>\n<p>Bottom line, we love our new basement and I would very highly recommend Basement Masters. My only regret is that I only have one basement or I&rsquo;d definitely use them again myself!</p>','Mount Airy, MD',5,'129',37,'2018-04-18 16:19:00'),(17,'Darlene Orr, Columbia, MD testimonial','','','darlene-orr-columbia-md','Darlene Orr','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/17/684d9bb07914077d0a67a5fd10eab780','Doing this project with Basement Masters was actually a very enjoyable experience. I had a vague idea of what I wanted and Pavel Abaev was able to pick up on that and make it a reality. The first night he came out, it was after dark and our basement was s','<p>Doing this project with Basement Masters was actually a very enjoyable experience. I had a vague idea of what I wanted and Pavel Abaev was able to pick up on that and make it a reality. The first night he came out, it was after dark and our basement was so full of stuff that I was wondering if he would be able to figure out a floor plan. I had to shove boxes aside to show him where the rough-in for a toilet was. Interestingly enough, I had already had 2 other companies come out and the first thing those companies did was pull out their measuring tape and start figuring out how much to charge per square foot. Pavel didn&rsquo;t even need a measuring tape &ndash; he instantly knew the space to be finished was about 700 square feet. I was amazed. Then he looked at the toilet rough in and instantly knew it would have to be moved about 2 feet to make room for a shower and that he could fit a 5&rsquo; X 3&rsquo; shower into the space between the existing furnace and stairs. Mind you, there were boxes piled as high as my head and you had to squeeze sideways between my stuff. Pavel is so experienced with basements and their many idiosyncrasies that things I thought would be difficult, such as how to hide the furnace and get around random plumbing, were not obstacles at all for him. He already had an eye on where to put walls so that I would gain the most space while at the same time keep things aesthetically pleasing.</p>\n<p>After a good half-hour of listening to my inexperienced ramblings we went upstairs and Pavel pulled out a Welcome Brochure that is actually a booklet that contains everything you might ever want in your basement with a cost breakdown. Pavel pointed out the company&rsquo;s credentials, license numbers, insurance policy, etc. &ndash; everything you want a company to have but are generally afraid to ask. &nbsp;Pavel is very upfront with everything and I learned to trust him early into the project &ndash; something I never felt I could do with previous projects or companies. Other companies suggest things that make it easier for them but may not be in your best interest. The total opposite is true of Pavel &ndash; he brings up things you may not have thought of even though it will make more work for him and his crew, but knowing that if he didn&rsquo;t bring it up you might later realize you should have done it that way and you wouldn&rsquo;t be totally happy.</p>\n<p>As others have said, his crew and the people he orchestrates to do the tile, painting, flooring, granite, and carpet are all experts in their field and reliable. Even so, Pavel is constantly checking that they are doing perfect work and doing things in a world class manner. Even as picky as I am, Pavel was pickier and held the workers to a very high standard. Any basement that Basement Masters creates could go in the finest mansion- the work is that good. At the same time, Pavel&rsquo;s price was the best out of the three companies I had come out. One company, also on Angie&rsquo;s list, had never heard of LVT, and every time I brought up some of the things I had learned from Pavel, such as using soundproofing drywall and spray-foam insulation, the &nbsp;guy looked pained and said that would really run up the cost. With Basement Masters, it cost a little more but was still in the reasonable range. What I liked also with BM was that I could pay a little more and get the best, such as Benjamin Moore paint and the highest finishing grade on the drywall so I could use the eggshell finish I preferred. &nbsp; Just for a comparison, the other company wanted upwards of $75,000 to finish my basement on a comparable level. On the other hand, Basement Masters, even with all of my &ldquo;upgrades&rdquo; such as full tile shower, frameless shower door, LVT flooring, level 5 finish on the drywall, spray-foam insulation, sound-proof ceiling drywall and Benjamin Moore paint, my total cost was $53,753. I could go on and on with how happy I am with my basement and how easy it was to work with Basement Masters. The only reason you should get other estimates is so that you feel great when you get Basement Masters&rsquo;.</p>\n<p>The best part of the project is working with Pavel because he is always available, always gets you an answer right away, and you can trust him.</p>','Columbia, MD',5,'180',36,'2018-07-10 17:06:00'),(18,'Janet Cara, Potomac, MD testimonial','','','janet-cara-potomac-md','Janet Cara','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/18/d2430699e99b351203ff9c463f3bef89','My husband and I spend a great deal of time in Maryland at my daughter’s house with her, our son-in-law, and our grandson. When they announced that they were expecting another child, we decided to renovate their 1000 square foot basement into a comfortabl','<p>My husband and I spend a great deal of time in Maryland at my daughter&rsquo;s house with her, our son-in-law, and our grandson. When they announced that they were expecting another child, we decided to renovate their 1000 square foot basement into a comfortable space for the two of us. I had no prior experience planning a renovation. I naively thought that I would simply hire a contractor, tell him what I wanted, and the work would be done, within the limits of my budget. Little did I know that my choice of a contractor would turn out to be the single most important factor in determining the outcome of my renovation.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I began my online search for a contractor in the Maryland area through the Houzz app. I chose five contractors based their exemplary reviews from former clients. I met with each one of them and obtained estimates for the basement renovation. The estimate I got from Basement Masters was the most reasonable, however, my decision to use them was not based on that alone. I chose Basement Masters because when I met Pavel, he didn&rsquo;t just &ldquo;yes&rdquo; me to death. He really listened to my ideas for the basement, and thoughtfully offered his expertise and guidance when necessary. I thought I had a pretty good idea of what I wanted, but I learned that there were numerous details to be discussed and decisions to be made as the work proceeded. In retrospect, I realize that my original plan was really very vague and without Pavel&rsquo;s knowledge, support, and guidance, I would have been totally lost.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The location of the renovation presented an unusual challenge. I was not going to be on site for a majority of the time. Pavel and I kept in very close contact through calling and texting. I knew that I could text him at any time and receive a response from him immediately. I was always able to reach him directly within seconds.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Once the work began, I did not anticipate the possibility that I might change my mind about decisions I had made. However, when that did happen, Pavel not only tolerated my questions and indecisiveness; he actually encouraged me to consider and explore all of the options available. He often sent me pictures or websites that had examples of materials for me to consider. For example, in an effort to save money, we were going to keep the original laminate flooring in the majority of the basement and install a different flooring in an area that was being torn up to remove an unwanted bar. Midway through the reno, we decided to replace the entire floor. I&rsquo;m sure it threw off his entire crew&rsquo;s work schedule. He was extremely flexible and it was never a problem for him to change the original plans to accommodate us. And the finished floor is spectacular!</p>\n<p>Pavel was on site on a regular basis to see that every aspect of the reno was being addressed properly, from paint to electric to finishes. He takes obvious pride in his work. His attention to detail is phenomenal. I absolutely love the custom work on the cabinets, the kitchen island that he designed, the wainscoting throughout the main living space, and the millwork surrounding the fireplace.</p>\n<p>I am, undeniably, a perfectionist. Fortunately for me, Pavel shares my passion for perfection. I am thrilled with the renovation! It is exquisitely beautiful and exceptionally functional! I would not change a thing. It surpasses anything that I could ever have imagined. We will enjoy this space for many, many years to come. I am certain that if I had not chosen Basement Masters and Pavel had not been my contractor, the result would have been very different. Pavel is the ultimate professional. It was a pleasure working with him and his highly competent crew. Thank you, Basement Masters!</p>','Potomac, MD',5,'120',35,'2018-11-14 18:13:00'),(19,'Matthew Eapen, Rockville, MD testimonial','','','matthew-eapen-rockville-md','Matthew Eapen','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/19/5ae80167e97ce86116354d7c9ac01f60','I found Basement Masters on Angie’s List and, because of the outstanding reviews, decided to get a quote from them in addition to another local company who I’ve had experience with in the past.  From the first meeting with Pavel, I was...','<p>We have worked with many contractors in the past, as our house was a fixer upper. I wish I had discovered Pavel earlier because the basement is now the nicest part of our house. We had our roughly 1300SF basement finished by Basement Masters, and could not be any happier with the results. This was a very large project, which required converting our underground basement into a walk out with double doors. The transformation has been amazing, and our friends can\'t believe what we were able to do with such a large dark space. We finished a beautiful full bathroom, and the workmanship on the tile work is wonderful. In fact, all of the contractors that worked on our house were very professional, courteous and skilled at their trade. Pavel hires specialists for every line of work (painters, drywall, etc.), so you get contractors who really know what they are doing and aren&rsquo;t a jack-of-all-trades. Pavel, who is the owner and operator, was very good at responding to questions, and worked with us to make sure the end product was exactly what we wanted. I would not hesitate to recommend Pavel and Basement Masters to anyone.</p>','Rockville, MD',5,'130',34,'2019-01-27 18:15:00'),(20,'Anthony Trueba, Fulton, MD testimonial','','','anthony-trueba-fulton-md','Anthony Trueba','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/20/3bfbd3a6ad351bd89406d12fc47daf76','Basement Masters did an outstanding job finishing 1000 sq. ft. basement. I got estimates from 4 contractors, all found through Angie\'s list. Pavel impressed me right away with his straight forward very organized and itemized estimate. He was very competit','<p>Basement Masters did an outstanding job finishing 1000 sq. ft. basement. I got estimates from 4 contractors, all found through Angie\'s list. Pavel impressed me right away with his straight forward very organized and itemized estimate. He was very competitive with the others but the others were just not as detailed and clear. Pavel came to my house twice and spent all the time I needed to make sure we were on the same page before I decided to go with his company. The contract detail also was very key in making us at ease. &nbsp;We knew what to expect. Pavel is very easy to get a hold of throughout the build. He uses email and texts to keep you aware of the schedule and any changes. We were in contact as much as I needed, he responds very quickly. &nbsp;Whenever I saw something I thought needed to be changed or if I just had questions they had no problem listening and either changing or explaining their plan. Pavel is very detail oriented and wants to do a good job. He understands that if we are happy with the final product that we will recommend him to others. During the build we made decisions jointly and easily before any work was done so there were no surprises. All the workers were punctual, polite and made an effort to keep the work space as quite and clean as possible.</p>\n<p>I am as pleased with Basement Masters as I have ever been with any contractor. I can feel very comfortable recommending Pavel and his crew to friends and family.</p>','Fulton, MD',5,'228',33,'2019-02-20 18:21:00'),(21,'Anna Giallo, Gaithersburg, MD testimonial','','','anna-giallo-gaithersburg-md','Anna Giallo',NULL,'We bought our next home and wanted to finish the basement. We got quotes from several contractors. Pavel\'s quote was not only reasonable, but also very clear, everything is clearly priced in the booklet, no hidden...','<p>We bought our next home and wanted to finish the basement. We got quotes from several contractors. Pavel\'s quote was not only reasonable, but also very clear, everything is clearly priced in the booklet, no hidden gimmicks. We felt very comfortable with him, he was not pushy, always quick to respond via text or email. In the end we felt we\'ve made the best choice and can\'t be happier with his crew. His crew arrived on time everyday to work in the house. His men are very courteous and professional. No one is wandering around or talking on the phone, everyone worked together efficiently. As much as we loved to have our basement done sooner, we were almost sad to see them go, they are just that good! Pavel kept in touch with us throughout the process. He was on top of everything, from ordering parts to discussing different options, we learned a lot from him as well, things we amateur could not have thought of before the worked started! Pavel\'s team finished our basement and created a good size bedroom/closet, added a modern bathroom, media room and a beautiful bar that we\'ll enjoy for many years to come.</p>\n<p>Overall we would recommend his team to anyone who needs basement work. It\'s been a pleasure working with his team, they are the best you can get in town.</p>\n<p>Thanks Pavel!</p>','Gaithersburg, MD',5,'',32,'2019-03-07 08:18:00'),(22,'Ben O\'Gradney, Frederick, MD testimonial','','','ben-o-gradney-frederick-md','Ben O\'Gradney','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/22/9317133246a6d162b71aa68bc714fb73','If you are reading this review, then there is no need to look any further. Basement Masters sets the industry standard and far exceeded my expectations in my recent 1400 SF complete basement renovation. Their competitive pricing, superior attention to det','<p>If you are reading this review, then there is no need to look any further. Basement Masters sets the industry standard and far exceeded my expectations in my recent 1400 SF complete basement renovation. Their competitive pricing, superior attention to detail, impeccable cleanliness &amp; courtesy and ability to adhere to a very strict timeline sets Basement Masters apart as the BEST!!!</p>\n<p>Pavel, the owner, is probably the most knowledgeable, dedicated and hands-on owner I have ever encountered, and we have done many home improvement projects in multiple houses within multiple states. He delivers a detailed, very reasonable quote before he leaves your house on the day of the estimate. He has a sharp, creative eye for design and at times sent multiple emails for suggested products to use, even late at night. He personally went to three different Home Depots gathering specific tile that we wanted to use for our large, ADA compliant bathroom. Multiple times we changed our minds on a selection, sometimes after it was already installed, and Pavel willingly accomodated our choices, almost immediately. Every single employee in Pavel\'s crew abides by the same expectation for excellence and delivers superior work with a very pleasant, dedicated attitude.</p>\n<p>7 1/2 weeks after starting with a concrete slab, Basement Masters delivered an absolutely breathtaking basement \"condo\" equipped with a bedroom, handicapped accessible bathroom, gorgeous kitchenette, family room and a kid\'s playroom. On April 3rd, 2015 we welcomed my 84 year old grandmother into our home and her life as well as our own are forever changed. Thank you Basement Masters for bringing our vision to life and allowing Grandma to safely spend the rest of her days with us. All of us are forever grateful!</p>','Frederick, MD',5,'208',31,'2019-04-30 07:23:00'),(23,'Bess Altweeger, Columbia, MD testimonial','','','bess-altweeger-columbia-md','Bess Altweeger','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/23/8312bda5b6c30c430eaf058e3b2c1223','We used this Basement Masters to have our basement completely remodeled to include a new bathroom, a bedroom and a kitchenette. Pavel is an expert at what he does. From beginning to end he demonstrated a thorough knowledge of the entire project (electrica','<p>We used this Basement Masters to have our basement completely remodeled to include a new bathroom, a bedroom and a kitchenette. Pavel is an expert at what he does. From beginning to end he demonstrated a thorough knowledge of the entire project (electrical, plumbing, construction, etc) and was extremely efficient and professional. He offered excellent suggestions on design but also bent to our preferences as they came up. He also gave us a checklist of everything we needed to purchase and everything that was included in the project. Unfortunately, we slowed him down because we fell behind in the purchases and selections we needed to make. Otherwise, we are certain that the project would have been done in the time he estimated. The crew Pavel assembled and supervised was outstanding - great craftsman, punctual and considerate. They kept everything clean and orderly as they worked. I was totally comfortable with having them in the house.</p>\n<p>The final result is a gorgeous basement that far exceeds our expectations. Pavel inspected everything toward the final stages and either repaired or replaced any materials that had even the slightest imperfection (such as the closet doors in our kitchenette). He is a perfectionist with all the work he performs and clearly takes great pride in his work. We ended up paying more than we had planned, but that was due to selections we made that exceeded the allowances he gave us. We also added a built in gas fireplace with a stone surround that is simply gorgeous and the highlight of the basement. I highly recommend Pavel to anyone that wants outstanding workmanship and great value.</p>','Columbia, MD',5,'131',30,'2019-05-26 07:25:00'),(24,'James and Agnes O\'Connell, Marriotsville, MD testimonial','','','james-and-agnes-o-connell-marriotsville-md','James and Agnes O\'Connell','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/24/995abc542399d91c16b984aadfe7aebd','After deciding to finish the basement, we interviewed five contractors. Most of the contractors came with a tape measure and took some notes and promised to get back with us. Almost all of the contractors came back with a lump sum quotes with very little ','<p>After deciding to finish the basement, we interviewed five contractors. Most of the contractors came with a tape measure and took some notes and promised to get back with us. Almost all of the contractors came back with a lump sum quotes with very little breakout. We were more interested in line item costs so we could add or delete per our budget.</p>\n<p>Basement Masters provided a booklet with all the prices set and in great detail. That is what we wanted. We explained our hopes and dreams and Pavel helped us put them into reality within our budget. The communication between Pavel and us was fantastic! He must sleep with the phone tied to his ear. Responses to our question and concerns were always within minutes. Construction began exactly on the appointed day and the workers were very experienced and excellent workers. They encouraged us to make changes as we saw fit and willingly made the changes. At the end of each day the work area was swept clean and all tools were piled neatly out of the way. A refreshing change from other construction projects we had undertaken. All during the construction Pavel talked to us and offered suggestions on how to make things better and for a better price.</p>\n<p>John and George, the onsite mechanics, worked with the utmost concern to detail and precision with all the trim and cabinet work. The electrician and painter and drywall people also exhibited the same concern for a perfect finished product. During the entire project Pavel continued to be onsite reviewing the work and answering our questions and concerns.</p>\n<p>Payment for the project was staggered to coincide with the work progress, a helpful alternative to lump sum payments.</p>\n<p>We are extremely happy with the end result and even happier that we chose Pavel and his team at Basement Masters.</p>','Marriotsville, MD',5,'147',29,'2019-06-07 07:31:00'),(25,'Paul Hallowell, Millersville, MD testimonial','','','paul-hallowell-millersville-md','Paul Hallowell','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/25/25b8eaa1154960aafcfd8eaaf0598808','If you are searching for a contractor to finish your basement, you needn\'t look any further - Basement Masters is the one. The quality of their work is second to none; and their price is more than competitive. We couldn’t be happier with our basement, and','<p>If you are searching for a contractor to finish your basement, you needn\'t look any further - Basement Masters is the one. The quality of their work is second to none; and their price is more than competitive. We couldn&rsquo;t be happier with our basement, and we&rsquo;ve never met a more organized, professional and meticulous general contractor than Pavel Abaev. Every aspect of the project was flawlessly performed, as Pavel managed the finishing of our basement like a well-oiled machine. From framing to electrical to drywall to finishing and trim, Pavel has an outstanding team behind him; every one of them very professional, tidy, and cared for our house as if it was their own. But it&rsquo;s the quality of the work that will amaze you. We even had comments from county inspectors on the superb craftsmanship exhibited by Pavel and his team. That&rsquo;s when you know you have the right contractor!</p>\n<p>Throughout the process, Pavel was very accommodating in helping us with any and all questions we had; plus, he and his crew were quite receptive to handling minor changes in the design that we had along the way. Pavel kept us well informed about next steps and work schedules from week to week. And, much to our delight, he finished two weeks ahead of the promised completion date.</p>\n<p>In short, we are extremely pleased with the final product, and would strongly recommend Basement Masters for your remodeling needs.</p>','Millersville, MD',5,'247',28,'2019-07-17 07:34:00'),(26,'Jason and Shauna Vlosich, Ellicott City, MD testimonial','','','jason-and-shauna-vlosich-ellicott-city-md','Jason and Shauna Vlosich','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/26/15e0b9ff36bc8d4d67517643ba1901e7','We highly recommend Basement Masters. From the first consultation to the last walk-through, Pavel and his crew were professional, respectful, and courteous. Pavel was quick to understand the big-picture of how we wanted the finished basement to look. It w','<p>We highly recommend Basement Masters. From the first consultation to the last walk-through, Pavel and his crew were professional, respectful, and courteous. Pavel was quick to understand the big-picture of how we wanted the finished basement to look. It was obvious to us that one of Pavel&rsquo;s top concerns was our satisfaction and that did not change as we made decisions down to the smallest details.</p>\n<p>One thing, in particular, that was important to us was that the finished basement flow from the rest of the house. We were concerned about the small details like moldings, doors, door knobs, window frames, and railings. Pavel heard our concerns and made sure that the details in the basement matched the rest of the house. Another thing that was very important to us was the balance of the basement. Pavel worked closely with us on the designs to ensure that the basement would feel balanced and meet our expectations.</p>\n<p>We were also extremely pleased with the level of craftsmanship displayed by Pavel&rsquo;s subcontractors. As we watched the progress of the project, we were pleased at the level of skill, efficiency, and cleanliness of the workers. As a result, they not only finished a basement that looks amazing, but they finished two weeks ahead of schedule!</p>','Ellicott City, MD',5,'177',27,'2019-08-28 07:37:00'),(27,'Miriam Nager, Silver Spring, MD testimonial','','','miriam-nager-silver-spring-md','Miriam Nager','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/27/4fc1df38334910e1e7508421037b831d','From start to finish, this is how working with a contractor should be. We obtained quotes from 2 other contractors before decided to move forward with Pavel and Basement Masters. One of the other contractors was perfectly nice and provided a reasonable qu','<p>From start to finish, this is how working with a contractor should be. We obtained quotes from 2 other contractors before decided to move forward with Pavel and Basement Masters. One of the other contractors was perfectly nice and provided a reasonable quote, but it was clear that basements were not their expertise. The other contractor must have upcharged every item by more than 200%, because the quote we obtained from them was outrageous. Pavel came by and had every detail down to a science, complete with a booklet outlining all of the options and precise costs. He also answered all of our questions in a thoughtful and meaningful way and gave us advice on how to improve the design and reduce costs. One thing we really appreciated is that Basement Masters not only offers a 10% discount to Angie\'s List members, but Pavel will round every number down when he applies the discount. It\'s little touches like that that make you feel like you\'re not being nickel and dimed.</p>\n<p>The construction process kicked off right when expected and finished about 2 weeks ahead of schedule. All along the way, Pavel communicated clearly as to what would happen next, let us know when we needed to take action or make a decision, and was always available via text and email to help with questions.</p>\n<p>The end result is a basement that hardly looks like a basement anymore. It is a bright, beautiful space. We are so pleased with the final result and would recommend Basement Masters to anyone looking for quality work done the right way at a reasonable price.</p>','Silver Spring, MD',5,'234',26,'2019-09-12 07:45:00'),(28,'Martin and Allison Tong, Severna Park, MD testimonial','','','martin and allison tong, severna park, md','Martin and Allison Tong','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/28/3bb4d40484206910647d3de3a99bcbdb','We were referred to Basement Masters from a friend, and couldn\'t have been happier with our experience! There are so many unique things to consider when remodeling a basement (water/flooding, pipes, septic, etc.) And I was glad to have a team that special','<p>We were referred to Basement Masters from a friend, and couldn\'t have been happier with our experience! There are so many unique things to consider when remodeling a basement (water/flooding, pipes, septic, etc.) And I was glad to have a team that specialized in basements. They were professional and finished well ahead of projections! Pavel, the owner, was very responsive to all our questions, and was involved in every step of the process. We\'ve already recommended them to some of our neighbors &amp; friends!</p>','Severna Park, MD',5,'227',25,'2019-10-13 07:51:00'),(29,'Michelle Kobryn, Annapolis, MD testimonial','','','michelle-kobryn-annapolis-md','Michelle Kobryn','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/29/393c00f2e2be3d9be6165bd758d6e2ac','From the first meeting, after already getting 4 other quotes, I was BLOWN AWAY. The team at Basement Masters has basement remodeling down to a science, and the first consultation was informative and clearly showed an understanding that all the others lack','<p>From the first meeting, after already getting 4 other quotes, I was BLOWN AWAY. The team at Basement Masters has basement remodeling down to a science, and the first consultation was informative and clearly showed an understanding that all the others lacked.</p>\n<p>From the first meeting, I trusted them to do a great job - and they did not disappoint. They were punctual, did what they said they would at every step, took my family needs into account, and made sure I was comfortable with every possible decision. When the lumber yard dropped off the materials to get started, he raved about the team, so I went in with high expectations, and they did not disappoint. Have you ever heard of a contractor doing MORE than you thought they needed to? Basement Masters - multiple times - went above and beyond to make sure as Pavel of Basement Masters said \"that it would look and function like I would expect in my own home\". Design ideas were shared that made the basement much better than originally planned, and the process went so smoothly I can rank Basement Masters has the best contractor I\'ve ever worked with, or heard of for that matter.</p>\n<p>You can go out and get other quotes for your basement, I urge you to get them before you call Basement Masters. Because when they show up, the competence they have and attention to detail will shine in the very first meeting, and will continue to show up all throughout the project.</p>\n<p>The basement is beautiful. On budget, exceeded expectations, and the process was painless.</p>','Annapolis, MD',5,'202',24,'2019-11-12 08:58:00'),(30,'Marsha Rose, Ellicott City, MD testimonial','','','marsha-rose-ellicott-city-md','Marsha Rose',NULL,'I cannot overstate how fantastic it was working with Pavel and Basement Masters. Our case was especially awkward as the work was being done in Ellicott City and I live in Coral Springs, Florida. During my visits to Maryland, I met with 9 contractors befor','<p>I cannot overstate how fantastic it was working with Pavel and Basement Masters. Our case was especially awkward as the work was being done in Ellicott City and I live in Coral Springs, Florida. During my visits to Maryland, I met with 9 contractors before deciding to go with Basement Masters. My daughter, son-in-law (at whose house the work was being done) and I were amazed at Pavel\'s honesty, patience, and insistence on quality without increasing his original price. The work is absolutely perfect. As you open the French doors to the bedroom, it is apparent that the work was completed by professionals. The walls are three different colors, the carpet and the LVT floors look fantastic.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Here are some special reasons why I strongly recommend Basement Masters:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Pavel kept each of us (my daughter, son-in-law and me) informed on the week\'s schedule of work.</li>\n<li>Regardless of the improvements, the price was never increased. For example, instead of an exhaust fan in the bathroom, they installed a combination, fan, light, and heater - without any cost increase. Similarly, they encased the basement window and installed blinds, again without any price increase.</li>\n<li>It was clear that Pavel took pride in his work.</li>\n<li>In order to select the LVT flooring, Pavel mailed to me (in Florida) the samples from which to select. He mailed them at his expense, and again did not add it to our final cost.</li>\n<li>The vanity I purchased was extremely difficult to assemble. The correct parts were not included and it required a worker to buy some parts at Home Depot. Again, there was not increase in cost.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>I told my daughter we may have found one of the last honest contractors. I cannot imagine what more you could ask for in a contractor - honesty and top-notch quality. My only regret is that Pavel in is Maryland and not Florida!!</p>','Ellicott City, MD',5,'',23,'2019-12-24 09:02:00'),(31,'Paul and Darlene Mattocks, Columbia, MD testimonial','','','paul-and-darlene-mattocks-columbia-md','Paul and Darlene Mattocks','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/31/3895ef79dea01dfaf130eceb8bfe159c','I found Basement Masters on Angie\'s List and could not be happier. From the first meeting it was clear to us that Basement Masters was the contractor to hire. We had our basement with wet bar, full bathroom and two storage areas completely finished in our','<p>I found Basement Masters on Angie\'s List and could not be happier. From the first meeting it was clear to us that Basement Masters was the contractor to hire. We had our basement with wet bar, full bathroom and two storage areas completely finished in our home. Pavel, from day one, was professional, knowledgeable and ALWAYS available whenever we had questions, either by phone or text. Having an organized brochure, which lists the project cost breakdown, was a great tool to keep track of the budget. We also added an extra project that Pavel completed for us, which saved me from having to look for another contractor.</p>\n<p>I would HIGHLY RECOMMEND Pavel and his hard working crew to anyone who wants a beautiful basement.</p>','Columbia, MD',5,'162',22,'2020-01-15 09:06:00'),(32,'Hanli Ni, Bethesda, MD testimonial','','','hanli-ni-bethesda-md','Hanli Ni',NULL,'Pavel is the ultimate professional. He made a big impression on us the first day discussing our basement remodel. I would describe him and his team as experienced, efficient, responsive, and most of all trustworthy. He certainly takes his work with a sens','<p>Pavel is the ultimate professional. He made a big impression on us the first day discussing our basement remodel. I would describe him and his team as experienced, efficient, responsive, and most of all trustworthy. He certainly takes his work with a sense of pride. We consulted several contractors on our basement, Pavel is the only one who is able to provide us with a detailed price break down the first day. And his price is actually very reasonable. To our surprise, what came after we signed the contract with him greatly exceeded our expectations. He was always very clear on the schedule so we know what to expect. His team came to our house on time, very polite and efficient. And always willing to accommodate our requests and privacy. Any email or text to Pavel was answered within hours, if not minutes and always to the point. During the whole project, we always felt a piece of mind and everything is under control. We are very happy with the end result in terms of the quality of work. I would recommend him to anyone without reservation.</p>','Bethesda, MD',5,'',21,'2020-02-28 09:20:00'),(33,'Susan Lee, Columbia, MD testimonial','','','susan-lee-columbia-md','Susan Lee',NULL,'I interviewed three contractors for this job, and the prices were remarkably similar. Two of the three estimated 2 weeks to complete the job. Frankly, this sounded unbelievable to me. Pavel of Basement Masters...','<p>I interviewed three contractors for this job, and the prices were remarkably similar. Two of the three estimated 2 weeks to complete the job. Frankly, this sounded unbelievable to me. Pavel of Basement Masters estimated 6-8 weeks - in my experience, a lot more likely. Still, I pressed Pavel for the reason that his estimate was so much longer than the others. He proceeded to reel off every task that had to be done, the order in which they had to be done, how long each would take, which ones could overlap and which could not, and why. This had the unmistakable ring of a man who knows his job - and one that would say what was right, not what he thought the customer wanted to hear.</p>\n<p>On this basis, I hired Basement Masters, and I don\'t believe I could have done better. Everyone who worked at my house was skilled, worked hard, was polite and professional. Pavel kept everything moving, including me. When I had a decision to make or an order to place, I heard about it. The basement came out great - better than I would have thought. It\'s gone from an eyesore to a showpiece.</p>\n<p>Normally, this would be the end - good experience, good product. I feel I have to go a little further for this exceptional company. Normally, I hate the contractor experience - frustrating, or annoying, or both - but it was a pleasure to work with Pavel and Basement Masters. I felt like I had gone to watch my son\'s middle school basketball game and somehow ended up watching the Harlem Globe Trotters. For those of you who don\'t like sports - I bought tickets for rodeo and saw the Lipizzaners. Oh, well, you get the picture. If I have another job these people say they can do, I will hire them in a heartbeat.</p>','Columbia, MD',5,'',20,'2020-03-14 08:22:00'),(34,'Dawn Holmgren, Ellicott City, MD testimonial','','','dawn-holmgren-ellicott-city-md','Dawn Holmgren','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/34/fa6d64f9b9fa82c245990095aa9b326f','Basement Masters was impressive from the initial meeting. Their prompt communication, detailed explanations, personal meetings, expansive portfolio and transparent pricing led us to pick them for our large renovation project. Our project was begun and com','<p>Basement Masters was impressive from the initial meeting. Their prompt communication, detailed explanations, personal meetings, expansive portfolio and transparent pricing led us to pick them for our large renovation project. Our project was begun and completed on schedule. All work was built and finished to a high quality standard. The estimation and design process was clear, and the final cost of the project (barring any customer changes) was clearly stated prior to work beginning. Basement Masters accommodated our needs, and were polite and informative as we reviewed each construction step in the process in detail. Once work was under way, Pavel was easily accessible for any concerns about how something was done, or a request to change something on our end. As with any construction project of this size, things don\'t always go according to plan--but when there were issues, Pavel resolved our concerns in each case. The resolution always met or exceeded our expectations. We were extremely impressed that while there were design changes during construction, Basement Masters finished our project prior to the quoted date. The Basement Masters team is talented and experienced. The team made a number of very informed recommendations that we hadn\'t even considered.</p>\n<p>We highly recommend Basement Masters to anyone looking to finish a large basement space. We knew what we wanted, and we got what we asked for. We are very happy with the result!</p>','Ellicott City, MD',5,'187',19,'2020-04-07 08:25:00'),(35,'Catharine Rector, Chevy Chase, MD testimonial','','','catharine-rector-chevy-chase-md','Catharine Rector','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/35/9ed104b5523c80abf7fd145eaa3e5ed4','Working with Basement Masters was a wonderful experience! I read tons of reviews online and we got several quotes prior to starting our project. We wanted to add a bathroom which meant drilling into the basement floor...something that made me very nervous','<p>Working with Basement Masters was a wonderful experience! I read tons of reviews online and we got several quotes prior to starting our project. We wanted to add a bathroom which meant drilling into the basement floor...something that made me very nervous. Pavel was actually our first quote - he gave us a brochure that included EVERYTHING - prices, insurance, etc. and talked us through the project. I immediately trusted him. After several other quotes I still wanted Basement Masters and the prices were good compared to some of our other quotes.</p>\n<p>Pavel was very easy to get a hold of and always responded to our messages. We made a couple of changes (like paint color) mid-project and he was great about working with us. The pricing was straightforward and we paid what we expected to. We weren\'t stressed about the timeline, but everything was completed within the projected time- even with all of the snow!</p>\n<p>We love the basement - everything is gorgeous and the space turned out beautifully - all thanks to Basement Masters. We left a lot of decisions about the layout, lights, outlets, etc. to Pavel and he was fabulous! We couldn\'t be happier with the basement and we\'ve had tons of compliments on it! We would definitely recommend them to anyone who is thinking about finishing their basement.</p>','Chevy Chase, MD',5,'271',18,'2020-05-13 08:30:00'),(36,'Erica Rose, Woodstock, MD testimonial','','','erica-rose-woodstock-md','Erica Rose','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/36/3bf47942c669315300b154422440fa2b','I began the process of interviewing contractors starting in January of 2014. I had a good idea of what I wanted to do after looking at pictures online and research of basement-related issues. When Pavel came to see us, I knew he was our guy. Although he s','<p>I began the process of interviewing contractors starting in January of 2014. I had a good idea of what I wanted to do after looking at pictures online and research of basement-related issues. When Pavel came to see us, I knew he was our guy. Although he seemed rushed, he took measurements, pulled out an uber-detailed pricing brochure, and we started to talk. He seemed very knowledgeable about basement-related construction issues. We were able to finalize the contract without too much hassle, and he was willing to work with me on the lien releases I wanted.</p>\n<p>As soon as construction started, it was smooth-sailing. Pavel is probably one of the best general contractors I\'ve ever worked with on any of my homes. He was always available by text, email, and phone, and really kept us informed of the project plan. Pavel runs a tight ship. I can\'t say enough about his wonderful crew, and all of the subs he used. They were all fantastic, hard-working individuals who clearly take pride in their workmanship. Pavel finished almost three weeks ahead of schedule. Any issues we had, he fixed (or tried his best to fix). They even came back to install light fixtures when they finally came in after weeks on backorder.</p>\n<p>We now have a beautiful basement - a bright, beautiful living space. It doesn\'t feel like a basement at all! Thank you to Pavel and his entire crew for a job well done.</p>','Woodstock, MD',5,'124',17,'2020-06-29 08:36:00'),(37,'Rob and Mandy McIntyre, Silver Spring, MD testimonial','We recently remodeled our original 1980s-style basement with Basement Masters, and we are extremely happy with the end results.','testimonials, reviews, clients, past clients, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','rob-and-mandy-mcintyre-silver-spring-md','Rob and Mandy McIntyre','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/37/bef3afbdede19dbc2aaa3ad55005ff65','We recently remodeled our original 1980s-style basement with Basement Masters, and we are extremely happy with the end results. Our remodel was extensive; we added a full bathroom, converted a hallway and closet into a larger guest room,...','<p>We recently remodeled our original 1980s-style basement with Basement Masters, and we are extremely happy with the end results. Our remodel was extensive; we added a full bathroom, converted a hallway and closet into a larger guest room, consolidated our laundry room, and added a wet bar and entertainment area with soundproofing.</p>\n<p>When we were looking for the best contractor for this project, we spent a lot of time researching, and we had three different contractors provide estimates. Needless to say, we didn&rsquo;t need another estimate after talking with Basement Masters. Their pricing was easy to understand and very competitive.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Before the work began, the owner, Pavel, gave us checklists so we knew what items to pick out (and how much to spend to stay within our budget), which made the planning stage so much easier. The dimensions of our basement (bulkheads, ductwork, etc.), and the changes we wanted to make, required some creative thinking. Pavel really helped us think through the planning before starting. He had great ideas for ways we could use the different spaces, and his advice was very helpful towards finalizing our plans.</p>\n<p>Pavel was always easy to reach by phone, text or email, and he was very patient with our questions and ideas - and we had many throughout the remodel. We had a few specific custom requests that Basement Masters had not dealt with before; instead of telling us \"no,\" they figured out how to get it done. During the remodel process, Pavel and his team were consistently on time, respectful and clean. They were willing to work around our schedule, and even worked on weekends (as long as it didn&rsquo;t interfere with our plans) so they could expedite the project. Once the project was complete, Pavel came back and inspected everything with us.</p>\n<p>In the end, our basement went from being an outdated, unattractive and rarely used space to a modern, comfortable and inviting entertainment area where we spend most of our time happily hosting our visiting friends and family. I would definitely recommend Basement Masters to anyone interested in finishing or remodeling their basement.</p>','Silver Spring, MD',5,'148',16,'2020-07-24 08:39:00'),(38,'Review by Kate Hickman','BasementRemodeling.com is absolutely AWESOME!  We get so many compliments on our basement and we are truly enjoying it! \r\n','testimonials, reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish\r\n','Kate_Hickman_Review','Kate Hickman',NULL,'BasementRemodeling.com is absolutely AWESOME!  We get so many compliments on our basement and we are truly enjoying it! ','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">BasementRemodeling.com is absolutely AWESOME!&nbsp; We get so many compliments on our basement and we are truly enjoying it!&nbsp; I met with 3 or 4 companies before deciding on BasementRemodeling.com.&nbsp; They are not the least expensive company but they are definitely the best and worth every penny!&nbsp; My neighbors used them as well.&nbsp; Their basement style is very different than mine but just as fabulous!&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">From the very first consultation, Pavel, the owner of the company came out, gave me some ideas on designing my basement, provided a package of materials, an itemized price list of every conceivable option and a timeline.&nbsp; He wrote down my ideas and went into problem solver mode to find solutions.&nbsp; My basement is between 2000-2500 sf so it was a lot of work.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pavel is the consummate professional as is everyone on his team.&nbsp; I have worked with contractors before but never a company so organized.&nbsp; His operation runs like a well-oiled machine.&nbsp; He was available from start to finish to answer any questions and address any issues.&nbsp; He works 24 hours a day because I would send emails at 11pm and he would respond immediately.&nbsp; He had a full team of specialists, including an interior decorator and project manager, paint team, drywall team, electrician, plumber.&nbsp; This company has truly thought of everything to help you realize your dream basement and enjoy the entire process.&nbsp; I still use one of the companies that I learned about thru BasementRemodeling.com. &nbsp; If you are finishing your basement, you owe it to yourself to check out BasementRemodeling.com!</span></p>','Maryland',5,'',15,'2020-08-03 21:14:00'),(39,'Review by Alexandra Mottern','Pavel and his team were outstanding. We couldn\'t have asked for a better experience with our basement project.','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','Alexandra_Mottern_Review','Alexandra Mottern',NULL,'Pavel and his team were outstanding. We couldn\'t have asked for a better experience with our basement project.','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pavel and his team were outstanding. We couldn\'t have asked for a better experience with our basement project. Pavel\'s pricing was clear-cut and easy to understand and there were no surprises or adjustments to the scope of work on his end throughout the project- he included everything in his price up front.&nbsp; He made sure every time we made a change to the scope of work, the pricing adjustment was outlined clearly before the change was finalized.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">One of the greatest things: He is incredibly organized and runs his entire project based on a detailed project plan and Gantt Chart, with every little task outlined to the exact date the project is planned to be completed and he STICKS to that schedule.&nbsp; Each time we changed the scope of work, he updated and sent me a new Gantt chart that reflected the change in scope and the new completion date so I knew exactly when to expect each part of the work and what our responsibilities were in the project.&nbsp; The project only ever varied by 2 days at most. This was amazing!&nbsp; Pavel and his staff are incredibly detail-oriented.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Everyone on his team was incredibly friendly and professional, and went above and beyond to answer all of our questions and make sure we understood every step of the process.&nbsp; We weren\'t the easiest clients- we made a BIG change to the scope of the project in the middle of the construction, greatly altering the layout of the project and as a result, altering much of the framing, plumbing, electrical, cabling, etc that Pavel\'s team had already done.&nbsp; Pavel was great about it- he adjusted the price very fairly for the changes and didn\'t miss a beat on the project. In spite of all the changes and the fact that we threw off his carefully planned project schedule, he adjusted his contractors and they kept moving smoothly.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pavel was so responsive - anytime we had a question, he responded very quickly and was very transparent. He was incredibly helpful throughout every step of the process.&nbsp; And the quality of the work was outstanding - everyone who sees our basement raves about how great it looks!&nbsp; The outcome was phenomenal. We are so happy with the work. We would recommend Pavel and his team to anyone considering having their basement done/remodeled. We had a fabulous experience with them and are so happy with our new basement!</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>','Maryland',0,'',14,'2020-09-17 01:20:00'),(40,'Review by Lucas Swanepoel','BasementRemodeling.com finished our nearly 100 year old unfinished DC row-house basement.','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','Lucas_Swanepoel_Review','Lucas Swanepoel','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/40/f657c91553e105009ebe99b401361dd3','BasementRemodeling.com finished our nearly 100 year old unfinished DC row-house basement.','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">BasementRemodeling.com finished our nearly 100 year old unfinished DC row-house basement.&nbsp; The location was very tight and required some creativity but the final product looks great and very functional. Prices were reasonable and upfront pricing model allows you to have an idea of how much each extra bell and whistle will cost.</span></p>','District of Columbia',0,'171',2,'2020-10-10 02:34:00'),(41,'Review by Barry Baiorunos','Best choice of contractors!','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','Barry_Baiorunos_Review','Barry Baiorunos','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/41/307dd00f07edc76c62ed1a5c55d946fb','Best choice of contractors\r\n\r\nWe did a lot research to find the best contractor to convert our dark, dank 1000 sq foot basement into a modern living area.   ','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Best choice of contractors</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We did a lot research to find the best contractor to convert our dark, dank 1000 sq foot basement into a modern living area. &nbsp; Based on the advice of neighbors and online reviews we chose 8 contractors to give us estimates. &nbsp; We were most impressed with Basement Remodeling/ACH Group.&nbsp; Because of their standardized business model we were able to receive an estimate during the initial appointment.&nbsp; It was immediately transparent that this company was extremely well organized.&nbsp; The fact they specialize in basements is like having a heart condition and having a cardiologist rather than a general practitioner.&nbsp; The owner, Pavel, is a unique hands on mastermind of the operation.&nbsp; He possesses an energy and enthusiasm that worked in our favor many, many times.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">After deciding Basement Remodeling.com/ACH Group was at the top of our list, we vetted them to ensure they were everything we were looking for. &nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>','Maryland',0,'',13,'2020-11-16 22:43:00'),(42,'Review by Rick Denham','We are so excited to use our newly remodeled basement! This has changed our lives and made living in our home so much better! ','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish\r\n','Rick_Denham_Review','Rick Denham','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/42/9ccba4f3d7f5374f5549102b58ec5fd5','We are so excited to use our newly remodeled basement! This has changed our lives and made living in our home so much better! \r\n','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We are so excited to use our newly remodeled basement! This has changed our lives and made living in our home so much better!&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;Working with the basement remodeling tram has been nothing short of a wonderful experience!&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;They helped us make decisions along the way and supported the whole process.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;Their Architect Bindu was amazing and worked well with their project managers Eric and Gheorghe to make sure the execution was precise. Her plans were insightful and she helped with the selection of materials. I loved her idea of the waterfall stone quartz! It turned out amazing!&nbsp; I also loved how large the spaces are! Every inch was maximized in this project!&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Their building team was organized, worked well together and it were available to help us make good decisions.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;I also can&rsquo;t say enough about their finishing and punch list team. These brothers can do anything! The doors, cabinets, electrical, shelves installation was amazing! Igor and Jorge are the equivalent of remodeling ROCK ⭐️!!</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;My wife was so happy that she went out and bought them a box of pastries each! They were so kind and there was nothing they could not do!&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;In fact, we had also decided to order a new fridge for the upstairs kitchen, and Igor just so happened to be there that day. The delivery man could not get it in the door and wanted to cancel. Igor came up and did everything needed to get my wife&rsquo;s fridge in this row house l! We have IGOR to thank for that!!!&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;Their team was amazing!</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>','District of Columbia',0,'',4,'2020-12-05 22:45:00'),(43,'Review by Stephanie Cash','We had an unfinished basement that needed finishing! From the get go, we loved the program that Basementremodeling.com offered.\r\n','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','Stephanie_Cash_Review','Stephanie Cash','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/43/280b801b816d74726e275a8ed0bf4f8e','We had an unfinished basement that needed finishing! From the get go, we loved the program that Basementremodeling.com offered.\r\n','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We had an unfinished basement that needed finishing! From the get go, we loved the program that Basementremodeling.com offered. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The approach, starting with the estimate was clear, definitive, explained so we felt informed about the plan and approach. At the first visit, we were introduced to the Project Manager, the Operations/QA Lead and Designer. They walked us through the space, offered insights and ideas for changes, solicited our feedback and really worked WITH us. Once the work began, the crew was timely, efficient, neat, respectful. This was especially important and relevant given we were in the throes of COVID and extra care and caution needed to be undertaken. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As the work progressed, if there were questions or concerns, they were followed up and addressed 100% to our satisfaction. Note, this is construction work, there were some surprises and some changes needed, but we felt the team listened to us or explained things to us as those things arose. If my arm were twisted to provide for one area of improvement, there were two times where a decision was made (as needed due to the construction and timing) where it would have been good (and in the end cost less in time, energy, effort, materials) to advise us of what needed to be done and why. In the end though, those items did not have a negative impact on the whole; totally just a communication thing. All told, we could not be any happier with our basement! </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It looks FABULOUS and we HIGHLY recommend this team!</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>','Maryland',0,'',12,'2020-12-22 22:52:00'),(44,'Review by Joe Santanello','Want to know what our past clients have to say about their experiences with BasementRemodeling.com? You can find all the references here!','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','Joe_Santanello_Review','Joe Santanello','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/44/2f49a4179ff82ceb95c1f8abc38dcef1','Having had work done to our home in previous years we had never been confident to pass along any referrals, until now, with ACH Group/BasementRemodeling.com!! ','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Having had work done to our home in previous years we had never been confident to pass along any referrals, until now, with ACH group basement remodeling!! We had noticed their advertisement posted on someone\'s lawn from walking around the neighborhood.&nbsp; We decided to give them a call after we had other contractors either ghosted us (blow us off) or by giving us the runaround.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">ACH Group was different right from the start.&nbsp; We had a senior design consultant (Tom) come by to see the space and hear our vision.&nbsp; He was able to give us an estimate that same day.&nbsp; We never felt any pressure.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Start date we met with the Project Manager&nbsp; (Eric) and his team.&nbsp; Again we went over our vision and discussed our goals with the limited and complicated space we have.&nbsp; We live in an attached, 864 sq foot home built in 1939.&nbsp; The home definitely comes with its issues on space coupled with our goals, we knew we were in for a hell of a ride (many of them due to city permitting issues, not ACH).&nbsp; As with any project problems arise but the solutions to the problems actually made the space even MORE amazing than I could have envisioned! Who would have thought!&nbsp; We are so incredibly happy how the space turned out.&nbsp; Eric the lead project manager is absolutely someone with a gift.&nbsp; My husband and I joked how he can make anyone feel pretty zen after speaking to him.&nbsp; He would explain things to us in detail, he was understanding if we felt frustrated and only to reassure that all would be well and it was. Just shows us how confident he is in his team to deliver something really spectacular. We should also add that they are probably the only company, due to their vast experience and organization, who would have been able to navigate the city code, permitting, issues and be persistent and creative to work through it with us.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The contractors were all so great and worked extremely hard.&nbsp; Never did we ever feel anything but pure kindness and professionalism.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">My only problem with ACH Group is that I can\'t hire them for remodeling upstairs! Guess that is what makes them so wonderful with what they do. We strongly believe they were the only ones to navigate our project to the quality it had come out to and in perfect time.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">My advice to anyone is if you need your basement remodeled go with ACH and stand out of their way! Sit back and let them do their thing as they are top notch.&nbsp; 5 stars all the way!</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>','Virginia',0,'',5,'2021-01-12 22:57:00'),(45,'Review by Elizabeh Curran','We can say enough about the quality and professionalism of BasementRemodeling.com.','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','Elizabeh_Curran_Review','Elizabeh Curran','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/45/dd4e4f06a6566c805cd81e388aaf474c','We can say enough about the quality and professionalism of BasementRemodeling.com.','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We can say enough about the quality and professionalism of BasementRemodeling.com. In 2019, they did our basement and we couldn&rsquo;t be more pleased with the results! So much so that we asked them to do a renovation of our Master Bathroom this year. The results were spectacular. Tom is a pure professional, a great listener and his overall design helped us achieve our goal of modernizing our bathroom. During the pre-construction meeting with Eric, Bindu and Igor, we ironed out all the details which ensured a smooth construction process. Eric, the project manager, was courteous, professional and communicated with us throughout the whole project. Bindu was a joy to work with and offered several design options when we met at the tile shop, and she worked with us to achieve our vision&mdash;she was great! Igor was fantastic! With any custom project, there are bound to be multiple decisions that arise during construction. Igor gave us options that we were very happy to implement and they actually improved the end result. Igor really took ownership of the project and the pride in his work is evident with the finished result. The same is true for Josimer, who is a magician with tile! We had several different kinds of tile with a complicated design on the floor and shower, which he matched beautifully. The result is stunning. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The schedule slipped a little due to weather&mdash;several ice storms, and material delays, but these were unavoidable and well communicated. In the end, the project ended less than a week from originally scheduled. We are really pleased with all of the employees and recommend them highly. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Five out of five stars&mdash;wish we could give them six!!</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>','Maryland',0,'',11,'2021-02-21 23:02:00'),(46,'Review by Bernadine Bowyer','My husband and I reviewed about 5 companies before I chose this company. It was the best decision we ever made.\r\n','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','Bernadine_Bowyer_Review','Bernadine Bowyer','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/46/cb1d010658627bfefd919e2e1dc4431b','My husband and I reviewed about 5 companies before I chose this company. It was the best decision we ever made.','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Excellent. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">My husband and I reviewed about 5 companies before I chose this company. It was the best decision we ever made. They remodeled over 1500 sq. ft. of an unfinished basement (3/4 bathroom with niche and tiled shower and floor; L shaped kitchen bar, office) within 90 days through bad weather and a pandemic. The payment process was easy and the entire team was professional and responsive.</span></p>','Maryland',0,'',10,'2021-02-25 23:04:00'),(47,'Review by Thomas Bath','BasementRemodeling.com is a very professional group.  We were impressed with the company from the initial consultation to the finished job.','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish\r\n','Thomas_Bath_Review','Thomas Bath','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/47/c8d6ad8f6004ac5d5f8ac811729e032a','BasementRemodeling.com is a very professional group.  We were impressed with the company from the initial consultation to the finished job.','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">BasementRemodeling.com is a very professional group.&nbsp; We were impressed with the company from the initial consultation to the finished job.&nbsp; </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each contracting team that entered our home was respectful and they always left the work area clean.&nbsp; Weekly communication with the Senior Project Manager was excellent and I am sure help to make the project run smoothly and completion on time.&nbsp; When we had questions they were address immediately.&nbsp; My husband and I were extremely please with the company and how they handled the project especially with the Covid-19 protocols they had in place.&nbsp; We did not have a walk-out basement, so they entered through the living quarters.&nbsp; We seldom saw the workers, we just heard them working.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> It was a comforting&nbsp; and enlightening experience and we are very pleased with our finished basement and the team that put it all together for us.&nbsp; They are the best and I highly recommend them.</span></p>','Virginia ',0,'139',1,'2021-03-06 23:11:00'),(48,'Review by Mai Ling Malloy','We HIGHLY RECOMMEND. ACH Group/BasementRemodeling.com is a top-notch company. They are professional, organized and they work with integrity.','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','Mai_Ling_Malloy_Review','Mai Ling Malloy','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/48/e17a50b035f093c89fdd95e32b8cd0a6','We HIGHLY RECOMMEND. ACH Group/BasementRemodeling.com is a top-notch company. They are professional, organized and they work with integrity.\r\n','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We HIGHLY RECOMMEND. ACH Group/BasementRemodeling.com is a top-notch company. They are professional, organized and they work with integrity. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We are truly impressed not only with the results of our beautiful basement but also their customer service. They think about everything. Communication, quality, and safety (especially during this pandemic as they all have masks on, signage for temperature checks, bring their own porta potty and dumpster.) They cleaned up every time they were in our home and always locked the door when they left. They even installed their own lock box. They worked so quietly in our home we did not even know at times when they were working in our basement. This was helpful for our son&rsquo;s virtual learning and my remote work. Most of all, we really appreciate their honesty and there were no surprises or misleading tactics. They went above and beyond any basement company we interviewed (3 others) and the price was very reasonable. We had a couple of issues, but they always fixed the concern without hesitation. We wish more companies would work like ACH-BasementRemodeling.com. We are especially grateful for the amazing team, Eric (Project Manager is fantastic), Tom, Greg, Mike, Gheorge, Jorge, Paul (the electrician) and all the contractors. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">T</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">his company is the real deal and AMAZING. We love our basement and bathroom! Thank you, ACH-BasementRemodeling.com, for an outstanding job and service!! We have already recommended your company to our neighbor.</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>','Maryland',0,'141',9,'2021-04-11 02:14:00'),(49,'Review by John Chavez','Our basement was destroyed in the recent flooding experienced in Pavel. Pavel gave us a fair estimate for the work','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','John_Chavez_Review','John Chavez','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/49/ae3d6d8cf0f1eb3ad037077f83b0fbc6','Our basement was destroyed in the recent flooding experienced in Pavel. Pavel gave us a fair estimate for the work','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Our basement was destroyed in the recent flooding experienced in Pavel. Pavel gave us a fair estimate for the work, which included re-framing, drywall installation, painting, laying, flooring, framing and hanging new doors, bathroom tiling, installing plumbing fixtures, reinstalling electrical fixtures, and general touch-up. Pavel was consistent in his communications and accommodated our travel schedules to get the work done around our calendar. His crew did a great job in all aspects, and were professional and friendly. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We\'re very pleased with the outcome and We highly recommend them to everyone</span></p>','Virginia',0,'126',8,'2021-04-16 22:16:00'),(50,'Review by Charles Fercazzi','We are very satisfied with our new basement. Eric, Bindu, and the rest of the staff were professional and extremely hard working.','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','Charles_Fercazzi_Review','Charles Fercazzi','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/50/16184e8eeff66d460aedd9ef2025403d','We are very satisfied with our new basement. Eric, Bindu, and the rest of the staff were professional and extremely hard working.','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We are very satisfied with our new basement. Eric, Bindu, and the rest of the staff were professional and extremely hard working. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Any time workers finished up for the day, they always made sure to clean the site before leaving. We added some additional bedrooms, egress window, bathroom, laundry, and flooring. Our project was completed on time and within our modest budget. I had a lot of questions throughout the project and had direct access to Eric, our project manager who was very patient with me and responded very promptly to my many texts. We are very pleased with the final outcome. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Would very much recommend them!</span></p>','Maryland',0,'136',7,'2021-05-26 22:17:00'),(51,'Review by Chris Lange','After 10 years in our house my wife and I decided to finally move forward with finishing our basement.','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish\r\n','Chris_Lange_Review','Chris Lange','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/51/6a676cb4ce828953e959ab865241f66d','After 10 years in our house my wife and I decided to finally move forward with finishing our basement.','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">After 10 years in our house my wife and I decided to finally move forward with finishing our basement.&nbsp; It is a large space, ~1200 sq feet of finished area (included a full bath, amazing bar, main tv/living room, teens play area, and a home gym) so we knew it would be a large job.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We did our due diligence and got quotes from several companies.&nbsp; Now that the project is complete, we are very happy we decided on ACH Group as our contractor.&nbsp; The space looks amazing.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Our experience has been very good overall, from the initial consultation with Tom Hummer to begin discussing the project and get the initial quote&hellip; to then moving into the actual job and meeting Eric, Mike, and Bindu&hellip; and working with each of them throughout the process.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We wanted a company that did it by the books &ndash; ACH handled all that exceptionally &ndash; all permits were pulled timely; all inspections were completed by the county.&nbsp; In all honesty, I had a few of the county inspectors compliment ACH&rsquo;s work to me&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As with most projects of this size, we had our share of &ldquo;situations&rdquo; and &ldquo;surprises&rdquo; that came up.&nbsp; Each time, ACH explained the issue to us clearly&hellip; answered our questions&hellip; explained our options, and then worked with us to find and implement the best possible solution.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every crew/sub-contractor that was involved in the project were great.&nbsp; They were polite, professional, respectful of our home and family (and pets), and just downright friendly and helpful.&nbsp; The work area was kept very clean and orderly throughout the project.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Eric Campbell was excellent.&nbsp; Knowing how many hours he is likely working, he always made time to address my questions and concerns and did so in a timely manner.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As we neared the end of the project there were a few things that I was very particular about&hellip; some a/v wiring issues, etc.&hellip; and despite having to undo some completed work to solve the issue, Eric did exactly that and made sure that everything was done just as I requested.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In hindsight, if there was any negative or any thing we would change, I think it would be to possibly upgrade our paint selection from a flat paint to something a bit more stain resistant.&nbsp; Don&rsquo;t get me wrong, the actual painting itself was fantastic &ndash; no issues with the painters - the place looks amazing and the painters did very good work.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We&rsquo;ve just realized that either the color we selected (which we love by the way), or the fact that it is a &ldquo;flat&rdquo; paint&hellip; or the combination of the two &ndash; have resulted in marks/smudges very quickly and from very light contact.&nbsp; Lesson learned.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">All in all, we are extremely happy with ACH Group and the job they did for us.&nbsp; They actually finished a bit ahead of schedule on right on budget &ndash; actually, it was just slightly under budget.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">I highly recommend ACH Group for your basement finishing projects.&nbsp; They have been an absolute pleasure to work with, they were thorough, polite, professional, and very nice to work with.</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>','Maryland',0,'132',6,'2021-07-05 02:20:00'),(52,'Review by Laura Beers','We completely remodeled our partially finished basement with BasementRemodeling.com this fall. We tore out all of the existing walls, and redrew the floor plan to create a finished rec room, office/guest room and full bathroom and an unfinished laundry/fu','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','Laura_Beers_Review','Laura Beers','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/52/1369cf24e488693c73b7c789c0ec63b5','We completely remodeled our partially finished basement with BasementRemodeling.com this fall. We tore out all of the existing walls, and redrew the floor plan to create a finished rec room, office/guest room and full bathroom and an unfinished laundry/fu','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We completely remodeled our partially finished basement with BasementRemodeling.com this fall. We tore out all of the existing walls, and redrew the floor plan to create a finished rec room, office/guest room and full bathroom and an unfinished laundry/furnace room. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">BasementRemodeling.com also added an egress window (and I wish in retrospect that I\'d had them add two!) There were various hiccups along the way, not least because we were doing the project during Covid, but our project manager Eric Campbell was responsive and easy to work with. When we encountered an unexpected structural issue that required putting in a new column and footer, the firm took case of this with the least possible hassle and stress. In the end, while we didn\'t finish by Thanksgiving as initially hoped, we spent Christmas morning in our new basement. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Four months later, it is our favorite place in the house, and it is nearly impossible to get my sons to appear upstairs.</span></p>','Maryland',0,'131',3,'2021-07-22 22:23:00'),(53,'Review by Curtis Francisco','We could not be more satisfied as we are with Eric Campbell and his team at BasementRemodeling.com.','testimonials,reviews, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish\r\n','Curtis_Francisco_Review','Curtis Francisco','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/53/1cba5fcec1b119063f9c099dcabd0f7c','We could not be more satisfied as we are with Eric Campbell and his team at BasementRemodeling.com.','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We could not be more satisfied as we are with Eric Campbell and his team at BasementRemodeling.com.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Consummate professionals at every step of the process. Whenever we had questions or requests, Eric and his team were on it. And the final product is nothong short of spectacular. We vetted many vendors before deciding on Basement</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Remodeling.com, and it was the best decision we could have made. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Highly recommended!</span></p>','Maryland',0,'121',0,'2021-08-05 08:00:00'),(54,'I was extremely impressed with the methodical system that was utilized throughout the project','I am sincerely excited to be providing this review of Basement Remodeling\'s finishing of my basement in Odenton, Md. I was extremely impressed with the methodical system that was utilized throughout the project, from the first day when the project manager and his managerial crew visited our property to review and initiate the finish plans and change our basement lock for theirs (eliminating the need for us to have to share our house keys) to the final day - only 7 weeks later - when they returned to replace our basement lock and close out the job.','','craig_winn_review','Craig Winn','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/54/DSC_1743','I was extremely impressed with the methodical system that was utilized throughout the project, from the first day...','<p>I am sincerely excited to be providing this review of Basement Remodeling\'s finishing of my basement in Odenton, Md. I was extremely impressed with the methodical system that was utilized throughout the project, from the first day when the project manager and his managerial crew visited our property to review and initiate the finish plans and change our basement lock for theirs (eliminating the need for us to have to share our house keys) to the final day - only 7 weeks later - when they returned to replace our basement lock and close out the job. Our basement finishing involved transforming @ 800 sq. ft of unpartititioned unfinished space into a music studio, media room, small office and fully tiled bathroom, with linen closet. All of the trade professionals - plumbers, electricians, HVAC crew, carpenters, interior designer, cleaners, etc. - integrated seamlessly with the project manager. They were all professional, courteous, always on time to the job site and all did excellent work. The project manager sent weekly emails detailing the work schedule for each upcoming week; 95% of the time, his projections were totally on point! The finished product is beautiful and we are totally pleased. A special shoutout to Tom Hummer, who was our initial contact who visited our home to discuss our initial design concept and provide ides and the eventual price quote. Whereas other contractors took over a week to quote the project, Tom got it done in 24 hours, with detailed drawings, and a total cost breakdown - with stayed consistent throughout the project!</p>','Maryland',0,'',NULL,'2021-11-12 20:01:00'),(55,'5 star review by Alonni Sullivan | BasementRemodeling.com','From start to finish, designing our basement with BasementRemodeling.com has been first rate. ','','alonni_sullivan_review','Alan Sullivan','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/55/efa5fe76ac049bc61fe8e0b93655665d','From start to finish, designing our basement with BasementRemodeling.com has been first rate. ','<p>From start to finish, designing our basement with BasementRemodeling.com has been first rate. When it comes to project management, project execution, and allowing the customer to enjoy the process, BasementRemodleing.com has the right formula. When you have a company that takes professionalism and craftmanship seriously it is apparent in the final product. Our project consisted of a complete basement buildout. While we had established an idea of what we wanted, there were still a few details that needed to be fleshed out. To our delight the team jumped right in to bring our ideas closer to execution by providing suggestions that were aesthetically pleasing and logically sound. We specifically want to give acknowledge the team we worked with Tom Hummer, Eric Campbell, Bindu Maneyapanda, and Gheorghe Caminschi. As top-notch professionals they each played a part in ensuring transparency in the build process and ensuring we had an enjoyable experience. We never had to guess where money was being allocated because Tom walked us through every line item within our budget. We never had to guess what was next and received expert hand holding because Eric was always available. We never felt pressured into colors or selections we didn&rsquo;t want, and we were able to explore different ways to express our personalities in paint, countertops, flooring because Bindu listened to our ideas and offered great design suggestion. Lastly but not the least important, we never had to worry about anything not meeting a standard because Gheorghe made sure that any inspection we had went off without a hitch. Another point to note is that throughout the project, as the different trades (e.g., plumbers, electricians, etc.) completed their portion of the project, several consistent themes amongst the crew include: &nbsp;Cleanliness, Efficiency, and Consideration for our property. All that to say, we are extremely pleased with the final product and would recommend this team to anyone looking to complete a project.</p>','Maryland',5,'',NULL,'2022-01-23 20:04:00'),(56,'5 star review by John Rowland | BasementRemodeling.com','They finished our basement last winter and we couldn’t be happier with it. They were a great team. ','','john_rowland_review','John Rowland','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/56/8b5aee6b8f3d4c4e163b15fd41fa8858','They finished our basement last winter and we couldn’t be happier with it. They were a great team. ','<p>They finished our basement last winter and we couldn&rsquo;t be happier with it. They were a great team. Very responsive to questions, creative, organized, and professional. Highly recommended for basement projects!</p>','Maryland',5,'',NULL,'2022-02-12 20:07:00'),(57,'5 star review buy Evelyn Heil | BasementRemodeling.com','They did an outstanding job and finished within the estimated timeframe provided.','','evelyn_heil_review','Evelyn Heil','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/57/remodeled-basement-warrenton-va-modern-design931','They did an outstanding job and finished within the estimated timeframe provided.','<p>Basement Remodeling didn\'t just remodel our basement, they built it in from scratch. They did an outstanding job and finished within the estimated timeframe provided. We love the basement, including the spacious laundry room pictured below. We would recommend the company for any size project.</p>','Virginia',0,'',NULL,'2022-03-03 20:14:00'),(58,'5 star review by Bion Kim | BasementRemodeling.com','I would highly recommend BasementRemodeling.com for anyone looking to finish their basement. ','','bion_kim_review','Bion Kim','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/58/43992df8c9642c527f0657744c41ff25','I would highly recommend BasementRemodeling.com for anyone looking to finish their basement. ','<p>I would highly recommend BasementRemodeling.com for anyone looking to finish their basement. The experience from start to finish was great. We talked to a few other companies in the area and decided to go with BasementRemodeling.com based on our interactions with Tom. One of their selling points was that basements was what they do, so they know how to do it, which was evident. I felt they were very open with the pricing and were able to provide an actual start and estimated finish date, which they met! Eric was our project manager who was also a pleasure to work with. He was able to address any issues or concerns that came up. I would consider this our 3 time dealing with a contractor/company for a major home renovation project, and it has been our best experience.</p>','Virginia',5,'',NULL,'2022-04-27 19:15:00'),(59,'5 star review by Stephany Manuel','One of the smoothest remodeling experiences I have ever had!','','stephany_manuel_review','Stephany Manuel','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/59/fa118c92f49264c78914e71c576bb278','One of the smoothest remodeling experiences I have ever had!','<p>One of the smoothest remodeling experiences I have ever had! BasementRemodeling.com team was all very professional, quick turnaround time, and quick install. I now have a spacious basement which is not only perfect for me, but will add value to our house when we sell one day. What a night and day improvement from what was in it before. Bindu did an excellent job designing our rec room, full bathroom and adding the accent on wood paneling on staircase gives it such a nice touch. Installation was also flawless and all workers showed up on time and cleaned up daily after each day. They suggested better ways of improving certain things in our basement and were all friendly during the process. They all were invested in making sure we had a smooth process and made sure I was happy keeping me up to date with all the work. They were very attentive, kind, and friendly to our needs which shows a lot about their customer service and how they run their company. It is a very accommodating company and I love our new basement more than ever. I wish I would&rsquo;ve known them years ago. Highly recommending this company to anyone interested in basement remodeling.</p>','Maryland',5,'',NULL,'2022-05-18 19:38:00'),(60,'5 star review by Jen Kain','Absolutely recommend this company! They are organized, friendly, knowledgeable and get the job done right. We can’t thank them enough.','','jen_kain_review','Jen Kain','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/60/white-cabinets-basement-kitchen','Absolutely recommend this company! They are organized, friendly, knowledgeable and get the job done right. We can’t thank them enough.','<p>Absolutely recommend this company! They are organized, friendly, knowledgeable and get the job done right. We can&rsquo;t thank them enough.</p>','Maryland',0,'',NULL,'2022-06-05 19:39:00'),(61,'5 star review by Annie Snider','We were absolutely thrilled with the team at BasementRemodeling.com and the work they did finishing the basement in our 90 year-old house.','','annie_snider_review','Annie Snider','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/61/DSC_2516','We were absolutely thrilled with the team at BasementRemodeling.com and the work they did finishing the basement in our 90 year-old house.','<p>We were absolutely thrilled with the team at BasementRemodeling.com and the work they did finishing the basement in our 90 year-old house. The project was completed three months ago and we are happier than ever with the modern, functional space they built for us. We chose the company initially because their pricing and approach was transparent and straight forward, and that held up throughout the process. This was our first remodeling project and the team guided us through with great patience. We&rsquo;ve of course heard horror stories of contractors disappearing halfway through a job, but that couldn&rsquo;t have been further from our experience with BasementRemodeling.com: Eric was a magician, managing to keep everything on schedule, even when surprises cropped up (again, it&rsquo;s a 90-year-old house, so it&rsquo;s full of &lsquo;em!). Our neighbors began a similar basement finishing project 3 months before we did and, 8 months later are STILL trying to get it done. Every time we see them, they tell us how much they regret not going with Basementzemodeling.com!</p>','Washington DC',0,'',NULL,'2022-07-29 19:40:00'),(62,'5 star review by Alan Fader','After searching several contractors, I was impressed with the process with BasementRemodeling.com! ','','alan_fader_review','Alan Fader','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/62/DSC_2938','After searching several contractors, I was impressed with the process with BasementRemodeling.com! ','<p>After searching several contractors, I was impressed with the process with BasementRemodeling.com! The quote was very detailed and clear, unlike others I received. As the work began, the team communicated with me during several meetings including pre-demolition and pre-construction. The timelines were clear and remained according to schedule. Eric provided a weekly schedule, a weekly check in email, project cost breakdown and payment plan. I am very pleased with their service and work. The finished project looks amazing!</p>','Maryland',0,'',NULL,'2022-09-14 19:41:00'),(63,'5 star review by Valarie Sheppard','Expert, professional team.  Project was done timely and looks beautiful.','','valarie_sheppard_review','Valarie Sheppard','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/63/e770ffd7b59f33e6a508c998e986793d','Expert, professional team.  Project was done timely and looks beautiful.','<p>Expert, professional team. Project was done timely and looks beautiful.</p>','Maryland',0,'',NULL,'2022-10-06 19:42:00'),(64,'5 star review by Kym Gunthorpe','After reviewing several contractors, I selected Basement Remodeling because I loved the detailed original estimate with all the cost broken down.','','kym_gunthorpe_review','Kym Gunthorpe','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/64/DSC_2849','After reviewing several contractors, I selected Basement Remodeling because I loved the detailed original estimate with all the cost broken down.','<p>After reviewing several contractors, I selected Basement Remodeling because I loved the detailed original estimate with all the cost broken down. I must admit it was one of the best decisions I made. From the beginning to the end of the project I was updated on the schedule and cost. Of course I made changes and they were very accommodating. All of the teams were very professional, skilled, and always left my house clean. If I had issues or concerns they were addressed immediately. Even with the changing of project managers, my project kept moving without interruption to the schedule. It is obvious Basement Remodeling has worked hard to create an impeccable process. I am very happy with the way everything turned out.</p>','Maryland',0,'',NULL,'2022-11-20 20:43:00'),(65,'5 star review by Alvin Duque','We love our basement! We used Basement remodeling to finish our basement, and it looks great. ','','alvin_duque_review','Alvin Duque','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/65/basement-remodel-olney-md75','We love our basement! We used Basement remodeling to finish our basement, and it looks great. ','<p>We love our basement! We used Basement remodeling to finish our basement, and it looks great. The crews followed our layout exactly. Communication with the group was good. The overall construction time took a little longer than we had hoped, but they were pretty much on schedule. We are satisfied with their work.</p>','Maryland',5,'',NULL,'2022-12-15 01:44:00'),(66,'5 star review by Jameson Kisling','I had a great experience using Basement Remodeling. I liked that they sent a schedule each week outlining what to expect.','','jameson_kisling_review','Jameson Kisling','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/66/DSC_1709','I had a great experience using Basement Remodeling. I liked that they sent a schedule each week outlining what to expect.','<p>I had a great experience using Basement Remodeling. I liked that they sent a schedule each week outlining what to expect. The project manager was easy to get in touch with if we ever had any concerns. The basement looks great and I\'m excited to start spending time down there.</p>','Maryland',0,'',NULL,'2022-06-16 19:49:00'),(67,'5 star review by Claire Anderson','We had our basement renovated in January 2022, and every time we go downstairs, we comment, \"Wow, they did such a great job.\" ','','claire_anderson_review','Claire Anderson','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/67/DSC_1043','We had our basement renovated in January 2022, and every time we go downstairs, we comment, \"Wow, they did such a great job.\" ','<p>We had our basement renovated in January 2022, and every time we go downstairs, we comment, \"Wow, they did such a great job.\" The whole process was smooth, on-time, professional, responsive, and conducted with great communication. Highly recommend!</p>','Maryland',0,'',NULL,'2022-10-26 19:50:00'),(68,'5 star review by David Whitfield','We had a great experience with Basement Remodeling.','','david_whitfield_review','David Whitfield','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/68/DSC_2745','We had a great experience with Basement Remodeling.','<p>We had a great experience with Basement Remodeling. The work was completed about four months ago, but I waited to share a review until after we had lived in the space for a little while. Our remodeling project involved finishing half our basement to put in place a bedroom, full bathroom, and a rec room&ndash;and we are very pleased with the results. The folks at Basement Remodeling did a great job (no issues at all!), and they were very easy to work with. The scheduling was clear, and they were communicative throughout. Our main objective in moving forward with this project was to create a space that would allow us to better host guests, and we feel that we now have it. I would definitely recommend Basement Remodeling to others.</p>','Virginia',0,'',NULL,'2022-12-04 20:51:00'),(69,'5 star review by Tanya Lervik','They made the process nearly painless with detailed quote info and consistent communication. ','','tanya_lervik_review','Tanya Lervik','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/testimonials/69/DSC_2178','They made the process nearly painless with detailed quote info and consistent communication. ','<p>They made the process nearly painless with detailed quote info and consistent communication. They\'ve got systems in place with weekly updates to make everything go very smoothly. Any issues I had were addressed in a timely manner, and they were proactive. Also, they demonstrated pride in workmanship and attention to detail. I\'m very happy with the finished project.</p>','Maryland',5,'',NULL,'2023-01-13 20:52:00');
