INSERT INTO `tips` VALUES (16,'Carroll County MD Building Permits & Fees (Updated 2021)','Looking for a quick and easy-to-understand guide covering building permits (and their fees) in Carroll County Maryland? You\'ve come to the right place!','carroll county md permits, carroll county building permits, permit fees, fee schedule, 2021 permits carroll county, carroll county md, Maryland, basement blog, permits guide, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement renovations, basement remodeling, basement finishing','carroll-county-md-building-permits--fees-updated-2020','Carroll County MD Building Permits & Fees (Updated 2021)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/16/739ed44f75c937fdd925729420b94084','This weeks basement remodeling blog post is a 2021 updated guide to building permits and and their fees in Carroll County, Maryland.','<div class=\"html\">\r\n<p>No matter what state you live in, including <strong>Carroll County, Maryland</strong>, permits are almost always required if you\'re planning on making some changes to your home. This rings especially true if you\'re planning any sort of home renovation, addition, or remodel. Here\'s a simple guide on how to get started with the permit process and how much it will cost you!</p>\r\n<h2>Submitting a Building Permit Application</h2>\r\n<p>Due to the current pandemic, applying for a <a href=\"https://www.carrollcountymd.gov/media/1741/building-permit-application-2020.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Carroll County building permit</strong></a> is a tinge more complicated than usual, though you won\'t have to deal with anything too extravagant. Applications for building permits will currently only be accepted by appointment (Electrical, gas, plumbing, and fire permits can be submitted via their building\'s drop-box, appointment, or mail-in). To schedule an appointment, call the government permits office at 401-386-2674. Be sure to check the website\'s <a href=\"https://www.carrollcountymd.gov/government/directory/public-works/permits-inspections/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">current safety requirements</a> before going in!</p>\r\n<h2>Carroll County Building Permit Fees</h2>\r\n<p>Once you\'ve determined whether or not you\'ll actually <a href=\"https://www.carrollcountymd.gov/government/directory/public-works/permits-inspections/quick-links-for-permits-inspections/frequently-asked-questions/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">need a permit</a>, it\'s important to note what fees you\'ll have to pay, as they can easily stack up. Each building permit requires a filing fee, but the pricing can vary depending on the specifics of what you\'ll be doing.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Residential Fees</span></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">New Residential Construction:</span> $170 plus $0.12 per sq. ft. (this includes a $70 filing fee)<br /><br /></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Additions, Garages, Pole Building, Sheds (over 500 sq. ft.):</span> $60 plus $0.12 per sq. ft.<br /><br /></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Carports, sheds (500 sq ft or less), porches, decks, gazebos:</span> $60<br /><br /></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Interior/Exterior alterations, repairs, remodeling, finished basements:</span> $85 (includes $60 filing fee)<br /><br /></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Swimming Pools, above ground &amp; in-ground:</span> $60 for above ground, $120 for in-ground (includes $60 filing fee)<br /><br /></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Detailed building permit fees</span>: see the <a href=\"https://www.carrollcountymd.gov/media/12057/building-fee-schedule-coded-effective-january-8-2021.pdf\">government website</a>.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>If you\'d like to see a complete list of every possible fee (or if you\'re looking for commercial permits and fees), then be sure to check out the fee schedule on the Carroll County <a href=\"https://www.carrollcountymd.gov/media/12057/building-fee-schedule-coded-effective-july-1-2020.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">government website</a>.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2>Have Any Other Questions About Carroll County Building MD Permits?</h2>\r\n<p>If you\'re still unsure or curious about the county\'s permits and fees, feel free to ask a question in the comments below! BasementRemodeling.com has remodeled countless basements in Carroll County, MD and we know the permit process inside and out! Keep in mind that this article reflects current 2020 pricing schedules. We\'ll update this article or write a new one next year if the fees and/or requirements change!</p>\r\n<h2>Basement Finishing in Carroll County</h2>\r\n<p>If you reside in Carroll County, and you would rather have a licensed and experienced basement remodeling company handle permitting for you, click the link below for your location, and get in touch today!</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"../../../basement-finishing-area/md/carroll/sykesville\">Basement finishing in Sykesville</a></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"../../../basement-finishing-area/md/carroll/westminster\">Basement finishing in Westminster</a></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"../../../basement-finishing-area/md/carroll/\">Basement finishing in Carroll County</a></p>\r\n</div>',2,'',0,'2020-08-25 13:50:17'),(17,'More Ways to Maximize the Space in Your Small Basement','Have a small basement that you\'re tired of neglecting? Make it feel large and comfortable with these simple tricks.','small basement space, small basement storage, small basement ideas, small basement design ideas, maximize basement space, basement design, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, decorating a basement, decorate a basement 2020, basement ideas, basement design ideas','more-ways-to-maximize-the-space-in-your-small-basement','More Ways to Maximize the Space in Your Small Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/17/3dd30fca284c9015efbc1a05019da823','Searching for more ways to make your small finished basement feel larger? Try these simple tricks!','<div class=\"html\">\n<p>In a <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/maximizing-your-small-finished-basement-space\">previous article</a> on our basement remodeling blog, we touched on how you can make your small basement feel much larger and more comfortable simply by decorating it in different ways. Here are some more ways to truly maximize the space, comfort, and feel of your small finished basement!</p>\n<h2>Lighting</h2>\n<p>One of the most important, and arguably the most difficult to achieve, aspects of a basement is proper lighting. Many basements have only a few small windows, leaving only artificial light to pick up the slack. While powerful LED lights can completely light-up your entire basement with ease, and do so efficiently, natural lighting is the way to go</p>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Artificial light</span></h3>\n<p>These days, LEDS are exceptional at providing ample light while also being incredibly efficient. If there&rsquo;s no way to bring in any more natural light, or you can&rsquo;t afford a remodel window installation, LEDs are your best bet.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/8/53b0c847fa1df381b141add887efaee5_1000x670.jpg\" alt=\"Hidden LED lighting is a great way to improve the lighting in your basement, especially if you have no way of increasing natural light\" width=\"1000\" height=\"670\" /><br /><em>Hidden LED lighting is a great way to improve the lighting in your basement, especially if you have no way of increasing natural light.</em></p>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Natural light</span></h3>\n<p>Letting natural light pour into your basement is the single best way to make it feel larger and more comfortable. Combined with a well-placed mirror or two, your basement will look beautifully bright. As previously mentioned though, it&rsquo;s not always the most accessible option.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/9/97c6ce5493d16b1d1bd1372fbb29adf8_1000x670.jpg\" alt=\"A single egress window is enough to let a mountain of natural light through, though installing one is not always an option\" width=\"1000\" height=\"670\" /><br /><em>A single egress window is enough to let a mountain of natural light through, though installing one is not always an option.</em></p>\n<h2>Space Savers</h2>\n<p>When it comes to saving space in a small basement, there are quite a few different clever engineering hacks you can try out.</p>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Under the stairs</span></h3>\n<p>Under-the-stairs space has become increasingly more popular over the years, and for good reason. Depending on your staircase&rsquo;s structure, it&rsquo;s an almost entirely empty area&mdash;perfect for setting up shelving, drawers, or even a play room that doubles as a toy storage area.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/10/6de88a00ce0f575680f84741cd19f6a2_1000x745.jpg\" alt=\"Under-the-stairs storage area with multiple large shelves.\" width=\"1000\" height=\"745\" /><br /><em>Under-the-stairs storage area with multiple large shelves.</em></p>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Smaller Furniture</span></h3>\n<p>Though somewhat obvious, replacing some of your larger furniture can make a huge difference in how big your basement looks. A giant couch will certainly make the space look smaller compared to a set of reclining chairs. Cut down on the furniture sizes and the room will look larger, especially when combined with other decorations like mirrors or a giant rug.</p>\n<h2>Make the Space Your Own</h2>\n<p>While all of these options are great ways to maximize the space in your basement, a sense of personal flair is vital. Personal touch is the key to all great aesthetics, so be sure to keep that in mind when planning a basement change!</p>\n</div>',4,'',1,'2020-08-18 13:51:00'),(18,'Laminate Flooring Vs Vinyl Plank: Which is Better?','Laminate flooring and vinyl plank are both great options when it comes to flooring, but which one is a better choice?','basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','laminate-flooring-vs-vinyl-plank-which-is-better','Laminate Flooring Vs Vinyl Plank: Which is Better?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/18/c7e435e716b4787ffd89d6c180a9b0d6','Both Vinyl Plank and Laminate offer many different features, but either one better than the other?','<div class=\"html\">\n<p>Choosing what type of flooring to use is not always as easy as it sounds. There are a variety of different options, each with different price tags. Both <strong>Vinyl Plank and Laminate</strong> flooring share quite a few similarities. Both are relatively affordable, durable, and come in multiple different styles and colors, but which one is better? Is there an option that would work better for you?</p>\n<h2>Laminate Flooring</h2>\n<p>Laminate flooring is fairly similar to vinyl plank, but there are some distinct differences. Laminate is exceptionally durable, easy to install, its color remains vibrant for a long time, and it comes in wide selection of different colors and styles. However, it does have some flaws. It&rsquo;s not waterproof and you have to clean it with a laminate-specific cleaner. Despite being quite durable, it still tends to show wear and tear faster than vinyl plank.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/11/7bafb204231564e77d90a8c3ea13db26_1000x670.jpg\" alt=\"Shiny new laminate flooring for a basement remodeling project. Laminate floor retains its shine for many years without fading.\" width=\"1000\" height=\"670\" /><br /><em>Shiny new laminate flooring for a basement remodeling project. Laminate floor retains its shine for many years without fading.</em></p>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Pros of Laminate Flooring:</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Exceptionally durable</li>\n<li>Installation is a breeze</li>\n<li>Wide selection of colors</li>\n<li>Many different styles to choose from</li>\n<li>Color won&rsquo;t fade for a long time</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Cons of Laminate:</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Not waterproof</li>\n<li>Durable, yet easy to succumb to general wear and tear (especially if not properly maintained)</li>\n<li>Cleaning is a bit more complicated</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Vinyl Plank</h2>\n<p>In addition to laminate, vinyl plank is a great alternative to more expensive and maintenance-heavy hardwood flooring. Vinyl plank is extremely durable, waterproof, easy to clean, easy to install, and comes in many styles and colors. As for its flaws, it&rsquo;s far more prone to color fading than laminate and can&rsquo;t be waxed back to health. Objectively, vinyl plank has less flaws than laminate, but that doesn&rsquo;t necessarily make it better than laminate.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/12/e170656b61351d9c6d7b2dec82d79f10_1000x670.jpg\" alt=\"Vinyl plank is a great alternative to hardwood flooring. It remains durable through heavy use and pretty easy to clean.\" width=\"1000\" height=\"670\" /><br /><em>Vinyl plank is a great alternative to hardwood flooring. It remains durable through heavy use and pretty easy to clean.</em></p>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Pros of Vinyl Plank:</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Extremely durable, capable of withstanding heavy use</li>\n<li>Waterproof</li>\n<li>Installation is a breeze</li>\n<li>Wide selection of colors</li>\n<li>Variety of styles</li>\n<li>Easy to clean</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Cons of Vinyl Plank:</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Color fading is more likely to happen with vinyl plank</li>\n<li>No way to restore color if fading does occur</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>So, which is better?</h2>\n<p>Neither vinyl plank nor laminate flooring are necessarily better than each other. Each has its own good and bad traits, though it&rsquo;s worth mentioning that neither is a bad choice of flooring. You can way to pros and cons objectively, but the choice ultimately depends on your personal preferences and tastes!</p>\n<p>If this quick outline of differences between Vinyl Plank and Laminate helped you make a decision, let us know in the comments below!</p>\n</div>',1,'',2,'2020-08-11 15:03:10'),(19,'Maximizing Your Small Finished Basement Space','Have a small finished basement and aren\'t sure how to make it feel larger? Try these simple ideas!','small basement ideas, small basement space ideas, maximize basement space, basement storage, basement decorating ideas, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, decorating a basement, decorate a basement 2020, basement designs 2020, basement design ideas, basement space ideas','maximizing-your-small-finished-basement-space','Maximizing Your Small Finished Basement Space','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/19/e0f74e4407bce4e71bd64c79484f7803','Have a small basement and aren\'t sure what to do about it? Here are simple but effective ways to make it feel larger and cozier.','<div class=\"html\">\n<p>Basement spaces are already notoriously neglected, often being used simply for clutter storage and not much else. This is especially true for small basements, as there&rsquo;s not much space to work with. However, if you have a small basement, there are plenty of ways to make it feel larger and cozier&mdash;while remaining space-efficient.</p>\n<h2>Decorations</h2>\n<p>When working with a small basement space, a great place to get started is with decorations. Small and simple decorations can go a long way at creating the atmosphere you&rsquo;re looking for. In many cases, adding some simple but effective decorating is all you&rsquo;ll need to do!</p>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Wall Decorations</span></h3>\n<p>Your basement walls most likely consist of a single color, and are probably devoid of any patterns or designs as well&mdash;both of which can make your basement feel smaller than it actually is (even if it is small already). Wood wall paneling and wainscoting can truly change the depth of your basement, making rooms appear larger and more aesthetically pleasing.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/13/7b4521aa7a0ce8a709d0a71996f8d1f4_1000x670.jpg\" alt=\"Image Wainscoting Wood wall paneling and wainscoting can transform your small basement into an elegant space\" width=\"1000\" height=\"670\" /> <em>Wood wall paneling and wainscoting can transform your small basement into an elegant space.</em></p>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Rugs</span></h3>\n<p>Slapping a stylish rug into the center of your basement space can make a considerable difference to the space&rsquo;s feel. Not only is it a relatively cheap option, it also offers an extremely simple solution.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/14/d56d0769f14eb61418798b81edfcdf94_1000x670.jpg\" alt=\"While this isn&rsquo;t exactly a small basement, a rug in the center of the room helps tie things together and makes the room appear larger\" width=\"1000\" height=\"670\" /><br /><em>While this isn&rsquo;t exactly a small basement, a rug in the center of the room helps tie things together and makes the room appear larger.</em></p>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Mirrors</span></h3>\n<p>Installing a mirror (or mirrors) in your basement is a tried-and-true method of making the space seem bigger. Combined with natural light, which we&rsquo;ll go over below, this is a great and cheap option.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/15/cd6bc22610a5718eeb4902b03f00126d_1000x460.jpg\" alt=\"A well-placed mirror&rsquo;s optical illusion effect provides an easy way to bulk-up the feel of your basement.\" width=\"1000\" height=\"460\" /><em>A well-placed mirror&rsquo;s optical illusion effect provides an easy way to bulk-up the feel of your basement.</em></p>\n<h2>Get Creative</h2>\n<p>There are dozens of ways to transform a small dark and depressing basement into something amazingly comfortable and nice to look at. If you believe your basement looks too small, optical illusions are an excellent and affordable option (like the mirror trick we covered earlier). Don&rsquo;t overthink your plans, though. Find something you think would work and try it out!</p>\n</div>',4,'',3,'2020-08-04 15:03:35'),(20,'Frederick County MD Building Permits & Fees','Planning a new project for your home in Frederick County MD? Check here for what permits you\'ll need and how much they\'ll cost.','building permits frederick county md, electrical permits, mechanical permits, Frederick County MD, Maryland, building codes, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, building permits guide, frederick county county permits guide, permit fees, fee schedule','frederick-county-md-building-permits--fees','Frederick County MD Building Permits & Fees','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/20/ae5aa4d7f5965f5468dd226af5cf97ea','A basic guide covering relevant building, plumbing and electrical, permits and their fees for Frederick County, Maryland.','<div class=\"html\">\r\n<p>This is a simple guide outlining every <strong>Frederick County MD permit</strong> you could need if you\'re planning to start a building, remodeling, or refinishing project this 2022. We\'ve included all of the relevant fees and links to the forms for each permit.</p>\r\n<h2>Frederick County, Maryland Building, Plumbing, Electrical, Mechanical, &amp; Permits &amp; Fees</h2>\r\n<p>Frederick County requires submitting a permit application at <a href=\"https://planningandpermitting.frederickcountymd.gov/\">https://planningandpermitting.frederickcountymd.gov/</a>. Permit status may be found online at https://planningandpermitting.frederickcountymd.gov/ <a href=\"https://planningandpermitting.frederickcountymd.gov/\">Online Permit Inquiry</a></p>\r\n<dl>\r\n<dd id=\"dd_444\" class=\"fr-view\">\r\n<h2 class=\"subhead1 \">Approval Requirements</h2>\r\n<p>Approval is required for all new construction in the county or in the municipalities, with the exception of the City of Frederick and Mt. Airy. The City of Frederick and Mt. Airy are responsible for their own building permits. Zoning certificates for properties within municipalities must be applied for prior to Building Permit application at the Department of Permits and Inspections. Approval is required for modifications, alterations or changing the usage of any building or structure. Approval is required for accessory structures, such as a shed, pool, deck, garage, sign, etc.</p>\r\n<h2 class=\"subhead1 \">Online Payments</h2>\r\n<p>Permits and Inspections will now accept credit cards, debit cards and online payments. Pay online on the <a href=\"https://planningandpermitting.frederickcountymd.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"through the citizen portal here Opens in new window\">through the portal here</a>. Please note there is a service charge on all credit card, debit card and online check transactions. The <strong>service fee for an online check</strong> payment is $1.49 per transaction. The <strong>service fee for using a credit card or debit card</strong> is 2.5% per transaction total.</p>\r\n</dd>\r\n</dl>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Residential Building Permit Fees:</span></h4>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 2\">\r\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n<div class=\"column\">\r\n<p><strong>Basement Finish</strong><br />$ 10.00 Automation Enhancement Fee<br />$ 27.00 Filing Fee<br />$ 112.00 &ndash; 500sf or less Building Fee<br />$ 222.00 &ndash; 501sf to 1500sf Building Fee<br />$ 333.00 &ndash; More than 1500sf Building Fee $ 46.00 Zoning Review Fee</p>\r\n<p><strong>Covered or Screened Porch or Deck 499sf or less $ 10.00 Automation Enhancement Fee</strong><br />$ 27.00 Filing Fee<br />$ 91.00 Building Fee</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"column\">\r\n<p><strong>Garage or Pole Building</strong><br />$ 10.00 Automation Enhancement Fee $ 27.00 Filing Fee<br />$ 182.00 Building Fee</p>\r\n<p><strong>Covered or Screened Porch or Deck 500sf or more $ 10.00 Automation Enhancement Fee</strong></p>\r\n<p>$ 27.00 Filing Fee<br />$ 116.00 Building Fee<br />$ 46.00 Zoning Review Fee</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Residential Plumbing Permit Fees:</span></h4>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Any new plumbing requires a plumbing permit. Any replacement appliance or fixtures that are not \"like-kind\" (same mechanical and electrical rating as the appliance being replaced) or if the replacement causes piping to be added or moved..</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>New construction, One- and Two- Family detached dwelling unit, per dwelling unit\r\n<ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>4,000 SF or less\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Including gas: $396.00</li>\r\n<li>Excluding gas: $336.00</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>More than 4,000 SF and less than 6,500 SF<br />\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Including gas: $455.00</li>\r\n<li>Excluding gas: $396.00</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Additions, Alterations, &amp; Accessory\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>1 - 4 plumbing fixtures: $91.00</li>\r\n<li>5 - 9 plumbing fixtures: $152.00</li>\r\n<li>10 or more plumbing fixtures: $214.00<br /><br /></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Swimming pools &amp; Hot tubs: $51</li>\r\n<li>Boilers, steam and hot water equipment installation: $51/per uni<br /><br /></li>\r\n<li>Water-cooled air conditioning, refrigeration, Machinery, and compressor installation: $51/per unit</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Check the <a href=\"https://frederickcountymd.gov/DocumentView.aspx?DID=20431\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">fee schedule</a> for a complete list of fees, and for fees regarding commercial applications.</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Residential Electrical Permit Fees:</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>New construction, One- and Two- Family dwelling unit, includes low voltage work by same contractor on same application: <br />\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Up to 200 amp service: $272.00</li>\r\n<li>201 to 400 amp service: $365.00</li>\r\n<li>More than 400 amp service: $505.00<br /><br /></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Alterations, Additions, &amp; accessory Structures (includes low voltage work by same contractor on same application): $120.00<br /><br /></li>\r\n<li>Low Voltage Permit only: $121.00<br /><br /></li>\r\n<li>Swimming Pools and Hot Tubs (including motors, lights, receptacles &amp; bonding)\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Above ground: $51.00</li>\r\n<li>In ground: $182.00</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>There\'s quite a bit more that covers a variety of different projects, so check the <a href=\"https://www.frederickcountymd.gov/DocumentCenter/View/326556/FY21-Proposed-Fee-Schedule-\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">official form covering each fee</a> if you\'re uncertain about something.</p>\r\n<h2>Future Blog Updates</h2>\r\n<p>This list is current based on 2021 figures provided by the Frederick County government website. The fees will undoubtedly increase in 2022, at which point we\'ll update this blog post (or make a new one) with the new information.</p>\r\n<p>Let us know in the comments below if we missed anything or if there\'s any other information you\'d like to see here!</p>\r\n<h2>Basement Finishing in Frederick County</h2>\r\n<p>If you are in Frederick County, you can have a licensed and experienced basement contractor handle your basement project for you! Explore our locations below, and get in touch with us today!</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"../../basement-finishing-area/md/frederick/adamstown\">Basement Finishing in Adamstown, Maryland</a></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"../../basement-finishing-area/md/frederick/\">Basement Finishing in Frederick County</a></p>',2,'',4,'2020-07-28 15:04:05'),(21,'Comfortable Vs Stylish: Which is Better for Your Basement?','Think it\'s time to change up your basement\'s style? Should you go with something comfortable or stylish? Find out here.','basement comfort vs style, comfortable basement, stylish basement, comfortable or stylish, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement style, basement design ideas, basement style ideas, comfortable basement ideas','comfortable-vs-stylish-which-is-better-for-your-basement','Comfortable Vs Stylish: Which is Better for Your Basement?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/21/07d4198b924be3c4e68b5a2ab39f167d','Recently discovered your basement isn\'t as comfortable or stylish as it could be? If so, should you focus on comfort or style? Find out in this week\'s basement remodeling blog post!','<div class=\"html\">\n<p>Most working people here in the US don&rsquo;t spend a lot of time in their home. From full-time jobs to handling kids to running errands&mdash;the most consecutive time they spend at home is when they&rsquo;re sleeping. However, with the recent pandemic raging across the world, millions have spent weeks, or even months, quarantined in the very place they spend the least amount of time.</p>\n<p>While we won&rsquo;t dive into anything about the virus itself, quarantining indefinitely may have opened your eyes to how you<em> truly</em> feel about how your home&rsquo;s basement interior. We mention basements because that&rsquo;s where most keep recreational areas, like a game room, playroom, home theater, or even a second living room. Spending so much time in your basement can change your perspective. Do you love it more now? Is it too dark? Do you think it needs some tweaks to make it more comfortable and/or aesthetically pleasing?</p>\n<h2>When to Keep Your Basement Comfortable</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"margin-bottom: 5px; margin-top: 5px;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/16/6ee68b37eb714aa22c97172910cfe239_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Basic family room layout with comfortable couch and natural light pouring in from double-door entrance. A comfortable approach is both affordable and still aesthetically pleasing.\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Basic family room layout with comfortable couch and natural light pouring in from double-door entrance. A comfortable approach is both affordable and still aesthetically pleasing.</em></p>\n<p>While it may seem obvious to some, your number one priority when redesigning your basement&rsquo;s style should be personal comfort. Though many use it for storage and extra space, a basement is essentially an extension of your home. Basements no longer have to be dark and depressing, they can be vibrant and full of life. A bright and <strong>comfortable basement design</strong> can even surpass the aesthetic appeal and allure of your main floor.</p>\n<p>In short, if you plan on spending the rest of your life in that house, always keep this in mind: <em>you&rsquo;re going to be there for a while</em>. Comfort is generally cheaper, faster, and much easier to pull-off.&nbsp;</p>\n<h2>When to Go All-Out</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img class=\"auto-center\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px; margin-top: 10px;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/17/db68ad53beb97e39e76f0061baf1d27c_2400x1489.jpg\" alt=\"Stylish basement wine cellar with private staircase access, wine racks, seating area, and mini-fridge\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1489\" /><em>Stylish basement wine cellar with private staircase access, wine racks, seating area, and mini-fridge.</em></p>\n<p>When to keep things comfortable and when to maximize your finished basement&rsquo;s style all depends on your priorities. Should you go all-out on your <strong>stylish basement design</strong>? Only if you have a lot of disposable income and lavish tastes, or you simply want to spruce up your basement so you can sell your home at a higher price. Either way, the changes you make are only limited by your imagination. Buy fancy wallpaper, put in a brand new tiled bathroom, buy larger furniture&mdash;whatever you choose will considerably increase the value of your home.</p>\n<h2>Why not both?</h2>\n<p>You may be thinking: &ldquo;Can&rsquo;t you just do both?&rdquo; Well, yes, you could find a nice balance between comfortable and stylish but committing to one or the other makes things less complicated. It also makes the decision more final, keeping you from changing your mind about the style every few months.</p>\n<p>It is important to note that there are obvious crossovers. Would your finished basement be more comfortable with a large, perfectly-soundproofed home theater with cozy reclining chairs and snack holders? Almost certainly. Installing a fancy home theater could definitely be considered &ldquo;going all-out&rdquo; but it also sounds awesome. There are exceptions to every rule, but choosing one and sticking with it will be your best option.</p>\n</div>',1,'',5,'2020-07-21 15:04:35'),(22,'How Much Does It Cost to Remodel a Basement?','Thinking about remodeling your basement and aren\'t sure how much it will cost? Find our here.','cost of remodeling a basement, basement remodel cost, basement remodel prices, remodeling prices, basement finishing cost, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, remodeling basement, VA, MD, DC','how-much-does-it-cost-to-remodel-a-basement','How Much Does It Cost to Remodel a Basement?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/22/47f625a537a14de5073d6d98963c8a3d','Remodeling a basement is a great way to breathe new life into your home and increase its overall value—but how much does it cost?','<div class=\"html\">\n<p>Remodeling or refinishing is a great way to make your basement feel like a part of your home again, and not just a dark (often unfinished) space used for storage. A proper basement remodel offers a variety of advantages, from improving the aesthetic of your home to increasing your property&rsquo;s value. But, remodeling a basement can be a pretty costly endeavor&mdash;depending on what exactly you&rsquo;re trying to accomplish. So, <strong>how much does it cost to remodel a basement?</strong></p>\n<h2>The Average Cost</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img class=\"auto-center\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/18/f45cbcadc118f2c6dff49a6ee0ffd29e_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"A complete basement remodeling job for a home in Springfield VA. On average, the typical basement remodel costs around $20,000.\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /><em>A complete basement remodeling job for a home in Springfield VA. On average, the typical basement remodel costs around $20,000.</em></p>\n<p>The actual cost of a basement remodel depends on the project&rsquo;s complexity and where you live, but, on average, <strong>the</strong> <strong>typical basement remodel costs around <a href=\"https://www.homeadvisor.com/cost/basements/remodel-a-basement/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">$20,000</a></strong>, but the overall prices range wildly. If you want a simple remodel with nothing fancy, you can pull it off with less than $5,000. If you want to transform your basement into a luxurious entertainment and relaxation haven, it can cost up to $45,000. Home Advisor has a handy <a href=\"https://www.homeadvisor.com/cost/basements/remodel-a-basement/#calculator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">cost calculator</a> that will show you the estimated cost of your basement remodeling project based on submissions from others in your zip code.</p>\n<h2>Adding a Bathroom</h2>\n<p>Though it&rsquo;s almost always entirely worth it, adding a bathroom to your basement isn&rsquo;t exactly an easy undertaking, nor is it cheap. Aside from the obvious increase in pricing due to installing new plumbing, you&rsquo;ll also undoubtedly require a permit from the County. Permit fees can range from $50 up to $3,000, though they aren&rsquo;t likely to go beyond a few hundred dollars.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img class=\"auto-center\" title=\"A newly remodeled bathroom in Pasadena, Maryland. Installing a new bathroom often requires getting a permit and having your home inspected.\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/19/91ec06dc589d6cb580623a26e2757d27_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><em>A newly remodeled bathroom in Pasadena, Maryland. Installing a new bathroom often requires getting a permit and having your home inspected.</em></p>\n<p>After taking care of extra costs from plumbing and permits, you may want to (or have to) have your new bathroom inspected. Inspection fees and requirements vary wildly between states and counties, so check with your local county website for more info. You can also check out our <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/\">Documentation</a> section here on BasementRemodeling.com; we cover relevant building/remodeling/finishing permits and fees for every county in VA, MD, and DC.</p>\n<h2>Basement Remodeling Blog</h2>\n<p>If you&rsquo;re interested in hearing more possible scenarios and what they cost, we&rsquo;ll be posting more about this in the future. We&rsquo;ll be covering everything from the cost of installing a wet bar to building a whole new theater room!</p>\n</div>',1,'',6,'2020-07-14 15:04:51'),(23,'2022 Prince William County VA Building Permits & Fees','A complete list of every relevant permit (and their fees) for Prince William County VA!','prince william county permits, prince william county va permits, building permits, electrical permits, mechanical permits, plumbing permits, va building permits, 2020 building permit fees va, prince william county permit fees, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','2020-prince-william-county-va-building-permits--fees','2022 Prince William County VA Building Permits & Fees','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/23/7f5e0bdf3af3f6042c3416c9e315920f','A simple guide covering relevant building, electrical, and mechanical permits and fees for Prince William County, Virginia.','<div class=\"html\">\r\n<p>The following simple guide outlines every <strong>Prince William County VA permit</strong> you could possibly need if you\'re planning to start a building, remodeling, or refinishing project this 2022. We\'ve included all of the relevant fees and links to the forms for each permit.</p>\r\n<h2>Will you need a permit in Prince William County?</h2>\r\n<p>The Prince William County government website provides a full list of situations and circumstances outlining when and if you\'ll need a permit before starting a new project. We\'ve broken down some of the most common.</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">You\'ll need a permit if you\'re:</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Building a porch or deck where the floor is 16.5 inches or more above the finished grade</li>\r\n<li>Making an addition to your home</li>\r\n<li>Accessibility Upgrades (i.e., temporary ramps, permanent ramps, grab bars, widening doors and existing interior openings, wheelchair lifts)</li>\r\n<li>Additions</li>\r\n<li>Garages or carports</li>\r\n<li>Finishing your basement</li>\r\n<li>All retaining walls supporting more than three feet of unbalanced fill</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Installing a prefabricated fireplace, insert, or wood stove</li>\r\n<li>Installing/replacing doors and/or windows when structural alterations are made</li>\r\n<li>Installing a new electrical circuit, fixture, or receptacle (unless the total voltage required is under 50 volts)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">You won\'t need a permit if you\'re:</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Building a storage shed (accessory building) one story and 256 square feet or less in the area</li>\r\n<li>Building a fence (you\'ll need a permit for fences used as a swimming pool barrier)</li>\r\n<li>Re-roofing or fixing your current siding</li>\r\n<li>Pouring a new concrete patio slab, provided it\'s not meant to support a future building addition</li>\r\n<li>Replacing windows and doors with windows and doors of similar operating and opening dimensions that do not require changes to the existing framed opening</li>\r\n<li>Re-glazing windows (glass replacement)</li>\r\n<li>Installing/replacing cabinetry, trim, or floor finishes</li>\r\n<li>Painting the interior or exterior of your home or wallpapering</li>\r\n<li>Replacing gutters or downspouts</li>\r\n<li>Replacing plumbing fixtures (water closets, tubs, sinks, garbage disposals) where no alteration to the supply or drain/waste/vent systems are involved</li>\r\n<li>Installing low-voltage wiring (as mentioned earlier, it has to be under 50 volts)</li>\r\n<li>Replacing light-fixtures, electrical appliances, electrical water heater, electric furnace, heat pump, or air conditioning condensing unit, air-conditioners or furnaces</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>You can see the full list <a href=\"https://www.pwcgov.org/government/dept/development/bd/Pages/permit-work.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</p>\r\n<p>If you\'ve checked over the list and identified you\'ll need a permit, your next step involves submitting a <a href=\"http://eservice.pwcgov.org/eBuildingDevelopmentForms/forms/BuildingPermitApplication.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit application</a>.</p>\r\n<h2>Prince William County VA Building, Electrical, Mechanical, &amp; Plumbing Permits &amp; Fees</h2>\r\n<p>All finished basement permit applications and floor plans are required to be submitted via Prince William County&rsquo;s <a href=\"https://egcss.pwcgov.org/SelfService#/home\">ePortal </a>system. Consult the <a href=\"https://www.pwcva.gov/assets/documents/development/Customer%20ePlans%20Guide.pdf\">Customer Electronic Plan Review (ePlans) Guide</a> for information on how to prepare and submit documents for electronic plan review and the <a href=\"https://www.pwcva.gov/assets/documents/development/ePortal%20-%20Submitting%20a%20Building%20ePlan%20-%20CSS%202019.pdf\">electronic plan review guide</a> for building ePlan submission guidelines..</p>\r\n<p>The Building Plan&nbsp;Intake Counter is open 8 a.m. to 4 p.m., Monday through Friday.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Floor plan showing room dimensions, square footage, their intended uses, and whether the room is already finished, will remain unfinished, or to be finished.</li>\r\n<li>Complete the appropriate permit applications for&nbsp;<a href=\"http://eservice.pwcgov.org/eBuildingDevelopmentForms/forms/BuildingPermitApplication.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"http://eservice.pwcgov.org/eBuildingDevelopmentForms/forms/MechanicalPermitApplication.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mechanical permit</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"http://eservice.pwcgov.org/eBuildingDevelopmentForms/forms/PlumbingPermitApplication.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">plumbing permit</a>,&nbsp;and/or&nbsp;<a href=\"http://eservice.pwcgov.org/eBuildingDevelopmentForms/forms/ElectricalPermitApplication.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">electrical permit</a>.</li>\r\n<li>Obtain fee pricing.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Note: you\'ll have to submit a separate application if you need a permit for anything electrical, mechanical, or plumbing related.</span></p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Building Permit Fees:</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Residential New Construction/Additions\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Fee per square foot of the gross floor area, to include basements and garages: $0.2232</li>\r\n<li>Minimum fee for new dwelling units, garages, carports, additions, breezeways, gazebos, open porches with roofs, decks greater than 250 square feet, and detached sheds greater than 256 sf: $233.04</li>\r\n<li>Minimum fee (decks and detached sheds 250 sq. ft or less): $93.85<br /><br /></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Non- Residential Structures:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>fee per square foot of gross floor area: $0.2559</li>\r\n<li>Minimum fee per structure or tenant space: $312.44</li>\r\n<li>Framing and Rough-in Permit: $312.44<br /><br /></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Repairs and Alterations\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Residential: $97.43</li>\r\n<li>Non-residential Structures: $0.0119<br /><br /></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Finished Residential Basements\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Fee per square foot of gross floor area: $0.2788<br /><br /></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Other Misc Fees:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Private residential swimming pool: $155.35</li>\r\n<li>Building demolition: $155.35</li>\r\n<li>Retaining walls: $155.35\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Retaining walls with less than 8 ft of backfill: $0.5205</li>\r\n<li>Retaining walls with 8 ft or more of backfill: $0.6244</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Outdoor sign (per sign): $155.35</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Electrical Permit Fees:</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Residential<br />\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>New residential\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>New construction of dwelling units, fee per square foot (includes basement/floor area): $0.1064</li>\r\n<li>Minimum fee: $93.85</li>\r\n<li>Temporary service: $139.20<br /><br /></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Existing dwellings (additions, remodeling, and repairs)\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Base fee, plus additional items (<a href=\"https://www.pwcgov.org/government/dept/development/bd/Documents/12288.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">listed here</a>, under the \"Electrical Fees\" section): $46.92</li>\r\n<li>Service connection: $93.85</li>\r\n<li>Swimming pools: $93.85<br /><br /></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Non-residential\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Base fee: $155.35</li>\r\n<li>Appliances and stationary equipment (includes, but not limited to, bathroom exhaust fans, dishwasher, disposal, dryer, water heater, kitchen range, car charging station and solar panel)\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>For the first 25 pieces of equipment, each: $13.96</li>\r\n<li>For each additional piece of equipment: $1.38</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Circuits (new, extensions, and feeders): $3.51</li>\r\n<li>Duct Heaters\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>For first unit: $50.62</li>\r\n<li>For additional units, each: $27.93</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>There\'s quite a bit more on this list, so check the <a href=\"https://www.pwcgov.org/government/dept/development/bd/Documents/12288.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">official form covering each fee</a> if you\'re uncertain about something.</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Mechanical Permit Fees:</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Residential:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Duct work only\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>One zone fee plus: $192.41</li>\r\n<li>Each additional zone: $121.97<br /><br /></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>A/C equipment replacement\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Indoor or outdoor: $93.85</li>\r\n<li>Both: $139.20<br /><br /></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Furnace replacement, each: $93.85<br /><br /></li>\r\n<li>Wood stoves, gas logs, each: $93.85</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Plumbing Permit Fees:</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Residential\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>New residential<br />\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Base fee: $93.85</li>\r\n<li>Each fixture and appliance, which includes floor drains, ice makers, hose bibbs, potable water connections to boilers or other nonpotable tanks or equipments, and roughed-in fixtures: $7.82</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Additions/remodeling\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Base fee: $93.85</li>\r\n<li>Each fixture and appliance (same as above): $7.82</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Water service (per service when new, repaired, or replaced): $93.85</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>If you\'re planning any sort of non-residential or commercial project, your fees will be substantially different (and much larger). The government <a href=\"https://www.pwcgov.org/government/dept/development/bd/Documents/12288.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">fee schedule form</a> covers everything you\'ll need to know if so.</p>\r\n<h2>Future Blog Updates</h2>\r\n<p>This list is current based on 2021 figures. The government will undoubtedly increase the fees in 2021 (the Prince William County fee schedule document already lists potential changes for 2022), at which point we\'ll update this blog post (or make a new one). Let us know in the comments below if we missed anything or if there\'s any other information you\'d like to see here!</p>\r\n</div>',2,'',7,'2020-07-07 15:05:17'),(24,'Fairfax County VA Building Permits & Fees','Starting a remodeling or finishing project in Fairfax County VA? Find out what permits you\'ll need and how much they\'ll cost you.','Fairfax County VA permits, building permits fairfax county, permits fairfax county va, building permits, electrical permits, plumbing permits, mechanical permits, permit fees, fairfax county permit fees, fairfax county building fees, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','fairfax-county-va-building-permits--fees','Fairfax County VA Building Permits & Fees','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/24/060a56ecad0b44b3981678f4a734cded','A complete list of all the permits you may (or may not) need when starting a project in Fairfax, County Virginia!','<div class=\"html\">\r\n<p>The following simple guide outlines every <strong>Fairfax County VA permit</strong> you could possibly need if you\'re planning to start a building, remodeling, or refinishing project this 2022. We\'ve included all of the relevant fees and links to the forms for each permit.</p>\r\n<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n<h2>When You\'ll Need a Permit in Fairfax County</h2>\r\n<p>Permits are&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/fido\">applied for online</a>.&nbsp; Building plans and other reviews may be&nbsp;required.&nbsp; For more information on plans, reviews, fees, land disturbance&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/landdevelopment/codes-and-standards\">current building code</a>, visit <a href=\"https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/plan2build/development-process-overview/4-review-process-and-permitting\">Development Process Overview</a>.</p>\r\n<p>For the most part, you\'ll need to have some sort of permit for a remodeling or refinishing project, but there are some exceptions. Here are some of the most common projects where<strong> you <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">will</span> need to have a permit</strong>, pulled from the <a href=\"https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/landdevelopment/when-permit-required\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fairfax County website</a>:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>New buildings, additions, and structures</li>\r\n<li>Interior alterations (including finished basements) except new floors, carpet, paint, trim work</li>\r\n<li>New plumbing fixtures</li>\r\n<li>New exterior stairs or stoop</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n<h2>When You Won\'t Need a Permit</h2>\r\n<p>Though most projects require a permit, there are minor and uncommon circumstances where you <strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">won\'t</span> need a permit</strong>:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Residential window or door replacements</li>\r\n<li>Residential reroofs</li>\r\n<li>Kitchen cabinets</li>\r\n<li>Gutters</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The Fairfax County government website has a complete list of situations and projects&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/landdevelopment/when-permit-required\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</p>\r\n<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n<h2>Fairfax County VA Building Permits</h2>\r\n<p>If you\'re working on a project that requires a permit, your first step will be heading to the <a href=\"https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/landdevelopment/permit-process\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Permit Application Center</a> (the application form is online) to get started. There is a base fee of<strong> $108</strong> for all permits, and building permit fees vary depending on the type of project you\'re undertaking. The county website offers an extremely helpful page that will <a href=\"https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/apps/feecalc/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">estimate your permit fee</a>. Total fees mainly depend on the total square footage of the project.</p>\r\n<p>For a full (rather convoluted) breakdown of every fee, check the <a href=\"https://library.municode.com/va/fairfax_county/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=THCOCOFAVI1976_APXQLADESEFESC\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">full fee schedule</a> code of ordinances</p>\r\n<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n<h2>Electrical Permits</h2>\r\n<p>To submit an application for an electrical permit, you\'ll follow the same steps through the Permit Application Center. Electrical permit fees:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Electrical service size\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>0 - 149 amps: $240</li>\r\n<li>140 - 399 amps: $254.40</li>\r\n<li>400 amps: $350.40</li>\r\n<li>More than 400 amps (you\'ll need to view the itemized list under \"Electrical Equipment Installation Fees\" in the <a href=\"https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/landdevelopment/sites/landdevelopment/files/assets/documents/fee-schedule_0.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">fee schedule</a>)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n<h2>Plumbing Permits</h2>\r\n<p>The plumbing permit application follows the same steps as the others&mdash;use Fairfax County\'s Permit Application Center. Plumbing fees are a bit more straightforward:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>New plumbing systems in new buildings, existing unplumbed buildings, or portions thereof, changes in existing systems: $58\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp; Each fixture, appliance, appurtenance, area-way drain, floor drain, and roof drain is an extra $8.70</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Setting or replacing fixtures without changes in existing system: $58.50\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Each fixture is an additional $6.78</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Sewer, new, replacement or repair: $58.50</li>\r\n<li>Sump pump: $8.70</li>\r\n<li>Water service, new, replacement or repair: $58.50</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n<h2>Future Blog Updates</h2>\r\n<p>This list is current based on 2022 figures. Governments often change permit fees each year, so we\'ll update this blog post next year! Let us know in the comments below if we missed/messed up anything or if there\'s any other information you\'d like to see here!</p>\r\n</div>',2,'',8,'2020-06-30 15:05:34'),(25,'Prince George\'s County MD Remodeling & Finishing Permits','Wondering what permits you\'ll need (and how much they\'ll cost) for a remodeling or finishing project in Prince George\'s County, MD? Find out here!','building permits prince georges county md, electrical permits, mechanical permits, Prince George\'s County MD, Maryland, building codes, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, building permits guide, prince georges county permits guide','prince-georges-county-md-remodeling--finishing-permits','Prince George\'s County MD Remodeling & Finishing Permits','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/25/6a4f5ebf2e22ac5c7612e928818db46c','A current 2022 list of permits (and their fees) required for a variety of different basement remodeling or finishing projects. Check out this week\'s post on the best basement remodeling blog around!','<div class=\"html\">\r\n<p>This helpful and simple guide outlines every single permit you may need if you\'re planning to remodel or refinish your basement in Prince George\'s County, Maryland this 2022. We\'ve included all of the relevant fees and links to the forms for each permit.</p>\r\n<p>Note: Prince George\'s County has moved most of its permit applications to an online system, so you\'ll need to apply online. Also, it\'s important to check if you\'ll even need a permit before getting started, and the county website has a <a href=\"https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/DocumentCenter/View/37314/Permit-Types-PDF?bidId=\">handy list</a> covering every possible instance of when you may or may not need one.</p>\r\n<h2>Prince George\'s County MD Building Permits</h2>\r\n<p>All building permit applications are filed through their <a href=\"https://dpiepermits.princegeorgescountymd.gov\">online system</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Permit fees vary wildly depending on the depth and complexity of your project. The following is a list of the most relevant basement remodeling or finishing fees. For the sake of brevity, fees are based on the minimum&mdash;projects that exceed the minimum require more (you can see the full fee schedule and extra fees&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/DocumentCenter/View/23559/DPIE-Fee-Schedule-PDF?bidId=\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>).</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Residential Building Fees</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Residential Addition: $340</li>\r\n<li>Interior Alteration/Repair: $90</li>\r\n<li>Alteration/Repair without U&amp;O: $150</li>\r\n<li>Basement Finishing: $340</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The county website has an extremely handy <a href=\"https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/1501/Residential-Building\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">permit requirements list</a> detailing every possible instance of when you may or may not need a permit.</p>\r\n<h2>Electrical Permits</h2>\r\n<p>You\'ll need to fill out and submit an electrical permit application through the <a href=\"https://dpiepermits.princegeorgescountymd.gov/Customers/Login.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">county\'s online system</a>. You can see the pdf of the application form and fees <a href=\"https://md-princegeorgescounty.civicplus.com/DocumentCenter/View/4896/Electrical-Permit-Application-Form-Fees-PDF\">here</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Electrical permit fees are also highly situational, depending on your project.</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Electrical Permit Fees</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A/C Equipment Unit: $30</li>\r\n<li>Appliance: $45</li>\r\n<li>Audio/Visual Equipment: $85</li>\r\n<li>Heating Equipment Unit: $30</li>\r\n<li>Thermostat: $45</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>There are quite a few more list items on the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/DocumentCenter/View/23559/DPIE-Fee-Schedule-PDF?bidId=\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the fee schedule form</a>, but most are for very specific things, such as installing a swimming pool, an MRI, or dentist chair.</p>\r\n<h2>Mechanical Permits</h2>\r\n<p>The fee for a mechanical permit is 1% the cost of the mechanical work or $65, whichever is higher, plus a 5% technology fee tacked on. Unfortunately, most projects modifying or installing any type of mechanical equipment will require a permit (you won\'t have to submit any <a href=\"https://md-princegeorgescounty.civicplus.com/DocumentCenter/View/4349/Mechanical-Plan-Review-Requirements-PDF\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mechanical drawings or plans</a>), but be sure to adhere to what the <a href=\"https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/Faq.aspx?QID=764\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Prince George\'s County website</a>&nbsp;says:</p>\r\n<p>\"A&nbsp;mechanical permit is required to erect, install, enlarge, alter, repair, remove, convert, or replace a mechanical heating, ventilating, or air-conditioning system, the installation of which is regulated by the International Mechanical Code (IMC), International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC), or the International Residential Code (IRC), as appropriate. These pieces of equipment include, but are not limited to furnaces, heat pumps, air-conditioning units, range hoods, cooling towers, chillers, fuel-oil tanks and piping systems, and boilers.\"</p>\r\n<p>On the plus side, there seems to be no additional fees for mechanical permit applications. However, you will need an HVAC contractor\'s license to apply for a mechanical permit.</p>\r\n<h2>Future Updates</h2>\r\n<p>We\'ll either update this list next year or create another article when any permit fees change or any other requirements are changed. Let us know in the comments below if we missed/messed up anything or if there\'s any other information you\'d like to see here!</p>\r\n</div>',2,'',9,'2020-06-23 15:07:07'),(26,'Howard County, MD Basement Remodeling & Finishing Permits','Check out this handy guide covering everything you need to know about building, electrical, and plumbing permits (and how much they cost) in Howard County, MD!','howard county, MD, building permits, electrical permits, plumbing permits, hvac permits, gas permits, howard county MD permits, Howard County electrical permits, Howard County plumbing permits, Maryland permits, basement blog, basement remodeling, basement renovation, foundation repair, basement wall system, flooded basement, waterproofing membrane, foundation waterproofing, basement sealer, basement remodeling blog, basement waterproofing blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement remodeling in Howard County MD, basement finishing in Howard County MD','howard-county-md-basement-remodeling--finishing-permits','Howard County, MD Basement Remodeling & Finishing Permits','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/26/76fc78f4d0a34a521da89258a3a38bbd','Current (2022) pricing & info about building, electrical, and plumbing and gas permits in Howard County, Maryland.','<div class=\"html\">\r\n<p>Here\'s a simple guide to all of the possible permits you may need on your next basement remodeling or refinishing project in Howard County, Maryland! The list includes links to residential forms and current (2022) prices of building, electrical, and plumbing permits in Howard County.</p>\r\n<h2>Howard County MD Building Permits</h2>\r\n<p>The fee for a <a href=\"https://www.howardcountymd.gov/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=489H4jw6RWs%3d&amp;tabid=1207&amp;portalid=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit</a> in Howard County, MD is <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">$0.18 per square foot</span> for a residential single-family home, and <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">$0.22 per square foot</span> for multi-family buildings (a 10% technology fee is also included on all permits).</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Foundation Permit</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Requires prior approval, payment of all applicable fees associated with the building permit and payment of water/sewer utility fees: $200 (plus filing fee)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Alterations &amp; Repairs to Attached and Detached Single Family Dwellings</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Filing Fee (non-refundable): $25</li>\r\n<li>Single/small room or area (200 square feet or less): $50</li>\r\n<li>More than single floor or area (over 200 square feet): $100</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The full fee schedule form, which covers everything from private swimming pool permits to temporary structure permits (satellite dish, arbor, trellis, detached kiosk, etc.), is <a href=\"https://www.howardcountymd.gov/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=-RhdP8ws3Ek%3d&amp;tabid=1207&amp;portalid=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</p>\r\n<p>If you\'re still unsure about the process and what you\'ll need to do, check out the the <a href=\"https://www.howardcountymd.gov/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=yKR25p_c23s%3d&amp;tabid=1207&amp;portalid=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Residential Building Permit Checklist</a> to make sure all of your bases are covered.</p>\r\n<h2>Electrical Permits</h2>\r\n<p>The application fee for a residential&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.howardcountymd.gov/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=rBB4Cz3qckA%3d&amp;portalid=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">electrical permit</a>&nbsp;in Howard County, MD is <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">$50</span> (a 10% technology fee is also included on all permits). The permit itself starts at $150 and goes up depending a variety of different factors:</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Residential Flat Rate Schedule (for new construction)</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>1 or 2 family dwelling (0-200-amp service): $150</li>\r\n<li>1 or 2 family dwelling (over 200-400-amp service): $200</li>\r\n<li>1 or 2 family dwelling (over 400-600-amp service): $300</li>\r\n<li>1 or 2 family dwelling (over 600-amp service): $500</li>\r\n<li>Multi-family dwelling\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>(including service and comon area wiring): $100 each unit</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Residential Alteration &amp; Additions</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Flat fee of $50</li>\r\n<li>Multi-Family Flat Fee of $50 per apt unit.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>There a lot more fees on <a href=\"https://www.howardcountymd.gov/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=lA14uGp7C8E%3d&amp;tabid=1207&amp;portalid=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the schedule form</a>, but don\'t typically apply for most people (it depends on the depth and complexity of your project).</p>\r\n<h2>Plumbing &amp; Gas Permits</h2>\r\n<p>The cost of a plumbing and gas permit in Howard County depends on a few different factors, but the <a href=\"https://www.howardcountymd.gov/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=yUun89uOuJo%3d&amp;portalid=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">application itself</a> is a flat <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">$50</span> (plus the 10% tech fee on all permits). Here are the additional fees for residential plumbing projects.</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #2980b9;\">Fixtures</span></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>1st fixture: $25</li>\r\n<li>Each additional fixture: $5</li>\r\n<li>Exceptions:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Sump pump: $25 each</li>\r\n<li>Laundry tray pump: $25 each</li>\r\n<li>Sewer Ejector: $25 each</li>\r\n<li>Swimming pool pump: $25 each</li>\r\n<li>Hot water heater: $25 each</li>\r\n<li>Hot water boiler: $25 each</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The fee for commercial plumbing fixtures starts at $50, but each additional fixture is still only an extra $5. However, similar to the residential list above, there are exceptions that cost $50 each instead of $25. Check the <a href=\"https://www.howardcountymd.gov/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=taviw2SXb78%3d&amp;tabid=1207&amp;portalid=0\">fee schedule form</a> for more details.</p>\r\n<h2>Heating-Ventilation-Air Conditioning (HVAC) Permits</h2>\r\n<p>An <a href=\"https://www.howardcountymd.gov/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=taviw2SXb78%3d&amp;tabid=1207&amp;portalid=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">HVAC permit application</a> in Howard County costs <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">$50</span> (additional 10% tech fee as well). The permit itself depends on the type of building. For a multi-family or multi-occupancy residential dwelling, per dwelling unit (apts. or condos) and per room (hotel/motel) costs <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">$80</span>. If you only need a permit for a single family attached or single family detached dwelling, the cost per heating/cooling zone is <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">$40</span>.</p>\r\n<p>The HVAC fee schedule is much less convoluted than the rest, but here\'s a link to the <a href=\"https://www.howardcountymd.gov/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=JtIA6SyURdA%3d&amp;tabid=1207&amp;portalid=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">permit fee form</a> if you want to check it out.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</div>',2,'',10,'2020-06-16 15:07:22'),(27,'BasementRemodeling.com’s Latest 2020 Projects (With Pictures)','Looking for design ideas for your basement? Get inspired by some of the many basement\'s we\'ve finished this year!','basement remodeling ideas, basement finishing examples, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, finishing a basement, decorate a basement 2020, basement designs 2020, basement design ideas, portfolio','basementremodeling.coms-latest-2020-projects-with-pictures','BasementRemodeling.com’s Latest 2020 Projects (With Pictures)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/27/773d7f4543af8ed26eacdb8c7d514adc','Some of our most recent projects from this year!','<p>We&rsquo;ve decided to follow up on the previous post made here on our <strong>basement remodeling blog</strong>&mdash;which showcased some of our <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/our-four-latest-basement-finishing--remodeling-projects\">most recent projects</a> this year. We&rsquo;ve remodeled and finished a lot of basements this year, in homes across Virginia, Maryland, and Washington DC. We have a lot more planned for this year, but we&rsquo;d like to show off a few that were finished this year!</p>\n<p>Without further ado, here are four beautiful <strong>basement finishing and remodeling</strong> projects from VA and MD by BasementRemodeling.com!</p>\n<h2>Massive Basement Finishing Project in Springfield VA</h2>\n<table class=\"previews\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/115/cc27ec075a9ec34bac571983d159aafc_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews1\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/115/cc27ec075a9ec34bac571983d159aafc_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/116/a2900bd65c3f7183083874fac6fb185f_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews1\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/116/a2900bd65c3f7183083874fac6fb185f_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/117/a9649553b9b912891de1eeaf0d5c0dc8_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews1\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/117/a9649553b9b912891de1eeaf0d5c0dc8_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/118/9b76e19ced4a82908d2ff211a4be8e71_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews1\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/118/9b76e19ced4a82908d2ff211a4be8e71_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>This extensive, 1,800-square-feet basement remodeling project in Springfield VA is basically an entire second home on its own. It includes a large living area with a comfortable amount of space for decorating, a full-size kitchenette with a lovely wet bar and seating area, a nearby pool table, full-size bathroom, and an entire home-theater room. &nbsp;</p>\n<p><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-in-springfield-va-20\">Full portfolio project gallery and description</a></p>\n<h2>Space-Optimizing Basement Remodeling Project in Montgomery Village, MD</h2>\n<table class=\"previews\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/119/af69531b1fb1434e0e8105ed047b8ad9_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews2\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/119/af69531b1fb1434e0e8105ed047b8ad9_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/120/9e959332d2f7a182ad7e38096cb552e4_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews2\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/120/9e959332d2f7a182ad7e38096cb552e4_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/121/4ca488998a2a17c559323bac747cc231_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews2\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/121/4ca488998a2a17c559323bac747cc231_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>This Montgomery Village, MD basement was re-designed to provide plenty of storage compartments, while still remaining comfortable. The basement includes a family room is decked out with custom cabinetry and individual shelving, a nearby closet with custom-designed shelving, a half-bath, and a newly installed double-door entrance&mdash;all underneath lovely and resistant LVT flooring.</p>\n<p><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-in-montgomery-village-md\">Portfolio gallery here</a></p>\n<h2>Spacious Remodeling Project in Urbana, Maryland</h2>\n<table class=\"previews\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/122/ec8abe4b5dd2428b36f6d87f561bf89c_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews3\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/122/ec8abe4b5dd2428b36f6d87f561bf89c_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/123/eaf0f6693a9d23493ef2c989cf31d4e7_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews3\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/123/eaf0f6693a9d23493ef2c989cf31d4e7_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/124/95d1767dbb69232e82fd6eb8b8924dd9_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews3\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/124/95d1767dbb69232e82fd6eb8b8924dd9_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/125/32e458b415a0da3affa9f2b60694b41e_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews3\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/125/32e458b415a0da3affa9f2b60694b41e_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Designed and implemented by BasementRemodeling.com for a home in Urbana MD, this 1,500 square-feet basement offers endless decorative and practical possibilities! It features a large living area with high-quality LVT flooring, a small wet bar directly near a full-size bathroom, large home theater, and a guest bedroom.</p>\n<p><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-in-urbana-md\">Full image gallery and description</a></p>\n<h2>Simple &amp; Design-Flexible Finished Basement in Silver Spring, MD</h2>\n<table class=\"previews\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/126/6c453f805f074aa7291e7aa73dabec30_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews4\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/126/6c453f805f074aa7291e7aa73dabec30_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/127/6af52596406fb446759f1bea4c1a6e86_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews4\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/127/6af52596406fb446759f1bea4c1a6e86_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/128/5cb11e43b618040fed81973657f6d910_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews4\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/128/5cb11e43b618040fed81973657f6d910_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>A top-to-bottom basement refinishing project for a home in Silver Spring, MD. This basement project features a spacious family room, a large guest bedroom, a full-size bathroom, soft carpeted flooring, and a stand-alone column suitable for many different design layouts.</p>\n<p>We\'ll be posting more in the future so check back on the \'Our News\' section of <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/\">our blog</a> or <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BasementRemodelingCom/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook page</a> regularly!</p>',5,'',11,'2020-06-09 15:10:38'),(28,'Our Four Latest Basement Finishing & Remodeling Projects','Check out our latest basement remodeling and finishing projects in VA, MD, and DC on our basement blog!','basement remodeling blog, BasementRemodeling.com news, new projects, 2020 basement projects, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas, basement design inspiration','our-four-latest-basement-finishing--remodeling-projects','Our Four Latest Basement Finishing & Remodeling Projects','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/28/222a9bafeeab73b55d3b74f09aa9d3ae','In this week’s basement remodeling blog post we’ll be featuring some of BasementRemodeling.com’s latest projects!','<p>It&rsquo;s been a while since we updated the news section of our&nbsp;<strong>basement remodeling blog</strong> with any info about recent projects, but BasementRemodeling.com is still going strong (and staying safe)!</p>\n<p>Despite the current coronavirus pandemic raging across the world, we&rsquo;ve been busy transforming multiple basements in homes across Maryland, Virginia, and Washington DC. Us being busy doesn&rsquo;t mean we don&rsquo;t take the pandemic seriously, though. We&rsquo;ve implemented a variety of different COVID-19 safety protocols to ensure the safety of our crews and customers, including requiring all personal to wear N95 face-masks and perform daily temperature checks before beginning work.</p>\n<p>Now that we&rsquo;ve covered the pandemic situation and how we\'re responding, time to show off four of our most recent projects!</p>\n<h2>Basement Remodeling &amp; Finishing Project in Mclean, VA</h2>\n<table class=\"previews\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/129/245a91a4d9bcc3b3f5425ed1b9e926a3_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews1\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/129/245a91a4d9bcc3b3f5425ed1b9e926a3_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/130/66b1c6a23de40724cf66dab9990adee8_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews1\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/130/66b1c6a23de40724cf66dab9990adee8_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/131/e9c94d2889eeec43f239ecc8a2aeb2cc_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews1\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/131/e9c94d2889eeec43f239ecc8a2aeb2cc_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A beautiful and spacious basement remodel with spiral staircase leading from the main floor, countertop bar with seating area and nearby wine-rack, spacious living space, and full-size bathroom with a tiled shower.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-in-mclean-va-1\">Check out the full photo gallery and description</a></p>\n<h2>Finishing Project in District Heights, MD</h2>\n<table class=\"previews\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/132/a0bd7da3ca59209277f4c6e4a90fef99_1920x1078.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews2\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/132/a0bd7da3ca59209277f4c6e4a90fef99_1920x1078.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1078\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/133/6626e3cd53cabe2d5d526486a980db46_1920x1078.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews2\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/133/6626e3cd53cabe2d5d526486a980db46_1920x1078.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1078\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/134/79dc9f2e45e2c6bb8224e9c9245c1658_1920x1078.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews2\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/134/79dc9f2e45e2c6bb8224e9c9245c1658_1920x1078.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1078\" /></a></td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Clean and bright basement design project for a home in District Heights, MD. The basement features stand-alone columns, high-quality LVT flooring, a mid-size wet bar,&nbsp;a&nbsp;laundry room,&nbsp;a half bathroom, and a large bedroom with a new-installed egress window.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-in-district-heights-md\">Portfolio description and more images</a></p>\n<h2>Basement Remodeling Project in Laurel, MD</h2>\n<table class=\"previews\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/135/6b48b48f6c29227791545afc1ae46053_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews3\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/135/6b48b48f6c29227791545afc1ae46053_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/136/6e1b14f65f500a10e3348c46388ba518_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews3\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/136/6e1b14f65f500a10e3348c46388ba518_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/137/fd1f8a40067a0d1fcf14dc9d7ca89442_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews3\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/137/fd1f8a40067a0d1fcf14dc9d7ca89442_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">This basement remodeling and refinishing project in Laurel MD includes a family room, home theater, bedroom, and full bathroom&mdash;all with new remodeled features.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-laurel-md-1\">Full image gallery and description</a></p>\n<h2>Apartment Remodeling Project in Washington DC</h2>\n<table class=\"previews\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/138/bec5e8782fcf4aa4e1cff879abe417a3_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews4\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/138/bec5e8782fcf4aa4e1cff879abe417a3_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/139/190aff7f1c38649eb9a27c2601f487f8_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews4\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/139/190aff7f1c38649eb9a27c2601f487f8_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/140/4f55b70beac60d48b3014226e7ed67f2_1920x1280.jpg\" data-fslightbox=\"previews4\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/140/4f55b70beac60d48b3014226e7ed67f2_1920x1280.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" /></a></td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">This project by BasementRemodeling.com is a complete remodel of a home in Washington, DC. We transformed this home\'s basement into an apartment! We installed a new outside entrance, a kitchen-like wet-bar and LVT flooring in the family room, a new egress window in the bedroom, and a bathtub enclosure in the bathroom.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-in-washington-dc-1\">View the rest of images here</a></p>\n<h2>The Masters of the Basement&mdash;BasementRemodeling.com</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">BasementRemodeling.com is the leading <strong>basement finishing and remodeling contractor</strong> in three states. Our designs, craftsmanship, and passion are second to none. If you&rsquo;re interested in seeing more of our past projects, check the portfolio page. We&rsquo;ll be posting up more projects as they&rsquo;re completed throughout the year. We also post weekly remodeling blog articles covering everything you could possibly need to know about basements&mdash;so check back here often!</p>',5,'',12,'2020-06-02 15:11:02'),(29,'Enhance Your Basement with These Clever Engineering Ideas','Use common ideas with unique designs to make your basement stand out. Check out these clever basement engineering ideas.','basement engineering ideas, downstairs engineering ideas, basement walk-outs, basement HVAC ideas, basement egress windows, clever engineering, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas','enhance-your-basement-with-these-clever-engineering-ideas','Enhance Your Basement with These Clever Engineering Ideas','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/29/62ed2d6870affbe2cd36e4456b587d5c','Looking for a way to make your home\'s basement stand out from the rest? Try these common engineering ideas with clever designs.','<p>When it comes to having a comfortable and protected home, your basement is just as important as your main floor. It&rsquo;s often hard to decide what architectural designs you&rsquo;d like in your basement&mdash;just a few simple ideas can make a huge difference in the overall look, feel, and security. Implementing the right basement engineering ideas will not only make it a comfortable and peaceful place to spend time in, they&rsquo;ll increase the value of your home! We&rsquo;ve outlined a few great and clever engineering ideas to make your basement stand out from the rest, while also ensuring it withstands the test of time.</p>\n<h2>Install an Egress Window</h2>\n<p>Installing <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/egress-windows/\">egress windows</a> in your basement is the best way to let natural light in. They act as the perfect escape route during an emergency situation and they look pretty good too. They also help prevent water from reaching the foundation, which will keep your infrastructure in good condition!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/111/e1e45de61d375726d7fa4c72c2eacd03_2400x1963.jpg\" alt=\"Egress window installation beautifully layered with a decorative, stacked-stone design \" width=\"2400\" height=\"1963\" /><br /><em>Egress window installation beautifully layered with a decorative, stacked-stone design </em></p>\n<p>Many egress windows have a small ladder attached to the end or are even specifically designed with decorative steps to make getting in and out easier. Aside from emergency situations, decorative steps provide a neat and fun way for guests to enter your home! Egress windows are fairly common these days, but adding something unique to them is something you don&rsquo;t often see.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/112/fa3b1fbc37ec168c36637ffd29849a6c_2400x1941.jpg\" alt=\"Egress window with cleverly engineered decorative steps for easy access\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1941\" /><br /><em>Egress window with cleverly engineered decorative steps that both look aesthetically pleasing and provide easy basement access.</em></p>\n<h2>Turn Your Back Entrance into a Walk-Out</h2>\n<p>While they&rsquo;re a bit more complicated to install, basement <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/walk-outs/\">walk-outs</a> add an additional flair to your home. They flood your basement with natural light and, when properly installed, add additional value to your property! A private entrance for your basement allows guests to come and go during early or later hours without disturbing other members in the home. Walk-outs also serve some practical purposes as well. For example, if you&rsquo;re planning on buying a big couch, it&rsquo;ll be much easier to get it into your house with a walk-out!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/113/b9b824ab04fbfbb37f2c963df56b584c_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"A private walk-out entrance enhances the home with a unique look\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>A private walk-out entrance enhances the home with a unique look.</em></p>\n<h2>Get Creative with Your Heating, Ventilation, and Air Conditioning (HVAC)</h2>\n<p>HVAC is an obvious necessity for every home. But there are some cool and uncommon ways to cleverly place your <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/hvac/\">HVAC system</a>. A large majority of homes have their heaters in awkward locations on the floor. Sometimes these locations are seemingly random, which can lead to heating loss and a higher bill. A clever engineering technique is to identify the key locations in your home that provide the best air circulation, which can include the ceilings. Placing your heating and cooling systems in the right locations, on both the ceilings and floors, means better efficiency and less money!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/114/0f00c3c60a586fcf461007f0ea71d2d3_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"HVAC systems are typically placed on the floor, this uniquely placed system provides better circulation and extra space\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>HVAC systems are typically placed on the floor, this uniquely placed system provides better circulation and extra space.</em></p>\n<h2>Common Ideas, Uncommon Designs</h2>\n<p>Many of these ideas are fairly commonplace, but it&rsquo;s not about what you&rsquo;re installing&mdash;it&rsquo;s about what you do with it. A lot of homes have egress windows, but not many have decorative designs or stairs inside them. Many homes have a basement back entrance, but not a fully-fledged walk-out. Constant adaptation and tweaking current ideas are an integral part of engineering. Clever engineering ideas continuously provide new and interesting quality of life upgrades for homeowners. Your basement deserves to be treated well!</p>',1,'',13,'2020-05-26 15:11:16'),(30,'5 MORE Ways to Decorate Your Basement in 2020','Currently quarantined and have a lot of time on your hands? Think about decorating your basement space with these five ideas.','basement decorating, basement interior design 2020, basement design ideas, decorating empty space, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas','5-more-ways-to-decorate-your-basement-in-2020','5 MORE Ways to Decorate Your Basement in 2020','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/30/54ebf47ebe9a9b788046aa4097b26696','Discover five more clever but relatively simple interior design ideas for your home in 2020.','<p>In our <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/5-creative-ways-to-decorate-your-basement-in-2020\">previous article</a>, we covered five different ways you can <strong>decorate your basement</strong>, from designing a full home entertainment center to installing a wall-mounted fireplace. There are hundreds of possibilities when it comes to your home&rsquo;s interior design, especially for a downstairs area, but we&rsquo;ve chosen five more ideas you can use to breathe a bit of fresh air into your basement!</p>\n<h2>1. Tile Flooring</h2>\n<p>If you&rsquo;re going for a polished and refined look, decorating your basement with tile flooring is a timeless and practical decision. It&rsquo;s not only beautiful, durable, and customizable to any of your specific design choices, its polished surface helps fill the basement with more natural light. It&rsquo;s also very easy to keep clean!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/106/162fdb9dc9380f33890877dab327ee85_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Basement with diamond-shaped tile flooring\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Basement with diamond-shaped tile flooring.</em><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/flooring/tile/\">Full gallery of tile flooring ideas</a></p>\n<h2>2. LED Lighting</h2>\n<p>Lighting is a fun aspect of basement design. Aside from the energy advantages that come with LEDs, they are customizable in color and style. A room with colored LEDs can easily make the room &ldquo;pop.&rdquo; Colored LEDs hooked up to dimmer switches pair exceptionally well with living areas and entertainment centers!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/107/cea4ae5a0c71b5f966f1ef48e4669a9d_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Basement entertainment center with off-colored LED lighting to accentuate the room\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Basement entertainment center with off-colored LED lighting to accentuate the room.<br /></em><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/ceilings/hidden-led-lights/\">Full gallery of LED lighting ideas</a></p>\n<h2>3. Basement Staircase Steps</h2>\n<p>The stairs leading down to your basement play a pretty important role to its overall aesthetic. An elegantly designed set of stairs, working together with the surrounding colors and textures, will create a beautiful entrance to your basement.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/108/806f55c18369bd7f08b22274abb6403b_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Elegantly designed staircase with expanding stairs that gently flow down into the bottom floor\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Elegantly designed staircase with expanding stairs that gently flow down into the bottom floor.<br /></em><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/basement-stair-steps-ideas.html\">Full gallery of basement stairs ideas</a></p>\n<h2>4. Under-Stairs Space</h2>\n<p>From practical to fun, there are a ton of ways to decorate the extra space under your stairs. Bookshelves, closet space, a storage area, or even a fancy play area for children&mdash;the possibilities are only limited by your imagination!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/109/664f0c0cf72a501443cc1a4f32c3d2a1_2400x1763.jpg\" alt=\"Cleverly placed children&rsquo;s playhouse built right under the staircase\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1763\" /><br /><em>Cleverly placed children&rsquo;s playhouse built right under the staircase.<br /></em><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/stairs-and-railing/stair-steps/\">Full gallery of under stairs space ideas</a></p>\n<h2>5. Stacked Stone Walls</h2>\n<p>Whether it&rsquo;s to encase a fireplace or to compliment the surrounding environment, stacked stone walls are an excellent way to provide an extra layer of beauty to your basement. Since stacked stone is molded from actual stone, it&rsquo;s identical in every way and considerably cheaper. With plenty of colors and textures to choose from, it&rsquo;s a great decoration choice for fireplaces, walls, decorative columns, and more!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/110/7aeb73346be07a5822edfd6a28a8ccfb_2400x2400.jpg\" alt=\"Stacked stone design on a column nestled near a small kitchen and seating area\" width=\"2400\" height=\"2400\" /><br /><em>Stacked stone design on a column nestled near a small kitchen and seating area.</em><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/wall-treatments/stacked-stone-wall/\">Full gallery of stacked stone wall decorating ideas</a></p>\n<h2>Quarantine\'s a Great Time for Interior Design</h2>\n<p>These ideas are only scratching the surface of just how many ways you can decorate your basement. Ranging from complex and practical to simple and fun, there are thousands of creative basement decoration possibilities. With many people working from home at the moment, the opportunity to do something neat with your basement space is a real possibility!</p>',1,'',14,'2020-05-19 15:11:33'),(31,'5 Creative Ways to Decorate Your Basement in 2020','Need help thinking of ways to decorate your basement this 2020? Here are five great design ideas to consider.','basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, decorating a basement, decorate a basement 2020, basement designs 2020, basement design ideas','5-creative-ways-to-decorate-your-basement-in-2020','5 Creative Ways to Decorate Your Basement in 2020','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/31/1c67772d3e413a78b33e7e30666957ba','Here are five things you can do to spruce up your basement\'s interior aesthetic. From the best basement remodeling blog around, BasementRemodeling.com','<div class=\"html\">\n<p>Making interior design choices is never easy. Every single aspect plays an important role in the overall look you&rsquo;re going for. This especially applies to basements. When you hear the word &ldquo;basement&rdquo; it&rsquo;s often preceded by the word &ldquo;unfinished.&rdquo; Which does make sense, there&rsquo;s a ton of space to use! If you&rsquo;re looking for creative ways to fill out or remodel your basement, here are five creative basement decoration ideas.</p>\n<p>Keep in mind, not all of these are brand new ideas (nor are they easy or cheap to install). In fact, many of them have been used for years, but some things simply never go out of style!</p>\n<h2>1. Entertainment Center</h2>\n<p>A basement is a traditionally perfect place for an entertainment center, and for good reason! Designating a room specifically for your entertainment center, or for a complete home-theater, can make a huge difference in your viewing experience. Paired with shelving or even a nearby fireplace, an entertainment center is an excellent basement decoration choice.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/99/c3467ce32b60d2091bab8e1bd4aa8a7f_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"715\" height=\"477\" /><br /><em>Basement home theatre system with convenient nearby shelving and LED lighted ceilings.<br /></em><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/built-ins-and-shelving/entertainment-center/\"><em>Gallery of entertainment center ideas</em></a></p>\n<h2>2. Advanced Ceilings</h2>\n<p>When first entering a home, the ceiling isn&rsquo;t typically the first thing you notice. But that certainly doesn&rsquo;t make it any less important! A creative ceiling design can really compliment the overall appearance of a room. From LEDs arranged in intricate patterns to tray ceilings delightfully paired with a fully-functional kitchen, there are definitely plenty of outside-the-box ideas to choose from!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/100/0c389c379918834cbc960dc8cde8651d_2400x1526.jpg\" alt=\"Fully functional basement mini-kitchen with tray ceiling and island seating area. Beautiful and perfect for drinks and conversation with guests!\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1526\" /><br /><em>Fully functional basement mini-kitchen with tray ceiling and island seating area. Beautiful and perfect for drinks and conversation with guests!</em></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/101/1018e4dd552b1cd4d87213d368068c45_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Tray ceiling with LED lighting to really give the room an open, yet still cozy feel.\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Tray ceiling with LED lighting to really give the room an open, yet still cozy feel.&nbsp;<br /><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/ceilings/advanced/\">Gallery of advanced ceiling ideas</a></em></p>\n<h2>3. Stand-Alone Columns</h2>\n<p>Aside from obviously providing structural support, stand alone columns can really add a sophisticated and polished look to a basement interior. They can be used to beautifully frame an entrance to another room. If your basement feels as though it&rsquo;s missing something, even a single pillar can really tie a room together.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/102/0b6b9a1b165fb2cb4bed8f15e0888b2d_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Beautifully crafted square pillars marking the entrance to an eating area.\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Beautifully crafted square pillars marking the entrance to an eating area.</em></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/103/54d9fd1f2948997af39c3b786c6b2434_2102x1486.jpg\" alt=\"Living room area with small kitchen, cleverly tied together with a single column design.\" width=\"2102\" height=\"1486\" /><em>Living room area with small kitchen, cleverly tied together with a single column design.</em><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/columns/stand-alone/\"><em>Full gallery of stand-alone column ideas</em></a></p>\n<h2>4. Glass Doors</h2>\n<p>Opposed to standard doors, glass doors are a stylish way to provide a more welcoming feel to a basement. They allow two rooms to seamlessly transition into each other, without hindering natural light!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/104/b975dc17915376820abe9c5bad020fd0_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Beautiful pair of glass doors providing comfortable room separation.\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Beautiful pair of glass doors providing comfortable room separation.</em><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/doors/glass/\"><em>Full gallery of glass door ideas</em></a></p>\n<h2>5. Wall-Mounted Fireplace</h2>\n<p>A fireplace is a great addition to a basement. The mesmerizing and pleasant effects of a crackling-fire provide a calming effect to those surrounding, making it a perfect addition to a family room or seating area. It also pairs quite well with a nearby entertainment center or bookshelves!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/105/84f7ab61f6f0eb16fa36d09ad4df88cd_2400x1590.jpg\" alt=\"A small seating area with a modern fireplace design.\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1590\" /><br /><em>A small seating area with a modern fireplace design.<br /></em><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/fireplaces/\"><em>Full gallery of fireplace ideas</em></a></p>\n</div>',1,'',15,'2020-05-12 15:12:00'),(32,'3 Requirements for A Perfect Basement Entertainment Center','Planning on setting up an entertainment center in your basement? Here are three essential things to consider before getting started!','basement entertainment center, basement media center, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, best basement blog, home-theater, hidden led lighting, media center soundproofing, media center ideas, entertainment center requirements, basement home theater ideas','3-requirements-for-a-perfect-basement-entertainment-center','3 Requirements for A Perfect Basement Entertainment Center','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/32/09d5cdecb4d930944f053513cd197db2','Thinking about setting up an entertainment center in your basement? Here are three crucial things to keep in mind before getting started.','<p>Whether you&rsquo;re planning out a multipurpose room or a full home-theater, an <strong>entertainment center</strong> is always a good decorative choice for your basement. There are quite a few things to consider when setting up a <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/built-ins-and-shelving/entertainment-center/\">basement entertainment system</a> though. Anything from location and distance to equipment and atmosphere play an important role in the overall performance and feel of your setup. This can all seem pretty daunting, so we&rsquo;ve outlined a few specific things to keep in mind when you&rsquo;re setting up your home for the perfect basement entertainment center.</p>\n<h2>1. Location, Location, Location</h2>\n<p>Regardless of the specific use you have in mind for your system, you&rsquo;ll want to pick out a spot that has both optimal acoustic range and a cozy feel. The choices are endless when it comes to deciding a good location, but it really all depends on what you&rsquo;re looking to get out of your entertainment system. If you&rsquo;re looking for a simple place to setup a TV for casual watching with family or guests, directly nearby a fireplace is a classic choice.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/95/05973a48ceec8f05b36e2285d5e36a21_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Basement entertainment center with the TV directly above a fireplace.\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Basement entertainment center with the TV directly above a fireplace.</em></p>\n<p>On the other hand, if you&rsquo;re aiming for the perfect home-theater experience and want crystal-clear image and no glare, you&rsquo;ll ideally want an area that natural light can&rsquo;t easily reach. You&rsquo;ll also need to consider the shape of the ceiling above your home-theater location. Though the difference isn&rsquo;t too noticeable, a standard flat ceiling will provide a bit less acoustic performance compared to a tray ceiling. Even if you can&rsquo;t tell the difference, when paired with some hidden, colored LED lighting, a <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/3-fantastic-basement-ceiling-options\">tray ceiling</a> is definitely the way to go to nail a great setup aesthetic.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/96/8c9d07486f2fb0260aa511cc258426bb_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Entertainment Center with tray ceiling and hidden LED lighting for atmosphere.\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Entertainment Center with tray ceiling and hidden LED lighting for atmosphere.</em></p>\n<h2>2. The Right Equipment</h2>\n<p>Arguably, this is the most important part of the process! Aside from picking out a good location, the size and configuration of the TV obviously makes a difference as well. What equipment you use is up to your own specific tastes, but a quality HD-TV and a decent surround-sound system make a huge difference in the overall setup.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/97/8b4829c17f74b45f31d607eeb2dfd720_2400x1596.jpg\" alt=\"Luxury home theater with surround sound system.\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1596\" /><br /><em>Custom luxury home theater setup with projector, raised seating, and surround sound.</em></p>\n<h2>3. Soundproofing</h2>\n<p>This step isn&rsquo;t too important if you&rsquo;re just looking to install an entertainment system to complete a room and aren&rsquo;t planning on heavy use. However, if you&rsquo;re setting up a home-theater, this is a very important step! If your walls aren&rsquo;t properly sound proofed, the sound vibrations from a loud action movie will travel throughout your entire house!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/98/5ac6b43f754077908a93341c8d60e12e_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>A simple but effective home entertainment center setup</em></p>\n<p>Acoustic sound absorbing panels are an absolute necessity for a home-theater. They are pretty decently priced nowadays, especially if you buy them in bulk and install them yourself! If you have a sound system with deep bass, be sure to get panels that specifically help filter out those sounds, as they can travel through walls quite easily. With a properly soundproofed room, the inside will provide a delightful and thrilling home-theater experience, without disturbing others in your home.</p>\n<h2>Basement Entertainment Center Essentials</h2>\n<p>To sum up, the perfect basement entertainment center needs three things:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>An optimal location</li>\n<li>High-quality equipment</li>\n<li>Excellent sound-proofing</li>\n</ol>\n<p>There are obviously more things that go into creating the perfect home theater, but these three things are vital to keep in mind! If you need some inspiration, take a look through our <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/media-rooms/basic-media-rooms/\">media rooms gallery</a>!</p>',1,'',16,'2020-05-05 15:12:20'),(33,'3 Fantastic Basement Ceiling Options','Searching for basement ceiling ideas? Here are three of the best basement ceiling options around.','basement ceiling options, basement ceiling ideas, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, best basement blog, tray ceilings, hidden led lighting, led lighting, box beam, ceiling ideas, basement ceiling ideas, basement ceilings','3-fantastic-basement-ceiling-options','3 Fantastic Basement Ceiling Options','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/33/d239bfee88f18182969430f3a5f62629','Choosing a correct basement ceiling is essential for providing a warm and comfortable basement space. But what are your options?','<p>A ceiling is a commonly overlooked aspect of basement design, but it plays an important role for both lighting and visual appeal. Choosing the right ceiling can make the difference between a dark and cold-feeling basement, and a bright and warming space. There are a variety of different <strong>basement ceiling options</strong> to choose from, but which ones are the best? We&rsquo;ve narrowed down the top three most popular, trendy, and fantastic basement ceiling designs around.</p>\n<h2>Basement tray ceiling</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/89/5791ee087c1661d75214575dd0ff539a_2400x1526.jpg\" alt=\"Half-tray rounded ceiling design showcasing a lovely basement kitchen\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1526\" /><em> </em><em>Half-tray rounded ceiling design showcasing a lovely basement kitchen</em></p>\n<p>Tray ceilings, also known as inverted or recessed ceilings, look exactly like they sound; an upside-down tray. They&rsquo;re a versatile design choice, allowing large, long, small, short, rounded, and squared design combinations, which makes them a stylish choice for practically any location in your basement.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/90/07d92a9e09825bb502f890ee1da75022_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Large rectangular tray ceiling paired with an open-concept design and LED lighting\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /> <em>Large rectangular tray ceiling paired with an open-concept design and LED lighting</em></p>\n<p>Overall, whether your basement is a simple open-concept design or a complex and fancy layout, tray-ceilings add an extra layer of visual aesthetic and elegance. Additionally, they provide excellent acoustic capabilities, so they&rsquo;re a particularly worth-while addition to a music or entertainment room.</p>\n<h2>Hidden LED lighting option</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/91/370d5d25fee2d33285798632cedf6927_2048x1362.jpg\" alt=\"Tastefully hidden LED-lighting maximizes your at-home theater experience\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1362\" /> <em>Tastefully hidden LED-lighting maximizes your at-home theater experience</em></p>\n<p>In this golden age of technological advancement, every home in 2020 should have LED lighting. LEDs are more <a href=\"../../../../education-center/basement-tips-blog/how-to/3-steps-to-an-energy-efficient-basement.html\">energy-efficient</a>, more powerful, and generate little to no heat compared to traditional light bulbs. They provide exceptional mood or atmosphere lighting for a basement space. In and of themselves, LEDs can be considered a ceiling option. Hidden LEDs also pair quite well in combination with a tray ceiling.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/92/389754b20d3efa169da014d7ed419c7c_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Hidden LEDs work quite well with a tray-ceiling design of any kind\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /> <em>Hidden LEDs work quite well with a tray-ceiling design of any kind</em></p>\n<h2>Box beam ceiling</h2>\n<p>Box beam ceilings are typically considered a high-end design choice, as they&rsquo;re far more complicated, time-consuming, and expensive to design and install. However, their complexity is what makes them truly stand out from all other ceiling designs.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/93/8ffcfc8aa2c034c64eff8cd66164d975_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Rustic box beam ceiling accentuating a kitchen/bar basement space\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /> <em>Rustic box beam ceiling accentuating a kitchen/bar basement space</em></p>\n<p>Box beam ceilings are primarily meant to dazzle and charm your guests with an air of luxury and sophistication, but they also have practical applications. They can help hide pipes and wiring from view, particularly for basement remodeling projects.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/94/4f7cf67349ed793d88c429d271b7a476_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Box beams can provide practical solutions to noticeable wiring and pipes\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><em>Box beams can provide practical solutions to noticeable wiring and pipes</em></p>',1,'',17,'2019-12-18 15:12:37'),(34,'Pursue Your Passion with a Basement Hobby Room','Decided it\'s finally time to stop waiting and pursue one of your side interests? Dedicate a space specifically for it with a basement hobby room!','hobby space, hobby room, basement hobby room, home workshop, home hobby space, home space ideas, basement space ideas, best basement ideas, great basement ideas, basement ideas, space ideas, basement blog, blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','pursue-your-passion-with-a-basement-hobby-room','Pursue Your Passion with a Basement Hobby Room','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/34/69ba2da8036c989100bca7250e5aecd7','Have an extra room in your basement? Use it as a hobby room!','<p>Almost everyone has a side-passion or a hobby they&rsquo;d love to spend more time on&mdash;hobbies are exciting, enriching, and, most importantly, therapeutic. But, without having a designated location to adequately pursue your chosen passion, it&rsquo;s easy to simply drop the idea and never look back. So, whether you\'re into crafting, art, writing, whittling, pottery, or practically anything else, consider setting up a <strong>basement hobby room</strong>!</p>\n<p>The main reason (aside from money) people don&rsquo;t dedicate a room for their side interests is that they don\'t have enough main-floor space. However, if you have a basement with extra rooms, you already have space you can use! Most homes are planned around the main floor, leaving the basement either unfinished or relatively vacant, so a hobby room is a great <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/\"><strong>basement space idea</strong></a>.</p>\n<p>Here are a few basic things you&rsquo;ll need to consider before getting started on a hobby space in your basement.</p>\n<h2>Room Space</h2>\n<p>One of the most crucial parts of the planning process is making sure you have the right amount and type of space. While extra basement rooms are practically perfect for a hobby room, exactly how much space you&rsquo;ll need depends on what you&rsquo;re going to be using it for! For instance, if you want a quiet place to set up a small library and writing desk where you can write or read peacefully, you won\'t have to get too extravagant with the planning. On the other hand, if you&rsquo;re interested in building a music room, you&rsquo;ll need more space, planning, and, of course, money.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Basement hobby music room\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/86/402b4c7c30cebf59927c22fbc95db18f_2154x1430.jpg\" alt=\"A music hobby room will require more planning and more basement space, but it\'s entirely worth it!\" width=\"2154\" height=\"1430\" /><em>A music hobby room will require more planning and basement space, but it\'s entirely worth it!</em></p>\n<h2>Flooring &amp; Design</h2>\n<p>The next step is deciding what type of flooring you&rsquo;ll need. For the most part, carpet or a hard floor alternative are acceptable. However, if you&rsquo;re planning something a bit more hands-on, such as a workshop or woodshop, you&rsquo;ll want to use a hardy flooring (stone, laminate, or vinyl with flexible mesh mats are good combos).</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Laminate flooring\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/87/432f32b78471ff9c53fb097d42a95b96_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Laminate flooring is an excellent and hardy flooring choice for a basement hobby room&mdash;it excels at deterring scuffs and scratches.\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><em>Laminate flooring is an excellent and hardy flooring choice for a hobby room&mdash;it excels at deterring scuffs and scratches.</em></p>\n<h2>Power &amp; HVAC requirements for a hobby room</h2>\n<p>This is the part everyone hates to think about&mdash;most hobby rooms will require some extra utilities or power sources. However, this is highly situational as well based on what you&rsquo;re planning to do with the space. If you&rsquo;re going to put in an art studio, you&rsquo;ll need to make sure the room is well-lit and well-ventilated. If you&rsquo;re thinking about installing a workshop, you&rsquo;ll need to make sure your electrical panel can handle the additional strain.</p>\n<p>While we don&rsquo;t really consider these things necessary, other things you can think about adding to your basement hobby room are additional Wi-Fi access, an extra bathroom, and maybe even a place for a television!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Consider power requirements for your basement hobby room\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/88/a3270f1cd48695ff576b97ac11e09e28_2400x2782.jpg\" alt=\"Office or crafting hobby spaces typically require additional lighting and some extra power considerations.\" width=\"2400\" height=\"2782\" /><em>Office or crafting hobby spaces typically require additional lighting and some extra power considerations.</em></p>\n<hr />\n<h2>The Ultimate Basement Remodeling Blog</h2>\n<p>Our basement remodeling blog is the ultimate go-to blog for all of the hottest basement designs, ideas, tips, news, and more&mdash;delivered weekly. Leave a comment below sharing your thoughts, questions, or critiques!</p>',1,'',18,'2019-12-03 15:12:52'),(35,'2019\'s Most Unique Basement Wet Bar Designs','Searching for unique and relevant basement wet bar designs? Here are the top five of 2019!','basement wet bar designs, wet bar trends, unique basement wet bars, unique wet bar designs, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement remodeling blog, top wet bar designs of 2019, best wet bars, wine bar, open shelving, space saving, classy, bar-like','2019s-most-unique-basement-wet-bar-designs','2019\'s Most Unique Basement Wet Bar Designs','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/35/a730d6a9ba6275b1dca87ee5cd0a9d58','2020 is almost here—take a look at the five most unique and practical basement wet bar designs of 2019!','<p>The wet bar design scene is constantly evolving, with fancy, unique, and practical variations popping in and out every year. Now that 2020 is coming up, what were the most popular <strong>2019&nbsp;basement</strong> <strong>we</strong><strong>t bar designs</strong>? Here are five of the most unique (and our personal favorite) designs of the year.</p>\n<h2>1. Wine bar</h2>\n<p>A new and popular trend for wet bar design involves shelving or refrigeration specifically made for wine. These not only add a unique aesthetic look to your wet bar, but they\'re also pretty handy! Wine bars are perfect if you have a small, but worthy, wine selection and prefer to show it off instead of hiding it away in a cellar.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Wine bars are one of the most popular basement wet bar design choices of 2019\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/78/43d48298b6a4038f3f979d69f2eee640_2400x1800.jpg\" alt=\"Full-size basement wet bar with wine bar shelving\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1800\" /><em>Full-size basement wet bar with wine bar shelving</em></p>\n<h2>2. Open shelving design</h2>\n<p>An open shelving look is a timeless wet bar design choice. The open shelves provide a unique look to a basement wet bar, and you can showcase your spirits collection. An open shelving design is also often paired with wine bar shelving, which looks great together. Overall, open shelving is stylish, practical, and works well with pretty much any wet bar design size.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Open shelving is a unique basement wet bar design decision worthy for any home\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/79/b949a312d3804c18a598413267245f4b_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Open shelving wet bar designs are perfect for showcasing your spirits collection\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Open shelving wet bar designs are perfect for showcasing your spirits collection</em></p>\n<h2>3. Classy basement wet bar</h2>\n<p>Aside from boosting the value of your home, a fancy wet bar can add an extra layer of class to your downstairs space. Building a classy wet bar is a more expensive and complicated undertaking than other designs, but that&rsquo;s why they&rsquo;ve earned the title of &ldquo;classy&rdquo;&mdash;they&rsquo;re entirely worth it for the beauty alone.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Add a luxurious look to your home with a classy basement wet bar\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/80/229b6cb1e242c866547f81a00a5a71f8_2400x1920.jpg\" alt=\"Classy basement wet bar design idea\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1920\" /><br /><em>Classy basement wet bar design idea</em></p>\n<h2>4. Unique space-saving</h2>\n<p>We\'ve included this entry for anyone who\'s more practically minded. While under-the-stairs wet bars don\'t allow you to go all-out with the design, they\'re typically simple to build, save a significant amount of space, and offer a pleasant combination of practicality and aesthetic appeal.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"A unique basement wet bar nestled underneath the stairs for maximum space usage\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/81/d5c1e1d64b9d9d87e3bd7065bb4f57dc_2136x1482.jpg\" alt=\"An under-the-stairs basement wet bar design with open shelving and a wine bar.\" width=\"2136\" height=\"1482\" /><br /><em>An under-the-stairs basement wet bar design, tastefully combined with a bit of open shelving and a wine bar.</em></p>\n<h2>5. Authentic experience</h2>\n<p>This type of wet bar offers an authentic bar-like experience without having to leave your home. It\'s perfect for any occasion, whether it be a quiet night with a significant other or a rowdy game night (and if 2019 hasn\'t been a great year for you, it\'s a classic, tried-and-true environment in which you can cry and contemplate existence).</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"A pub-like wet bar design is perfect at capturing that authentic feel in 2019\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/82/02f82e3763a249ed96f2f4f9e1dedbf5_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Basement wet-bar designed for a true pub-like experience\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Basement wet-bar designed for a true pub-like experience</em></p>\n<h3>Want more 2019 design ideas?</h3>\n<p>For more fantastic and <strong>unique wet bar design ideas</strong>, take a look through our <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/wet-bars/\">ideas section</a>!</p>',1,'',19,'2019-11-27 15:13:54'),(36,'Adding a Bathroom to Your Basement','Thinking about adding a bathroom to your basement? Here\'s what you need to consider before getting started.','adding basement bathroom, basement bathroom, basement design, basement bathroom drainage, basement bathroom restrictions, basement bathroom cost, basement bathroom price, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, bathroom remodeling, bathroom remodel, remodel the bathroom','adding-a-bathroom-to-your-basement','Adding a Bathroom to Your Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/36/ebd7ea6fdc0d2be099f21b7b6f452c7f','Having a basement bathroom is not only convenient, it also increases the value of your home. Still, what do you need to consider before getting started?','<p>Adding a bathroom to your basement provides some distinct advantages. It&rsquo;s a perfect and essential addition if you plan on providing private bedrooms for guests or family. An extra bathroom also offers additional convenience and boosts the value of your home. However, the process of <strong>adding a basement bathroom</strong>, especially if your basement is already finished, does present a few hurdles you\'ll need to jump over.</p>\n<h2>Design restrictions</h2>\n<p>The first thing you should do when contemplating a new bathroom addition is to make sure you won\'t be breaking any local zoning ordinances or quirky neighborhood covenants. This includes considering what type of bathroom you want (bathtub, standing shower, half bath, etc.), and then determining if you have any existing free space you can use for it or if you&rsquo;ll need to build an addition.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Adding a bathroom to your basement is much easier if you have a clear 3d image of what you want\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/77/6a62a113fb38755f8f304675d4bbb8bf_1280x705.jpg\" alt=\"An excellent way to determine your design restrictions before getting started is to use 3d modeling software!\" width=\"1280\" height=\"705\" /><br /><em>An excellent way to determine your design restrictions before getting started is to use <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/3-reasons-to-use-basement-3d-modeling-software\">3d modeling software</a>!</em></p>\n<h2>Drainage restrictions</h2>\n<p>The next step is to make sure you have the proper plumbing&mdash;it&rsquo;s the most important thing to consider when planning a new bathroom. Basement bathrooms have certain plumbing restrictions that need to be fulfilled to function correctly. Those restrictions come down to the depth of your plumbing and the size of your waste pipe. Since most plumbing relies on gravity to help with the removal process, the depth of your plumbing plays a crucial role. The plumbing drain has to be deep enough for waste to make it through to the septic system. Modern homes typically have a larger pipe as a default these days, but it\'s something you\'ll need to either ask a plumber to check or check yourself before getting started.</p>\n<h2>How much does adding a basement bathroom cost?</h2>\n<p>In general, installing a downstairs bathroom can cost anywhere between <a href=\"https://www.angieslist.com/articles/how-much-does-it-cost-add-bathroom.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">$3,000 and $25,000</a>. The exact price point of installing a basement bathroom really depends on what your floor plan situation is, i.e., whether or not you&rsquo;ll need to build an addition for it, and how big of a budget you have. Some of the potential challenges that we previously mentioned can also affect the overall price.</p>\n<h2>Overall, is it worth it?</h2>\n<p>For the most part, yes&mdash;it is worth it to put in a basement bathroom. It adds an extra layer of convenience and increases your home&rsquo;s value. However, be sure to check into all of the special considerations and potential issues before you get started!</p>',1,'',20,'2019-11-16 15:14:08'),(37,'3 Steps to an Energy-Efficient Basement','Having an energy-efficient basement is vital to keeping annual energy costs low, but how do you make it happen? Here\'s what you need to know!','energy-efficient basement, basement energy saving, energy-efficient design, eco-friendly, energy conservation, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design, energy efficiency, energy saving','3-steps-to-an-energy-efficient-basement','3 Steps to an Energy-Efficient Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/37/f270832fa3e8350755f395f24d2bc09d','If you\'re looking to lower your energy bill, the best place to start is with your basement. Here are three steps you can take to improve your home\'s energy-efficiency and lower your annual costs.','<p>Most home designs focus on the main floor, often disregarding the importance of the basement. An <strong>energy-efficient basement</strong> can drastically improve the energy-efficiency of your entire home, costing you less money in the long run. But what steps can you take to lower your monthly energy bill and make your home more eco-friendly?</p>\n<p>Here are the three best ways to make your basement energy-efficient and lower your annual costs.</p>\n<h2>1. Replace windows with energy-efficient alternatives</h2>\n<p>Homes in 2019 should all have energy-efficient windows. They cost a bit more than a standard window, but they perform much better in nearly every aspect and last much longer. Unfortunately, many older (and still some new homes) continue to use regular windows, despite the advantages. Replacing your basement windows with <strong>energy-efficient alternatives</strong> is one of the best ways to lower your energy costs.</p>\n<h2>2. Swap lighting</h2>\n<p>Basements are often inherently dark, with an extensive lighting system to compensate. The light bulbs used in basements are typically fluorescent or incandescent, which in combination with the sheer amount needed to completely light a dark basement, lead to higher annual energy costs. The best way to handle this is to replace your traditional lightbulbs with LEDs. They last longer, are always cool to the touch, and are <a href=\"https://www.sepco-solarlighting.com/blog/bid/145611/the-advantages-of-led-lights-for-the-environment#:~:targetText=Energy%20Efficient,and%20only%205%25%20into%20light!\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">80% more energy-efficient</a> than regular lightbulbs.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"LEDs are an excellent way to make your basement more energy-efficient\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/76/01c89430edc57dde2eff518fcb56802d_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"LEDs are an excellent alternative to traditional lighting&mdash;they\'re more powerful, safe, and energy-saving\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>LEDs are an excellent alternative to traditional lighting&mdash;they\'re more powerful, safe, and energy-saving</em></p>\n<p>Another, (albeit more expensive) way to lower your light usage is to install egress windows or a walkout in your basement. Both allow natural light easy access to your basement space, meaning less overall energy expenses.</p>\n<h2>3. Check basement insulation</h2>\n<p>Improperly sized thickness or length of insulation is a major unseen culprit of sky-rocketing energy costs. This especially applies if your basement is unfinished&mdash;having little to no insulation at all means heat is able to leave your home almost entirely unhindered. The easiest way to determine if your basement is properly insulated or not is to consult with a contractor. If anything is wrong, and you have the motivation, it&rsquo;s entirely possible to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KGjO1wddX7A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">install the insulation yourself</a>!</p>\n<p><iframe style=\"width: 100%; height: 600px;\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/KGjO1wddX7A\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"></iframe></p>\n<p>It takes some time to notice the changes, but all of these options will significantly lower your energy bill, especially if you combine all three steps!</p>',4,'',21,'2019-11-12 15:14:30'),(38,'Walkout Basements: The Pros & Cons','Thinking of installing a walkout basement but want to weigh both the pros and the cons first? Here\'s everything you need to know.','walkout basement, walkout pros and cons, dark basement solution, basement foundation, partial basement, walkouts, natural lighting, walkout installation, pros and cons, natural light, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','walkout-basements-the-pros--cons','Walkout Basements: The Pros & Cons','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/38/cbcd5bf1bc5c7b3198f24d6b671e9a97','Walkouts bring a lot of advantages to a basement, including better lighting and accessibility, but what are some of the disadvantages?','<p>When it comes to home design, deciding what to do with your basement is harder than it seems. Do you want a <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/how-to-choose-the-right-basement-windows\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">dark basement</a>, or would you rather it be bright and comfortable? Would you like to provide extra rooms for family and guests, but don&rsquo;t want them disturbing the main floor when they come and go? In both cases, a walkout solves the problem! A <strong>walkout basement</strong>&nbsp;has both <strong>pros and cons</strong>, but it\'s a great way to spice up your home\'s design, not to mention the increase of value to your property.&nbsp;While they do offer significant practical and aesthetic advantages, there are a few disadvantages to consider.</p>\n<h2>Pros of installing a walkout entrance</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Walkout basements offer a variety of different pros and cons, but their advantages outweigh the disadvantages\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/74/df2bdfe775efcbf91f0773483fa70884_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Walk-outs provide better lighting and accessibility to a basement, while also increasing the value of a home\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><br /><em>Walk-outs provide better lighting and accessibility to a basement, while also increasing the value of a home</em></p>\n<h3 style=\"padding-left: 20px;\">Pro: Better lighting</h3>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 20px;\">Perhaps the most essential feature of a walkout is its ability to boost the natural light in your basement. Natural light often has an understandably difficult time reaching a regular basement space, making the basement feel closed off and dungeon-esque. Adding a door (or double door) walkout provides the light the opportunity to flood into the basement. Not only is the additional light aesthetically pleasing, but air will also flow with much greater ease through the basement, helping with <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/how-to-prevent-mold-in-your-basement-5-tips\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>mold prevention</strong></a>.</p>\n<h3 style=\"padding-left: 20px;\">Pro: Accessibility</h3>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 20px;\">This is a rather obvious feature&mdash;an additional entrance means easier access. Walkouts are perfect if you have people living or staying in your basement. Family, guests, teens with their friends, renters, and so on can keep odd hours without waking the rest of the house. It&rsquo;s really the best way to keep the night owls and the morning people in your home from disturbing each other. Additionally, the new entrance is also useful for emergency situations, such as a fire!</p>\n<h3 style=\"padding-left: 20px;\">Pro: Increase in property value</h3>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 20px;\">Since a walkout is both beautiful and practical, installing one in your basement will significantly increase the overall value of your home!</p>\n<h2>Cons of adding a walkout to your basement</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"The primary con of installing a walkout basement is the landscaping price\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/75/c40f6451600024d6a259ddf5e43a5f7f_2400x1800.jpg\" alt=\"Installing a walkout requires excavating part of your basement foundation, which can be pricey\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1800\" /><em>Installing a walk-out requires excavating part of your basement foundation, which can be pricey</em></p>\n<h3 style=\"padding-left: 20px;\">Con: Price</h3>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 20px;\">Installing a brand new shiny walkout in your basement is not easy, and anything not easy is bound to cost you money. Part of the basement foundation has to be excavated, and you also need to know how to get the permits that allow it. If you&rsquo;re thinking about adding a walkout to your existing home, or even a partially finished basement, expect it to be pretty pricey!</p>\n<h3 style=\"padding-left: 20px;\">Con: Feasibility</h3>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 20px;\">Another unfortunate downside about installing a new basement entrance point is that it&rsquo;s not always possible to pull off. Walkouts work best on properties where the land is already sloping down toward the back of the house. As we mentioned previously, your basement has to be excavated to make room for the new opening, and sometimes city codes, covenants, or even the topography of your land simply won\'t allow it&mdash;especially if your basement is entirely underground.&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Overall, basement walkouts can be both practical and lucrative for your home. But the installation will definitely not be cheap. So, provided you have the extra cash, the right land layout, and the proper permits, installing a walkout entrance to your basement is a fantastic design choice for homeowners.</p>',1,'',22,'2019-11-08 15:15:43'),(39,'Hottest Basement Design Trends—Top Four Designs of 2019','Wondering what basement design trends were the hottest in 2019? Here are the top for designs of this year, broken down into the pros & cons.','basement design trends, hottest design trends, basement design, basement design trends 2019, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, hot basement designs, basement ideas, open concept, walk out, home extension, guest rooms','hottest-basement-design-trendstop-four-designs-of-2019','Hottest Basement Design Trends—Top Four Designs of 2019','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/39/81ce542f86d603f4a6ee7b5bacd8754a','As we approach the new year, look back at some of the hottest design trends of 2019 broken down into the pros and cons.','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Home design trends, including basement design trends, are always in a constant state of flux. What was trendy last year can easily be considered obsolete by the next year&mdash;or it could stay popular for decades.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Basements are often disregarded when it comes to design, but they&rsquo;re no longer merely <a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-columbia-md-14-11\">a place for storage</a> or basic rooms. Aside from adding a lovely new look to your home, taking the time to design a beautiful basement can actually prove quite lucrative for the overall value of your home. But, with the market constantly changing, what trends should you be on the lookout for in 2019?</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We&rsquo;ve compiled a list of the four <strong>hottest basement design trends</strong> of 2019&mdash;each with a broken down pros and cons list. Many of these trends directly complement each other and work exceptionally well when combined together.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<h2>1. Open concept</h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While an <strong>open concept</strong> is a basement design trend that&rsquo;s not really unique to 2019, it&rsquo;s a rather timeless floor plan decision that&rsquo;s unlikely to die any time soon.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A vast majority of homes with two or more floors typically put far more consideration into the design of the main floor. Basements are traditionally left dark, relatively closed off, and divided into multiple secluded sections or rooms&mdash;often only accessible from a long, single hallway. An open concept design simply opens-up your basement space!</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"One of the hottest basement design trends of 2019 - open concept design\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/70/307824ef0f7ac276d0b59062d4c83c35_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Roomy, open concept design for a home in Rockville, MD\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em>Roomy, open concept design for a home in <a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-rockville-md-15-05\">Rockville, MD</a></em></span></p>\n<h3>Pros</h3>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Flexibility</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">:</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Open concept designs provide a greater range of flexibility. Instead of committing different rooms for particular purposes, you can instead have a large multipurpose room. To avoid a \"vacant\" feel with an open concept, you can strategically break the space up by using furniture, columns, or even something a bit more extravagant like a wet bar!&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Improved natural lighting</span></em><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">:</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> An open concept floor plan allows natural light to easily fill your basement space. If you&rsquo;re looking for a way to bring more natural light into your basement, an open concept is definitely the way to go.&nbsp;</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Cons&nbsp;</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em>Lack of privacy:</em> An open concept design is just that&mdash;open. The area doesn&rsquo;t allow for much privacy.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Overall, we recommend an open concept design if you&rsquo;re looking for a way to make your basement more comfortable and allow more natural lighting to flood the space. If you&rsquo;re planning on using rooms for multiple different purposes, or simply want some extra privacy, an open concept may not be the best choice.</span></p>\n<h2>2. Walkouts</h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Similar to an open concept floor plan, a walkout isn&rsquo;t necessarily a basement design trend unique to 2019&mdash;but they still remain just as popular. <strong>Walkout basements</strong> are an interesting design choice for a home. They offer distinct advantages, both practical and aesthetic, including adding an extra point of access, as well as adding a unique look to your home.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Walk out basements are both a practical and beautiful addition to a home\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/71/e30ac16e02cb235185e299b1ec5ab724_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"A walkout basement improves the look and value of your home\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em>A walkout basement improves the look and value of your home</em></span></p>\n<h3>Pros</h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Improved natural lighting:</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> A walkout allows natural light to pour into your basement space freely. A walkout is quite literally the best way to allow natural light into your basement&mdash;especially when combined with an open concept design.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Increased home value:</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Walkouts boost the overall sale value of your home.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Unique aesthetic:</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> They offer a unique look and feel to your home.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Extra accessibility:</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> A walkout basement provides a private entrance to the downstairs area. This is especially useful if the people living in the basement keep different hours than those living upstairs&mdash;they can come and go without disturbing anyone.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Cons</h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pricey installation:</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Installing a walkout basement is more expensive and complicated than the alternative. A significant section of your basement has to be excavated and then modified to suit the new design. However, it&rsquo;ll be less expensive (albeit only minimally) if your home is already built on a slope or hill.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>3. Home extension</h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A home extension, in this case, simply means following the same design choices for your basement as the ones you used on your home&rsquo;s main floor. This includes using nearly every aesthetic choice&mdash;the same trim, paint, flooring, etc.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A home extension isn\'t the best choice for everyone, though. Many people see their basement as a sort of separate entity from their home&mdash;an experimental area where you can let your imagination run wild. So, a home extension would undoubtedly put a damper on that!</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Home extension isn\'t the newest basement design trend, but it\'s still going strong in 2019\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/72/23fa0abe6bf3f9646ccb7fe14067d1f0_2400x1595.jpg\" alt=\"Wall colors and railing style remain the same as you transition into the basement\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1595\" /><em>Wall colors and railing style remain the same as you transition into the basement</em></p>\n<h3>Pros</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Seamless transition</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: The style of your main floor will flow quite nicely into your basement space, and vice versa.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Cons</h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Less design flexibility</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">:</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> While you&rsquo;ll still be able to choose what to do with the rooms and general space, your design options will be limited.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4. Guest Rooms</h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Guest rooms are perhaps the most popular basement design trend in 2019. <strong>Guest rooms</strong> or &ldquo;suites&rdquo; are a perfect design choice if you have family or guests or come over often or stay for extended visits.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In addition to having rooms that guests and family can use, guest rooms are also a great way to make some extra cash. Renting out your guest rooms yourself or using a third-party company like Airbnb can help pad the mortgage payment!</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Though the concept itself is old, a guest room is one of the hottest new basement design trends\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/73/366c090a1faf22cbe4ccf6a61ac48fee_2400x1600.jpg\" alt=\"Example of a stylish basement guest room in Mount Airy, MD\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" /><em>Example of a stylish basement guest room in <a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-mount-airy-md-15-06\">Mount Airy, MD</a></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><br /></em></span></p>\n<h3>Pros</h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Guest comfort</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: Guests and family will always be happy to stay with you when visiting. They won&rsquo;t be in a cramped room or have to pay for a hotel&mdash;you&rsquo;ll have a comfortable and private room for them to use!</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Passive income</span></em><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">:</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> You can rent out your guest suites to long-term tenants or short-term ones with Airbnb.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Cons</h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Space limitations</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: Designating rooms for guests limits their capability, and you don&rsquo;t want to constantly move stuff around if you plan to try and use the room for multiple purposes.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Can be pricey</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: This is more of a neutral aspect rather than a con. How much extra money it will cost you to design guest quarters in your basement really depends on your budget and vision. For example, if you want each room to have access to a private bath, it&rsquo;ll cost you quite a bit more than having guests use a shared bathroom.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Keep up with the latest design trends with the best basement remodeling blog around</h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you&rsquo;re struggling to decide which basement <strong>design trends</strong> to use this year, a professional service may be your best option.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At BasementRemodeling.com, we&rsquo;re constantly aware of the ever-changing housing environment. We stay up to date on the latest and greatest trend designs. We&rsquo;ll help you choose what designs would best suit your needs! With experts in 3D modeling and design, you can narrow down a design without actually having to do any work!</span></p>',1,'',23,'2019-10-27 15:15:58'),(40,'3 Reasons to Use Basement 3D Modeling Software','Looking for an easy way to visualize a basement design without having to commit to a specific layout? Use basement 3D modeling software!','Basement 3D modeling, basement 3D models, basement design, basement finishing, basement remodeling, basement 3d modeling software, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, home design, design, 3d models, basementremodeling.com','3-reasons-to-use-basement-3d-modeling-software','3 Reasons to Use Basement 3D Modeling Software','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/40/029e0554fd8503ea2955d112ef530343','Designing a new home is a difficult process, but using 3D modeling software makes it much easier! In today\'s basement blog post, we outline three reasons why you should use basement 3d modeling before getting starting on your next project.','<div class=\"html\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Architectural design is complicated, especially when it comes to effectively <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/hottest-basement-design-trendstop-four-designs-of-2019\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">designing a basement</a>. If you&rsquo;ve ever gone through the design or home-building process, you know that what you plan and what actually happens tend to be a little different. The good news is that technology has come a long way, and in 2019 we don&rsquo;t simply have to use traditional 2D house-plans anymore&mdash;we have access to highly sophisticated and advanced software for <strong>basement&nbsp;3D modeling</strong>!</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Not only does 3D modeling software help mitigate the difficulty of designing a layout, but it\'ll also save you countless hours of trial-and-error. There&rsquo;s a lot that goes into design decisions that you don&rsquo;t quite realize until you try it yourself. Colors, fixtures, angles, materials, pricing&mdash;these all play a vital role in the process.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">So, whether you&rsquo;re planning on remodeling, finishing, or just want to poke around at ideas for your basement, using 3D modeling software is your best, easiest, and cheapest starting point. We&rsquo;ve narrowed down three distinct reasons you should use basement 3D modeling software before you get started on your next project.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<h2><strong>1. 3D modeling puts things in perspective</strong></h2>\n<p>Unless you&rsquo;re an artist, architect, or generally design-savvy, it can be extremely hard to convey a basement design you&rsquo;re visualizing in your mind. Even if you can see it pretty clearly, how do you describe it to someone else without some of the details being &ldquo;lost in translation?&rdquo; With 3D modeling software, it&rsquo;s much easier to translate what you&rsquo;re picturing onto paper.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">3D modeling software provides access to hundreds of different options and design choices&mdash;all neatly organized and easily accessible. Your designs are limited solely by your imagination and creativity (and perhaps your willingness to dish out some cash). Basement 3D models will bring your ideas to life. Aside from actually physically being there, it&rsquo;s one of the best ways to visualize your basement design.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"Basement 3d modeling software brings design ideas to life\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/142/3d-model-white-kitchen-with-wetbar_1200x675.jpg\" alt=\"Basement kitchen nook designed entirely with 3D modeling software\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" /><br /><em>Basement kitchen nook designed entirely with 3D modeling software</em></p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>2. You save on energy costs</strong></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Most house-plans these days are designed specifically with energy efficiency in mind. But basements in new houses notoriously go unfinished, and that can have a significant impact on your energy savings.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Keeping your basement energy efficient is all about design choices. Some rather simple aspects of your design directly affect your year-round energy savings. For instance, strategically placing more windows on the side of your home facing the sun during the winter months will reduce your heating costs. It\'ll also provide more light to your basement!</span></p>\n<h2><strong>3. Flexibility</strong></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Arguably the finest feature of 3D modeling software and most computer software is flexibility. Having a flexible 3D plan to work with allows for meticulous design choices&mdash;without fear of having to replace anything later.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Don&rsquo;t like the way that furniture, fixture, or wall looks? Simply remove it! Want to see how a room would look in different colors? Change it! Floors can be modified to show carpet, tile, hardwood, and more. Walls can be painted with different colors and textures. You can even experiment with tiny details such as fixtures and furniture. With a comprehensive drag-and-drop interface, you have endless possible combinations and aesthetic choices.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">After you&rsquo;re satisfied with a particular design, you can simply print it out or save your 3D design as a traditional 2D house plan. This plan will look precisely the same as if someone did it by hand! You can then use the floor plan for practical reasons, such as adhering to health and safety practices, ensuring you&rsquo;re following proper building codes, and for sharing it with your contractor.</span></p>\n<h2><strong>Bring your basement design to life with professional 3D modeling</strong></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Once you dig a little deeper into your 3D modeling software, you&rsquo;ll realize you can only go so far. While the free software does offer some pretty neat features, it&rsquo;s highly limited. Even the top-tier software will be limited unless you know how to design 3D models yourself. Having a seasoned professional work with you on the design makes things much easier in the long run. If you have a general idea of what you want, and you want to make it happen, it&rsquo;s time to call a professional.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img title=\"basement 3d models help maximize your square footage space\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/69/f087189bf9763d01efdcfe6569eee12d_1280x801.jpg\" alt=\"3D modeled, top-down view of an elegant basement design that maximizes floor space usage\" width=\"1280\" height=\"801\" /><br /><em>3D modeled, top-down view of an elegant basement design that maximizes floor space usage</em></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At BasementRemodeling.com, we&rsquo;re experts in every aspect of 3D modeling and design. Simply providing a description to our team is enough to map out what you\'re looking for accurately; and if it\'s not quite right, we\'ll change it until it is! Brilliant basement 3D modeling designs of your space are a part of our service. Not only do we walk you through your plan, but we\'ll also give you a free estimate on how much it&rsquo;ll cost!</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Contact us today for a free quote and in-house consultation!</span></p>\n</div>',1,'',24,'2019-10-25 15:16:14'),(41,'4 Minimalist Design Ideas for Your Luxury Basement Remodel (With Pictures)','Use these basement design ideas and pictures to tastefully incorporate minimalism into your next luxury basement renovation.','basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement remodeling ideas, luxury basements, luxury basement remodeling, basement remodeling Maryland, basement remodeling Virginia, basement remodeling Washington DC, basement design, basement blog','4-minimalist-design-ideas-for-your-luxury-basement-remodel-with-pictures','4 Minimalist Design Ideas for Your Luxury Basement Remodel (With Pictures)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/41/a888b8859d531d346e5b5f4718b3bdc7','Use these basement design ideas and pictures to tastefully incorporate minimalism into your next luxury basement renovation.','<p><strong>4 Minimalist Design Ideas for Your Luxury Basement Remodel (With Pictures)</strong></p>\n<p>Minimalism is taking over basement remodeling in 2019. A basement with a minimalist touch will still look warm and cozy when done properly. Use these basement design ideas and pictures to tastefully incorporate minimalism into your next luxury basement renovation. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Minimalist Furniture</strong></p>\n<p>Minimalism does not mean getting rid of all of the furniture. In fact, oversized furniture with soft and round edges is the ideal minimalist basement design. Chairs and couches with an angled pitch are in vogue; straight-back furniture, not so much. Coffee tables and basement entertaintment centers are still in-style, though they are condensed and no longer the centerpiece of the room. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/64/5bcbb9a94ed94d444bf8c17c331e4b27_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>Angled minimalist furniture with soft, round edges in a Columbia, MD basement remodel. The basement entertainment center has been condensed into a two-level miniature table. </em></p>\n<p><strong>Natural Colors</strong></p>\n<p>Minimalism emphasizes texture over color. A natural palette consisting primarily of white, beige and brown will make subtle textural design choices more noticeable from up-close and at a distance. LVT flooring can show off earthy minimalist tones; rugs will add texture.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/65/bb314a3595348154470ff8abb6967689_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /> <em>A multi-textured rug on LVT flooring with rounded furniture and a small off-centered coffee table creates the minimalist look for a basement refinishing in Arlington, VA.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Neutral Accessories</strong></p>\n<p>A &ldquo;minimalist accessory&rdquo; is not an oxymoron in basement remodeling terminology. Pillows, blankets and throws add texture and are acceptable. For the ultimate minimalist look, layer the room with muted neutral-colored accessories spread far apart.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/66/a995240127c4dc354147c7c25a0bbcba_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>Sparse, neutral-colored accessories add minimalist warmth and textures to a basement remodel in West Friendship, Maryland.</em></p>\n<p><strong>How to Avoid Monotony</strong></p>\n<p>One of the biggest challenges of embracing minimalism is keeping the area cheerful. Tasteful recessed lighting can help properly angle shadows and make the area look tidy instead of drab. Finally, don&rsquo;t be afraid to break up the room with an accent wall as long as it looks natural.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/67/28091fa9ef2027e0974d8d40ea200bd1_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>An unpainted brick accent wall against a round black banister adds the perfect minimalist finish to this Washington DC rebuild.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Luxury Basement Remodeling with BasementRemodeling.com</strong></p>\n<p>As a leading basement contractor in business since 2006, BasementRemodeling.com understands the importance of keeping up with modern trends and designs each and every year. Trust Basement Masters with your luxury basement remodel or finishing project in Maryland, Washington DC and Virginia. Contact us today to get an online quote and schedule an in-house consultation. &nbsp;</p>',1,'',25,'2019-04-14 15:17:21'),(42,'Luxury Basement Remodeling in Virginia (4 Examples)','From Arlington to Springfield, here are our latest basement remodeling and finishing projects in VA.','basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement remodeling Arlington VA, basement finishing Arlington VA, basement remodeling Fairfax VA basement finishing Fairfax VA, basement remodeling Lorton VA, basement finishing Lorton VA, basement remodeling Springfield VA, basement finishing Springfield VA, basement remodeling Annandale, basement finishing Annandale, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement blog','luxury-basement-remodeling-in-virginia-4-examples','Luxury Basement Remodeling in Virginia (4 Examples)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/42/945703a71084e19beb3313e664ca13e4','Here are our latest basement remodeling and finishing projects in Arlington, Burke, and Springfield, VA!','<p>Luxury basement remodeling in Virginia with Basement Masters adds style, value and livability to an unfinished basement. Remodeling and finishing luxury basements since 2006 is what makes Basement Masters the best basement remodeling contractor throughout Maryland, DC and Virginia.</p>\n<p>From Arlington to Springfield, here are our latest basement remodeling and finishing projects in VA.</p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\"><br /><strong>Arlington, VA Basement Remodeling #1</strong><br /><br /><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/60/e11a04554cb917255592a0a74008035d_624x416.png\" alt=\"A tasteful Arlington, VA basement remodel with LVT flooring, contemporary wall paneling and LED lights.\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /></h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><em>A tasteful Arlington, VA basement remodel with LVT flooring, contemporary wall paneling and LED lights.</em></p>\n<p><em><em><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-arlington-va-18-12\">View the full photo gallery and description.</a></em></em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Arlington, VA Basement Remodeling #2</strong></h2>\n<p><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/61/bad9eae7990f64daf9cf70122a7376ad_624x416.png\" alt=\"A second basement remodel in Arlington, VA contains a kitchen-like wet bar, laundry area (not shown) and more.\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><em>A second basement remodel in Arlington, VA contains a kitchen-like wet bar, laundry area (not shown) and more.</em></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><em><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-arlington-va-17-08\">View the full photo gallery and description.</a></em></p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Burke, VA Remodeling Project</strong></h2>\n<p><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/62/89a1e9e3381be4bded37cafb14f084b5_624x416.png\" alt=\"A neutral palette adds a welcoming family room to this Burke, VA basement remodel.\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><em>A neutral palette adds a welcoming family room to this Burke, VA basement remodel.</em></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><em><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-burke-va-17-11\">View the full photo gallery and description.</a></em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Springfield, VA Basement Finishing Project<br /></strong></h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/63/10b642a86c2d071cab570b1822311e1e_624x416.png\" alt=\"An open and airy Springfield, VA basement remodel neatly fits an entertainment center &amp; wet bar.\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /></p>\n<p><em>An open and airy Springfield, VA basement remodel neatly fits an entertainment center &amp; wet bar.</em></p>\n<p><em><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-springfield-va-17-11\">View the full photo gallery and description.</a></em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3><strong>Contact BasementRemodeling.com in Virginia for Expert Services!</strong></h3>\n<p>BRC has additional basement remodeling and finishing experience in these VA locales:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-alexandria-va-12-06\">Alexandria</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-annandale-virginia\">Annandale</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-fairfax-va-11-11\">Fairfax</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-lorton-va-11-11\">Lorton</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/\">and much more!</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Contact BasementRemodeling.com for an <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">online quote</a> and schedule an in-home consultation.</p>',5,'',26,'2019-04-08 15:17:38'),(43,'Do Houses in Virginia Have Basements?','Wondering if homes in Virginia have basements, or if they\'re all one floor? Here\'s what you need to know.','Do houses in Virginia have basements, Virginia basements, VA basement remodeling, basement remodeling Fairfax VA, basement remodeling Vienna VA, basement remodeling Arlington VA, basement remodeling Alexandria VA, basement remodeling, basement remodeling contractor, basement finshing, basement rennovation, basement remodel, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement remodeling blog, best basement blog','do-houses-in-virginia-have-basements','Do Houses in Virginia Have Basements?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/43/db925b025f9353af07b0918bc61d9e81','When is basement remodeling in Virginia possible?','<div class=\"h1\"><strong>Do Houses in Virginia Have Basements?</strong></div>\n<p>Virginia houses do have basements &ndash; but not all throughout the state. Virginia basements are the most popular in Northern Virginia. Remodeling a basement in Virginia always depends on two conditions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Frost line</li>\n<li>Soil type</li>\n</ul>\n<p>When the ground freezes during winter, the pressure can be enough to push in the very foundation of a building. It can even lift a building off of its foundation if enough frost gathers underneath the floor. This is not a problem, however, when the basement is constructed beneath the frost line because the soil does not freeze.</p>\n<p>A frost line close to the surface makes the space too shallow for a basement. This usually happens in states farther south than Virginia (which is why most states in the South do not have basements).</p>\n<p>Soil type is usually the deciding factor with Virginia basements. Expansive subsoils like clay are very common in Virginia, which is not good for basements because changes in moisture can cause structural damage to the foundation. The soil puts pressure on the foundation walls when it becomes saturated, and when the soil is dry, it leaves gaps and creates instability.</p>\n<p>Ideally, bedrock is the best type of soil for Virginia basements. The rock and other hardened materials that consist of bedrock are below the frostline and will not easily expand or otherwise shift in accordance to changes in moisture. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<h2><strong>Northern Virginia Basement Remodeling</strong></h2>\n<p>Northern Virginia often has the correct soil composition and frost line for basement remodeling, renovation and finishing. The following areas are the most popular for Virginia basement remodels:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-alexandria-va-12-06\">Alexandria, VA</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-arlington-va-14-02\">Arlington, VA</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-fairfax-virginia-2\">Fairfax, VA</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-vienna-va-14-04\">Vienna, VA</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>With the right contractor, Virginia basements can be stylish, functional, and a unique selling point when the time comes. If you need basement remodeling in Northern Virginia, BasementRemodeling.com can add, remodel or renovate a basement for your luxury home or business. Be sure to contact&nbsp;<a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">BasementRemodeling.com</a> today for an online quote and an in-home consultation.</p>',1,'',27,'2019-02-28 15:17:51'),(44,'How to Tell if Your Basement Remodeling Contractor Has Done a Good Job','Many blogs cover questions to ask before hiring a basement remodeling contractor, but how can you tell if they did a good job after they\'re finished?','Basement remodeling contractor, how to, Maryland Basement finishing contractors, Maryland Basement contractors DC basement finishing contractors, Basement remodeling contractors, Basement finishing contractors, Basement remodeling companies, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement remodeling blog','how-to-tell-if-your-basement-remodeling-contractor-has-done-a-good-job','How to Tell if Your Basement Remodeling Contractor Has Done a Good Job','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/44/4b5fb7f5d7b1fcbe405ee034298f00fb','Many blogs focus on questions to ask before hiring a basement contractor, but what about questions to ask after the basement remodeling project has been finished?','<p><strong>How to Tell if Your Basement Remodeling Contractor Has Done a Good Job</strong></p>\n<p>Many blogs focus on <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/10-questions-to-ask-before-hiring-a-basement-contractor\">questions to askbeforehiring a basement contractor</a>, but what about questions to ask <em>after</em> the basement remodeling project has been finished? You should always follow up on the basement remodeling contractor&rsquo;s work by consulting with a(n):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Architect</li>\n<li>Engineer</li>\n<li>Home inspector (the most common choice)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Remember: the majority of basement remodeling companies are honest, but it is up to you to make sure they have installed everything exactly as outlined. Just because the basement remodeling project passed state and county inspections does not necessarily guarantee that corners were not cut somewhere.</p>\n<h2><strong>What a Professional Inspector Looks for After a Basement Remodeling Project</strong></h2>\n<p>A professional architect, engineer or home inspector will be able to detect moisture in the basement that can cause mold and structural damage. They must doublecheck to make sure groundwater does not significantly flow towards the home (by inspecting the gutters and other <a href=\"https://www.epa.gov/sites/production/files/2014-08/documents/moisture-control.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">moisture control systems</a>).</p>\n<p>They should inspect each item on the contract to ensure that everything has been installed properly using the correct materials. For example, inspectors will be able to tell you what kind of wiring was used and if it is the correct gauge (thickness) that you agreed upon with the contractor.</p>\n<p>Don&rsquo;t be afraid to ask them questions about any newly-installed home appliances (washers and dryers, sinks, etc.) and systems (water heaters, HVAC units) to make sure their information matches what you&rsquo;ve been told by your basement contractor. They can even demonstrate various features you may not have been made aware of.</p>\n<h2><strong>What You Can Check on Your Own</strong></h2>\n<p>A simple visual inspection can be enough to determine the quality of craftmanship in certain respects. Basement tiling, for example, should line up at a 90-degree angle without any sections jutting out or sinking. The grout lines should be even and thin to create a smooth overall appearance.</p>\n<p>The quality of basement painting can be determined by feeling an area for rough patches, drip marks and other similar textural errors. The lines denoting the wall and ceiling should be straight and with an even distribution of paint.</p>\n<p>For basement trimming, check for straightness and symmetry. Make sure the corners are well-put together around the crown molding as well as any door and window casings. There should be nail holes and no noticeable seams. Everything must be level.</p>\n<p>The basement doors and custom cabinets should not stick (a sign that foundation problems have not been corrected). The basement countertops should have no gaps that are filled with caulk (a sign of mismeasurement).</p>\n<p>Basement LED lighting should be evenly spaced and not flickering or flashing in any way. Dimmers should work smoothly. If they flicker or do not dim correctly it means the LED bulb and dimmer are incompatible or there is a wiring problem.</p>\n<h2><strong>BasementRemodeling.com Does Basement Remodeling the Right Way</strong></h2>\n<p>Whether you are looking for basement remodeling contractors in Maryland, DC, or Virginia, Basement Masters stands apart from other basement remodeling companies with an exceptional level of quality, experience and enthusiasm. Contact Basement Masters today for your next basement remodeling or finishing project. &nbsp;</p>',4,'',28,'2019-02-05 15:18:57'),(45,'Luxury Basement Remodeling in Bethesda, MD','Looking for a commercial or luxury home basement remodel in Bethesda, MD? Consider BasementRemodeling.com!','basement remodeling Bethesda MD, basement finishing Bethesda MD, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement remodeling contractor, basement remodeling Maryland, basement remodeling contractor Maryland','luxury-basement-remodeling-in-bethesda-md','Luxury Basement Remodeling in Bethesda, MD','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/45/2b9a1855ac2ff0215288a0d690c1acc7','Looking for a commercial or luxury home basement remodel in Bethesda, MD?','<h2><strong>Luxury Basement Remodeling in Bethesda, MD</strong></h2>\n<p>Looking for a commercial or luxury home <a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-bethesda2-md\">basement remodel in Bethesda, MD</a>? Call the leading Maryland basement remodeling contractor at BasementRemodeling.com. With well over a decade of luxury basement remodeling and finishing experience throughout Maryland, Basement Masters will give you a professional quote for a basement remodel in Bethesda.</p>\n<p>Contact BasementRemodeling.com for your next commercial or luxury home basement remodel in Bethesda. You will love your finished basement for years to come!</p>\n<h2><strong>Our Remodeling Mission</strong></h2>\n<p>For basement remodeling and finishing in Bethesda&mdash;and the rest of Maryland&mdash;we do it best. Anything is possible with our custom basement remodels:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Family rooms / kids rooms</li>\n<li>Wet bars</li>\n<li>Home offices</li>\n<li>Gyms</li>\n<li>Home theaters</li>\n<li>Gamer rooms</li>\n<li>Wine cellars</li>\n<li>Basement walk-ins</li>\n<li>Basement dig-outs</li>\n<li>Much more</li>\n</ul>\n<p>BasementRemodeling.comis a fully-licensed architectural basement remodeling company specializing in basement remodels in Bethesda. We design, remodel, finish, renovate and furnish basement remodels using the latest basement remodeling methods and the most stylish custom designs. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>We focus solely on basement remodeling and finishing. Our extensive waterproofing, finishing, renovating and remodeling experience is what makes us the true basement masters.</p>\n<h2><strong>Contact BasementRemodeling.com Today!</strong></h2>\n<p><a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact BasementRemodeling.com</a> for a free basement remodeling quote in Bethesda, MD.</p>',5,'',29,'2019-01-07 15:19:13'),(46,'Get a Basement Remodel in Annapolis, MD','Get a basement remodel in Annapolis, MD that includes all of the commercial or residential features you need.','Maryland basement remodeling, Maryland basement finishing, basement remodeling companies Maryland, Maryland basement contractor, basement remodel, basement remodel Annapolis MD','get-a-basement-remodel-in-annapolis-md','Get a Basement Remodel in Annapolis, MD','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/46/ea966cc80e35ea4ae92a8a873b830974','Get a Basement Remodel in Annapolis, MD that includes all of the residential or comercial features you need.','<p><strong>Get a Basement Remodel in Annapolis, MD</strong></p>\n<p>If you need a commercial or luxury home <a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-annapolis-13-08\">basement remodel in Annapolis, MD</a>, BasementRemodeling.com is the Maryland basement remodeling contractor to call. As one of the most highly-commemorated basement remodeling and finishing companies in the state of Maryland, we\'ll will give you a professional quote for a basement Remodel in Annapolis quickly.</p>\n<p>Contact Basement Masters in Maryland for your next commercial or luxury home basement remodel in Annapolis. We keep our clients completely satisfied for years to come.</p>\n<p><strong>Our Annapolis, MD Basement Remodel Promise</strong></p>\n<p>For basement remodeling and finishing in Annapolis, there is no better Maryland basement remodeling contractor than BasementRemodeling.com. Anything is possible with our custom basement remodels:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Family rooms / kids rooms</li>\n<li>Wet bars</li>\n<li>Home offices</li>\n<li>Gyms</li>\n<li>Home theaters</li>\n<li>Gamer rooms</li>\n<li>Wine cellars</li>\n<li>Basement walk-ins</li>\n<li>Basement dig-outs</li>\n<li>Much more</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We\'re a fully-licensed architectural basement remodeling company specializing in basement remodels throughout Annapolis and the rest Maryland. We design, remodel and fully furnish basement remodels using specialized in-house staff and a close-knit team of subcontractors whom we have known since the beginning in 2006. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>We specialize in full custom basement remodeling only. Other contractors may work on the entire building, but we choose to focus on what we know best: the basement. Waterproofing, finishing, renovating and remodeling expertise is what makes us the true masters of the basement.</p>\n<p><strong>Contact BasementRemodeling.com in Maryland</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact BasementRemodeling.com</a> for a free Annapolis basement remodeling quote!</p>',5,'',30,'2018-12-25 15:19:27'),(47,'3 Style Tips for Finished Basements','A finished basement is only as great as its style! Here are three simple style tips to make your basement shine!','finished basements, finished basement ideas, finish basements, finish basement ideas, basement finish, ideas for finishing a basement, finish basement, basement remodel, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement remodeling contractor, basement remodeling Maryland, basement remodeling Virginia, basement remodeling Washington DC, basementremodeling.com, basement blog, best basement ideas, best basement blog','3-style-tips-for-finished-basements','3 Style Tips for Finished Basements','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/47/a31dba2d2a289b4a0f22404624ef2421','Any finished basement can benefit from these three easy-to-follow style tips.','<p>As the leading basement remodeling contractor in Maryland, Virginia and Washington DC, BasementRemodeling.com understands what most people are looking for in a finished basement. Here are 4 style tips we always include in all of our basement remodeling projects!</p>\n<h2>Flooring That&rsquo;s Comfortable</h2>\n<p>A cold concrete basement floor is the last thing you want to cross in the middle of the night with no shoes. Basement flooring should be as comfortable as the rest of the home, which is why we offer many&nbsp;<a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/flooring/\">basement flooring options</a>.</p>\n<h2>Basement Paint Options</h2>\n<p>Basements have limited natural light, which makes paint appear a few shades darker than it would upstairs. Use lighter paint colors in rooms with artificial <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/lighting/\">basement light options</a>. You may be able to get away with darker tones in rooms that have natural light (from <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/egress-windows/\">egress windows</a> or a <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/walk-outs/\">walk-out entrance</a>).</p>\n<h2>Large Basement Furnishings</h2>\n<p>A finished basement has a lot of room for large furniture and other furnishings that would look too big in a smaller room. Sectional furniture and center tables are two popular basement furnishings. Modular furniture is a safe bet for matching the various spatial arrangements of a finished basement. Choosing furniture without arms will make the room look less crowded.</p>\n<h2>Want More Finished Basement Design Tips?</h2>\n<p>BasementRemodeling.com is ready to provide a Maryland, Virginia or Washington DC basement remodel full of style and functionality. All of our basement remodeling and basement finishing projects are furnished using an in-house basement design team. Contact us online to schedule a free consultation and estimate.</p>',1,'',31,'2018-12-09 15:19:49'),(48,'How to Get the Best Basement Lighting for Each Room','A guide for getting the best basement lighting results for each room of your next remodel.','basement lighting options, led lighting options, basement lighting ideas, basement remodeling lighting, basement remodeling, basement remodeling Maryland, basement remodeling Washington DC, basement remodeling Virginia, basement finishing, basement finishing Maryland, basement finishing Washington DC, basement finishing Virginia, basement remodeling contractors, basement remodel, basement blog','how-to-get-the-best-basement-lighting-for-each-room','How to Get the Best Basement Lighting for Each Room','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/48/5ab7c59e551f32925e09b48682ff6657','A guide for getting the best basement lighting results for each room of your next remodel.','<h2><strong>How to Get the Best Basement Lighting for Each Room</strong></h2>\n<p>The best basement lighting accentuates all of your basement decorating ideas and spaces. Basement lighting options vary from room to room and different <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/lighting/\">basement lighting ideas</a> can even be used in place of physical walls to create fun spaces.</p>\n<p>So, whether you have a basement remodel with half-walls, full walls or a wide-open space with no walls at all, you (and the basement remodeling contractors) still need to find the best basement lighting for each room . . .</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Kids basement playroom &ndash; Soft white bulbs evenly spaced apart will avoid creating dramatic shadows that can scary kids. Basement playrooms with recessed LED lighting will create the right mood for your children&rsquo;s basement playroom.</li>\n<li>Spare basement bedroom &ndash; Soft white LED basement lighting options, combined with eye-level furnishings such as lamps, enhances the room with intimacy.</li>\n<li>Full basement bathroom &ndash; Bright ceiling or recessed lighting options provide general ambiance,. The vanity area should have additional lighting options above the mirror or on both sides. The shower and tub area should be lit as well. Wall-mounted cabinets can be fitted with strip lighting.</li>\n<li>Kitchen-like wet bars &ndash; Soft white LED lightbulbs on a dimmer switch will allow you to adjust the atmosphere as needed. Areas for food preparation should ideally have brighter lights than counters meant for lounging, which can use softer recessed LED lighting.</li>\n<li>Basement family room &ndash; Eye-level lighting options (lamps, etc.) should combine with recessed lighting around artwork and fireplaces.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><strong>Basement Wall Colors and Lighting Options</strong></h3>\n<p>Basement remodeling generally involves a brighter color scheme than the rest of your home due to the lack of natural light. Brighter lightbulbs highlight the contrast between colors for a more dramatic effect, so if you use dark wall colors in combination with bright lights, you are going to get a lot of shadows (this is generally not wanted, but can be used to create a sophisticated look in certain situations).</p>\n<h3><strong>Get the Best Lighting Options at BasementRemodeling.com</strong></h3>\n<p>For all basement remodeling and finishing projects in Maryland, Virginia and Washington DC, contact <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">BasementRemodeling.com online</a> or call <strong>301-798-4444</strong>. Get a free quote and more today!</p>',1,'',32,'2018-11-25 15:20:01'),(49,'Basement Space Planning Guide','The ultimate basement space planning guide for residents in Maryland, DC, and Virginia basements.','basement space, basement space planning, basement space planning guide, Maryland basement remodeling, Maryland basement finishing, Maryland basement contractors, Washington DC basement contractors, Washington DC basement remodeling, Virginia basements, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement blog, basement blog ideas','basement-space-planning-guide','Basement Space Planning Guide','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/49/b6658eeb935948a1386f39b6c3e65839','A basement space planning guide for Maryland, Washington DC and Virginia basements.','<p>Basement contractors can remodel a basement in many different ways, but it always helps to do some <strong>basement space planning</strong> on your own first. In fact, the more basement space planning you do, the more easily you&rsquo;ll be able to communicate ideas with your basement contractor.</p>\n<h2>What to Consider Before Finishing or Remodeling a Basement</h2>\n<p>Basement finishing and remodeling turns a basement into a true extension of your home. Here are three main considerations to work into your plans:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Basement space &ndash; Make sure you are able to realistically fit all of your <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/\">basement ideas</a> into your basement layout plan. Multipurpose rooms generally require a lot of space and an open layout.</li>\n<li>Moisture &ndash; Be prepared to waterproof a basement to keep water from damaging your design.</li>\n<li>Utility Systems &ndash; Basement contractors can remodel a space into whatever you desire; however, they may have to move ductwork, electrical wiring, plumbing and even entire gas lines to do so. Keeping your mechanical hookups the same will save on basement remodeling costs.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Common Basement Remodeling &amp; Finishing Problems</h2>\n<p>As the leading basement contractors in Maryland, Virginia and DC, we often see these problems while remodeling and finishing basements. Fortunately, we a basement remodeling company that knows how to solve them!</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Moisture &ndash; All water leaks must be addressed before any basement remodeling or finishing can begin. Even if there are no leaks, water can still get into the basement through humidity.\n<ul>\n<li>BasementRemodeling.com can solve this with an appropriate <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/waterproofing/\">basement waterproofing system</a>.<br /><br /></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Utility layout &ndash; Mechanical systems such as furnaces and hot water heaters can be expensive to remove and reinstall. Knowing the <a href=\"https://www.energyvanguard.com/service-category/hvac-load-calculations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">load calculation</a> of your current basement layout will help basement contractors immensely.\n<ul>\n<li>We have the experience needed to pick out the appropriate HVAC system for your basement.</li>\n<li>We try to design around existing mechanical systems whenever possible.<br /><br /></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Columns &ndash; Basement columns are often needed for support.\n<ul>\n<li>We can add decorative columns or remove a support column in favor of other load-bearing solutions that look nicer.<br /><br /></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Ductwork &ndash; Leaving exposed ductwork does not look attractive and can even sometimes be a low-hanging hazard.\n<ul>\n<li>BasementRemodeling.com can cover your ductwork with a variety of stunning <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/ceilings/\">ceiling options</a>.<br /><br /></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Low ceilings &ndash; Low-hanging ceilings can sometimes be resolved with tray ceilings and other similar designs. If all else fails, digging out a basement to lower the floor is always an option.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>BasementRemodeling.com: Basement Space Planning and Remodeling Experts</h2>\n<p>BasementRemodeling.com has remodeled hundreds of basements across Maryland, Washington DC, and Virginia. Contact us today for your free basement space planning estimate. We are the best Maryland-based basement contractors, so call today! &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',4,'',33,'2018-11-18 15:21:43'),(50,'Basement Remodeling & Finishing Company for Baltimore MD','The city of Baltimore knows to call BasementRemodeling.com for superior basement finishing and remodeling in Maryland.','Baltimore MD basement remodeling, Baltimore MD basement finishing, basement remodeling company, basement finishing company, basement remodeling company MD, basement finishing company MD, basement remodeling contractor, basement finishing contractor, basement remodeling contractor Maryland, basement remodeling contractor Baltimore, basement blog','basement-remodeling--finishing-company-for-baltimore-md','Basement Remodeling & Finishing Company for Baltimore MD','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/50/c5142a7bfd45d439864f23217c6ae4d3','The city of Baltimore knows to call BasementRemodeling.com for superior basement finishing and remodeling in Maryland.','<h2><strong>Basement Finishing Company for Baltimore MD</strong></h2>\n<p>Remodeling your basement adds value and functionality to your home, but only BasementRemodeling.com has the reliable architectural solutions you&rsquo;ll need for the best basement experience possible. The city of Baltimore knows to call us for superior basement finishing and remodeling in Maryland.</p>\n<h2><strong>The Best Basement Remodeling Company in Baltimore</strong></h2>\n<p>Using a quality Maryland basement contractor will provide you with a long-lasting home improvement that can increase the resale value of a property. As the best basement contractor in Maryland, BasementRemodeling.com believes in providing the highest-quality remodeling experience at a fair cost.</p>\n<p>From Maryland basement designing to finishing and remodeling, we are fully-licensed and insured &ndash; meaning we have what it takes to turn your unfinished basement or crawlspace into a beautiful addition to your home.</p>\n<h2><strong>Baltimore Basement Remodeling Ideas</strong></h2>\n<p>Complete your Baltimore basement with a:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/media-rooms/home-theaters/\">Basement home theater</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/wet-bars/\">Basement wet bar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/wet-bars/kitchen-like/\">Basement kitchenlike area</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/bathrooms/\">Basement bathroom</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Contact BasementRemodeling.com today for a free estimate!</p>',5,'',34,'2018-10-28 15:21:57'),(51,'Basement Finishing Company in Maryland  ','At BasementRemodeling.com, we provide a wide variety of basement finishing and remodeling services for Maryland!','basement finishing, basement remodeling, basement finishing contractor, basement remodeling contractor, basement remodeling maryland, basement finishing maryland, basement finishing company, basement remodeling company, basement remodeling company maryland, basement finishing company maryland, basement finishing md, basement remodeling md, basement contractor md','basement-finishing-company-in-maryland--','Basement Finishing Company in Maryland  ','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/51/95f6a58161321de8e10633258fffcc3a','At BasementRemodeling.com, we provide a variety of finishing and remodeling services for basements across Maryland!','<h2><strong>Basement Finishing &amp; Remodeling Company in Maryland</strong></h2>\n<p>There are plenty of ways to remodel or finish your Maryland basement so that you have an enhanced living space for you and your family. An experienced company will have the best techniques for transforming an unfinished basement into a completely remodeled space. At BasementRemodeling.com, we provide a multitude of finishing and remodeling services to Maryland residents!</p>\n<h2><strong>Experienced &amp; Fully-Licensed Basement Contractor</strong></h2>\n<p>Basement Masters has established lifelong working relationships with its basement contractors, training them in the latest basement remodeling and finishing techniques all the while. Over the years, we have completed hundreds of basement remodeling and finishing projects in Maryland, continuously obtaining awards from Houzz, Home Advisor and Angie&rsquo;s List.</p>\n<p>You can trust with your basement finishing project because BasementRemodeling.com has always been a fully-licensed, bonded, and insured company with the knowledge, skills, and resources needed to help you through every step of the way.</p>\n<p>We can custom design any basement remodel to fit your needs, including the successful installation of:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/wet-bars/\">Basement Wet Bars</a>:&nbsp;Perfect for entertaining guests during holidays, sporting events, or simply &ldquo;just because&rdquo;.</li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/family-rooms/\">Basement Family Room</a>:&nbsp;Spend time playing with your children and enjoying the company of family.</li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/wet-bars/kitchen-like/\">Basement Kitchen-Like Wet Bar</a>:&nbsp;No more carrying dinner downstairs.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Contact the contractors at BasementRemodeling.com to find the beautiful finished or remodeled basement that you&rsquo;ve always wanted. Call us today or fill out our online form to receive a free quote and learn more about our amazing basement remodeling services.</p>',5,'',35,'2018-10-21 15:22:18'),(52,'3 Things to Know Before Remodeling or Finishing a Basement','Here’s what you need to know before remodeling/finishing a basement in Maryland Washington DC or Virginia.','basement remodeling, basement finishing, finishing a basement, basement remodeling Maryland, basement remodeling Virginia, basement remodeling Washington DC, basement finishing Virginia, basement finishing Washington DC, basement finshing Maryland, basement contractors, Maryland basement contractors','3-things-to-know-before-remodeling-or-finishing-a-basement','3 Things to Know Before Remodeling or Finishing a Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/52/8026921cef11984e107fbd3609184ef6','Here’s what you need to know before remodeling/finishing a basement in Maryland Washington DC or Virginia.','<p>Whether you are remodeling or finishing a basement in Maryland, Washington DC, or Virginia, the general approach is still going to be the same. You should always have some idea of the process before contacting a basement remodeling company for an estimate. Here&rsquo;s everything you need to know before getting started on a remodeling or finishing project in MD, DC, or VA.</p>\n<h2><strong>Budget for Soundproofing</strong></h2>\n<p>It&rsquo;s exciting to have a new playroom, billiards room or family room in the basement, but you need to insulate the basement ceiling to keep the noise from traveling throughout the house. Fiberglass or stone wool insulation are two common soundproofing materials that your basement contractor will be able to readily use.</p>\n<p>In addition, special drop ceilings and other architectural solutions can change the acoustics of the room to contain noise. Attachment clips that go onto the drywall are one of the most cost-efficient noise barriers available.</p>\n<h2><strong>Spacious Ceilings</strong></h2>\n<p>The minimum ceiling height for Maryland and Washington DC basements is 7 feet, and <a href=\"https://www.fredericksburgva.gov/DocumentCenter/View/8200/Basement-Guidedocx-2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">6&rsquo;8 feet</a> in Virginia (this can vary from county to county), but many clients want to raise the ceiling to make it look as roomy as the rest of their home. Fortunately, we are a basement remodeling company that is familiar with <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/ceilings/advanced/\">advanced ceiling options</a> and <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/ceilings/high-end-ceiling-designs/\">high-end basement ceiling designs</a>.</p>\n<h2><strong>Pay Attention to Permits</strong></h2>\n<p>A good basement remodeling contractor will be able to provide all permits so that you will not have to worry about this stage of development. There is a lot of paperwork and approval during this process that your basement contractor will be able to routinely handle. If you don&rsquo;t have a basement contractor with all of the permits, the building department could penalize you and even make you tear down your basement remodeling project.</p>\n<h2><strong>Contact BasementRemodeling.com for Basement Remodeling and Finishing</strong></h2>\n<p>Only the expert basement contractors at BasementRemodeling.com can handle your next basement remodeling/finishing project with the utmost attention and a keen eye. Contact us today and let us know how we can make your next basement remodeling and finishing project look its very best &ndash; and last for years.</p>',4,'',36,'2018-10-14 15:22:41'),(53,'4 Reasons to Invest in Custom Cabinets for Your Basement','Homeowners and businessowners across the country are choosing custom cabinets for their basement designs, but why? Find out here.','basement remodeling, basement remodeling contactors, basement remodeling Maryland, basement remodeling Baltimore, basement remodeling Virginia, basement cabinets, custom basement cabinets, basement blog, basement cabinet blog','4-reasons-to-invest-in-custom-cabinets-for-your-basement','4 Reasons to Invest in Custom Cabinets for Your Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/53/fd5ba8efe78dc0a765a541aa53278955','Homeowners and businessowners around the country are choosing custom cabinets for their basement designs because of these four reasons.','<p>Custom cabinets in the basement are made from the finest materials and craftsmanship. Homeowners and businessowners are choosing custom cabinets for their basement design because of the following reasons.</p>\n<h2><strong>1. Custom Cabinet Styles</strong></h2>\n<p>Custom cabinets for the basement have a wider variety of colors, glazes and other finishing styles to choose from. Custom basement contractors can use specialty glazes, die stains, and other hand touchups to match the current design (like distressing wood for an antique look).</p>\n<h2><strong>2. Exact Dimensions</strong></h2>\n<p>Custom basement cabinets are built to an exact width, depth or height, easily opening up new custom basement design solutions. A custom cabinet is great for basement storage because it uses every square inch and does not need filler strips to fit nonstandard angles.</p>\n<h2><strong>3. Durable Construction</strong></h2>\n<p>BasementRemodeling.com installs cabinets using the best construction methods and can last generations, never losing their great look and feel. Standard cabinets, however, can actually cost more than custom basement cabinets over time due to replacement accessories and repairs.</p>\n<h2><strong>4. Property Value</strong></h2>\n<p>Custom basement cabinets in a luxury home or a commercial space can increase the value of your property. Many of our clients later recoup the value installing their custom cabinets after selling their property.</p>\n<h2><strong>BasementRemodeling.com Provides Custom Cabinets in Maryland, DC and Virginia</strong></h2>\n<p>BasementRemodeling.com includes custom cabinets as part of our basement remodeling process in Maryland, DC and Virginia, so contact the best basement remodeling contractors on the East Coast to discuss your next basement remodeling project.</p>',1,'',37,'2018-10-07 15:22:55'),(54,'What You Need to Know Before Turning Your Crawl Space into a Basement','Looking to turn your crawl space into a livable basement? Here\'s what you need to know to prevent mold, mildew, rodents, pests and other problems from forming!','Basement contractor, basement contractors, basement remodeling, basement remodeling company, basement remodeling companies, crawl space renovation, dig out crawl space, waterproofing crawl space, turning a crawl space into a basement, basement masters, basement blog, basement finishing blog','what-you-need-to-know-before-turning-your-crawl-space-into-a-basement','What You Need to Know Before Turning Your Crawl Space into a Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/54/435c2804ed9f50299c360842e48a748f','Here\'s what you need to know about turning your crawl space into a basement.','<p>Turning your crawl space into a basement requires the expert knowledge of basement contractors who know how to keep the project within cost and building code requirements. Here is how a basement contractor will successfully prevent mold, mildew, rodents, pests and other problems from forming when turning your crawl space into a basement.</p>\n<h2><strong>Basement Remodeling Consultation and Assessment </strong></h2>\n<p>Before turning your crawl space into a basement, remodeling companies will assess the condition of the crawl space for damage or mold. A basement contractor has the professional equipment to detect trace sources of mold on the walls, joists, ductwork, and insultation. All mold and moisture must be removed before turning your crawl space into a basement or else additional problems will require more basement remodeling in the future.</p>\n<h2><strong>Moisture Control (Waterproofing) in the Basement</strong></h2>\n<p>A crawl space with a soil floor invites moisture and humidity into the home that needs to be dealt with. A basement remodeling company will be able to line the floor and foundation with a vapor barrier and then properly tape the seams so that moisture from the floor no longer evaporates into the air you breathe. The basement contractor will know exactly which type of vapor barrier to use, as they vary in composition, thickness, strength and overall durability.</p>\n<p>Aside from mold prevention, basement remodeling companies reduce moisture in the home so that the electric work does not short out, the metal does not rust, and the wood and drywall do not rot. Less moisture in the air means your HVAC system does not have to work as hard, lowering energy bills. Applying a vapor barrier also extends the length of your pipes since they will not rust as easily.</p>\n<h2><strong>Basement Construction</strong></h2>\n<p>Turning your crawl space into a basement is a delicate process that requires expert basement architectural and design knowledge from a professional basement remodeling company. Digging out a crawl space requires permits and the proper submission of complex engineering drafts and other documents to various appropriate city departments for approval. Improperly turning your crawl space into a basement without a professional basement remodeling company is costly and dangerous, so leave nothing to chance and hire a basement remodeling company.</p>\n<h2><strong>Turning Your Crawl Space into a Basement with Basement Masters</strong></h2>\n<p>Turning your crawl space into a basement is a professional experience with BasementRemodeling.com. We have the expertise and resources needed to turn your crawl space into a luxury basement with all of the latest amenities. If you need basement remodeling contractors in Maryland, Washington DC, or Virginia, then <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">contact us</a> today.</p>',1,'',38,'2018-09-30 15:23:11'),(55,'Is Washington DC Basement Remodeling/Finishing a Good Idea?','Not all cities are meant for basement remodeling, but what about Washington DC?','Washington DC basement remodeling, basement remodeling DC, basement remodeling Washington DC, basement remodeling contractors, digging out a basement from a crawl space, digging out a basement, basement dig out, basement dig out contractors, basement remodeling contractors, basement finishing','is-washington-dc-basement-remodelingfinishing-a-good-idea','Is Washington DC Basement Remodeling/Finishing a Good Idea?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/55/64f31188ebabd9217db8334017d5f08c','Not all cities are meant for basement remodeling. Is Washington DC one of them?','<p>The <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/8-pros-and-cons-of-having-a-basement\">pros and cons of having a basement</a> largely depend on where you live. In the heavily-populated Metro Area of Washington DC, basement remodeling is often the only way to obtain more living space. However, Washington DC basements tend to be small and too shallow to stand in.</p>\n<p>Fortunately, digging out a basement from a crawl space is always an option. Digging out a basement is a large process that involves many considerations and a lot of manpower. Hiring a dig-out basement contractor is always recommended.</p>\n<h2><strong>Responsibilities of Washington DC Basement Dig-Out Contractors</strong></h2>\n<p>Basement dig-out contractors have to do a lot more than just make sure the basement has a minimum legal ceiling height of 7 feet. The basement contractor must also know how to . . .</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Make new concrete footings</li>\n<li>Pour new concrete slab flooring</li>\n<li>Install foundation walls</li>\n<li>Lift the house to pour slab and foundation</li>\n<li>Create a legal emergency exit</li>\n<li>Connect sewer lines and decide on a water or gravity-based system</li>\n<li>Install lighting, heating, plumbing and electricity</li>\n<li>Decide on drain systems to prevent flooding</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>BasementRemodeling.com: Expert Dig-Out Contractors</strong></h2>\n<p>We are the experts of basement remodeling in Maryland, DC and Virginia. If you are considering digging out a basement in Washington DC, let BasementRemodeling.com give you a fair estimate and professional advice. <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact us</a> for a free quote today.</p>',1,'',39,'2018-09-23 15:23:26'),(56,'Custom Wood Countertops Vs Granite Countertops (Pros and Cons)','Custom wood countertops vs granite countertops—which is right for you? Let\'s weight the pros and cons.','Basement remodeling, basement remodel, basement countertops, granite countertops, custom granite countertops, wood countertops, custom wood countertops, basement countertops, basement blog','custom-wood-countertops-vs-granite-countertops-pros-and-cons','Custom Wood Countertops Vs Granite Countertops (Pros and Cons)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/56/a5abc29e0bec558a9b96032507bfe74e','Custom wood countertops are trendy once again, and granite countertops never go out of style, but which one is the right choice for you?','<p>Custom wood countertops are trendy once again, and the timeless look of granite countertops is always in style, but which is right for your home or place of business? Let&rsquo;s compare the pros and cons of custom wood and granite countertops.</p>\n<h2><strong>Custom Wood Countertops </strong></h2>\n<p>Custom wood countertops have a classic feel dating back to the chop blocks of old butcher shops. They have since been redesigned and gussied up countless times over the years into the familiar wood countertop design we know today.</p>\n<p>The pros:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Texture &ndash; Custom wooden countertops are elegant and durable, offering long-lasting strength while cushioning dropped items so they don&rsquo;t break as often. Items often sound softer when placed on them. An expert basement remodeling contractor can even strategically place the wood countertops in such a way that muffles noise from appliances.</li>\n<li>Easy refinishing &ndash; Marks, scratches and chipped areas can be easily sanded down and finished to for easy refinishing.</li>\n<li>Easy installation &ndash; Custom wood countertops can be easily installed in awkward corners and around appliances.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The cons:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Warping &ndash; Wooden countertops expand and contract with different humidity levels, which can be a problem with basement remodeling. Sometimes using thicker countertops can alleviate the problem of custom wooden countertops warping in the basement over time.</li>\n<li>Semi-frequent maintenance &ndash; Custom wooden countertops should be refinished about once every five years. It may need to be oiled monthly.</li>\n<li>Liquids &ndash; Liquids cause stains, cracks, and joint separation. Some people choose to go with custom granite countertops (especially around the sink area) instead.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Custom Granite Countertops</strong></h2>\n<p>Granite countertops have a timeless look &ndash; and many other timeless qualities as well. Custom granite countertops continue to remain a top choice for basement remodeling projects based on the following reasons:</p>\n<p>The pros:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>More than 20 shades of custom granite countertops to choose from</li>\n<li>Easily goes with custom wooden cabinets, flooring and wall coverings</li>\n<li>Scratch resistant</li>\n<li>No warping</li>\n<li>Repels stains</li>\n<li>Resists liquids (ask your basement remodeling contractor about professional sealants)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The cons:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Frequent treatments &ndash; Custom granite countertops need to be resealed as often as once a year</li>\n<li>They will no longer repel stains as well without the proper sealant</li>\n<li>Heavy items can crack or chip the custom granite countertop</li>\n<li>Granite countertops can be costly compared to other materials</li>\n</ul>',1,'',40,'2018-09-09 15:23:38'),(57,'5 Benefits of Custom Bulkhead Doors','Custom bulkhead doors can keep your home safe from intruders and keep your energy bills low. Here are the benefits.','Custom bulkhead doors, custom basement doors, bulkhead doors, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement blog, energy costs, benefits of bulkhead doors','5-benefits-of-custom-bulkhead-doors','5 Benefits of Custom Bulkhead Doors','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/57/ed28273faa1439a9b4d7e7fb6f69b105','Custom bulkhead doors can keep your home safe and your energy bills low.','<p>Custom basement doors come in many forms, including custom bulkhead doors. Custom bulkhead doors swing open from the ground; they are a tradition in the northeast region and were once used as the main entrance in homes. There is usually an indoor stairwell leading down to an interior doorway, giving you plenty of opportunities to impress with stair railing ideas and basement stair (steps) ideas. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>Though they have since lost their spot as the main entrance with the passage of time, custom bulk doors still have a place in your next basement finishing or remodeling project.</p>\n<h2><strong>Safety Compliance</strong></h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.dllr.state.md.us/labor/build/buildcodes.shtml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Maryland</a>, <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/Interpretations%202018-002_FINAL_Signed.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Washington DC</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.dhcd.virginia.gov/virginia-uniform-statewide-building-code-usbc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Virginia</a> building codes all require basements to have an easy way out in the event of an emergency. The outward opening motion of custom bulkhead doors provide the smoothest escape possible in case of emergency.</p>\n<h2><strong>Weather Resistant</strong></h2>\n<p>Basement doors can be customized to meet the needs of your geographical location. Custom bulkhead doors in Virginia, Maryland and Washington DC are typically built slightly submerged in the ground and sealed, making them immune to floods and high rains.</p>\n<h3><strong>Security</strong></h3>\n<p>Old basement doors can be pried open and are easy for criminals to break into. Custom basement doors come with the latest lock technologies meant to keep your valuables safe.</p>\n<h2><strong>Durability and Cost</strong></h2>\n<p>Custom basement doors are built to last for a long time and do not require much maintenance. The airtight sealant can also keep heat in your home, saving on energy bills every year.</p>\n<h2><strong>Custom Bulkhead Doors Look Fantastic</strong></h2>\n<p>Custom-built bulkhead doors are appealing to the eye. The intricate look of custom wooden bulkhead doors is simply stunning, while metal bulkhead doors have a style all of their own. Contact a professional <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">basement remodeling contactor near you</a> today to learn more.</p>',1,'',41,'2018-09-02 15:23:59'),(58,'3 Main Costs of Finishing (Remodeling) a Luxury Basement','Find out how to properly budget and plan your next basement remodeling or finishing project.','cost of a finished basement, basement finishing, basement remodeling, basement remodeling costs, luxury basement, costs of basement remodeling','3-main-costs-of-finishing-remodeling-a-luxury-basement','3 Main Costs of Finishing (Remodeling) a Luxury Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/58/c43868610a299c849d22cb1fca1e4052','Learn how to budget ahead of time for your next basement remodeling or finishing project.','<p>The cost of a basement finishing (remodeling) project always depends on the basement&rsquo;s size and the number of improvements being made. At the very least, luxury basement remodeling and finishing almost always involves adding or removing walls, installing new flooring, electricity and lighting. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>When budgeting for a finished basement or a basement remodel, remember these general guidelines:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Basement flooring and basement wainscoting, wooden panels and other wall custom coverings are usually the biggest expense.</li>\n<li>Basement plumbing and electricity usually costs around the same amount as basement flooring and wall coverings. Custom wet bars, kitchenlike areas, and home theaters will require extra electric work and plumbing.</li>\n<li>Interior custom millwork is usually the third biggest cost when finishing a basement (depending on the total amount of custom countertops, custom made-furniture and other interior custom millwork involved).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Other Cost Considerations When Finishing or Remodeling a Basement</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Design Layout</strong> &ndash; A finished basement with an open layout as opposed to a finished basement with many rooms is always going to be less expensive. The additional studs, wiring, drywall, doors and other costs for adding rooms can quickly add up.</p>\n<p><strong>Carpeting</strong> &ndash; Many luxury basement owners opt to use carpets in place of hardwood flooring or luxury vinyl tile (LVT) flooring. Some prefer the bounce of a fine carpet compared to wood when walking, others simply do not want objects to break as often during our clumsier moments, and others still appreciate its fine appearance fair price.</p>',1,'',42,'2018-09-02 15:24:22'),(59,'Are Custom Basement Cabinets Better Than Standard Cabinets?','Custom basement cabinets have many advantages over standard cabinets, but what exactly are they?','Custom basement cabinets, custom cabinets, basement bar cabinets, basement storage cabinets, basement remodeling company, Maryland basement remodeling company, basement remodeling, basement finishing','are-custom-basement-cabinets-better-than-standard-cabinets','Are Custom Basement Cabinets Better Than Standard Cabinets?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/59/c72b6df604b68bd339c216bd76af85ee','Custom basement cabinets have many advantages of standard cabinets, but what are they?','<p>When you own a luxury home; or business, installing custom basement cabinets will convey an appropriate atmosphere of your choosing. Aesthetic choice is the main reason for most custom basement cabinets. However, there are plenty of non-cosmetic reasons why custom basement cabinets are far better than their mass-produced counterparts.&nbsp;</p>\n<h2><strong>Custom Basement Cabinet Design</strong></h2>\n<p>Custom basement cabinets, unlike standard cabinet designs, can be built to specific measurements. Basement storage cabinets, basement kitchen cabinets, and basement bar cabinets are the three most popular designs.</p>\n<p>Since they are an exact fit, custom basement cabinets do not have to use what&rsquo;s known as a filler strip to cover gaps. A filler strip has to match the natural grain or it will look bad, a problem which custom basement cabinets do not have. Adhesives, screws or bolts are used to install filler strips, leaving room for additional setbacks and delays. Even when filler strips are successfully installed, there is less storage space overall..</p>\n<p>Storage space and visual appeal aside, <strong>custom cabinets </strong>are structurally superior to standard cabinets in every other way. Professional basement remodelers will handpick the solid wood inventory to make sure the highest quality materials are selected for the final product. Mass producers will not check for defects as closely as basement remodeling experts do (including after the finished product is ready for installation).</p>\n<h2><strong>Contact Basement Masters for Custom Cabinet Remodeling</strong></h2>\n<p>BasementRemodeling.com is the company of choice for basement remodeling in Maryland, Virginia and Washington DC. The tri-state area trusts our experienced and professional crew to implement stunning woodwork designs using only the highest quality materials and most efficient methods of installation available.</p>\n<p>When you are ready for the best basement remodeling company in Maryland, BasementRemodeling.com is ready to enhance your high-end home or place of business. Call <strong>301-250-1939 </strong>or <a href=\"https://www.brooklynmillwork.com/ask-for-quote/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">contact us online</a> to get more information about how our custom basement cabinets can drastically improve any property.</p>',1,'',43,'2018-08-26 15:24:35'),(60,'What is a Finished Basement (4 Requirements)','What exactly qualifies a basement as being \"finished\"? Are there any requirements to meet? Here\'s what you need to know.','What is a finished basement, basement finishing, best basement finishing companies, basement finishing Maryland, basement finishing companies Maryland, finished basement, basement finishing md, basement finishing va, basement finishing dc, basement blog, best basement blog','what-is-a-finished-basement-4-requirements','What is a Finished Basement (4 Requirements)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/60/51f5d9c6c2048c039f242230f412a5f9','Exactly what qualifies a basement as \"finished\"? Find out here.','<p><strong>Basement finishing </strong>is the process of making a basement suitable to live in all year long. The best basement finishing companies will make your basement look absolutely gorgeous and add value to the home, but what is a finished basement&rsquo;s minimum requirements?</p>\n<p>Basement finishing focuses on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/hvac/\">Heating</a> &ndash; Basement finishing companies must install a permanent heat source (electricity, natural gas, residential or commercial propane tank, or heating oil). Portable space heaters and window units are not enough (though permanent baseboard heaters are).</li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/flooring/\">Flooring</a> &ndash; Simply painting over a concrete floor is not basement finishing. Attractive basement flooring options such as luxury vinyl tiling or laminate flooring are good choices (regular hardwood is not a good choice due to moisture concerns). High-quality carpeting is fine.</li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/ceilings/\">Ceiling</a> &ndash; Most local building ordinances require a ceiling with a minimum height of seven feet. However, most basement finishing companies make the ceiling around seven-feet-nine-inches to avoid feeling too cramped. Basement tray ceilings can also add much-needed height to a room. After all, what is a finished basement good for if the ceiling is still too low?</li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/stairs-and-railing/\">Stairs &amp; railings</a> &ndash; A finished basement must be easily accessible from the rest of the house. Stairs are required; ladders will simply not do.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The best basement finishing companies can add additional finishing touches such as . . .</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/columns/\">Columns</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/storage-rooms/\">Storage rooms</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/fireplaces/\">Fireplaces</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/lighting/\">Lighting</a></li>\n<li>Much more</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Get a <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">basement quote</a> from BasementRemodeling.com&mdash;the best basement finishing company in Maryland, DC, and Virginia&mdash;and learn exactly how amazing your finished basement can be!</p>',1,'',44,'2018-04-30 15:24:49'),(61,'7 Things to Know About Basement Finishing','Do only basement contractors know how to properly finish an unfinished basement? Or can you do it yourself? Here\'s what you need to know.','basement finishing, finished basement, finished basement ideas, basement remodeling, basement finishing contractor, basement finishing contractors, Maryland basement remodeling company, basement remodeling companies, basement remodeling companies in Maryland, basement finishing md, basement finishing va, basement finishing dc, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, best basement blog','7-things-to-know-about-basement-finishing','7 Things to Know About Basement Finishing','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/61/66049f0ec62515513d4282a459b64146','Can you do a basement finishing job yourself? Do only basement contractors know how to finish an unfinished basement the correct way?','<p>Basement finishing does add value to any property, but typically only basement contractors know how to finish an unfinished basement the right way. The best finished basements always keep some expert finishing tips in mind (brought to you by BasementRemodeling.com, the best basement remodeling company in Maryland).</p>\n<h2>7 Essential Basement Finishing Tips:</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Build to maximize value</strong> &ndash; Whether you are focusing more bedrooms, better basement storage, or deluxe entertainment options, <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/can-a-finished-basement-add-value-to-your-home-or-business\">basement finishing does add value</a> to a property when done correctly. Finishing a basement will increase the value of a property per square foot, though it does not increase the amount of square footage shown in a listing. Basement contractors will know exactly which basement finishing improvements add the most value on the market.</li>\n<li><strong>Maximize the available light</strong> &ndash; Basements need to have plenty of light, sure, but it&rsquo;s much more than that. The light has to hit at just the right angles to show off the architecture in an inviting way; <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/what-color-should-you-paint-the-basement-walls\">different paint colors also need different amounts of light</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Eliminate moisture</strong> &ndash; Moisture is the enemy of any basement finishing project. The HVAC must be adequately circulating the air to avoid any moisture-causing humidity. The drainage system (gutters, gutter shields etc.) must be carrying water far enough away from your basement&rsquo;s foundation to prevent basement leaks.</li>\n<li><strong>HVAC</strong> &ndash; Your old heating, ventilation and air condition (HVAC) system may not be equipped to handle the basement and the upstairs floors at the same time, resulting in lowered performance levels and a shortened lifespan. Basement contractors will make sure you have an HVAC that can handle a finished basement in addition to the rest of your home.</li>\n<li><strong>Use below grade flooring</strong> &ndash; Basement flooring requires different materials than the rest of the home. LVT flooring, for example, is resistant to moisture and perfectly emulates many different surface types.</li>\n<li><strong>Radon</strong> &ndash; Invisible radioactive gas can sometimes leak from the soil into your basement. Contractors will make sure your basement is thoroughly tested and sealed to keep radon away from you, your family and your guests.</li>\n<li><strong>Follow every code</strong> &ndash; Almost everyone needs to rely on the expert knowledge of basement finishing contractors to pass inspections and stay on track. Trying to finish a basement without a contractor opens you up to legal liabilities, fines, and other setbacks.</li>\n</ol>',1,'',45,'2018-04-22 15:25:09'),(62,'Basement Finishing and Remodeling...and Pets','How do you keep your pets safe during a basement finishing and remodeling project? Here\'s what you need to know.','basement finishing, basement remodeling, basement finishing Virginia, basement remodeling Virginia, basement remodeling Maryland, basement finishing Maryland, basement remodeling Washington DC, basement finishing Washington DC, basement pets, what to do, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement remodeling blog, best basement blog','basement-finishing-and-remodeling...and-pets','Basement Finishing and Remodeling...and Pets','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/62/2439d5d9079d64520188eb9986d9dda1','Here\'s what you can do to keep your pets safe during a basement finishing and remodeling project.','<p>For over twelve years, BasementRemodeling.com has been successfully renovating commercial and residential basements. Many of our residential basement remodeling projects in Maryland, Washington DC, and Virginia have included spaces shared by house pets. We care about everyone in your home, so here&rsquo;s what you can do to keep your pets safe during a basement finishing and remodeling project.</p>\n<h2>Use safety precautions</h2>\n<p>The best advice we have is to treat the basement remodeling area the same as a construction site. That is to say, no pets. Keeping the pet away from the basement remodeling will ensure the animal&rsquo;s safety.</p>\n<h2>Keep pets confined&nbsp;</h2>\n<p>Pets can always be confined using interior doors. If you have an anxious pet that doesn&rsquo;t like being confined to one space, then a baby gate can keep them from feeling too closed off. Always include their favorite toys, food, water, bedding, and maybe a clothing article or two with your scent on it.</p>\n<h2>Consider another location</h2>\n<p>If your dog has extremely high levels of anxiety, then taking them to another home that they are familiar with could be an option. Babysitters and even kennels can solve the problem as well.</p>',4,'',46,'2018-04-15 15:25:25'),(63,'4 Reasons Why Basement Wood Wall Paneling is Back','Remodeling a basement and don\'t know why type of wall paneling to use? Here\'s why wood-wall paneling is back in style.','Wood wall paneling, wall paneling ideas, basement wall paneling, basement remodeling, remodeling a basement, basement remodeling Maryland, basement remodeling Washington DC, basement remodeling Baltimore, basement remodeling Baltimore City, Basement Masters, Basement Masters Maryland, basement blog, best basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','4-reasons-why-basement-wood-wall-paneling-is-back','4 Reasons Why Basement Wood Wall Paneling is Back','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/63/a8823122c8fa87aadd3cec2d2e8fd06a','Remodeling a basement? Use these expert wood wall paneling ideas.','<p><strong>Traditional wood paneling </strong>in basements harks back to the 60s, but now wall paneling ideas involving wood are back in style. Here&rsquo;s why traditional wood paneling is being reincorporated into basement remodeling projects in Maryland, Washington DC, and everywhere else.</p>\n<h2><strong>Natural Warmth</strong></h2>\n<p>When done tastefully, wood paneling adds a natural sense warmth to a room. Wood paneling can keep brighter paint colors from becoming overwhelming. Conversely, bright wood wall paneling ideas can keep darker colors from becoming too drab.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/59/fe00d6f569790035e42ef9324839818f_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>White wood wall paneling ideas contrast nicely with muted paint colors.</em></p>\n<h2><strong>Textural Enhancements</strong></h2>\n<p>The striped texture of certain wood wall paneling ideas can add visual height to a room &ndash; similar to how a striped shirt can elongate the torso. With the right style and placement, you can play with the visual depth of a room using different wall paneling ideas. An architect or a designer will best know how to achieve this look.</p>\n<h2><strong>Versatile Application</strong></h2>\n<p>Family rooms, bathrooms and kitchens are just three basement spaces that can be improved with traditional wall paneling. Different ideas can be as subtle or dramatic as you want. For an invitingly uniform appearance, try a paneled ceiling as well.</p>\n<h2><strong>Timeless</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Basement wood wall paneling </strong>is modern, yet classic. Traditional elegance and sophistication exudes from wall paneling made from rare wood. Choosing wooden wall paneling ideas in an art gallery adds architectural symmetry and framework. At the same time, modern, contemporary and transitional themes look great with wood paneling as well.</p>\n<h2><strong>Custom Wall Paneling with BasementRemodeling.com</strong></h2>\n<p>Remodel your basement tastefully using traditional wooden wall paneling ideas from the experts at BasementRemodeling.com. For more than ten years, we have been stylishly remodeling luxury basements throughout Maryland (recently expanding into Baltimore City, Washington D.C., and Virginia). Check out our luxury <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/wall-treatments/wood-wall-panelling/\">wall paneling ideas</a> and then contact BasementRemodeling.com for a <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">free quote</a> at (301) 798-4444!</p>',1,'',47,'2018-04-08 15:25:37'),(64,'8 Basement Organization Tips and Storage Strategies','Hunting for tips and storage strategies for your basement space? Here are 8 effective storage solutions for any basement.','Basement organization, basement storage, basement storage room, basement organization ideas, basement storage ideas, basement remodeling, Basement Masters, custom basement shelving, custom basement shelving ideas, basement access doors, basement finishing, basement remodeling, best basement blog, basement blog','8-basement-organization-tips-and-storage-strategies','8 Basement Organization Tips and Storage Strategies','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/64/017e1d30126279e5f57e584c4d986d00','Clean your downstairs more precisely with these sensible basement organization tips and basement storage ideas.','<p>Spring is the season for getting serious about <strong>basement organization</strong>. These basement storage ideas will keep every room looking tidy all year long (so you won&rsquo;t have to work so hard next spring)!</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sort the clutter &ndash; You don&rsquo;t want to store what you don&rsquo;t need, so the first step is to sort everything you don&rsquo;t want to keep into three piles: the stuff you want to donate, the stuff you want to ditch, and the stuff you want to sell.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Add extra basement shelving &ndash; <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/built-ins-and-shelving/basic-shelving/\">Basic basement shelves</a> (especially in the bathroom and laundry room) gives you more room to organize everything, while <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/built-ins-and-shelving/custom-cabinetry-shelving/\">custom cabinetry and shelving ideas</a> can add additional basement storage to tiny nooks and tight spaces (like <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/under-stairs-space/\">under the stairs</a>). Keep wires off the floor and your electronics safe with <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/built-ins-and-shelving/entertainment-center/\">entertainment center shelving ideas</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/57/cdae1615674da404b071599b42b104f4_624x936.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"936\" /><em>This basic basement shelf provides more basement organization opportunities in the bathroom.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Wires can also be safely tucked away behind the wall using&nbsp;<a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/doors/access-doors/\">basement access doors</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Plastic storage units make it easy to identify the contents inside but leaving them all over every room in the basement is tacky. Try to keep all plastic containers confined to a single basement storage room. These <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/storage-rooms/\">basement storage room ideas</a> demonstrate how to organize a basement the right way.</li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/58/acee8d0754ec8137d33339a265a3cf1b_624x415.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"415\" /><em>Ideally, only one room in your basement should look like this &ndash; not all of them.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Furniture Placement &ndash; Furniture should be kept three inches away from the walls to prevent any moisture damage (however likely).</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>If you ever have an emergency in the basement, organization is key. Hang a flashlight over the fuse box so you won&rsquo;t have to fumble in the dark if the lights go out. Make sure the fuses are labeled with a permanent marker. Install <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/doors/access-doors/\">basement access doors</a> to quickly get to important infrastructure.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Clean all basement appliances (refrigerators, washers &amp; dryers, dishwashers) and make sure they are completely dry before using. The washer and dryer doors should be left open a little to keep the air circulating (which prevents mildew from growing).</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Air out your basement (and its items) at least once every three months to avoid foul odors. Use a dehumidifier to help control the moisture levels.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>BasementRemodeling.com</strong></h2>\n<p>Basement remodeling is the best way to organize your basement and implement stylish new storage features. <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact BasementRemodeling.com</a> today to learn more about how we can keep your basement looking beautiful for generations to come.</p>',4,'',48,'2018-04-01 15:25:55'),(65,'6 Terrific Basement Entertainment Center Ideas','Make the basement entertainment center the focal point of your downstairs with these 6 terrific basement entertainment center ideas!','Basement entertainment center, basement entertainment center ideas, bar entertainment center, bookshelf with tv space','6-terrific-basement-entertainment-center-ideas','6 Terrific Basement Entertainment Center Ideas','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/65/c7e064643f0e58704e5e3dffe1de8ac4','Make the basement entertainment center the focal point of your downstairs with these 6 terrific basement entertainment center ideas!','<p><strong>6 Terrific Basement Entertainment Center Ideas</strong></p>\n<p>Movie nights, weekly television shows, and home videos are three common reasons to gather around the <strong>basement entertainment center </strong>as a family. Follow these basement <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/media-rooms/basic-media-rooms/\">entertainment center ideas</a> and choose the right basement entertainment center for both style and functionality within the home.</p>\n<p><strong>Traditional Basement Entertainment Center</strong></p>\n<p>A typical traditional basement entertainment center is essentially a large stand for the television flanked by multiple cabinets, drawers, and shelves for storing media and accessories. Basement entertainment centers keep wire tangles and clutter to a minimum but tend to take up a lot of space and should not be used in smaller rooms. Small rooms should go with these other basement entertainment center ideas.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/50/0762a15a29571f175a529c8c405043cb_624x468.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"468\" /><em>Even a mounted television can still benefit from a basement entertainment center.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Bookshelf with TV Space</strong></p>\n<p>Having a bookshelf with TV space tastefully presents guests with two starkly different styles of entertainment. The juxtaposition of low-tech books with high-tech televisions creates an artistic contrast and the colors books themselves can be matched with the floors and walls if desired.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/51/991f6ff9eef04a170d2d33dc223c4a29_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>A bookshelf with TV space can either have the television resting on top (pictured above) or on a shelf.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Basement Fireplace &amp; Entertainment Center</strong></p>\n<p>Having an electric basement fireplace affords plenty of space to put a television on top. The whole family can warm up while watching their favorite movies and shows. The basement fireplace / basement entertainment center combo especially looks fantastic in any family room, games room, or home office.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/52/651d0cded3ccf303c49305347163d4eb_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>Turning the basement fireplace into a basement entertainment center looks great and makes sense.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Wet Bar Entertainment Center</strong></p>\n<p>Guests will appreciate a full-sized wet bar even more when it&rsquo;s complete with a bar entertainment center to watch sports and other recreational events. The wet bar entertainment center generally should be placed up high so as to avoid any spills. Be sure to turn the televisions downward slightly for the best viewing angle from a stool.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/53/70bbad40f56918745ed6c5872c7aa06d_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>Wet bar entertainment centers can be as simple as a mounted television and recessed lighting.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Built In Entertainment Center</strong></p>\n<p>A skilled basement contractor can build an entertainment center into the wall for a custom look with plenty of storage options. Everything is kept out of the way and also has space to avoid overheating. This option is especially popular with full-sized home theaters or family rooms with projector screens.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/54/fe5068d004b9568b7ef90d2ea35cf39b_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>A built in basement entertainment center keeps electronics safely inside of the wall.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Basic Television Stand</strong></p>\n<p>A television stand is essentially a scaled-down version of the basement entertainment center without the extra drawers and shelves. All storage space is kept to a minimum, which makes it good for smaller rooms.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/55/d8fb43a8d040c0cb1ec4d2057ced2181_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>A basic TV stand fills out the room nicely.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Basement Entertainment Center Styles</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Contemporary basement entertainment center ideas are typically metal or glass with a very basic design.</li>\n<li>Modern basement entertainment centers are typically wood.</li>\n<li>Traditional basement entertainment centers are also wood but have crown molding on top and fancy downturned legs.</li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/56/3baf4fce0df765d3087a7cf0e10a5979_624x287.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"287\" /><em>A lack of crown molding makes this a modern basement entertainment center, not traditional.</em></p>',1,'',49,'2018-03-25 15:26:05'),(66,'5 Common Basement Problems','Practical basement solutions to five common basement problems.','basement problems, basement remodeling, basement remodeling contractor, basement solutions','5-common-basement-problems','5 Common Basement Problems','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/66/4b84e7671444a1cabd4fcdd0b5d49684','Practical basement solutions to five common basement problems.','<p><strong>5 Common Basement Problems</strong></p>\n<p>Whether your basement is finished or still needs to be remodeled, all basements tend to have the same types of problems due to the very location and design of the area itself. Basement Masters has remodeled countless basements throughout Maryland, Virginia, Baltimore and DC, and sometimes we see these fairly common basement problems. Here are 5 basement problems to check for in your home:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Humidity &ndash; Moisture in the air causes condensation on surfaces. This leads to mold, corrosion, and other forms of rot. Fix any leaks, make sure your gutters are clean and the right length to properly carry water away from your foundation, and grab a dehumidifier if needed.</li>\n<li>Bad Smells &ndash; A foul basement odor is another sign of water collecting somewhere in the basement or at least high levels of humidity. Check all surfaces that are wood, drywall, fiberglass, leather, cloth or painted.</li>\n<li>Cracks and Leaks &ndash; Whether it&rsquo;s in your windows or your foundation, cracks can let water into your basement and eventually cause structural damage. All basement cracks must be measured by a professional basement contractor using diagnostic tools to determine how serious it is to the integrity of your home.</li>\n<li>Mold &ndash; Early signs of mold can be eliminated with a fan and special mold-killing products. Large amounts of mold will require additional methods. If you see a small amount of mold, call a professional basement contractor. There may be mold on the other side of the surface or in other areas that you may not think to inspect.</li>\n<li>Needs Remodeling &ndash; If you feel like your basement might have an outdated design, it probably does! It&rsquo;s all-too-common to let a basement become drab and dreary, but once the basement has been remodeled, it often quickly becomes the most favorite area of the home!</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Solve Common Basement Problems with Basement Masters</strong></p>\n<p>Basement Masters has over 10 years of experience resolving all of these common basement problems. We are a Maryland-based basement remodeling company with the tools and expertise needed to update your design structurally and cosmetically. With Basement Masters, your common basement problems are transformed into beautiful and elegant solutions!</p>',4,'',50,'2018-03-18 15:26:22'),(67,'4 Main Types of Basement Construction Homebuyers Should Look For','Understanding the four different types of basement construction will make a big difference before buying a home.','different types of basement construction, poured concrete, block concrete, stone walls, clay tile walls','4-main-types-of-basement-construction-homebuyers-should-look-for','4 Main Types of Basement Construction Homebuyers Should Look For','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/67/463afba9f355c39a1ff52308e1d3413c','Understanding the four different types of basement construction will make a big difference when buying a home.','<p><strong>4 Main Types of Basement Construction Homebuyers Should Look For</strong></p>\n<p>The way a basement is constructed determines how stable the home is, yet many homebuyers don&rsquo;t think about what type of basement construction when looking at properties. While there is no &ldquo;best&rdquo; basement construction type per se, there are some important differences to know about before buying a new home.</p>\n<p><strong>Poured Concrete</strong></p>\n<p>Concrete footings and walls offer long-lasting stability and are the most common form of basement construction nowadays. Over time, small cracks can develop in the joints connecting the walls to the floor and let water in. &nbsp;<strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Concrete Block Walls</strong></p>\n<p>Using cinder blocks is a form of basement construction that is faster and less expensive. They generally hold up fairly well, but over time water can leak through each cinder block (in addition to the joints connecting the walls to the floor, as with poured concrete). Water can also fill up inside of the hollow cinder blocks. Some basements with concrete block walls are reinforced with rebar for added durability.</p>\n<p><strong>Precast Panel</strong></p>\n<p>The walls have been molded at a manufacturer and transported. This is not as durable as cinder blocks or poured concrete, but it is cheaper. However, they are more resistant to water damage than the other basement construction types. Sometimes water can get in through the joints connecting the walls to the floor.</p>\n<p><strong>Stone or Clay Tile Walls</strong></p>\n<p>These basement construction types are found in older houses (clay tile walls are usually in historic houses), which makes them visually quite attractive to some homebuyers. They are quite sturdy. However, clay and stone are not the best at keeping out water and will probably require a perimeter drain system.</p>',1,'',51,'2018-03-18 15:26:36'),(68,'Hiring a Basement Contractor Vs. DIY Basement Remodeling','If you have a great basement remodeling or finishing project idea, should you DIY or use a contractor? Here\'s what you need to know.','diy basement remodeling, diy basement finishing, DIY, do it yourself, basement contractor, basement contractor vs DIY, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement remodeling blog','hiring-a-basement-contractor-vs.-diy-basement-remodeling','Hiring a Basement Contractor Vs. DIY Basement Remodeling','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/68/1059c4ef3c8ebdfe5e83dfbcfc2bb3f0','Should you hire a basement remodeling company?','<p>A basement remodeling company is the easiest way to remodel a basement, but is it the most effective? Let&rsquo;s compare do-it-yourself (&ldquo;DIY&rdquo;) basement remodeling to hiring an actual basement remodeling company to see which way is more efficient.</p>\n<h2><strong>Basement Permits</strong></h2>\n<p>There are many basement codes and regulations that need to be met for a basement remodeling project to be legal. Failure to comply with these rules will result in fines, delays and even structural collapse. A basement remodeling company, on the other hand, will know how to pull the right permits to show building inspectors and make sure everything goes smoothly.</p>\n<h2><strong>Structural Integrity</strong></h2>\n<p>Basement contractors know how to manipulate the basement infrastructure without damaging the rest of your home. Knocking down a load-bearing wall, for example, could cause serious damage and even render the house uninhabitable until expensive repairs are made. For a good-looking basement that will last, basement remodeling companies provide the best results.</p>\n<h2><strong>Insurance</strong></h2>\n<p>Basement remodeling insurance plans can be expensive and difficult to navigate. A good basement remodeling company will already have all of the necessary insurance in effect, saving you from having to research and negotiate with companies yourself. Your involvement with insurance companies will be kept to a minimum.</p>\n<h2><strong>End Results</strong></h2>\n<p>Any basement remodeling company worth hiring will guarantee your satisfaction and work hard until you are pleased with the end results. When you are remodeling a basement yourself, however, it is up to you to make sure everything is up to your personal specifications. If you have completed everything to the best of your abilities and still don&rsquo;t like the way it looks, then you will have to hire a basement contractor anyway &ndash; so you might as well hire a basement remodeling company yourself and get it right the first time. &nbsp;</p>',4,'',52,'2018-03-04 15:26:49'),(69,'4 Important Basement Home Theater Ideas to Consider','Follow these crucial basement home theater ideas for the best moviegoing experience possible.','basement home theater, basement theater, basement home theater ideas, basement remodeling, basement remodeling contractor, Basement Masters, basement remodeling ideas','4-important-basement-home-theater-ideas-to-consider','4 Important Basement Home Theater Ideas to Consider','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/69/7ed8095609381d3291d80ce95d88942b','Follow these crucial basement home theater ideas for the best moviegoing experience possible.','<p><strong>4 Important Basement Home Theater Ideas to Consider</strong></p>\n<p>Of all the basement remodeling ideas we offer at Basement Masters, a home theater is one of the most often requested. These helpful basement home theater ideas will make sure your next private screening is a huge success!</p>\n<p><strong>Home Basement Theater Lighting</strong></p>\n<p>Lighting is one of the most important parts of owning a home theater basement. Any basement contractor can tell you that the room needs to be as dark as possible, but the experts at Basement Masters have advanced <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/lighting/\">basement lighting ideas</a> to make your picture look great. For example, hidden LED lights in the ceiling will keep direct light from hitting the projector and washing out the picture.</p>\n<p><strong>Give Your Electronics Room for Ventilation</strong></p>\n<p>You want to give your home theater system a place that&rsquo;s out of the way and well-ventilated. Otherwise, the electronics may overheat and breakdown. Whatever you do, don&rsquo;t put them in an ordinary cabinet without vents.<br /><br /></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/49/0e91672dab5043b34677dcb462569f4c_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><br /><em>Built-in shelving gives your home theater electronics a cozy resting nook. &nbsp;</em></p>\n<p><strong>Cable Wiring </strong></p>\n<p>Thick, well-insulated cable wires provide the strongest signal and lasts the longest. The expert basement remodeling contractors at Basement Masters will choose sturdy and reliable wiring to provide the highest quality of picture and sound. A custom basement home theater from Basement Masters will look great and experience no sound distortion (even at high volume) due to the professional wiring.</p>\n<p><strong>Speakers</strong></p>\n<p>A surround sound system will give you the most immersive experience, but you need to have the appropriate setup. Basement Masters will be able to identify the number of speakers you need by the size of the room. They will be able to position them appropriately to make the most of the room&rsquo;s natural acoustics.</p>',1,'',53,'2018-03-04 15:27:01'),(70,'5 Luxuriant Basement Stair Railing Ideas','Looking for beautiful basement stair railing ideas? Here are the 5 most luxurious railing ideas to impress your guests!','basement stair railing, basement stair railings, basement stair railing ideas, iron stair railing, glass stair railing, steel stair railing,  basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, best basement tips','5-luxuriant-basement-stair-railing-ideas','5 Luxuriant Basement Stair Railing Ideas','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/70/63f2bb1256c8487927cdd0949f3d9cd5','Here are 5 brilliant and luxurious basement stair railing ideas to make your home shine.','<p><strong>5 Luxuriant Basement Stair Railing Ideas</strong></p>\n<p>The basement stair railing is the first thing your guests will touch as they enter your downstairs area. That&rsquo;s why, when you&rsquo;re remodeling a basement, stair railings must not be neglected. These basement stair railing ideas will showcase the beauty of your home the next time you have guests over!</p>\n<h2><strong>Steel Stair Railing</strong></h2>\n<p><img title=\"Steel railings add a beautiful look to your staircase\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/44/957c09d70bbb58f1624d757f34e87af1_624x933.png\" alt=\"A steel stair railing conveys a professional look without being too formal for the home.\" width=\"624\" height=\"933\" /></p>\n<p>A steel stair railing conveys a professional look without being too formal for the home. Thin steel stair railings look especially sleek and are very popular for 2018. Just be sure to try and match color tones when choosing steel stair railings and flooring.</p>\n<h2><strong>Iron Stair Railing</strong></h2>\n<p><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/45/ae250b2be8dc0ac926c813de8afa3278_624x527.png\" alt=\"Iron stair railings are the go-to basement stair railing of choice for a traditional look.\" width=\"624\" height=\"527\" /></p>\n<p>Iron stair railings are the go-to basement stair railing of choice for a traditional look. Typically, vertical iron bars are the standard design, though custom iron stair railings can feature much more stylishly intricate patterns. Using an iron stair railing in a basement remodel can break up wood undertones. &nbsp;</p>\n<h2><strong>Wood Railings</strong></h2>\n<p><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/46/bab17f7dd40e50839d828f2b9c8e9142_624x832.png\" alt=\"Wood stair railings are a timeless and beautiful classic\" width=\"624\" height=\"832\" /></p>\n<p>Wood stair railings are a classic. Wood stair railings are no longer reserved for a downhome, country motif. Instead, many modern basement remodeling projects are taking full advantage of this timeless style.</p>\n<h2><strong>Lovely Glass Railing</strong></h2>\n<p><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/47/7ef79c7fb0e1a3323a02107eeeb7418e_624x831.png\" alt=\"Glass stair railings make the room look both larger and more elegant\" width=\"624\" height=\"831\" /></p>\n<p>Aside from looking absolutely elegant, glass stair railings also make the room look larger. With the right treatment and installation, a glass basement stair railing is safe and lasts for years.</p>\n<h2><strong>Stairs with Half-Wall</strong></h2>\n<p><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/48/7ea4b8bbe939b2b09093c752479d05dc_624x416.png\" alt=\"Half-wall stairs are an excellent architectural choice for narrow entrances.\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /></p>\n<p>An excellent entrance that adds architectural depth and fresh, clean lines while also matching the rest of the design layout. Stairs with half wall are especially good for narrow entranceways.</p>',4,'',54,'2018-02-25 15:27:14'),(71,'6 Questions to Ask Yourself Before Remodeling a Basement','A basement remodel will go smoothly with these questions in mind.','Remodeling a basement, basement remodeling, basement contractor','6-questions-to-ask-yourself-before-remodeling-a-basement','6 Questions to Ask Yourself Before Remodeling a Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/71/e4352713b4496eef91c5f27b322ff57c','A basement remodel will go smoothly with these questions in mind.','<p><strong>6 Questions to Ask Yourself Before Remodeling a Basement</strong></p>\n<p><strong>How many of your neighbors have a remodeled basement?</strong></p>\n<p>Try to find out how many people in your neighborhood have recently remodeled a basement. You don&rsquo;t want to be the last house on the block with an outdated basement (or no basement at all) when your neighbors all have new basement remodels. Otherwise, your property value could be lowered.</p>\n<p><strong>When will the basement contractor be working?</strong></p>\n<p>Ask the basement contractor what hours their crew will be remodeling a basement. If you need them to begin at a special hour during certain days (due to work, children, etc.), then be sure to tell them. All basement contractors should be able to give you a starting date and an expected finishing date.</p>\n<p><strong>What is the Basement Contractor&rsquo;s Payment Schedule?</strong></p>\n<p>Always confirm how the basement contractor expects to be paid. Some will bill bi-weekly based on the amount of work done, some monthly, and some bill in milestone payments.</p>\n<p><strong>Does anyone in your home regularly exercise?</strong></p>\n<p>If so, consider a <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/gym/\">basement gym</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Do you live with children or teenagers?</strong></p>\n<p>If so, a <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/media-rooms/\">media room</a> can keep them entertained and contain all of their messes downstairs. Add a nearby <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/bathrooms/\">basement bathroom</a> and you can have the rest of the house to yourself again.</p>\n<p><strong>Will you be entertaining guests?</strong></p>\n<p>A <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/wet-bars/\">wet bar</a> or a <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/media-rooms/home-theaters/\">home theater</a> can serve as amazing settings for a houseful of guests.</p>',4,'',55,'2018-02-11 15:27:33'),(72,'3 Ideas to Lower Basement Remodeling Costs','A luxury basement remodel costs less with these basement remodeling ideas specifically designed to reduce basement remodeling costs!','basement remodeling costs, basement remodel costs, basement remodeling, basement remodel, basement remodeling companies, basement contractors, basement contractor','3-ideas-to-lower-basement-remodeling-costs','3 Ideas to Lower Basement Remodeling Costs','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/72/7e3ee89d8ea6c23b651a716e42700f53','A luxury basement remodel costs less with these basement remodeling ideas specifically designed to reduce basement remodeling costs!','<p><strong>3 Ideas to Lower Basement Remodeling Costs</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Basement remodeling costs </strong>can add up quickly if you aren&rsquo;t careful. Fortunately, a skilled basement contractor knows exactly how to keep the basement remodeling costs down. These simple considerations will prevent you from adding unnecessary basement remodel costs.</p>\n<p><strong>Get at Least 3 Quotes from Basement Contractors</strong></p>\n<p>The best way to save on basement remodeling costs is not to get overcharged. Getting at least three separate quotes from basement remodeling companies is a good way to establish a general idea of the costs involved. Don&rsquo;t choose a basement contractor who charges way more or way less than the other two.</p>\n<p><strong>Build Around Existing Infrastructure</strong></p>\n<p>If you are looking for an easy way to save money, then try to build around the existing electrical and plumbing sources if possible. If you already have the plumbing installed for an existing basement bathroom, for example, then upgrading around the existing infrastructure can save you money. &nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Choose the Right Type of Insulation</strong></p>\n<p>You may need to reinsulate your basement depending on where you live to pass code. Basement insulation has a numerical value called the <a href=\"https://energy.gov/energysaver/weatherize/insulation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">R-value</a>. The heavier the insulation, the higher its R-value.</p>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://codes.iccsafe.org/public/document/iecc2018/chapter-4-re-residential-energy-efficiency\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2018 International Residential Code</a> sets the minimum requirements for basement insulation based on your designated climate zone. Climate Zones 1 and 2 do not require insulation.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Climate Zone 3 requires R-5 insulation</li>\n<li>Climate Zone 4 requires R-10 insulation (except the Marine portion)</li>\n<li>Climate Zone 5 (and Climate Zone Marine 4) need R-15 insulation</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Check out this <a href=\"https://basc.pnnl.gov/images/iecc-climate-zone-map\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">climate zone graph</a> to see which climate zone you are in.</p>\n<p>Going with lower R-value insulation may cost less upfront, but it will ultimately retain less heat and may require your heating and cooling system to work harder in the long run. A professional basement contractor will run tests on your basement (like a blower door test) to measure the air flow in your basement and determine how much insulation is necessary.</p>',4,'',56,'2018-02-11 15:28:08'),(73,'Should You Remodel a Basement with a Universal Design?','Here’s how you can remodel a basement so that it can be enjoyed by every member of the family . . .','remodel a basement, basement remodeling, universal design','should-you-remodel-a-basement-with-a-universal-design','Should You Remodel a Basement with a Universal Design?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/73/a89f3ff1e1b7cf9c14ab070c6300d762','Here’s how you can remodel a basement so that it can be enjoyed by every member of the family...','<p><strong>Should You Remodel a Basement with a Universal Design?</strong></p>\n<p>There&rsquo;s a new trend sweeping basement remodeling, and it&rsquo;s called <a href=\"https://www.dol.gov/odep/topics/UniversalDesign.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Universal Design</a> remodeling. This is where the basement is made readily-accessible for all age groups, and it&rsquo;s a good idea if you have young children or the elderly sharing the same space. Here&rsquo;s how to remodel a basement using a Universal Design . . .</p>\n<p><strong>Basement Bathroom Remodeling</strong></p>\n<p>A basement bathroom remodel with a Universal Design will have easy-to-use &ldquo;lever&rdquo; faucet handles that require little pulling. Showers can be made without a curb for wheelchair access (and to prevent falling hazards). Detachable handheld shower wands can easily be used by those who are handicapped while sitting down.</p>\n<p><strong>Kitchenette Remodeling </strong></p>\n<p>Lowering the counters can give your kitchenette a Universal Design (a section of the counter can still be normal barstool height if desired).The cabinets and drawers should be especially easy to open and the faucets can have lever handles or even run on motion sensors. &nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Lighting Remodels</strong></p>\n<p>Remodeling your basement lighting is essential to providing a Universal Design. The goal is to make sure there is adequate lightning in high-traffic areas (especially on the stairs). Light switches and outlets should be accessible from a wheelchair, too.</p>\n<p><strong>Entranceways</strong></p>\n<p>All doorways should be wide enough for wheelchairs and baby strollers to easily fit through. Avoid doorways with small ledges and steps, as these could be falling hazards.</p>\n<p><strong>Basement Masters Understands Universal Design</strong></p>\n<p>Basement Masters understands your needs and can custom remodel a basement to incorporate the standard principles of Universal Design while looking stylish and sleek. Whether you are expecting children or just want to live in your home well into your senior years, Basement Masters will work with you to remodel a fantastic-looking basement that can be enjoyed during all phases of life. <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact us</a> to learn more about what true Universal Design can do for you and your loved ones.</p>',1,'',57,'2018-02-04 15:28:30'),(74,'Is Your Basement Ready for Winter?','Follow these steps to “winterize” your basement and reduce energy costs.','basement dehumidifier, cold basement','is-your-basement-ready-for-winter','Is Your Basement Ready for Winter?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/74/2ac9fd5eb6bbb2747bfbdc3a904d15ad','Follow these steps to \"winterize\" your basement and reduce energy costs.','<p><strong>Is Your Basement Ready for Winter?</strong></p>\n<p>You prepare your home for winter by having energy efficient windows, installing weather strips, and other common methods, but have you given any thought to your basement this year? It&rsquo;s one of the most important areas to get ready for winter.</p>\n<p>Your basement is where the HVAC system, pipes, furnace, water heater and other important utilities can be found. When the basement is cold, these utilities require more energy to properly function. So if you have an extra cold basement, you are adding to your electric bill.</p>\n<p>A cold basement also means the floor upstairs will be cold, too. This feels uncomfortable to walk on and also puts extra demand on your HVAC system.</p>\n<p>Meanwhile, cold air can also be getting through your basement windows. If you have a single-pane, steel-framed window, it&rsquo;s more likely to become rusty and let cold air through. Choose thicker glass with a better frame designed to keep out the harsh winter winds.</p>\n<p>The next step, after sealing your windows, is to insulate the walls. Basement wall insulation retains heat and gives your HVAC system a break. The less your HVAC system has to work, the cheaper your utility bills will be.</p>\n<p>A basement dehumidifier (designed for below-grade spaces) will further alleviate cold basement problems.</p>',4,'',58,'2018-01-28 15:28:45'),(75,'5 Trendy Basement Ideas for 2018','Basement design ideas are always changing – here’s what’s new in 2018!','basement design, basement design ideas, basement designer, basement floor plans with walk out basement, walk out basement, open concept basement design, basement remodeling','5-trendy-basement-ideas-for-2018','5 Trendy Basement Ideas for 2018','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/75/03ff11d49b2aa3dc11080dc22ddabca3','Basement design ideas are always changing – here’s what’s new in 2018!','<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>5 Trendy Basement Ideas for 2018</strong><br /><br />The right&nbsp;<strong>basement design ideas&nbsp;</strong>can transform your basement from a drab and underutilized space into a delightful extension of your home. If you are thinking of doing some basement remodeling soon, you might want to pay attention to these 5 basement design ideas. Here&rsquo;s what&rsquo;s hot in 2018:</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Open Concept Basement Design Continues to Trend</strong></p>\n<p>The most important trend of 2017,&nbsp;<strong>open concept basement design</strong>, will keep going throughout 2018. Rooms no longer have to be divided by physical walls; instead, different spaces can be delineated by wall colors and flooring options (luxury carpet cascading into luxury vinyl tiling, for example). Removing the walls maximizes the square footage of your basement as well.</p>\n<p>Open floor plans with a&nbsp;<a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/walk-outs/\">walk out basement</a>&nbsp;have a door leading outside, windows, and plenty of natural light, and they are especially popular with houses built on a slope. &nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/43/9d551f33f0afb906c337ba1d961a3c18_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>An open basement concept uses different flooring options in place of physical walls.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Basement Home Theater Vs. Family Rooms</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/media-rooms/\">Basement media rooms</a>&nbsp;can either be a casual family room or an exclusive home theater. A basement home theater has recessed LED lights, a projection screen, and other dramatic architecture like stadium seating and a basement tray ceiling. Since open basement concept design is so popular right now, many people are choosing open family rooms versus closed-off basement home theater rooms.</p>\n<p><strong>Music Rooms</strong></p>\n<p>Basements, not garages, are where most musicians are striking a tune in 2018. A small soundproofed room in your house makes for a great one-man music room to practice in. Choose a larger room if you have a band, and choose the biggest space in the basement if you want an auditorium!</p>\n<p><strong>Sports Bars More Popular Than Ever</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Many residents are converting a sizeable portion of their basement into a sports bar, where they can have guests over and get as loud as they want without bothering others in the home. Multiple televisions, an integrated surround sound system, and of course a well-stocked</p>\n<p><strong>Basement Spa and Gym</strong></p>\n<p>Who needs to pay membership fees when you have a great<a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/gym/\">&nbsp;basement gym</a>&nbsp;with modern equipment and all the latest amenities? Add a&nbsp;<a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/bathrooms/upgraded/\">steam shower</a>&nbsp;and sauna for the full spa effect!</p>\n<p><strong>Overall, Basement Design Ideas Are . . .</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Wide Open &ndash; Basement design in 2018 is all about maximizing space and efficiency. Open basement concept design allows you to create multi-purpose rooms that go far beyond mere storage ideas!</li>\n<li>Bright &ndash; Open floor plans with a walk out basement have see-through doors and windows to let as much light in as possible.</li>\n<li>Stylish and Comfortable &ndash; Basically, most basements are designed to feel exactly like an upstairs area and serve as an extension of the home!</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Get Basement Remodeling Ideas from Basement Masters</strong></p>\n<p>Working with Basement Masters means you&rsquo;ll get to implement all of your basement ideas with a professional basement designer. Your own personal basement designer assistant will walk you through the process and build upon your ideas! Contact us now to see why&nbsp;<a href=\"#\">Basement Masters</a>&nbsp;has the best basement remodeling ideas for 2018!</p>',1,'',59,'2018-01-28 15:28:57'),(76,'How to Find the Best Basement Waterproofing Companies (MD, DC & VA)','','','how-to-find-the-best-basement-waterproofing-companies-md-dc--va','How to Find the Best Basement Waterproofing Companies (MD, DC & VA)',NULL,'Finding the best waterproofing companies for your basement is easy with this guide!','<p><strong>How to Find the Best Basement Waterproofing Companies (MD, DC &amp; VA)<br /><br />Basement waterproofing </strong>is a labor-intensive task that needs to be done correctly the first time. Only the best waterproofing companies should be allowed to work near the foundation of your home &ndash; but deciding who to hire is not always easy, especially if you are in a hurry. Follow these steps to find the best waterproofing companies.</p>\n<p><strong>Go With Basement Contractors </strong></p>\n<p>A waterproofing company that only sometimes works on basements is not good enough &ndash; you want basement contractors who focus on this specific area of the house every day. If you&rsquo;re having moisture problems in the basement, then it only makes sense to rely on specialized basement contractors.</p>\n<p><strong>Experience is Key</strong></p>\n<p>The best basement waterproofing companies have been around for at least 10 years, but even this is not enough. Look for a team page outlining how many years of experience each basement contractor has. This will keep you from hiring a basement waterproofing company that has been around for a long time, but suffers from a high turnover rate (which, in turn, can affect craftmanship and cause delays). &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Reviews Matter</strong></p>\n<p>Check the reviews for a basement waterproofing company by going on websites like <a href=\"https://www.angieslist.com/companylist/us/md/rockville/basement-masters-reviews-2346351.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AngiesList</a> and <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BasementMasters/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a>. When you speak with the waterproofing company, ask if they&rsquo;ve ever operated under a different company name and, if so, check for reviews under that name as well. The best waterproofing companies will have a good reputation with the <a href=\"https://www.bbb.org/washington-dc-eastern-pa/business-reviews/basement-remodeling/basement-masters-in-rockville-md-236009263\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Better Business Bureau</a>. &nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Complete Repair Jobs</strong></p>\n<p>The best basement waterproofing companies will do a complete repair job themselves. They will not make you hire additional basement contractors to complete simple tasks such as removing framework, drywall or plumbing. The best basement companies will always do a full clean-up job themselves after they are finished waterproofing the basement.</p>\n<p><strong>Get Basement Waterproofing (Foundational Waterproofing) With Basement Masters</strong></p>\n<p>Basement Masters has been in business since 2006 and provides expert waterproofing services in MD (Baltimore and surrounding counties), Washington DC, and VA. We are fully licensed in MD, DC, and VA and have the experience, connections, and permits to fully remodel your basement beyond expectations. When you are ready for professional waterproofing services, <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">contact</a> Basement Masters in Rockville, Maryland today!</p>',4,'',60,'2018-01-21 15:29:14'),(77,'When\'s the Best Time of Year for Basement Waterproofing?','Does it matter what time of the year it is when waterproofing a basement? Is it better to do it during a certain season? Learn more here.','basement waterproofing, waterproofing a basement, basement contractor, basement contractors, basement waterproofing MD, basement waterproofing Baltimore, basement waterproofing VA, basement waterproofing VA, basement waterproofing blog, basement remodeling blog','whens-the-best-time-of-year-for-basement-waterproofing','When\'s the Best Time of Year for Basement Waterproofing?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/77/fac73be709be620bf94e1cb83b470a7c','Is there an optimal time during the year to waterproof your basement?','<h2><strong>When is the Best Time of Year for Basement Waterproofing?</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Waterproofing a basement </strong>revolves around the weather. There are numerous ways to fix a basement crack, for example, but the weather will determine how many of them are available. Basement contractors are most affected by rain and cold weather when waterproofing a basement.</p>\n<h3><strong>Rainy Weather and Basement Waterproofing</strong></h3>\n<p>One method of waterproofing is to excavate (dig around) a foundation to make water flow away from the home. However, rainy weather can make some soils and clays practically impossible to work in when excavating. In addition, coating a foundation with a waterproof solution does not work well in the rain.</p>\n<p>Likewise, applying an epoxy crack injection to fix a basement wall in the rain is not very effective.</p>\n<h3><strong>Cold Weather and Basement Waterproofing</strong></h3>\n<p>If the weather gets cold enough, epoxy and polyurethane injections will take a longer time to bind to a crack. When it gets frozen outside, it can sometimes increase the chance of a cave-in during excavations. If the ground is covered in enough snow, there may not be any room to place piles of soil during excavations.</p>\n<p>Warm weather is best for basement waterproofing, but BasementRemodeling.com provides waterproofing services in throughout MD (including Baltimore), VA and DC. <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact us</a> for more information about wintertime waterproofing and learn about the extra steps BasementRemodeling.com takes every year to stay ahead of the weather!</p>',3,'',61,'2018-01-21 15:29:29'),(78,'Concrete Foundation Waterproofing, Explained','Wondering what concrete foundation waterproofing is or what\'s involved in the process? Find out here.','concrete foundation waterproofing, waterproofing, basement waterproofing, wet basement, damp basement, basement blog, basement waterproofing blog','concrete-foundation-waterproofing-explained','Concrete Foundation Waterproofing, Explained','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/78/86b3907cd510c24b1f18564b84aab535','What is concrete foundation waterproofing?','<h2><strong>Concrete Foundation Waterproofing&mdash;What is it?</strong></h2>\n<p>Concrete foundation waterproofing keeps the basement dry and ensures that your house can support its own weight. Finished or not, wet and damp basements can erode the concrete foundation as well as cause mold (along with unpleasant odors and unsightly stains). Since concrete itself is not waterproof, concrete foundation waterproofing is often a necessary step in regular home maintenance.</p>\n<h3><strong>How It Works</strong></h3>\n<p>Concrete foundation waterproofing can be performed in a variety of different ways. Since wet soil can become loose and cause the concrete foundation to shift, the goal is usually to keep water from pooling around or underneath your home. There are many different <a href=\"https://www.angieslist.com/articles/comparing-basement-waterproofing-methods.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">waterproofing methods</a> to choose from, but the general principles are almost always the same:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Install drains to keep water from pooling around the concrete foundation</li>\n<li>Treat the walls (either interior or exterior) to prevent water from entering the home</li>\n<li>If possible, alter the topography of the land through digging so that water flows away from the concrete foundation</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For more about waterproofing solutions (and their costs), <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">contact</a> BasementRemodeling.com in Rockville, Maryland today.</p>',3,'',62,'2018-01-21 15:29:42'),(79,'Five Features Your Egress Window Needs','These five egress window ideas will keep your basement looking tidy and charming all year long!','egress window, egress window ideas, basement egress window, egress window features, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','five-features-your-egress-window-needs','Five Features Your Egress Window Needs','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/79/b2dd1a84932c76227dba8e4abe018f48','These egress window ideas will keep your basement looking tidy and charming all year long!','<p>A good basement egress window needs to be structurally sound in addition to being visually pleasing. Here are five basement egress window ideas that you should implement as soon as possible.</p>\n<h2><strong>Grind and Core the Corners<br /></strong></h2>\n<p>Basement contractors tend to use a concrete saw to cut an opening for the window into the foundation wall. However, the round cutting blade means that they will overcut, and these deep cuts can crack and leak overtime. Instead of overcutting with a concrete saw, professional basement contractors first core the corners of the wall and then cut a 90-degree angle with a grinder. This is a more precise way of cutting into the concrete that will not promote leaks or cracks.</p>\n<h2><strong>Metal Liners for Window Wells</strong></h2>\n<p>Metal window well liners can prevent wet soil from expanding and pressing against the foundation walls. When wet soil expands, it can create cracks in the foundation from the pressure. Plastic window well liners are cheaper than metal window well liners, but they tend to crack and shift over time.</p>\n<h2><strong>Pick the Right Window</strong></h2>\n<p>A window casement can be specifically designed with a basement egress in mind. These have quick-snapping levers instead of a crank; they also swing open wide like a door for an easy escape. Vinyl-framed windows require the least maintenance and will not rust like steel-framed windows.</p>\n<h2><strong>Well Drains<br /></strong></h2>\n<p>Installing a drain outside of the egress window will prevent the well from filling with water and breaking the glass, leaving you with a flooded basement and a messy cleanup.</p>\n<h2><strong>Privacy Covers</strong></h2>\n<p>A strong privacy cover with a translucent lid will keep your children and pets from falling down the well, and also keep prying eyes from seeing into your basement area.</p>',1,'',63,'2018-01-14 15:29:55'),(80,'How to Dry Carpet in the Basement Yourself','Wet carpet in the basement can be saved in you act fast.','How to dry carpet in basement, basement flood','how-to-dry-carpet-in-the-basement-yourself','How to Dry Carpet in the Basement Yourself','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/80/51632d2aab6997585714c31dd78cd64d','Wet carpet from a basement flood can be saved if you act fast.','<p><strong>How to Dry Carpet in the Basement Yourself</strong></p>\n<p>If you have a basement flood and the source of the water is clean (not from the sewage system or appliance drain water), then you can probably dry the basement carpet yourself (though not always the pad). Here&rsquo;s how to dry carpet in basement that&rsquo;s been damaged by floodwaters.</p>\n<p>If the basement flood is from a burst pipe, shut off the water. Shut off the electricity before you step foot on the basement carpet to protect yourself from shock. Unplug everything from the wall and get all power cords and surge strips off the floor.</p>\n<p>Instead of a wet vacuum, try to rent an extractor &mdash; they are much more effective at removing water from the carpet &mdash; and rent a commercial dehumidifier, too. Use the extractor until all of the excess water has been removed.</p>\n<p>Roll back the carpet carefully and remove the wet pad underneath. You can cut this pad into strips and let it dry in your driveway or you can simply buy a new one to install.</p>\n<p>Go back inside and lay the carpet back down. Turn on the dehumidifier and set the temperature downstairs to 75 degrees or less. Anything higher encourages bacterial growth on the basement carpet.</p>\n<p>If any of the appliances in your basement were submerged in water, contact an electrician and have them inspected before plugging them back in.</p>\n<p>Hopefully, if you perform all of these steps within 72 hours of the initial basement flood, you will stop mold from growing on the carpet and can have it reinstalled.</p>',4,'',64,'2018-01-07 15:30:09'),(81,'4 Reasons Winter Is Best For Basement Remodeling','Here’s why winter is the best season for basement remodeling.','Basement remodeling, basement remodeling contractors, basement contractors','4-reasons-winter-is-best-for-basement-remodeling','4 Reasons Winter Is Best For Basement Remodeling','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/81/6ee3bbd07311027422dc6fee4b69ce16','Here’s why winter is the perfect season for basement remodeling.','<p><strong>4 Reasons Winter Is Best For Basement Remodeling</strong></p>\n<p>Winter is a time for friends, family . . . and basement remodeling! Contractors are ready to accommodate all of your luxury basement remodeling needs this winter. Here&rsquo;s why you should let them.</p>\n<p><strong>Winter Discounts</strong></p>\n<p>Manufacturers tend to raise prices on important basement remodeling materials such as lumber, windows and cabinetry during the warm seasons. Conversely, these prices tend to come down during the winter (and your basement contractor may be able to pass these savings onto you). If you are looking to add a kitchen-like wet bar or laundry room, appliances tend to cost less during the winter.</p>\n<p><strong>Faster Permits &amp; Inspections</strong></p>\n<p>Since there is less outdoor construction going on during the winter in general, local government agencies tend review and approve permits and inspections a lot faster than in the warmer months.</p>\n<p><strong>Ready By Spring</strong></p>\n<p>Starting a basement remodeling project in the winter means you&rsquo;ll have a remodeled basement well in-advance of the warmer seasons &mdash; so when when the weather gets warm and you are looking for a luxurious place to entertain guests and cool off, your basement will be fully ready for all parties to enjoy!</p>\n<p><strong>Potentially Better Contractor Availability</strong></p>\n<p>Contractors tend to have less exterior work in the winter and more time to dedicate to your basement remodeling project. Dedicated basement remodeling companies, on the other hand, tend to stay busy year-round and may experience no change in availability (or quality of service) during the winter months.</p>\n<p><strong>Get Your Basement Remodeled This Winter With Basement Masters</strong></p>\n<p>With over ten years in business and counting, Basement Masters knows the ins and outs of basement remodeling. We are a veteran collection of expert basement contractors who have skillfully created many residential and business basements. Contact Basement Masters today to see what this winter holds in store for your downstairs!</p>',1,'',65,'2018-01-07 15:30:20'),(82,'How to Finish An Unfinished Basement So It’s Livable','Just how much work goes into finishing an unfinished basement? Learn more here.','Finishing an finished basement, how to finish a basement, how to make an unfinished basement livable, basement contractors, finished basement ideas, basement finish, finish basement ideas, basement ideas, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','how-to-finish-an-unfinished-basement-so-its-livable','How to Finish An Unfinished Basement So It’s Livable','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/82/3c2aa54cfa6469e606f4ec0d57d88997','Just how much work goes into finishing an unfinished basement?','<p><strong>How to Finish An Unfinished Basement So It&rsquo;s Livable</strong></p>\n<p>You want to know how to finish an unfinished basement and you&rsquo;re also wondering what do you need to finish a basement, too. If you want to now how to make an unfinished basement livable, here is what you have to do.</p>\n<p><strong>Basement Documentation</strong></p>\n<p>Before you can do any basement finishing, you have to get your plans approved by local government. You must submit to them a copy (or sometimes multiple copies) of your site plans. This is a clear outline of the proposed basement plans on a piece of graph paper which clearly shows all necessary measurements.</p>\n<p>Your local city planner can go over the necessary requirements in person or over the phone. You should at the very list look up the site plan requirements online for your county and state before submitting them.</p>\n<p><strong>Basement Permits</strong><br /><br />Next you need to apply for the appropriate permits. At the very least you will need a local building permit to begin construction, and if you are going to be doing electrical, plumbing or HVAC work, then you will need an electrical, plumbing or mechanical permits as well (and probably a license, too. Otherwise you must hire a contractor with the appropriate license to do the installation).</p>\n<p><strong>Basement Inspections</strong></p>\n<p>You should remain in close contact with the basement inspector during the whole finishing process. Don&rsquo;t hesitate to contact them by phone or email with questions and suggestions for staying up to code. Extra inspections, however, will cost you in fines and delays, so be sure to have everything in place before the inspector comes!</p>\n<p><strong>Wall Framing</strong></p>\n<p>Framing your basement means installing the walls and floors. There are many different ways to frame a wall (in-place, floating, etc.) and they each depend on the ground soil conditions as well as other environmental and economic factors.</p>\n<p><strong>Plumbing</strong></p>\n<p>Unless you are familiar with taking a jackhammer to concrete, you should not attempt to do this on your own in most cases.</p>\n<p><strong>Electrical Wiring</strong></p>\n<p>Wiring a basement requires expert knowledge of both electrical components and local ordinances and codes. Faulty wiring is obviously dangerous and wiring that does not meet code will need to be removed and reinstalled, so most people hire a basement contractor to get it right the first time.<br />Hanging Drywall</p>\n<p>Surprisingly, hanging drywall over the exposed electrical wiring is one of the most technical parts of the job. Basement contractors spend decades learning to hang drywall appropriate and in a uniform layout. Any blemish is glaringly visible on the final product, so if you don&rsquo;t know the difference between mudding and taping dry wall, then now probably isn&rsquo;t a good time to learn as you go.</p>\n<p><strong>The End Result</strong></p>\n<p>At this point, you&rsquo;ve probably got some painting and staining left to do, but you&rsquo;ve succeeded in making your finished basement livable and up to code. However, if drafting site plans, pulling permits, doing heavy duty plumbing, electrical and mechanical installations and hanging drywall on your own sounds a little too difficult, then don&rsquo;t hesitate to contact basement contractors.</p>',4,'',66,'2018-01-07 15:30:34'),(83,'8 Pros and Cons of Having a Basement','See all of the major basement pros and cons before deciding if adding a basement is right for you.','Pros and cons of having a basement, basement pros and cons, basement contractors, basement remodeling','8-pros-and-cons-of-having-a-basement','8 Pros and Cons of Having a Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/83/cea3504ae5cdaad657e54d647a066d67','See all of the major basement pros and cons before deciding if adding a basement is right for you.','<p><strong>8 Pros and Cons of Having a Basement</strong></p>\n<p>A home basement has many pros and cons that need to be weighed heavily before deciding. Here are the main pros and cons of having a basement.</p>\n<p><strong>Pros of Having a Basement:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>More space &ndash; Adding a basement can double the amount of available floor space without sacrificing any outdoor property. A basement can add value to the home and is especially useful for growing families.</li>\n<li>New entrances &ndash; If your house is built on a natural slope, a basement remodeling company can easily carve a beautiful <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/walk-outs/\">walk out basement</a> that uses the natural geography to your advantage.</li>\n<li>Seasonal comfort &ndash; Basements have a tendency to stay warmer in the winter and cooler in the summer.</li>\n<li>Easy repair access &ndash; Workers won&rsquo;t have to crawl on their hands and knees to repair utilities with a basement foundation.</li>\n<li>Emergency shelter &ndash; If you live in an area with hurricanes, tornados or other natural disasters, having a basement can offer emergency protection.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Cons of Having a Basement</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Expense &ndash; Basements require digging at least eight-feet underground and adding a concrete slab at the bottom. It is more expensive than crawlspaces and aboveground slab foundations.</li>\n<li>Flooding &ndash; Basement moisture can cause damage and expensive repairs. Areas with a high water table will have a lot of trouble adding a basement.</li>\n<li>Finding professionals &ndash; You don&rsquo;t want to hire just any company when adding a basement to your home. Sometimes it can be hard to find basement contractors in your area who are well-qualified and available. Of course, if you live in Maryland, Washington DC, or Virginia, call Basement Masters to handle all of your <a href=\"../../../../\">basement remodeling</a> needs!</li>\n</ul>',4,'',67,'2017-12-24 15:30:46'),(84,'5 Must-Read Basement Maintenance Tips','Following these simple basement maintenance tips now will help prevent a leaking basement in the future!','basement maintenance, how to keep a basement dry, leaking basement, water in basement, basement seepage, basement contractor','5-must-read-basement-maintenance-tips','5 Must-Read Basement Maintenance Tips','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/84/8d36ed7f038c7b06b5ebb1083effdefa','Following these simple basement maintenance tips now will help prevent a leaking basement in the future!','<p><strong>5 Must-Read Basement Maintenance Tips</strong></p>\n<p>Water in the basement can cause structural damage and ruin precious valuables like yearbooks and photo albums, so knowing how to keep the basement dry is key. Fortunately, there are some simple basement maintenance rules that can stop scenarios like water coming up through the basement floor and walls before they get a chance to happen.</p>\n<p><strong>Puddles Are Bad</strong></p>\n<p>Keeping the basement dry surprisingly starts outside of your home. The next time your area receives a good rain, walk along the perimeter around the house afterwards and see if the water puddles near the foundation. Water should always flow away from your house and never towards it, where it can enter the home and cause basement seepage.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/42/b283933cae6cea839c78cc774df2d124_624x350.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"350\" /><br /><em>Puddles along the side of your house could indicate water in the basement.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Drain Pipes &amp; The 5-Foot Rule </strong></p>\n<p>The EPA urges homeowners to make sure their drain pipes are long enough to carry rainwater away from the home. If your gutters are not carrying the rainwater at least <a href=\"https://www.epa.gov/mold/text-version-mold-house-tour\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">5 feet away</a> from the foundation of your home, then they are not adequately doing their job.</p>\n<p><strong>Clean Your Gutters</strong></p>\n<p>Not many people realize that something on their roof can be causing water in the basement. If your gutters are full of leaves, then the rainwater is being dumped on the soil around your foundation instead of being carried away by your drain pipe. This can erode the soil from under the foundation and cause instability.</p>\n<p><strong>Clean Window Wells</strong></p>\n<p>Sometimes a leaking basement can be traced back to the window wells. Keep all window wells free of debris and water by periodically cleaning them out. You can even install a clear panel to let light in and keep debris and water out. These can often be found at your local hardware store.</p>\n<p><strong>Look For Foundation Cracks</strong></p>\n<p>Cracks in the basement walls could indicate serious structural and basement seepage problems. These problems need to be looked at by a licensed basement contractor as soon as possible. &nbsp;</p>',4,'',68,'2017-12-24 15:32:07'),(85,'What Color Should You Paint the Basement Walls?','If you’ve been asking yourself “what color should I paint the basement walls” lately, this quick guide will surely help narrow down your options.','Bright colors for basement walls, dark basement, best colors for basement walls, basement lighting ideas','what-color-should-you-paint-the-basement-walls','What Color Should You Paint the Basement Walls?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/85/376d009f0043759f8908beacca3902cd','If you’ve been asking yourself “what color should I paint the basement walls” lately, this quick guide will surely help narrow down your options.','<p><strong>What Color Should You Paint the Basement Walls?</strong></p>\n<p>It&rsquo;s 2017 and owning a dreadfully dark basement with wood paneling is thankfully a thing of the past. Now experimenting with&nbsp;<strong>bright colors for basement walls </strong>has become the norm, but choosing the very best colors still largely depends on the architecture of the basement itself. If you&rsquo;ve been asking yourself &ldquo;what color should I paint the basement walls&rdquo; lately, this quick guide will surely help narrow down your options.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/40/7a1955ca906e541e94e191bd0f75b649_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" />Bright colors for basements can be stylishly exciting and unusual!</em></p>\n<p><strong>How to Determine the Best Colors for Basement Walls</strong></p>\n<p>A dark basement can always be cheered up with bright colors, but choosing the best colors for basement walls mostly depends on the lighting:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Yellow paint reflects natural light the best. If you have a walk out basement or plenty of windows, then yellow paint will successfully brighten the atmosphere nicely. Without natural light, however, certain shades of yellow tend to fall flat.</li>\n<li>Avoid shiny paints for the basement. Although they reflect light better, Eggshell and Ulti-matte finishes look better on drywall.</li>\n<li>Matching your walls with your trim can make the basement look bigger and brighter, but only choose bright colors.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>When Are Bright Colors for Basements Not the Best Idea?</strong></p>\n<p>Shadows are the enemy of bright colors. Shadows can make even a fresh coat of bright paint look dirty and old instantly. This problem can always be corrected with the appropriate <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/lighting/\">basement lighting ideas</a>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/41/928820159c0d1b760252d4a8b5c71e95_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" />You can keep your colors crisp and shadows at bay with different basement lighting ideas.</em></p>',1,'',69,'2017-12-17 15:32:20'),(86,'4 Tips to Prepare Your Home for a Basement Remodel','Here are four essential tips to help you prepare your home for an upcoming basement remodel project.','basement remodeling, basement remodel, basement contractors, basement contractor','4-tips-to-prepare-your-home-for-a-basement-remodel','4 Tips to Prepare Your Home for a Basement Remodel','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/86/e9e0ea9bb27bf5eec3c23df5b0f7af3b','These expert tips will make sure your next basement remodel goes smoothly and keep everyone’s worrying at a minimum!','<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Communicate</strong></h2>\n<p>The best basement remodelers will have a project manager or a liaison within close reach. Make sure they have the best contact numbers for you and anyone else in the family who is involved. This includes phone numbers and emails.</p>\n<h2><strong>Remove Belongings From the Basement</strong></h2>\n<p>Most of your basement possessions should be packed up before the basement contractors arrive. All furniture, pictures, mirrors, and other breakables should be in another area of the home. If you&rsquo;ve moved your belongings to an adjacent room, make sure they are not by the walls.</p>\n<h2><strong>Create Walking Paths to Important Areas</strong></h2>\n<p>If your basement does not have a separate entrance, then the basement company will have to enter through another part of the home. They will lay plastic covering over this walkway to protect the floor and keep the house nice and tidy, but you can help the basement contractors move freely by keeping this area free of any clutter.</p>\n<h2><strong>Dust Control</strong></h2>\n<p>Basement remodelers use protective plastic around doorways and cover all furnishings to protect them from dust. Keeping the door to your basement closed during the basement remodeling hours will make sure the dust does not spread to other areas of your home. You also may want to turn off the central air during certain steps (like sanding) to keep the dust from going through the ventilation system into other parts of the home.</p>',4,'',70,'2017-12-10 15:32:32'),(87,'How to Clean a Concrete Basement Floor in 3 Steps','A quick how-to guide for a clean basement floor!','how to clean a concrete basement floor, basement floor, concrete basement floor','how-to-clean-a-concrete-basement-floor-in-3-steps','How to Clean a Concrete Basement Floor in 3 Steps','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/87/efc30e542e538875dea7db4b8985dce5','A quick how-to guide for a clean basement floor!','<p><strong>How to Clean a Concrete Basement Floor in 3 Steps</strong></p>\n<p>If you want to know how to clean a concrete basement floor with visible grime, here&rsquo;s what you&rsquo;ll need:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cleaning solution (detergent)</li>\n<li>&frac14; cup ammonia</li>\n<li>A bucket of water (warm)</li>\n<li>A nylon brush (stiff bristles)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>And here&rsquo;s how to clean a concrete basement floor:</p>\n<p>1.) Mix the detergent, ammonia and warm water together<br />2.) Apply the solution to the basement floor<br />3.) Vigorously scrub the surface with the nylon brush until the area is clean</p>\n<p>NOTE: A brush with metallic fibers can dislodge in the concrete and rust, leaving marks.</p>\n<p>If your basement has a musty smell, then you may have a mildew problem that needs some extra steps. Here&rsquo;s how to clean a concrete basement floor with mildew and mold problems. You&rsquo;ll need:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Household Bleach</li>\n<li>Water</li>\n<li>A spray bottle</li>\n<li>A nylon brush (stiff bristles)</li>\n<li>Fans</li>\n<li>A dehumidifier (optional)&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>1.) Open the basement windows for proper ventilation<br />2.) Turn on fans to further circulate fresh air<br />3.) Install the dehumidifier to take moisture out of the air, giving mold less opportunity to grow<br />4.) Mix 2 ounces of bleach per quart of water into the spray bottle<br />5.) Spray the floor (and walls if needed) with the mixture<br />6.) Scrub clean with a stiff nylon brush</p>\n<p>Alternatively, you could try this trick.&nbsp; You&rsquo;ll need:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bleaching powder (chlorinated lime)</li>\n<li>A vacuum or broom</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Bleaching powder can be found in the laundry aisle of any supermarket. All you need to do is to lightly sprinkle an even layer of bleaching powder on the basement floor, let it sit for 24 hours, and sweep or vacuum the powder away. This substance could potentially become a breathing hazard if left around for longer than a day, so be sure to throw it away in a trashcan outside immediately after getting it off the floor.</p>',4,'',71,'2017-12-10 15:32:45'),(88,'4 Great Basement Storage Ideas Under the Stairs','4 great ideas for basement storage under the stairs!','under stairs storage ideas, basement storage ideas','4-great-basement-storage-ideas-under-the-stairs','4 Great Basement Storage Ideas Under the Stairs','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/88/bebbabd38fbed1f5a095179713006cfe','4 basement ideas for storage under the stairs!','<p>If you can&rsquo;t figure out what to do with the basement area under your stairs, you&rsquo;re not alone. Fortunately, Basement Masters has put together some great <strong>under stairs storage ideas</strong>!</p>\n<p><strong>Hide the Washer</strong></p>\n<p>This bulky appliance doesn&rsquo;t have to take up precious space when you put it under the stairs. If you have a stacked washer and dryer combo, then you don&rsquo;t have to devote any more space to a laundry room!</p>\n<p><strong>Extra Kitchenette Space</strong></p>\n<p>If you have a kitchenlike area, then under the stairs can be where your fridge or wine cabinet goes. Add a few shelves and it can even be used as a makeshift pantry.</p>\n<p><strong>Seating</strong></p>\n<p>A padded bench under the stairs and a bookshelf or CD rack can transform this area into a cozy and relaxing nook.</p>\n<p><strong>Pet Den</strong></p>\n<p>This same padded area can become a private den for your cats or dogs to nestle together and catch some quality rest.</p>',1,'',72,'2017-12-03 15:32:58'),(89,'The 5 Best Basement Flooring Options (Pros and Cons)','Pros and cons of the best basement flooring options.','Flooring pros and cons, basement flooring, basement flooring options, below grade flooring options, LVT flooring pros and cons, laminate flooring pros and cons','the-5-best-basement-flooring-options-pros-and-cons','The 5 Best Basement Flooring Options (Pros and Cons)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/89/a119c6c70e297e7765f2314d01350dc8','Pros and cons of the best basement flooring options.','<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>The 5 Best Basement Flooring Options (Pros and Cons)</strong></p>\n<p>The quick-reference guide covers the five <strong>best flooring options for basements</strong> everywhere!</p>\n<p><strong>LVT Flooring (Pros and Cons)</strong></p>\n<p>Luxury vinyl tile (LVT) flooring is a beautiful basement flooring option that can mimic many different textured surfaces such as wood and stone without carrying an absorbant cost. LVT is very easy to install (snapping in place or else glued), resistant to water, and difficult to scoff. However, LVT flooring does not last as long as some other flooring options like ceramic tiling. &nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Laminate Flooring (Pros and Cons)</strong></p>\n<p>Basement laminate flooring is a synthetic material that can look like wood, stone, or ceramic tile. It is cheaper than LVT, scratch and stain resistant, and can be easily cleaned with a damp cloth when needed. However, this flooring option is not resistant to water and does not add as much value to the home as ceramic tile or stone.</p>\n<p><strong>Ceramic Tile (Pros and Cons)</strong></p>\n<p>Ceramic tile installs easily over concrete, looks elegant, and lasts virtually forever if well-maintained. Basement condensation can make the ceramic tiles slippery, however, but this can be offset with an anti-slip glazed finish. If the ceramic tile is ever damaged, it can be quite expensive to repair or replace.</p>\n<p><strong>Basement Carpet (Pros and Cons)</strong></p>\n<p>Carpet can add a limited degree of warmth and soundproofing to a basement. It&rsquo;s also one of the cheapest <strong>below grade flooring options </strong>and can be very durable if well-maintained. On the other hand, carpets capture dust and can harvest mold; as such, carpets can&rsquo;t get damp and aren&rsquo;t always the best choice.</p>\n<p><strong>Concrete (Pros and Cons)</strong></p>\n<p>Concrete can be painted or stained for a cheap and visually-pleasing effect. It is good for areas of the basement that receive little foot traffic such as storage rooms. On the downside, concrete usually needs to be repainted or re-stained every 3-5 years.</p>',1,'',73,'2017-12-03 15:33:11'),(90,'What is the Difference Between Vinyl and Laminate Flooring?','Luxury vinyl vs laminate flooring – which is better?','difference between vinyl and laminate flooring, vinyl vs laminate, hardwood vs laminate, luxury vinyl tile pros and cons, laminate flooring pros and cons, luxury vinyl vs laminate, lvt flooring, lvt','what-is-the-difference-between-vinyl-and-laminate-flooring','What is the Difference Between Vinyl and Laminate Flooring?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/90/bb210a57a289e5d829d4a4ef06a511b8','Luxury vinyl vs laminate flooring – which is better?','<p><strong>What is the Difference Between Vinyl and Laminate Flooring?</strong></p>\n<p>Vinyl and laminate flooring are commonly used in many different basement remodeling designs, but what&rsquo;s the difference, and which is better? Let&rsquo;s take an in-depth look at the luxury vinyl vs laminate flooring debate to see what material is better for basement remodeling. &nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>LVT (Luxury Vinyl Tiling) Flooring: Pros and Cons</strong></p>\n<p>Pros</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Flexible and resilient</li>\n<li>Does not scratch or dent easily</li>\n<li>Does not expand or contract with the weather (which causes cracks)</li>\n<li>Can get absolutely soaked and not warp</li>\n<li>The vinyl plank flooring is much more durable vs laminate flooring and lasts up to 15 years</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Cons</p>\n<ul>\n<li>More expensive than laminate flooring</li>\n<li>Needs time for glue to dry after installation</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Laminate Flooring: Pros and Cons</strong></p>\n<p>Pros</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cheaper than LVT flooring</li>\n<li>Literally snaps in place for a quick installation</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Cons</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Can&rsquo;t get wet</li>\n<li>Cannot be installed in basements with even a remote chance of flooding</li>\n<li>Cannot be installed in basements with any humidity (because of warping)</li>\n<li>Needs to be replaced after about a decade</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Luxury Vinyl Tiling vs Laminate Flooring: Which is Better?</strong></p>\n<p>Both materials look nearly identical to traditional hardwood floors. Aside from the initial upfront cost, LVT flooring wins against laminate in all other categories. Plus, when you use LVT flooring, it lasts longer than laminate flooring, which means you usually get your money back in the long run.</p>\n<p>When it comes to basement remodeling, there&rsquo;s nothing wrong with using laminate flooring to save on the budget. Otherwise, go with LVT.</p>',1,'',74,'2017-11-26 15:33:22'),(91,'4 Practical Solutions for a Cold Basement','Cold weather makes for a cold basement, but these cold basement solutions will keep you and your family warm throughout the winter!','cold basement, cold basement solutions, basement contractors, basement remodeling company, basement finishing, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement remodeling blog','4-practical-solutions-for-a-cold-basement','4 Practical Solutions for a Cold Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/91/240190b6a0e60e71bc58f7b9ed327cb3','Cold weather makes for a cold basement, but these cold basement solutions will keep you and your family warm throughout the winter!','<div class=\"html\">\n<div class=\"h1\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>4 Practical Solutions for a Cold Basement</strong></div>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A&nbsp;<strong>cold basement</strong>&nbsp;will never keep you from enjoying every last bit of your home again once you\'ve implemented these cold<strong> basement solutions</strong>. These effective cold basement solutions are brought to you by the expert basement contractors at Basement Remodeling Company, a leading finishing and remodeling company based in Rockville, MD since 2006. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Fireplaces</strong></h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If it&rsquo;s just a tad too cold, then a <strong>basement fireplace </strong>can heat up a single room or a small portion of an open design nicely. Basement fireplaces can be gas or electric. This is usually the most affordable heating option as far as solutions go.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/39/75cbc40cd23f0816390a24dd58a10014_624x415.png\" alt=\"A basement fireplace can really boost the heat of not only the downstairs, but the entire home as well. \" width=\"624\" height=\"415\" /><br /><em>Browse our wide variety of <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/fireplaces/\">basement fireplaces ideas</a>.</em>&nbsp;</p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Cold Air Return</strong></h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A cold air return in the basement is a special type of wall grill that lets air easily flow back to the furnace to be reheated. When it comes to installing a basement cold air return, placement matters. A basement cold air return that&rsquo;s close to the floor will ensure that warm continuously flows over the floor, which is the coldest part of a basement &ndash; so the lower they are installed, the better.</p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Basement Insulation</strong></h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Depending on the geographical climate of your location, installing extra insulation can help offset heat loss. Even basic door and window weatherstripping can keep warm air inside of your basement as well as plugging basic drafts. Sometimes installing basement insulation is not cost-effective, so it depends on the amount of insulation needed.</p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Waterproofing</strong></h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Aside from fixing and preventing leaks, <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/waterproofing/\">waterproofing the basement</a> also ensures that there are no cracks for outside air to get in. This improves the quality of your air and also keeps your basement at the desired temperature year-round.</p>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Get Cold Basement Solutions With Basement Remodeling Company</strong></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If you have a cold basement, solutions are available. Contact us today to speak to a live representative and receive a free basement quote.</p>\n</div>',4,'',75,'2017-11-26 15:33:41'),(92,'Is Basement Insulation Important?','Just how important is basement insulation? Is it something you can scrimp on or do you need to do it? Here\'s what you need to know.','basement insulation, insulating a basement, basement exterior walls, basement interior walls, basement interior, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement remodeling blog','is-basement-insulation-important','Is Basement Insulation Important?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/92/80f8369d98e2f4ddb85eabcaf2d5f260','Find out when basement insulation is important and when you can forget about it.','<p>The <strong>basement</strong> often tends to get overlooked when it comes to <strong>insulation </strong>even though it can be beneficial to many homes. The EPA, for example, thinks that anyone living in a &ldquo;<a href=\"https://www.energystar.gov/index.cfm?c=home_sealing.hm_improvement_insulation_table\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Zone 5</a>&rdquo; or colder location should get their basement insulated to save on energy costs. Basically, the colder your region is, the more money you will save by insulating your home.</p>\n<p>With that said, insulating your basement only works when the rest of your house is well-insulated. If you have drafts coming in from other areas of your home, you should get those fixed first. Otherwise, the heat (and the savings) will escape.</p>\n<h2><strong>Insulating Exterior Walls</strong></h2>\n<p>Insulating the exterior walls of your basement keeps the foundation heated and dry, which eliminates water condensation and therefore mold and mildew. Exterior insulation will not reduce the square footage of the basement (interior insulation will).</p>\n<p>If you are constructing a new home and live in a colder area, then you should insulate your interior walls. If you already live there, don&rsquo;t insulate the exterior walls. The process is lengthy and will take a long time to earn your money back through energy savings (depending, of course, on which basement contractors you choose).</p>\n<h2><strong>Insulating the Basement Ceiling</strong></h2>\n<p>Insulating the ceiling is cheaper than insulating the walls, but it&rsquo;s not always worth it. First, there are many pipes and wires to maneuver around, which makes this a job only expert basement remodeling companies can handle. Second, this is often less effective at keeping heat in than simply insulating the walls. Sometimes the perimeter of the ceiling is insulated when the walls are insulated, but insulating the entire ceiling (unless for soundproofing purposes) is generally not done.</p>',1,'',76,'2017-11-19 15:33:59'),(93,'5 Things to Know Before Digging Out a Basement','Digging out a basement can add value to your home, but take these 5 things into consideration first!','Digging out a basement, how much does it cost to dig out a basement, cost of digging out a basement, dig out a basement','5-things-to-know-before-digging-out-a-basement','5 Things to Know Before Digging Out a Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/93/f7e2772ba8d2fcee304c5a10fd115be3','Digging out a basement can add value to your home, but take these 5 things into consideration first!','<p><strong>5 Things to Know Before Digging Out a Basement</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Digging out a basement </strong>simply means creating enough space under your house for a basement to be installed. It&rsquo;s a great way to add living space and it&rsquo;s oftentimes less costly than adding additional rooms aboveground. However, there are some important things you need to know before digging out a basement!</p>\n<p><strong>Minimum Ceiling Height</strong></p>\n<p>Most basements must have a ceiling height between 7 and 8 feet to be legal, depending on state and county regulations.</p>\n<p><strong>Structural Stability </strong></p>\n<p>Digging a few feet deep usually doesn&rsquo;t require any serious modifications to the home, but digging out a full basement may require the house to be lifted using special construction piles. If you have a particularly old foundation, then this step may be necessary even for minor excavations.</p>\n<p><strong>Weather Patterns &amp; Climate</strong></p>\n<p>Basements in regions with a history of flooding or high humidity will need to have extra <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/waterproofing/\">waterproofing</a> precautions taken. If the climate is extremely wet, however, then the soil could be too loose to safely dig out a basement at all.</p>\n<p><strong>Frost Line</strong></p>\n<p>The frost line is the underground point where the ground starts to freeze. The exact depth changes from region to region, but since plumbing tends to crack past the frost line, no basements can be constructed deeper than this point. Frost lines tend to be closer to the surface in warmer climates, which is why places like Florida tend not to have basements.</p>\n<p><strong>How Much Does it Cost to Dig Out a Basement?</strong></p>\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>cost of digging out a basement</strong> just&nbsp;a few feet is usually cheaper than adding on to other parts of your home. Anything deeper than a few feet starts to get about as pricey as an aboveground addition. Contact us today for a <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">free basement quote</a>!</p>',1,'',77,'2017-11-19 15:34:13'),(94,'5 Reasons Why Basement Fireplaces Are Popular','5 Reasons Why Basement Fireplaces Are Popular','Basement fireplaces, basement fireplace, basement fireplace design ideas, basement fireplace ideas, fireplace in basement,','5-reasons-why-basement-fireplaces-are-popular','5 Reasons Why Basement Fireplaces Are Popular','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/94/3ff6515001dfbaafee3edc97d7f8b43c','Learn why basement fireplaces are popular and see popular basement fireplace designs.','<p><strong>5 Reasons Why Basement Fireplaces Are Popular</strong></p>\n<p>With winter fast approaching, <strong>basement fireplaces </strong>can keep your downstairs looking luxurious while simultaneously keeping out the cold. Here&rsquo;s 5 reasons why basement fireplaces are a smart choice for this upcoming season.<br /><br /><strong>1. Endless Aesthetic Options</strong></p>\n<p>Whether you have contemporary, traditional or modern tastes, an electric fireplace in the basement can easily enhance the decor. Aside from traditional mantel designs, basement fireplaces can be mounted on the wall, in the corner, inside of entertainment and media cabinets, and virtually anywhere else. &nbsp;Check out these different <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/fireplaces/\">basement fireplaces ideas</a> to see the astonishing variety!<br /><br /><strong>2. Complete Atmospheric Control</strong></p>\n<p>You can create just the right ambiance for intimidate get-togethers and large gatherings with an electric basement fireplace. Not only can you control how bright the flames are, but you can also determine the speed at which they flicker, their overall color, and many other attentive effects.<br /><br /><strong>3. Durability</strong></p>\n<p>Electric fireplaces last longer than wood and gas fireplaces. They don&rsquo;t rust or corrode, and they stay looking new for years.<br /><br /><strong>4. Low Cost</strong></p>\n<p>Installing an electric fireplace costs far less than traditional fireplaces, and the best ones look virtually identical under a mantel. Electric fireplaces will also heat a room in your basement quickly without costing much.<br /><br /><strong>5. Year-Round Use</strong></p>\n<p>Fireplaces in the basement can be used without heat if so desired, giving a warm cottage effect in the middle of the summer!</p>',1,'',78,'2017-11-12 15:34:25'),(95,'3 Reasons Why Basement Waterproofing Matters','Basement waterproofing is important because...','basement waterproofing, waterproofing basement, waterproofing your basement, basement contractor','3-reasons-why-basement-waterproofing-matters','3 Reasons Why Basement Waterproofing Matters','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/95/adb10158fd90aa9b83273d0f79348979','Basement waterproofing is important because...','<p><strong>3 Reasons Why Basement Waterproofing Matters</strong></p>\n<p>Basement waterproofing is important because . . .</p>\n<p><strong>Leaks Cost Money</strong></p>\n<p>The Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) <a href=\"https://www.epa.gov/watersense/fix-leak-week\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">estimates</a> that around 10 percent of all homes are wasting 90 gallons of water or more each and every day through leaks. Identifying these types of leaks is the first step when waterproofing a basement, and it can save you an extravagant amount of money over time.</p>\n<p><strong>Damp Air Increases Electric Bills</strong></p>\n<p>Damp air requires more energy to heat and cool, so when the basement has damp air from moisture, then you are paying more than you need to. Waterproofing your basement keeps the air nice and dry, which saves you in the long run.</p>\n<p><strong>Waterproofing Prevents Mold</strong></p>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://www.fema.gov/pdf/rebuild/recover/fema_mold_brochure_english.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EPA also reports</a> that mold can grow in the basement in as little as one or two days after water exposure. If you can see or smell mold, then it could already be time to call a basement contractor.</p>',3,'',79,'2017-11-12 15:34:41'),(96,'Get Professional Mold Prevention in Baltimore','Why we are the best at mold prevention in Baltimore.','mold prevention in Baltimore, mold prevention strategies, basement remodeling, basement remodeling company, basement waterproofing company, Baltimore waterproofing','get-professional-mold-prevention-in-baltimore','Get Professional Mold Prevention in Baltimore','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/96/15272afe4bd842edab02c2aa0c84504b','Why we are the best at mold prevention in Baltimore.','<p><strong>Get Professional Mold Prevention in Baltimore </strong></p>\n<p>Basement Masters is a basement remodeling and waterproofing company that can provide effective mold prevention strategies to keep moisture out of your basement and away from your foundation. If you have a wet or leaky basement, getting mold prevention in Baltimore can protect your property from serious structural damage. Not only can we craft the luxury basement you&rsquo;ve always wanted, but we can also keep it safe from any leaks and floods with effective mold prevention in Baltimore.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>As a basement remodeling and <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/waterproofing/\">basement waterproofing</a> company with over 10 years of professional experience, Basement Masters prevents top-notch mold prevention in Baltimore (and throughout the rest of Maryland), Virginia, and Washington DC. Your wet, leaky basement will be remodeled to meet local and federal standards using industry-insider materials at an affordable price. <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact us</a> now to learn more about mold prevention in Baltimore today.</p>',3,'',80,'2017-11-05 15:34:53'),(97,'5 Reasons You Need a Professional Basement Remodeling Company','What specifically can a basement remodeling company do better than everybody else?','basement remodeling company, basement remodeling, basement remodeling Maryland, basement remodeling DC, basement remodeling Virginia','5-reasons-you-need-a-professional-basement-remodeling-company','5 Reasons You Need a Professional Basement Remodeling Company','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/97/5319c28f1def24bd76050e3469f2e5c9','What specifically can a basement remodeling company do better than everybody else?','<h1>5 Reasons You Need a Professional Basement Remodeling Company</h1>\n<p>It&rsquo;s tempting to hire a basic team of handymen or even attempt to remodel a basement on your own, but only a basement remodeling company can easily . . .</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Provide Documentation &ndash; Everything from licenses and insurance certifications to remodeling permits are readily available when you are working with a basement remodeling company.\n<ul>\n<li>Sometimes a neighborhood homeowner&rsquo;s association (HOA) will require additional paperwork that unexperienced contractors won&rsquo;t know how to obtain.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Pass Inspections &ndash; Understanding federal and county regulations can be difficult, but a basement remodeling company will build everything up to code so that you won&rsquo;t be fined &ndash; or worse still &ndash; ordered to halt construction until a serious issue is fixed.</li>\n<li>Build Safely &ndash; When you hire a basement remodeling company, only professionals will be working on your home&rsquo;s plumbing, electrical and HVAC systems.</li>\n<li>Give a Timeline &ndash; You want a basement remodeling company that has experience working on multiple projects at once and knows how to show up on time.</li>\n<li>Source Materials &ndash; A basement remodeling company who has been around for a while will have developed business connections with suppliers and can get building materials for a discount (which can then be passed on to you, the customer).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Basement Masters is the Premiere Basement Remodeling Company of Choice</h2>\n<p>Basement Masters has been in business since 2006, originating in Maryland and expanding operations throughout Virginia and Washington DC. If you need basement remodeling in Maryland, Virginia or DC, then we want to do business with you. Check out our <a href=\"../../../../portfolio/\">portfolio</a> and then get free online <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">basement quotes</a> today!</p>',4,'',81,'2017-10-29 15:35:08'),(98,'4 Must-Know Facts About Basement Wainscoting','Basement wainscoting is in style – here’s what you need to know!','basement wainscoting, wainscoting in basement, basement remodeling, Maryland basement remodeling, basement remodelers, traditional wainscoting, wainscoting ideas','4-must-know-facts-about-basement-wainscoting','4 Must-Know Facts About Basement Wainscoting','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/98/ef48d93d1b0562c59b6420d17711a755','Basement wainscoting is in style – here’s what you need to know!','<p><strong>4 Must-Know Facts About Basement Wainscoting</strong></p>\n<p>For years, some of the best professional <strong>basement remodelers</strong> have been infusing traditional <strong>wainscoting in basement</strong> designs. Basement wainscoting refers to a classic interior wall treatment that uses decorative boards and panels to add an appealing visual texture to the lower half of a wall. As such, basement wainscoting is one of the many final touches used to make your downstairs just as appealing as the rest of your home.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/38/c399287b434bfcb0bcb0b3975deb6a24_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>When done correctly, basement wainscoting creates immersive depth.</em></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>1. Where to Use Basement Wainscoting</strong></p>\n<p>Traditional wainscoting is often used in kitchenettes, bathrooms and family areas, and these same rooms are perfect for wainscoting in basement areas, too.</p>\n<p><strong>2. What is Wainscoting Made Out Of?</strong></p>\n<p>Traditional wainscoting is always made of solid wood, and is therefore the most expensive. Walnut and cherry wood are highest quality selections, while pine is an excellent cost-efficient species. There are also plenty of alternative wainscoting building materials (in order of most expensive to least):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Medium density fiberboard (MDF) &ndash; Unlike solid wood, MDF does not expand from heat, contract from cold, or warp from moisture. &nbsp;</li>\n<li>Plastic &ndash; Usually made from a special type of PVC. Does not rot like real wood.</li>\n<li>Plywood &ndash; These pre-manufactured sheets are the easiest to install.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>3. How Much Maintenance Care is Required for Wainscoting?</strong></p>\n<p>PVC (plastic) wainscoting does not require any maintenance. Other types can be cleaned with a duster or a soft brush, followed by a vacuum. If the wood is sealed or painted with a semigloss paint or a clear polyurethane finish, then you can clean it with a damp microfiber cloth using two-parts vinegar with one part water. If the wainscoting has not been treated, skip the last step.<br /><br /><strong>4. What is the Difference Between Wall Panelling and Wainscoting?</strong></p>\n<p>Visually, the two can look identical. However, wall panels are much taller than wainscoting treatments. Wainscoting is normally done up to chair-level height; anything taller is classified as a wall panel.</p>\n<p><strong>Need Basement Wainscoting?</strong></p>\n<p>Basement Masters is a Maryland basement remodeling company also serving Washington DC, Delaware and Virginia. Check out our terrific <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/wall-treatments/wood-wall-panelling/\">wainscoting ideas</a> and then <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">contact us</a> to see how we can make your basement look as luxurious as the rest of your home! &nbsp;</p>',1,'',82,'2017-10-22 15:35:20'),(99,'Professional Basement Remodeling Services in Alexandria, VA','Looking for a professional basement remodeling and finishing contractor in Alexandria, VA? Check out Basement Remodeling Company!','basement remodeling services, alexandria, VA, Virginia, professional basement contractor, basement finishing company, expert basement services, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement remodeling blog','professional-basement-remodeling-services-in-alexandria-va','Professional Basement Remodeling Services in Alexandria, VA','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/99/1f8da2870577a0e645b221b800b5aa35','Get the best professional basement remodeling in Alexandria, VA.','<h2><strong>The Best Basement Remodeling Company in Alexandria, VA</strong></h2>\n<p>If you need <strong>basement remodeling in Alexandria, VA</strong>, then the experts at Basement Remodeling Company &ndash; the leading basement remodelers since 2006 &ndash; are ready to provide you with the highest quality materials and finest craftsmanship available. Take a look at our previous remodeling projects in Alexandria, VA, and then <a href=\"#\">contact us</a> to get a free basement quote today! &nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/36/4546a3fa44a59d9c582798ec33395cf4_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-alexandria-virginia\">See more pictures and read the full description.</a></em></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/37/d5c8ff4619c2790ec76bf76fe993edd7_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em><a href=\"../../../../portfolio/\">More pictures and the full description.</a></em></p>',5,'',83,'2017-10-22 15:35:35'),(100,'5 Egress Window Decorating Ideas for Your Basement','5 egress window decorating ideas to maximize your basement area.','egress window decorating ideas, egress window ideas, basement remodeling company, basement designers','5-egress-window-decorating-ideas-for-your-basement','5 Egress Window Decorating Ideas for Your Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/100/964a5d0548b8b663651017c459c9b156','5 egress window decorating ideas to maximize your basement area.','<p><strong>5 Egress Window Decorating Ideas for Your Basement</strong></p>\n<p>The word &ldquo;egress&rdquo; literally means &ldquo;to leave a place&rdquo;, and these classy <strong>egress window decorating ideas </strong>definitely provide a safe and stylish exit &ndash; all while letting in plenty of natural light and complying with the <a href=\"https://codes.iccsafe.org/public/document/code/542/9677240\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">International Building Code</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Plants &ndash; Decorating your egress window well with plants is a beautiful idea, but be sure they are small enough to let natural light through. Planting a shrub, for example, is not a good idea.</li>\n<li>Alternative Walls &ndash; Instead of basic metal wall designs, you can use decorative rocks &ndash; or even better, luxury vinyl tiling &ndash; for a more earthy feel.<br /><br /></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"text-align: center; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/33/870ac5ccb98c84a9bf935c23f0187ffd_624x510.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"510\" /><em style=\"text-align: center;\">Luxury vinyl tiling (LVT) can give you many natural looks at a fraction of the cost.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sunlight &ndash; Some egress window decorating ideas look great, but don&rsquo;t let in much natural light. Always consider the design in addition to the aesthetics.</li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"text-align: center;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/34/f52b293d4af44cfe05b3ddddc68b6b2a_624x468.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"468\" /><br /><em style=\"text-align: center;\">These special curved window wells force natural light into your room and amplify it.<br /></em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Well Covers&nbsp;&ndash; Adding a cover to your egress window well lets you control the amount of natural light that comes into your basement while also keeping the well clean of yard debris.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/35/230ca170704f96a359e972e9ce5c8825_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><br /><em>Leaves stay out of your well with a cover.<br /></em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Steps &ndash; Adding small steps to your egress window well can be a cheaper and quicker alternative to walk out basements.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Need More Egress Window Decorating Ideas?</strong></p>\n<p>As the premiere basement remodeling company for Maryland, Virginia and Washington DC, our team of basement designers have elegant <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/egress-windows/\">egress window ideas</a> that can bring in natural light and keep water away from your foundation. <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact us</a> to learn how our basement egress window ideas can transform your downstairs area into a luxurious new world.</p>',1,'',84,'2017-10-15 15:35:47'),(101,'10 Questions to Ask Before Hiring a Basement Contractor','Looking to hire a new basement contractor? Ask them these 10 crucial questions before hiring them!','basement contractors, basement contractor, basement remodeling, basement finishing, finish basement contractors, basement remodeling companies, basement finishing company, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement remodeling blog, questions to ask a basement contractor','10-questions-to-ask-before-hiring-a-basement-contractor','10 Questions to Ask Before Hiring a Basement Contractor','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/101/64d679042f2d8eafe8b9f997c02fe579','Don’t hire any basement contractors until getting this information first!','<div class=\"h1\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>10 Questions to Ask Before Hiring a Basement Contractor</strong></div>\n<p>Whether you want to finish or completely remodel, a&nbsp;<strong>basement contractor&nbsp;</strong>has the professional expertise that&rsquo;s required to ensure your downstairs area is fully up to code and looking fantastic for years to come. One of the hardest parts about remodeling or finishing a basement, however, is finding the right basement contractor to do the job. Fortunately, asking these 10 questions will give you all of the information you need to know to find the best basement remodeling company!</p>\n<h2><strong>1. How long have you been remodeling and finishing basements?</strong></h2>\n<p>Asking basement contractors how long they have been in the business for is better than asking how many basements they have worked on. You want a basement remodeling company who has stayed in business for a long time as opposed to a newer business who is taking on many projects at once.</p>\n<h2><strong>2. Are you a basement-only contractor?</strong></h2>\n<p>Companies that focus only on basements are almost always more efficient than general construction companies. They typically have the best quality materials at the lowest price due to business connections.</p>\n<h2><strong>3. Do you have a valid state license?</strong></h2>\n<p>If anything goes wrong and a basement contractor is not licensed, then you will not be able to go to the state&rsquo;s licensing board to seek restitution.</p>\n<h2><strong>4. How much are you insured for?</strong></h2>\n<p>With so many basement remodeling companies to choose from, you want to go with one that has more than just minimum coverage.</p>\n<h2><strong>5. How many people are on your team?</strong></h2>\n<p>Most companies should have a team page clearly showing who they work with. If they give jobs to subcontractors, then the company should know these subcontractors well and work with them for years.</p>\n<h2><strong>6. Can I go to a job site?</strong></h2>\n<p>Good basement contractors will have references who are willing to let you into their home and look at their work. If not, then they should be willing to take you to a site that is under construction for a brief tour so that you can see their work and ask questions.</p>\n<h2><strong>7. What is your timeframe?</strong></h2>\n<p>A general timeframe should clearly outline exact price points and estimated dates for each step.</p>\n<h2><strong>8. Do you pull permits?</strong></h2>\n<p>Every construction project requires permits from the stat. &ldquo;Pulling permits&rdquo; simply means that you receive a copy of each permit. Every basement contractor should do this for you.</p>\n<h2><strong>9. Do you use products that are specially designed for basements?</strong></h2>\n<p>Basement contractors should have waterproofing systems to prevent mold and moisture, and special products for foundation repairs as well.</p>\n<h2><strong>10. How are selections handled?</strong></h2>\n<p>Some companies let you pick products out at a local store on your own, but the best ones will have a designer and a selection catalogue of their own materials to choose from.</p>\n<h2>BRC&mdash;fully-transparent basement contractor with answers to all questions!</h2>\n<p>Basement Remodeling company offers comprehensive, basement-specific services to all of Maryland, Virginia, and DC. BRC\'s process is fully-transparent and none of your questions will go unanswered!</p>',4,'',85,'2017-10-08 15:35:58'),(102,'Get Professional Basement Waterproofing in Baltimore, MD','We offer luxury basement waterproofing in Baltimore, MD.','basement waterproofing Baltimore MD, Baltimore waterproofing, waterproofing MD, waterproofing Maryland, basement remodeling contractors, basement remodeling company, basement remodeling MD','get-professional-basement-waterproofing-in-baltimore-md','Get Professional Basement Waterproofing in Baltimore, MD','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/102/49e26e2572b7ee57e9f94a4c61870b17','We offer luxury basement waterproofing in Baltimore, MD.','<p>If you live in Baltimore, waterproofing your basement is <a href=\"https://www.baltimoresun.com/opinion/editorial/bs-ed-0925-sewage-backups-20190925-yfda2j6vdzcgvc7jsjgk2jvu5u-story.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">more important than ever</a> due to overloaded pipes and large storms. The city&rsquo;s plumbing problems aren&rsquo;t expected to be resolved until the next decade, so what can you do to help protect your home or business from excessive moisture in the meantime? Get <strong>professional basement waterproofing</strong> in <strong>Baltimore</strong> with BasementRemodeling.com.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<h2>Why Choose Us for Basement Waterproofing in Baltimore, MD?</h2>\n<p>Our basement <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/waterproofing/\">waterproofing solutions</a> extend far beyond basic sump pumps and drainage systems. If you have a serious moisture problem, then we have special barriers, chemical formulas and other cutting-edge technology needed to create a full Baltimore basement waterproofing system that can keep unwanted moisture out from the foundation up. We offer innovative wall crack repairs, crawl space repairs, foundation repairs and top-of-the-line interior and exterior systems to keep your home or business safe.</p>\n<h2>BasementRemodeling.com: A Baltimore Waterproofing Company You Can Trust</h2>\n<p>Basement Masters is an independently-owned-and-operated basement remodeling company from Rockville, MD. We have been in business for over ten years &ndash; recently expanding into Baltimore and Washington DC within the last two &ndash; and our basement remodeling contractors and subcontractors have a combined experience of over 350 years. Simply put, we know how to get basement waterproofing in Baltimore, MD finished the right way &ndash; at a reasonable price and always on time.</p>\n<p>If you need waterproofing in Baltimore, MD, then <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">contact us</a> for a free estimate today!</p>',3,'',86,'2017-10-01 15:36:16'),(103,'6 Trendy Basement Remodeling Ideas for 2017','Don’t touch your basement without checking out these 2017 basement remodeling ideas first!','Basement remodeling, basement remodeling ideas, basement built ins, basement built-in ideas, bunk bed ideas, built in entertainment center ideas under basement stairs storage, basement tray ceiling, gym in basement, gym basement, basement gym ideas, basement tray ceiling ideas, walkout basement ideas, music room ideas,  decorating a music room, basement walkout ideas, basement remodeling contractors','6-trendy-basement-remodeling-ideas-for-2017','6 Trendy Basement Remodeling Ideas for 2017','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/103/6301339d30b7530b5bdb47378caa2da1','Don’t touch your basement without checking out these 2017 basement remodeling ideas first!','<p><strong>6 Trendy Basement Remodeling Ideas for 2017</strong></p>\n<p>Basement remodeling has been on the rise in recent years. Homeowners are excited to put their downstairs area to good use and get a high return on their investment when the time to sell comes. If you are looking for <strong>basement remodeling ideas</strong>, then pay attention to these trendy concepts that will most likely carry on for years to come!&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<h2>1. Open Designs Are &ldquo;In&rdquo;</h2>\n<p>An open-concept basement takes the natural basement architecture and plays with light and space to create dramatic angles and inviting nooks. The best open-concept basements will designate spaces for different uses without putting up walls. This way, a person can seamlessly walk straight from the family room area to the kitchen-like area while keeping an eye on the kids or the television.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/27/28a9a5cc96f8d899398a5d564f46008a_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>Visual depth abounds with an open-concept basement.<br /></em></p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">2. Sweet Suites</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Why stop at a guest bedroom when you can create an entire suite? Connecting a bedroom to a full-size bathroom adds privacy and comfort. Of course, an expansive basement tray ceiling and a kitchenette would be even better. Who would have thought that basement remodeling would be a way to impress the in-laws!<br /><br /><br /></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/28/6e884f79b46ca9ea917c3e84f86a03b1_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>We have plenty of <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/ceilings/advanced/\">basement tray ceiling ideas</a> for your downstairs suite.</em></p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">3. Basement Walkouts Make a Grand Entrance</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A basement walkout is perfect for houses that have been built on a slope or hillside with a foundation wall that is aboveground. However, even if your home was not built on a hillside or slope, basement walkouts are also completely possible in the capable hands of the right basement remodeling contractors. Having an entrance allows for quiet access to your basement from the outside, along with more natural light.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/29/9dcb43815ff4d7be5d5122b3ca903043_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>These <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/walk-outs/\">walkout basement ideas</a> will breathe fresh air into your downstairs area!</em></p>\n<h2>4. Music Rooms Look as Great as They Sound</h2>\n<p>Forget the garage! Any serious or aspiring musician will love <strong>decorating a music room</strong> in their basement. A nicely soundproofed area offers a great look and a topnotch sound &ndash; and don&rsquo;t forget to include plenty of seating for your audience.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/30/cd460a2e32bf5cb5c730afe10d7df6e6_624x414.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"414\" /><em>See if any of these <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/music-rooms/\">music rooms ideas</a> &ldquo;strike a note&rdquo;!</em></p>\n<h2>5.&nbsp;Basement Gyms Offer Totally Private Workouts</h2>\n<p>Your gym in the basement lets you get fit without having to share equipment, pay a membership, or deal with the general public. With a <strong>gym basement</strong>, having to get in your car to go workout will be a thing of the past. You&rsquo;ll be glad you made this decision in the winter!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/31/3868a20f38210ed8e2fc8d63e18412fe_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><em>These exciting <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/gym/\">basement gym ideas</a> will get your blood pumping!</em></p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">6. Basement Built-Ins are Better</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">From bunk bed ideas and built in entertainment center ideas to under basement stairs storage ideas and more, basement built ins always offer a personalized touch that fits just right.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/32/bb0af46940fa05144cdfdb324afc3f7b_624x413.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"413\" /><em>Check out these trendy 2017 <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/built-ins-and-shelving/\">basement built-ins ideas</a> for your basement!</em></p>\n<h2>Realize Your Basement Remodeling Ideas Today with Basement Masters!</h2>\n<p>First established in 2006, Basement Masters is a basement remodeling company who can successfully implement all of your basement finishing and remodeling ideas into one luxurious downstairs space. Any of these 2017 basement design trends are possible under the expert craftmanship of our basement remodeling contractors, so contact us and <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">get a free quote</a>!</p>',1,'',87,'2017-10-01 15:36:30'),(104,'5 MORE Reasons Basement Finishing is Important!','Basement finishing is an essential part of owning a home – here’s why.','basement finishing, finished basement, basement storage, basement storage room ideas, under stairs storage basement, basement remodeling','5-more-reasons-basement-finishing-is-important','5 MORE Reasons Basement Finishing is Important!','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/104/64c14fae7cc203caabf04a63db1196a5','Basement finishing is an essential part of owning a home – here’s why.','<p>An unfinished basement can be more than just an eyesore &ndash; it&rsquo;s often a missed opportunity. We&rsquo;ve gone over the <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/4-reasons-you-need-to-finish-your-basement\">importance of <strong>basement finishing</strong></a> before, but here are 5 more reasons why it&rsquo;s so important!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/23/514d6a660f102294b17f94fc7623f6a4_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><br /><em>Basement finishing can make your downstairs look and feel like the rest of your home.</em></p>\n<h2>1. Basement Finishing Sells Houses Faster</h2>\n<p>Potential homebuyers want to see lots of space, and a finished basement provides an excellent initial impression. Whether they are looking for a home office, gym or a guest bedroom, a property with a finished basement is a lot easier to envision living in rather than a dreary downstairs with bare pipes exposed. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<h2>2. Basement Finishing Lets You Entertain Guests</h2>\n<p>Think of it this way: <strong>basement finishing</strong> gives you an additional floor for hosting large gatherings with ease. Your guests will have more room to mingle and you can even expand the guest list so no one feels left out. With the right basement <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/wet-bars/kitchen-like/\">kitchen</a> and <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/wet-bars/\">bar ideas</a>, your legendary get-togethers will quickly become the talk of neighborhood!</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/24/e6df0a8adb6139a18c73a86c861c4262_624x410.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"410\" /><br /><em style=\"text-align: center;\">Impress your guests with the right basement finishing!</em></p>\n<h2>3. Rental Possibilities Abound With Basement Finishing</h2>\n<p>Renting out your finished basement can be a great way to earn a little income on the side. Better still, a walkout basement lets your renters quietly enter and exit the house from downstairs without making a sound. These <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/walk-outs/\">walkout basement ideas</a> are a perfect way to perfect way to let in plenty of natural light and simultaneously attract renters.</p>\n<h2>4.&nbsp;Basement Finishing Leads to Basement Storage</h2>\n<p>A basement storage room is the perfect place storing away important items that you don&rsquo;t use often. There&rsquo;s no need to rent a storage unit or clutter up your garage with these<a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/storage-rooms/\"> basement storage room ideas</a>, including storage under basement stairs.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/25/356d7df0804af505c102de7276b208d4_624x415.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"415\" /><br /><em>Having a basement storage room can keep things looking tidy.</em></p>\n<h2>5.&nbsp;Home Theater Ideas &amp; Basement Finishing</h2>\n<p>A finished basement is really the best place in the house to install a home theater system. Take advantage of natural acoustics, dim lighting and a soundproof design with these <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/media-rooms/home-theaters/\">home theater basement ideas</a>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/26/05a82c151eaf77dfaf7ca4e462d4b35f_624x415.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"415\" /><em>Popcorn, anyone?</em></p>\n<h2>Basement Finishing With the Masters</h2>\n<p>BasementRemodeling.com are the masters of basement finishing and remodeling in Maryland, Virginia, and DC. In business since 2006, we\'re ready to provide you with a downstairs d&eacute;cor like never before. <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact us</a> and learn how we can quickly achieve your basement finishing goals on time and at the right price!</p>',1,'',88,'2017-09-24 15:36:41'),(105,'10 Important Questions to Ask Basement Remodeling Companies in Maryland','Ask these 10 questions to find the best basement remodeling companies in Maryland!','basement remodeling companies in Maryland, basement remodeling company in Maryland, Maryland basement remodeling, basement remodeler, basement remodeling contractors, basement finishing company, basement remodeling company','10-important-questions-to-ask-basement-remodeling-companies-in-maryland','10 Important Questions to Ask Basement Remodeling Companies in Maryland','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/105/c5cd956e1c71e1b9723594e29fba42db','Ask these 10 questions to find the best basement remodeling companies in Maryland!','<p><strong>Basement remodeling companies&nbsp;</strong>know how to make a downstairs area look absolutely amazing, but you need to find the most reliable and trustworthy ones to make sure everything gets completed on time and within budget. Asking these questions to any potential<strong> basement remodeler</strong> (and their references) will help you quickly find the absolute best remodeling companies in Maryland!</p>\n<ul>\n<li>&ldquo;How long have you been remodeling Maryland basements?&rdquo; &ndash; Newer businesses that have yet to prove themselves through multiple reviews may not be as trustworthy as an established business that has been remodeling basements in Maryland for years.</li>\n<li>&ldquo;Do you belong to any professional memberships?&rdquo; &ndash; Membership sites like <a href=\"https://www.houzz.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Houzz</a> and <a href=\"http://www.angieslist.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Angie&rsquo;s List</a> will help you verify the legitimacy of a basement remodeler.</li>\n<li>&ldquo;Do You Have Insurance?&rdquo; &ndash; Basement remodeling contractors need to have general liability insurance and a wide variety of other policies, including workers&rsquo; compensation insurance. They should also have an adequate amount of coverage.</li>\n<li>&ldquo;Are your warranties in writing?&rdquo; &ndash; Any basement remodeling company in Maryland should be able to give you some sort of written guarantee to ensure the quality of their basement remodeling services.</li>\n<li>&ldquo;How long will this take?&rdquo; &ndash; The best basement remodeling contractors will be able to provide you with a timeline clearly showing the sequence of events, deadlines and their cost.</li>\n<li>&ldquo;Do you have different material options?&rdquo; &ndash; Different levels of quality and cost will help you balance the budget and still look fabulous.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Questions for Basement Company References</h2>\n<p>All of the trustworthy basement remodeling companies in Maryland will have a list of satisfied customers to contact. Be sure to ask them these questions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>&ldquo;Were you satisfied?&rdquo; &ndash; The reference will almost always say yes, but some may have a thing or two that could have gone more smoothly, and these are often vital &ldquo;behind-the-scenes&rdquo; details.</li>\n<li>&ldquo;Was the job finished on time?&rdquo; &ndash; If not, why. How long did it take?</li>\n<li>&ldquo;Was the job finished on budget?&rdquo; &ndash; If they were able to complete it underbudget, then great. If not, then what were the extra expenses and why were they incurred?</li>\n<li>&ldquo;Would you recommend this basement contractor?&rdquo; &ndash; If they themselves would not use the basement contractor again, then you shouldn&rsquo;t be expected to either.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Looking for a Basement Remodeling Company in Maryland?</h2>\n<p>BasementRemodeling.com has been beautifully remodeling basements in Maryland for over ten years. Although we have since branched out to Washington DC and Virginia, our services remain high in-demand in &ldquo;The Free State&rdquo;. <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact us today</a> to discuss our excellent basement remodeling and basement finishing services!</p>',4,'',89,'2017-09-17 15:36:52'),(106,'LIMITED OFFER: Free In-Home Consultations for Maryland and DC','A limited offer from one of the best basement remodeling companies in all of Maryland and Washington DC!','basement remodeling companies in Maryland, basement remodeling companies in DC','limited-offer-free-in-home-consultations-for-maryland-and-dc','LIMITED OFFER: Free In-Home Consultations for Maryland and DC','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/106/1d7fb44c34dd9e6d1892da546d2d265c','A limited offer from one of the best basement remodeling companies in all of Maryland and Washington DC!','<p><strong>LIMITED OFFER: Free In-Home Consultations for Maryland and DC!</strong></p>\n<p>Basement Masters, the premiere basement remodeling company in Maryland, DC and Virginia, is pleased to announce that in-home consultations will be free of charge for Marylanders and those in Washington DC for a limited time. The in-home consultation fee will be waived for all Maryland and DC customers until October 1, 2017.</p>\n<p>An in-home consultation clearly outlines our award-winning fully-customizable basement remodeling process, so be sure to take advantage of this terrific Maryland and DC basement remodeling opportunity. &nbsp;If you live in Maryland or the DC area, please <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">contact us today</a> and schedule your free in-home consultation!</p>',5,'',90,'2017-09-17 15:37:04'),(107,'Hanover County, VA Basement Remodeling Permits','Quick links (and pricing guide) to all of the basement remodeling permits you need for Hanover County, VA!','Hanover County Virginia permits, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement remodeling companies Virginia, Hanover County VA, Hanover County Virginia, regulations, permits, building codes','hanover-county-va-basement-remodeling-permits','Hanover County, VA Basement Remodeling Permits','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/107/d07a98ddaf3bd4c22a8d45a862668b7e','Quick links to all of the basement remodeling permits you\'ll need for Hanover County, VA!','<p>You can easily get all the&nbsp;<strong>Hanover County, Virginia basement remodeling permits</strong> you need&nbsp;by following this guide.</p>\r\n<h2>Hanover County, VA Building Permits</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Hanover County, VA <a href=\"https://www.hanovercounty.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1276/Building-Permit-Application-PDF\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permits</a> cost a minimum of $99.75.</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 1\">\r\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n<div class=\"column\">\r\n<p>For a valuation over $15,000.00, the fee shall be $99.75 for the first $15,000.00, plus $5.25 or each additional thousand or fraction thereof.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Two site plans are required.</li>\r\n<li>A <a href=\"https://www.hanovercounty.gov/DocumentCenter/View/80/Site-Plan-Pre-Application-Meeting-Form-PDF\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">scheduled meeting</a> with the Hanover County Planning Department is recommended.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Hanover County, VA Electrical Permits</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>An <a href=\"https://www.hanovercounty.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1251/Residential-Electrical-Application-PDF\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">electrical permit</a> costs at least $99.75 in Hanover County, Virginia.</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 1\">\r\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n<div class=\"column\">\r\n<p>Does not exceed $5,000.00, the fee shall be . . . . . . . $99.75.</p>\r\n<p>Plus $4.20 for each additional $1,000.00 or fraction thereof.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Hanover County, VA Plumbing Permits</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A <a href=\"https://www.hanovercounty.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1247/Plumbing-Application-PDF\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">plumbing permit</a> in Hanover County, Virginia costs $99.75.</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 1\">\r\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n<div class=\"column\">\r\n<p>Does not exceed $5,000.00, the fee shall be . . . . . . . $99.75.</p>\r\n<p>Plus $4.20 for each additional $1,000.00 or fraction thereof.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Hanover County, VA Mechanical Permits</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A <a href=\"https://www.hanovercounty.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1296/Mechanical-HVAC-Application-PDF\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mechanical permit</a> costs $99.75 in Hanover County, Virginia.</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 1\">\r\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n<div class=\"column\">\r\n<p>Does not exceed $5,000.00, the fee shall be . . . . . . . $99.75.</p>\r\n<p>Plus $4.20 for each additional $1,000.00 or fraction thereof.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Hanover County, VA Gas Permits</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A <a href=\"https://www.hanovercounty.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1295/Mechanical-Gas-Application-PDF\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gas permit</a> costs $101.75 in Hanover County, Virginia.</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 1\">\r\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n<div class=\"column\">\r\n<p>Does not exceed $5,000.00, the fee shall be . . . . . . . $99.75.</p>\r\n<p>Plus $4.20 for each additional $1,000.00 or fraction thereof.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>',2,'',91,'2017-09-10 15:37:15'),(108,'Greene County, VA Building Department Information and Permits (Updated 2022)','A quick and easy guide to finding relevant building permits and regulations in Greene County, Virginia!','Greene County VA, Greene County Virginia, Greene County Building Department, Greene County building permits, Greene County building inspector, basement finishing, basement remodeling, basement remodeling companies Virginia','greene-county-va-building-department-information-and-permits-updated-2019','Greene County, VA Building Department Information and Permits (Updated 2022)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/108/3a12e79ee7aebd5b97be6f50a52de780','An easy-to-follow guide for building permits in Greene County, Virginia!','<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">Green County VA Building Permit Application</h2>\r\n<p>You can mail your Greene County <a href=\"https://www.greenecountyva.gov/forms/building-inspections/1954-new-residence-application-packet/file\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit application</a> to the Greene County building department. Their mailing address is:&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>P.O. Box 358<br />Stanardsville, VA 22973</p>\r\n<h2>Zoning and Sign Permits</h2>\r\n<p>Sign permits are covered under the <a href=\"https://www.greenecountyva.gov/forms/documents/1880-application-pz-2019-zc-signs/file\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">zoning certification/signs permit application</a>.</p>\r\n<h2>Plumbing, Electrical and Mechanical Permits</h2>\r\n<p>All other permits can be picked up at the Greene County building, which is located at:</p>\r\n<p>40 Celt Road (Room 226)<br />Stanardsville, VA 22973</p>\r\n<h2>Who is the Greene County Building Inspector?</h2>\r\n<p>The Greene County <a href=\"http://www.greenecountyva.gov/government/depts/building-inspections/staff\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building inspector</a> is Eric &ldquo;Peanut&rdquo; Woolford, who can be reached at <a>ewoolford@gcva.us</a>.</p>',2,'',92,'2017-09-10 15:37:27'),(109,'Baltimore County, MD Building & Other Permits (Updated 2022)','This simple guide has updated information for 2022 regarding Baltimore County permits—where to find them and how to apply!','Baltimore County building permits, Baltimore permit info, Baltimore building permits, Maryland basement finishing, Maryland basement remodeling, Maryland basement remodeling companies, Baltimore County permits, Baltimore County building permits, Baltimore County permit office, Baltimore County basement remodeling, basement blog','baltimore-county-md-building--other-permits-updated-2019','Baltimore County, MD Building & Other Permits (Updated 2022)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/109/04aa63a7e021bdf35b5d593921b335da','This simple guide has everything you need to know about Baltimore County permits!','<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Baltimore County Building Permits</strong></h2>\r\n<p>A <a href=\"http://resources.baltimorecountymd.gov/Documents/Permits/BuildingPermit/permitapp.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit application</a>&nbsp;with Baltimore county still has to be applied for in person, though now you have fill out the form online and email it to the office (<a href=\"https://www.baltimorecountymd.gov/Agencies/permits/pdm_permitsprocess/pdmfper.html#howtoapply\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">steps here</a>). After filling out and emailing the application, go to the Baltimore County permit office between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 4:30 p.m. to meet with an Engineering Assistant:<br /><br />County Office Building<br />111 West Chesapeake Avenue, Room 100<br />Towson, MD 21204</p>\r\n<p>You must bring property reports with you to the meeting with the Baltimore County permit office. These reports can be found using the <a href=\"https://bcgis.baltimorecountymd.gov/permitreview/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">county website\'s handy tool</a>.</p>\r\n<p>If you are a contractor, you\'ll also need to get the owner&rsquo;s signature and contact information on the building permit before turning it in. The <a href=\"http://resources.baltimorecountymd.gov/Documents/Permits/Permits%20Fee%20Schedules/15bldgpermitfees130924.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">fees</a> for a Baltimore County permit are always at minimum $100-$200, depending on your specific needs.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Plumbing Permits</strong></h2>\r\n<p>A <a href=\"http://resources.baltimorecountymd.gov/Documents/Permits/BuildingPermit/plumbapp.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">plumbing permit application</a> can be mailed to the Baltimore County permit office.</p>\r\n<p>Here is a full list of associated <a href=\"http://resources.baltimorecountymd.gov/Documents/Permits/Permits%20Fee%20Schedules/44plumbinspecfees.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">plumbing fees</a>.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Baltimore County, MD Gas Permits</strong></h2>\r\n<p>A gas permit in Baltimore County can be obtained by using a<a href=\"http://resources.baltimorecountymd.gov/Documents/Permits/BuildingPermit/plumbapp.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> plumbing permit application</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The fees for a gas permit are:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>$30.00 for the first appliance (up to 2-and-a-half inches)</li>\r\n<li>$14.00 for each additional appliance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>$79.00 for the first appliance (between 3 and 4 inches)</li>\r\n<li>$14.00 for each additional appliance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>$119.00 for the first appliance (5 inches)</li>\r\n<li>$14.00 for each additional appliance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>$169.00 for the first appliance (6 inches)</li>\r\n<li>$14.00 for each additional appliance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>$394.00 for the first appliance (8 inches)</li>\r\n<li>$14.00 for each additional appliance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>$506.00 for the first appliance (12 inches)</li>\r\n<li>$14.00 for each additional appliance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2><strong>Electrical Permits</strong></h2>\r\n<p>An <a href=\"http://resources.baltimorecountymd.gov/Documents/Permits/BuildingPermit/electricalapp.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">electrical permit application</a> can be mailed to the same address that you pick up your Baltimore County permit office.</p>\r\n<p>Here is the full list of <a href=\"http://resources.baltimorecountymd.gov/Documents/Permits/Permits%20Fee%20Schedules/elecinspecfee130715.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">electrical permit fees</a>. &nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3><strong>Sign Permits</strong></h3>\r\n<p>Sign permits in Baltimore County are at the same building as building permits, but they are in Room 111 (the <a href=\"https://www.baltimorecountymd.gov/Agencies/permits/pdm_zoning/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Zoning Review Office</a>). You can call (410) 887-3391 for more information on sign permits.</p>',2,'',93,'2017-09-03 15:37:39'),(110,'Is Basement Waterproofing Right For Your Maryland, Virginia, or DC Area Home?','How important is basement waterproofing in DC, Virginia and Maryland?','basement waterproofing, home waterproofing, waterproofing your basement, how to waterproof a basement, basement finishing, basement remodeling, Maryland basement remodeling companies','is-basement-waterproofing-right-for-your-maryland-virginia-or-dc-area-home','Is Basement Waterproofing Right For Your Maryland, Virginia, or DC Area Home?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/110/3bfb3b975914b92d7bf3ca9122bbdc1b','How important is basement waterproofing in DC, Maryland and Virginia?','<p><strong>Is Basement Waterproofing Right For Your Maryland, Virginia, or DC Area Home?</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Waterproofing your basement</strong> could be more urgent than most people think. The American Society of Home Inspectors (ASHI) <a href=\"http://www.homeinspector.org/HomeInspectionNews/knee-deep-in-water.3-25-2016.1195/Details/Story\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">recently announced</a> that an estimated 60 percent of U.S. homes have <strong>wet basements</strong>. Even if your basement looks bone dry, there are still many hidden areas where moisture can collect and wreck havoc on your possessions, health, and personal safety.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/20/6dbeb7e2e7b4d7f4398c43e1ce7c7f44_624x417.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"417\" /><em>Let&rsquo;s learn about how wet basements are a bad thing, and how you can stop them!</em></p>\n<p><strong>Basement Waterproofing and Your Health</strong></p>\n<p>Of the estimated 60 percent of wet basements in America, ASHI predicts that 38 percent of them can develop into harmful mold problems. Air circulates throughout your entire home, meaning that the air in your basement will reach other rooms soon enough &ndash; taking the mold spores with them. These nasty contaminants can aggravate asthma and allergies, and even cause serious illness over time</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/21/cb6dd2f49464e2f040591de28ae6f988_624x468.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"468\" /><em>Home waterproofing can get rid of these unwelcomed guests away from you and your family.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Home Waterproofing Lowers Heating and Cooling Bills</strong></p>\n<p>Wet basements can dampen the air. With a waterproofed basement, your heating and cool system will not have to work as hard to cool or heat the damp air &ndash; because there is none!</p>\n<p><strong>Home Waterproofing and Other Property Costs</strong></p>\n<p>Waterproofing your basement keeps water from finding its way through the cracks and weakening your foundation. Once your foundation has been weakened, everything from the ground to the roof can become affected. For example:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Unsightly cracks form in the walls, floor and ceiling</li>\n<li>Uneven floors</li>\n<li>Buckling hardwood surfaces</li>\n<li>Doors no longer close properly due to the uneven floor</li>\n<li>Windows swell from the increased moisture and often stick or won&rsquo;t close</li>\n<li>The shingles and sheathing on your roof becomes warped and no longer fits</li>\n<li>Eventual collapse</li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/22/21243189fb8f9d53c36b532d1cec32df_624x416.png\" width=\"624\" height=\"416\" /><br /><em>Many home problems start with a wet basement.</em></p>\n<p><strong>How to Waterproof a Basement (Maryland, Virginia and DC)</strong></p>\n<p>There are many different ways to waterproof a basement, but the easiest way is to leave it to the professionals. They will have done the procedure countless times and know which waterproofing materials and methods are the most effective. The basement remodeling experts at Basement Masters will be glad to tell you exactly how to waterproof a basement the best way.</p>\n<p>For all issues pertaining to waterproofing and basement remodeling, Maryland, Virginia and DC homeowners need to <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">contact Basement Masters</a> today!</p>',3,'',94,'2017-09-03 15:37:50'),(111,'All Culpeper County, VA Permits for Basement Remodeling','Follow this helpful guide to apply for a Culpeper County, VA building permit – and all other necessary permits for basement remodeling.','Culpeper County VA building permit, Culpeper County Virginia building permits, Culpeper County VA permits, Culpeper County Virginia permits, basement remodeling','all-culpeper-county-va-permits-for-basement-remodeling','All Culpeper County, VA Permits for Basement Remodeling','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/111/d3f6ec86d36039b7e68a1fae3ba1879d','Follow this helpful guide to apply for a Culpeper County, VA building permit – and all other necessary permits for basement remodeling.','<p><strong>All Culpeper County, VA Permits for Basement Remodeling</strong></p>\r\n<p>It&rsquo;s easy to obtain Culpeper County, VA permits for basement remodeling once you have the right links. Follow this helpful guide to apply for a Culpeper County, VA building permit &ndash; and all other necessary permits for basement remodeling.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Culpeper County, VA Building Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>To apply for a <a href=\"https://web.culpepercounty.gov/Portals/0/Departments/Building_Department/Documents/RESIDENTIAL%20BLDG%20APPLICATION.pdf?ver=m3rz7wfoNMRKzzhWrbCQbQ%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit</a> in Culpeper County, Virginia, you must have:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A health permit from the Health Department</li>\r\n<li>A <a href=\"http://web.culpepercounty.gov/Portals/0/Departments/Planning_and_Zoning/USE%20PERMIT%20APPLICATION.pdf?ver=2017-05-17-090247-983\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">zoning permit</a> from the Department of Development.</li>\r\n<li>Three copies of site plans drawn to scale (at least a &frac14;&rdquo; per foot)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>These site plans have a separate <a href=\"http://web.culpepercounty.gov/Portals/0/Departments/Planning_and_Zoning/SITE%20PLAN%20APPLICATION.pdf?ver=2017-05-17-090033-997\">a</a><a href=\"http://web.culpepercounty.gov/Portals/0/Departments/Planning_and_Zoning/SITE%20PLAN%20APPLICATION.pdf?ver=2017-05-17-090033-997\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">pplication form</a>, and must include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Basement dimensions and wall thickness</li>\r\n<li>If the basement is currently conditioned or unconditioned, finished or unfinished</li>\r\n<li>The size of the bedroom windows</li>\r\n<li>Fireplace dimensions</li>\r\n<li>Size and materials of any beams or girders (steel beams need an engineer&rsquo;s design with a seal)</li>\r\n<li>The location, species, size and type of joists.</li>\r\n<li>Two copies of &ldquo;engineered wood product&rdquo; plans that the supplier has provided for the floor, roof, or beams</li>\r\n<li>The backfill height on basement walls</li>\r\n<li>Door sizes and locations</li>\r\n<li>Crawl space vents</li>\r\n<li>Rooms labeled by their intended use</li>\r\n<li>Room dimensions, including halls and stairs</li>\r\n<li>Window and door types</li>\r\n<li>Two copies of engineered roof truss design and layouts</li>\r\n<li>Stair dimensions (width, rise and tread, and the height of handrails, guardrails and railings)</li>\r\n<li>Smoke detectors and carbon monoxide detectors</li>\r\n<li>The location of safety glazed walls</li>\r\n<li>Braced wall lines and braced panels</li>\r\n<li>Compliance with the wall bracing requirements of section 602.10 of the <a href=\"https://www.dhcd.virginia.gov/virginia-uniform-statewide-building-code-usbc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">USBC</a></li>\r\n<li>R-values of all insulation</li>\r\n<li>Full details can be found under the &ldquo;Construction Document Specifications&rdquo; section of the building permit.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>A building permit for an unfinished basement in Culpeper County, Virginia costs 15 cents per square foot.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Zoning Permits in Culpeper County, VA</strong></p>\r\n<p>A <a href=\"http://web.culpepercounty.gov/Portals/0/Departments/Planning_and_Zoning/USE%20PERMIT%20APPLICATION.pdf?ver=2017-05-17-090247-983\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">zoning permit</a> in Culpeper County, VA typically costs $1,200.00 for most basement remodeling projects.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Culpeper County, VA Electrical Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>An <a href=\"http://web.culpepercounty.gov/Portals/0/Departments/Building_Department/Documents/2015WebsiteLaunchDocuments/ELECTRICAL%20PERMIT%20APPLICATION%2020151.pdf?ver=2015-09-17-175935-230\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">electrical permit</a> in Culpeper County, Virginia costs at least $50.00.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Culpeper County, VA Plumbing Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>A <a href=\"http://web.culpepercounty.gov/Portals/0/Departments/Building_Department/Documents/2015WebsiteLaunchDocuments/2016%20MECHANCIAL%20PERMIT%20APPLICATION.pdf?ver=2016-02-02-161208-330\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">plumbing permit</a> in Culpeper County, Virginia costs $50.00 with an additional renewal fee of $25.00 every six months.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Culpeper County, VA Mechanical Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>A <a href=\"http://web.culpepercounty.gov/Portals/0/Departments/Building_Department/Documents/2015WebsiteLaunchDocuments/PLUMBING%20PERMIT%202017.pdf?ver=2017-02-07-115353-000\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mechanical permit</a> in Culpeper County, Virginia costs $50.00 with an additional $50.00 per generator and an extra $50.00 for working on gas lines.</p>',2,'',95,'2017-08-27 15:38:01'),(112,'3 Reasons Why You Might Have a Cold Basement','Having a cold basement can prevent you from using your downstairs area to its fullest potential – or even at all. Find out what to do about it!','cold basement, cold basement solutions, basement finishing, basement remodeling, Washington D.C., Virginia, Maryland','3-reasons-why-you-might-have-a-cold-basement','3 Reasons Why You Might Have a Cold Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/112/9b571eb7ae50ed42d4821e1a8da52ddc','Having a cold basement can prevent you from using your downstairs area to its fullest potential – or even at all. Find out what to do about it!','<p><strong>3 Reasons Why You Might Have a Cold Basement</strong></p>\n<p>Having a <strong>cold basement </strong>can prevent you from using your downstairs area to its fullest potential &ndash; or even at all. If you are thinking of finishing or remodeling your basement, don&rsquo;t let the cold get you down. There&rsquo;s plenty of reasons for having a cold basement, and fortunately they are all reversible. &nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>1.) Ground Level Cold</strong></p>\n<p>It&rsquo;s cold beneath the earth, and this coldness can invade your basement if you aren&rsquo;t careful. Using cheap flooring and wall materials can let the cold in more easily, but that is not always the problem. Believe it or not, vents and ducts that are poorly insulated are most often the culprits for an extra cold basement.</p>\n<p><strong>2.) Moisture</strong></p>\n<p>If a basement is cold and the air is humid, it can make things feel even chillier than normal. This can also cause condensation and lead to mold and mildew problems if left unchecked.</p>\n<p><strong>3.) Basements Are Slow to Heat Up</strong></p>\n<p>A basement is the last room in your home to ever get warm. Sometimes it can take months before a basement finally reacts to warmer weather, meaning that your basement is one season behind during most months.</p>\n<p><strong>What are Some Cold Basement Solutions?</strong></p>\n<p>If you are experiencing a cold basement, check the vents and ducts for poor insulation, install a dehumidifier to keep condensation at a minimum, and use high-quality materials for your walls and floor. If you have a cold basement in Maryland, D.C. or Virginia, <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">contact Basement Masters</a> for a free consultation and an estimate on how much it will cost to warm things up!</p>',4,'',96,'2017-08-27 15:38:44'),(113,'Lee County, VA Permits for Basement Remodeling Projects','A helpful guide with links for all basement remodeling-related permits in Lee County, VA','Lee County VA, Lee County Virginia, Lee County VA permits, Lee County Virginia permits, basement remodeling, Lee County VA basement remodeling, Lee County VA electrical permits, Lee County VA plumbing permits, Lee County VA mechanical permits, Lee County VA building permits','lee-county-va-permits-for-basement-remodeling-projects','Lee County, VA Permits for Basement Remodeling Projects','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/113/3a7ec26ca8bba139328d4c2f79415aa3','A helpful guide with links for all basement remodeling-related permits in Lee County, VA!','<p><strong>Lee County, VA Permits for Basement Remodeling</strong></p>\r\n<p>To obtain a building permit in Lee County, Virginia, you must submit your <a href=\"http://www.leecova.org/pdf/app%20to%20build.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit application</a> to:</p>\r\n<p>Lee County Courthouse<br />2<sup>nd</sup> Floor, Room 206<br />P.O. Box 367<br />Jonesville, VA 24263</p>\r\n<p>A building permit is required for any new construction, addition, or major renovation within the County, including but not limited to:</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Manufactured Home</li>\r\n<li>Construction of any Residential, Commercial, or Public Buildings</li>\r\n<li>Demolition of building or structure</li>\r\n<li>Additions to existing buildings</li>\r\n<li>Alterations of structural components</li>\r\n<li>Removal or disturbing of any asbestos containing material</li>\r\n<li>Repair or replacement of any required component of a fire or smoke rated assembly</li>\r\n<li>Electric wiring</li>\r\n<li>Fire protection system, mechanical system or fuel supply system</li>\r\n<li>Installation, Removal or Closure of Underground Storage Tank, and Above Ground Storage Tank</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>A building permit for an unfinished basement in Lee County, Virginia costs 3-cents per square foot and has a $35.00 minimum.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Lee County, VA Plumbing Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>To get a plumbing permit in Lee County, VA, you must submit a <a href=\"http://www.leecova.org/pdf/Plumbing%20Application.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">plumbing permit application</a>. Plumbing permits cost $35.00.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Lee County, VA Electrical Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.leecova.org/pdf/Electrical%20Application.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Electrical permits</a> in Lee County, Virginia cost at least $35.00.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Lee County, VA Mechanical Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.leecova.org/pdf/Mechanical%20%20HVAC%20Gas%20Heaters%20Application.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mechanical permits</a> in Lee County, VA cost $25.00 for each appliance.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Certificate of Occupancy in Lee County, VA</strong></p>\r\n<p>A Certificate of Occupancy in Lee County, Virginia costs $15.00. A Building Inspector will issue a Certificate of Occupancy once inspections have been passed.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Lee County, VA Sign Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.leecova.org/pdf/Mechanical%20%20HVAC%20Gas%20Heaters%20Application.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sign permits</a> in Lee County, VA are $25.00 for up to 100 square feet, $50.00 for over 100 square feet, and $100.00 for over 200 square feet.</p>',2,'',97,'2017-08-20 15:38:56'),(114,'4 Reasons You Need to Finish Your Basement','Remodeling or finishing your basement has many other benefits besides simply looking great!','finish your basement, finishing your basement, basement remodeling, basement finishing','4-reasons-you-need-to-finish-your-basement','4 Reasons You Need to Finish Your Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/114/e5300edd774482cf3082fdce49d4c9b2','Remodeling or finishing your basement has many other benefits besides simply looking great!','<p><strong>4 Reasons You Need to Finish Your Basement</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Finishing your basement </strong>should be a top priority for your home or place of business. If you have been thinking about finishing your basement lately, here are 8 reasons you should definitely trust your instincts.</p>\n<p><strong>1.) Bye-Bye Mold and Moisture</strong></p>\n<p>Finishing your basement eliminates moisture problems before they can have a chance to turn into harmful mold. Companies like Basement Masters will finish your basement using waterproof materials to keep mold away from your ceilings, floors and walls. No water in the basement ensures that your foundation stays in place and the rest of your house looks good for generations to come.</p>\n<p><strong>2.) Save on Utilities</strong></p>\n<p>A finished basement will have no leaks for cold air or moisture to get through. The right insulation and modern basement windows will make your downstairs feel comfortable while further reducing energy costs. You can even receive rebates for certain energy-efficient upgrades.</p>\n<p><strong>3.) Increase the Property Value</strong></p>\n<p>Homeowners and businesses love to see a well-maintained basement. Finishing or remodeling your basement improves the resale value of your property in the same way that remodeling your kitchen or bathroom does. In fact, remodeling your basement allows you to include a kitchen-like area and a full-sized bathroom within your basement.</p>\n<p><strong>4.) Extra Rooms</strong></p>\n<p>A basement remodeling gives you extra space and costs much less than adding onto your business or home residence. You will have plenty of extra room without reducing the amount of outdoor square footage.</p>\n<p><strong>Need to Remodel or Finish Your Basement in Maryland, D.C. or Virginia?</strong></p>\n<p>If you need to remodel or finish your basement, the experts at Basement Masters are ready to help. We have over 10 years of experience designing basements up and down the East Coast, and we are eager to provide basement design solutions for you &ndash; quickly, efficiently, and at a reasonable price. Contact us today to schedule a free consultation!</p>',1,'',98,'2017-08-20 15:39:07'),(115,'Bland, Virginia Building Permits','Everything you need to know to get a building permit in Bland, Virginia','Bland, VA building permits, Bland, Virginia building permits, basement remodeling','bland-virginia-building-permits','Bland, Virginia Building Permits','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/115/460ef3b0ced60f3e6cc1121935ba547c','Everything you need to obtain building permits in Bland, VA','<p><strong>Bland, Virginia Building Permits </strong></p>\r\n<p>As a small county of less than 500, obtaining a building permit in Bland, Virginia requires less paperwork than other areas. There&rsquo;s no building permit application, but rather a <a href=\"http://www.blandcountyva.gov/uploads/docs/BuildingPermitForms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">list of instructions</a>. You must print or type the following information on three sheets of paper and submit it to:</p>\r\n<p>Building Official<br />County of Bland<br />P.O. Box 510<br />612 Main Street<br />Bland, VA 24315</p>\r\n<p>Page 1:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Current Date</li>\r\n<li>Contractor&rsquo;s Contact Information</li>\r\n<li>Property Owner&rsquo;s Contact Information</li>\r\n<li>Street Address and Directions</li>\r\n<li>Type of project</li>\r\n<li>Estimated budget</li>\r\n<li>Building size and height</li>\r\n<li>Square footage of each floor (including basement)</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Page 2:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Tax Map (from the Commissioner of Revenue&rsquo;s Office)</li>\r\n<li>Real Estate District Electrical District (from the Office of the Building Official)</li>\r\n<li>Any chimneys or fireplaces</li>\r\n<li>Date and signature</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Page 3:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Leave blank</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>A building permit in Bland, VA costs 16 cents per square foot.</p>',2,'',99,'2017-08-13 15:39:26'),(116,'5 Reasons Why You Should Hire Basement Remodeling Contractors','Basement remodeling contractors can save you time, money and hassle: here’s how.','how to remodel a basement, basement remodeling contractors, basement remodeling, basement remodeling company','5-reasons-why-you-should-hire-basement-remodeling-contractors','5 Reasons Why You Should Hire Basement Remodeling Contractors','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/116/69e991fe796f777acca43aef6c39e695','Basement remodeling contractors can save you time, money and hassle: here’s how.','<p><strong>5 Reason Why You Should Hire Basement Remodeling Contractors</strong></p>\n<p>Learning <strong>how to remodel a basement</strong> on your own is a tempting way to potentially save money, but if you have a nice property and want to keep it that way, then choosing a professional <strong>basement remodeling company</strong> is ultimately the only way to go. Here&rsquo;s why hiring basement remodeling contractors is a wise investment for your home or place of business. &nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Reason #1: Basement Remodeling Contractors Will Save You Time</strong></p>\n<p>A basement remodeling project can take years to complete on your own, especially if you are working at it part-time. You are learning as you go and the pace is much slower (and if you don&rsquo;t pass inspections or have all of your permits, then you are further delayed). Basement remodeling contractors, on the other hand, have years of experience and can usually complete the job in weeks. &nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Reason #2: Legal Compliancy </strong></p>\n<p>As a property owner, it is your responsibility to make sure all repairs and renovations are up to county and federal code. Just as you would not represent yourself before a judge without a lawyer, you probably would not represent yourself in front of a state inspector without a basement remodeling company. You need somebody who has all of the appropriate basement remodeling permits for your county, somebody who can make sure all of the appropriate fees are paid for ensure that any mandatory inspection dates are scheduled.</p>\n<p><strong>Reasons #3: Structural Integrity</strong></p>\n<p>Legal reasons aside, you want to use <strong>basement remodeling contractors </strong>as a way to protect the value of your investment property. Amateur basement remodeling projects can create fire hazards, weaken the foundation and set conditions for dangerous mold situations. If you are installing fixtures, putting up walls or any other major design changes, then getting a basement remodeling company should be a priority</p>\n<p><strong>Reason #4: Money</strong></p>\n<p>Learning how to remodel a basement on your own is almost guaranteed to be more costly than hiring basement remodeling contractors. Any setbacks, either during the inspections process or from improper installations, will result in you spending more time and money to fix. You are fined for inspection violations and the penalty increases for every occurrence; you are also usually charged a review fee for improperly submitting applications.</p>\n<p><strong>Reason #5: Connections</strong></p>\n<p>Unless you are a plumber, an electrician, a mechanic, a carpenter, and an interior designer, then you are probably going to struggle assembling your own basement remodeling team. A good basement remodeling company will have spent years forging reliable business relationships with the best basement contractors in the industry. They will also have researched suppliers to find the absolute lowest prices &ndash; often given to them at a special discount. &nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Need a Basement Remodeling Company?</strong></p>\n<p>Basement Masters is here to help. For more than ten years, our company has relied on a successful blend of our own in-house talent and other basement remodeling contractors &ndash; who are just as experienced as we are &ndash; that we have used time and time again for years. Check out our <a href=\"../../../../about-us/testimonials/\">customer testimonials</a> and then <a href=\"../../../../book\">schedule an appointment</a> to see how we can help you! &nbsp;</p>',4,'',100,'2017-08-13 15:39:42'),(117,'Crucial Washington DC Permits for Your Next Basement Remodeling Project','Here you can find the links to all the most important regulations and procedures on how to get any permit in DC!','basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','crucial-washington-dc-permits-for-your-next-basement-remodeling-project','Crucial Washington DC Permits for Your Next Basement Remodeling Project','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/117/8fd65f278d0e6a9813de33e6fa891f57','Washington DC electrical, plumbing, and building permit application links!','<p><strong>Crucial Washington DC Permits for Your Next Basement Remodeling Project</strong></p>\n<p>Follow these links to quickly get Washington DC permits for your next basement remodeling project:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Electrical &ndash; A Washington DC electrical permit application can be found <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/electricalsupplemental_rev_fillable_ABC_final_0.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</li>\n<li>Plumbing &ndash; A Washington DC plumbing permit application can be found <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/plumbingsupplementalfy2013afillableb_final_0.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</li>\n<li>Air Conditioning and Refrigeration &ndash; A Washington DC air conditioning and refrigeration installation permit can be found <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/ACsupplemental_fillable_final_1.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</li>\n<li>Building &ndash; A Washington DC building permit can be found <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/Building%20Permit%20Application.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Need More Washington DC Permit Information?</strong></p>\n<p>Check out our<a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/how-to-get-a-building-permit-in-washington-dc\"> previous blog </a>for all other necessary permits for your next basement remodeling project in Washington DC!</p>',2,'',101,'2017-08-06 15:40:04'),(118,'How to Get a Building Permit in Washington DC','Getting a building permit Washington DC requires a lot of forms – fortunately, we’ve included direct links to all of them. Learn more here!','building, construction, building permit, department of building, building code, basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor','how-to-get-a-building-permit-in-washington-dc','How to Get a Building Permit in Washington DC','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/118/07e98eea4c4f87f35ac01bdebfd6373a','Getting a building permit Washington DC requires a lot of forms – fortunately, we’ve included direct links to all of them.','<p><strong>How to Get a Building Permit in Washington DC</strong></p>\r\n<p>Getting a Washington DC building permit requires more paperwork than most other areas, but it isn&rsquo;t too hard once you understand the basics. This guide will quickly show you how to get a building permit in Washington DC (with direct links to all of the most important forms) for your next basement remodeling project.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Washington DC Building Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>You can either apply for a <a href=\"https://acaprod.dcra.dc.gov/dcrapublicprod1/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit online</a> (and also <a href=\"https://eservices.dcra.dc.gov/obpat/default.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">check the approval status</a> online as well), or submit a <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/Building%20Permit%20Application.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit application</a> to:</p>\r\n<p>1100 4th Street SW<br />Permit Operations Center, 2<sup>nd</sup> Floor <br />Washington DC, 20024</p>\r\n<p>You must also submit 4 copies of building plans that are at least 11 x 17 inches with an 1/8<sup>th</sup> inch-to-foot scale minimum. These plans must also have:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>All materials used (wood species, grade, concrete and steel specs, etc.)</li>\r\n<li>Manufacturer&rsquo;s design specs for any premade fireplaces</li>\r\n<li>Architectural plans with dimensions and intended room use</li>\r\n<li>Entry and exit dimensions as well as details</li>\r\n<li>R-value of all insulation used</li>\r\n<li>Height from floor to ceiling and also from floor to lowest protrusion</li>\r\n<li>Foundation information</li>\r\n<li>Framing information with cross sections and stud details</li>\r\n<li>Piping and fixture connection details</li>\r\n<li>For a full list of required information, please refer to page 2 of the<a href=\"https://eservices.dcra.dc.gov/DocumentManagementSystem/Home/retrieve?id=Guidelines%20for%20Building%20Permits.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> building permit guidelines</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>You also need to fill out and submit with your application a <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/contract_agreement.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">contract agreement</a> with the property owner&rsquo;s signature as well as the estimated costs.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Mandatory Environmental Forms</strong></p>\r\n<p>Washington DC has strict environmental regulations in place, which means more forms for basement remodeling projects. You need to submit an <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/DCRA_DOEE_EnvironmentalIntakeFormUpdatedZR16_0.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Environmental Intake Form</a>. This will determine whether you will need to submit a more in-depth <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/EISFormfillable_0.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Environmental Impact Screening Form</a> in the future &ndash; you will be notified of this usually within 30 days of submitting.</p>\r\n<p>You also may be required to contact other environmental departments (such as the Air Quality Division and the Water Quality Division). Fill out and submit this <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/DDOE%2520Environmental%2520Questionnaire.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mandatory questionnaire</a> to learn which departments you need to contact.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Zoning Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>Submit a <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/Zoning%20Data%20Summary%20sheet%209%206%2016.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">zoning datary summary form</a> with your building permit to verify important dimensional information about the worksite.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Certificate of Occupancy</strong></p>\r\n<p>If you are remodeling a basement in anything other than a single-family dwelling, then you are going to need to fill out a <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/Zoning%20Data%20Summary%20sheet%209%206%2016.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">certificate of occupancy</a> and submit it with your building permit application. Single-family homes do not have to submit this form. If you are required to do this, you also have to submit a <a href=\"https://dcra.dc.gov/sites/default/files/dc/sites/dcra/publication/attachments/CertificateofOccupancy_Authorization12_12_0.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Certificate of Occupancy Authorization Form</a> for signed consent on behalf of the property owner.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Need More Washington DC Permits?</strong></p>\r\n<p>Check out our next blog for Washington DC electrical, mechanical, and plumbing permit applications!</p>',2,'',102,'2017-08-06 15:40:20'),(119,'When do You Need a Dehumidifier?','Everybody who owns a house has to deal with some moisture in their basement. Learn here how to figure out if you need a dehumidifier!','waterproof basement, dehumidifier, basement renovation, basement remodeling, basement dehumidifier','when-do-you-need-a-dehumidifier','When do You Need a Dehumidifier?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/119/48409023745dd4ee28e546e1ce3b492a','You should get a basement dehumidifier if...','<p><strong>When Do You Need a Basement Dehumidifier?</strong></p>\n<p>Whether you are living in your basement or simply using it for laundry and storage, you are still going to have to deal with potential moisture problems. Moisture can seep into basement through the foundation, from leaky pipes or simply in the form of condensation from high humidity levels, where it can develop into mold spores and lead to <a href=\"https://health.uconn.edu/occupational-environmental/wp-content/uploads/sites/25/2015/12/mold_guide.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">health problems</a>. One of the ways to prevent this from happening is by getting a basement dehumidifier.</p>\n<p>You should get a basement dehumidifier if:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mold is on the walls</li>\n<li>The air feels humid</li>\n<li>The basement smells moldy or of mildew</li>\n<li>The walls are damp (especially drywall)</li>\n<li>Household items in the basement are becoming moldy, have mildew or smell foul</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>If You Need a Basement Humidifier . . .</strong></p>\n<p>Then you might want to get one set up by the pros. Basement Masters can provide you with a full-fledged dehumidification system that will keep your basement dry for years to come. <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact us</a> now to discover how our top-of-the-line systems are better than anything you can buy in stores or online!</p>',3,'',103,'2017-07-30 15:40:35'),(120,'Arlington, VA Permits and Fees for Basement Remodeling (Updated 2022)','Looking for relevant building permits and fees in Arlington, VA? This helpful guide provides all of the permit links you\'ll need for your next basement project!','Arlington, Arlington Virginia, VA, Permits, Basement Remodeling Projects, basement renovation, building fees, building permits, basement building permits, basement renovation permits, basement finishing permits, electrical permits, plumbing permits, mechanical permits','arlington-va-permits-and-fees-for-basement-remodeling-updated-2022','Arlington, VA Permits and Fees for Basement Remodeling (Updated 2022)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/120/8b86d33ebe8d5234428a28f96a6d9653','This guide will help you find relevant links and information for building, electrical, plumbing, and mechanical permits in Arlington, VA!','<p>This guide provides links for all of the permits for your next Arlington, Virginia basement project.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Arlington, VA Building Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>The Arlington County Permit Office is &nbsp;<strong>CLOSED</strong> for in-person customer service.&nbsp;Many services are available online</p>\r\n<p>Types of projects that require a residential building permit:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Adding, removing or relocating walls or fixtures.</li>\r\n<li>Building a new house.</li>\r\n<li>Additions: including projects such as adding finished square footage to your home or building a porch. Exterior work such as building a deck or adding a window well for egress may also be considered an addition.</li>\r\n<li>Alterations: including projects such as renovating a kitchen, refinishing or waterproofing a basement and remodeling a bathroom. If you&rsquo;re planning to alter your kitchen or bathroom and you&rsquo;re only replacing cabinets or appliances (as long as they&rsquo;re not fueled by gas or oil), or fixtures (without relocating any pipes or dry wall), in the exact same location, there are no permits required and you may begin work immediately.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>For information about when a permit is not required, see&nbsp;&sect;108.2&nbsp;of the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.arlingtonva.us/Government/Programs/Building/Codes-Ordinances/Building\" target=\"_self\">Building Code</a>&nbsp;or contact the Inspection Services Division (ISD):&nbsp;<a href=\"tel:7032283800\">703-228-3800</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Building permits can be obtained by making an account with the<a href=\"http://archives.arlingtonva.us/planreview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> Arlington County E-plan Review</a>, which allows you to digitally submit your plans and building permit application. The site plans must:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Be scaled so that an 1/8<sup>th</sup> inch equals one square foot (minimum); all dimensions must be listed</li>\r\n<li>The year of the code used for the design</li>\r\n<li>Building designer&rsquo;s name, address, and occupation (with electronic signature, seal and date if possible)</li>\r\n<li>Material specifications (lumber grade, concrete and steel strength, etc.)</li>\r\n<li>Foundation plan</li>\r\n<li>Floor plans with labeled rooms</li>\r\n<li>Smoke alarm locations</li>\r\n<li>Sheathing thickness and type of a &ldquo;typical wall section&rdquo;</li>\r\n<li>R-value and U-factors of insulation</li>\r\n<li>Wall bracing (including locations for braced wall lines and panels)</li>\r\n<li>Building cross sections with labeled posts, joists and beams</li>\r\n<li>Frontal, side and rear elevations with window and door dimensions, along with exterior grade</li>\r\n<li>Safety glazing locations</li>\r\n<li>Design specifications for pre-fabricated fireplaces according to manufacturer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Building permits in Arlington, VA cost around $60.00-$120.00 for a typical residential basement remodeling project.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.arlingtonva.us/Government/Programs/Building/Permits/Fee-Schedules\">Fee Schedules</a>&nbsp;provide the range of fees charged for each type of application or activity related to land development in Arlington. Fees cover permitting, plan review, enforcement, inspection, service delivery, performance agreements and conditions. There are separate fee schedules for Inspection Services Division (ISD), Zoning and the Department of Environmental Services (DES). Some permits involve fees from more than one schedule.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><a class=\"opens-in-new-tab\" href=\"https://archives.arlingtonva.us/onlinepayment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" aria-describedby=\"new-window-0\">Pay ePlan fees online</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>The Architectural, Structural and Mechanical Plan Requirements</h2>\r\n<p>The Architectural, Structural and Mechanical Plan Requirements (<a href=\"https://building.arlingtonva.us/resource/architectural-structural-and-mechanical-plan-requirements/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ASMP</a>) is a strict list of regulations that all basement remodeling projects must follow. However, these requirements can sometimes be waived with the request of a <a href=\"https://arlingtonva.s3.dualstack.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/38/2016/08/mechanicalwaiver.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">waiver</a> that has been signed by the property owner.</p>\r\n<h2>Arlington, VA Electrical Permit</h2>\r\n<p>The average cost of an electrical permit in Arlington, Virginia is $60.00, with a $7.20 charge per circuit. An electrical permit application can be found <a href=\"https://arlingtonva.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/38/2019/09/Electrical-Permit-Application-2019.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>. Electrical, Plumbing, and mechanical permit fees can all be found in the <a href=\"https://arlingtonva.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/38/2019/06/Inspection-Services-Fee-Schedule-2019.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">same pdf file</a>.</p>\r\n<h2>Arlington, VA Plumbing &amp; Gas Permit</h2>\r\n<p>The average cost of a plumbing permit in Arlington, Virginia is $56.00, with an additional $24.00 charge for every fixture, drain and appliance. The plumbing and gas permit application can be found <a href=\"https://arlingtonva.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/38/2019/09/Plumbing-and-Gas-Permit-Application-2019.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>. Gas fixtures are included with a plumbing permit, but the rest of fees can be found&nbsp;<a href=\"https://arlingtonva.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/38/2019/06/Inspection-Services-Fee-Schedule-2019.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</p>\r\n<h2>Arlington, VA Mechanical Permit</h2>\r\n<p>A mechanical permit must be obtained for any boilers, furnaces, HVAC systems, refrigeration systems, and any other components related to these systems. You must submit a copy of the plan showing all new systems along with the <a href=\"https://arlingtonva.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/38/2019/09/Mechanical-Permit-Application-2019.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mechanical permit application</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The average cost of a mechanical permit in Arlington, VA is $171.00 for the first HVAC system (plus the base fee of $56.00). Additional HVAC systems will cost an extra $57.00 each. A total list of fees can be found inside the <a href=\"https://arlingtonva.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/38/2019/06/Inspection-Services-Fee-Schedule-2019.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Inspection Services Fee Schedule pdf file</a>.</p>\r\n<h2>More Information About Arlington, VA Basement Remodeling Permits</h2>\r\n<p>Any additional questions can be answered by calling a county permit specialist at 703-228-3800 between 8 a.m. and 4:30 p.m, Monday through Friday.</p>\r\n<p>You can also stop by the <a href=\"https://www.arlingtonva.us/locations/permit-office/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">office in person</a> at:<br />2100 Clarendon Blvd. Suite 1000 (10th floor)<br />Arlington, VA 22201</p>',2,'',104,'2017-07-23 15:41:01'),(121,'Charlotte County, Virginia Basement Remodeling Building Permits And Fees','This helpful guide will explain the permit process for your next Charlotte County, Virginia basement remodeling project!','Charlotte County, VA, Virginia, basement remodeling, basement renovation, building permit, building fee','charlotte-county-virginia-basement-remodeling-building-permits-and-fees','Charlotte County, Virginia Basement Remodeling Building Permits And Fees','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/121/46fdd75dcda8ff90e683de92cca9c771','This helpful guide will explain the permit process for your next Charlotte County, Virginia basement remodeling project!','<p><strong>Charlotte County, Virginia Basement Remodeling Building Permits And Fees</strong></p>\r\n<p>This helpful guide will explain the permit process for your next Charlotte County, Virginia basement remodeling project!</p>\r\n<p><strong>Charlotte County, Virginia Basement Remodeling Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p><span class=\"h4\">Building permit applications must be completed and approved before work can begin.&nbsp; A certificate of occupancy must be obtained from the Building Inspector before a building or structure can be occupied.&nbsp; <br /><br />Building permit applications can be obtained <a href=\"https://www.charlotteva.com/pdfs/Building%20Permit%20Application.pdf\">here</a> or at the County Administration Office.&nbsp; To obtain an approved building permit you will need the following:<br /></span></p>\r\n<ul class=\"h4\">\r\n<li>An approved zoning permit application (if applicable)</li>\r\n<li>A septic tank and well permit from the Health Department if new septic and/or well are being installed for the structure</li>\r\n<li>A health department septic system review if connecting new construction to an existing system or adding bedrooms or bathrooms to an existing structure</li>\r\n<li>Titles for singlewides (as proof of date of manufacture)</li>\r\n<li>Contractor\'s information (name, phone number and license number)</li>\r\n<li>Estimated cost of job</li>\r\n<li>Size of project (measurements or square footage of main structures, additions, porches, decks, etc.) and a copy of the building plans for new construction</li>\r\n<li>Payment in the form of a check, cash, or credit card.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Charlotte County Administration Office<br />250 LeGrande Avenue, Suite A<br />PO Box 608<br />Charlotte Court House Virginia, 23923<br />Phone: (434) 542-5117&nbsp;<br />Fax: (434) 542-5248</p>\r\n<p><br />You must include with your application the contractor&rsquo;s contact information and license number, the estimated basement remodeling project budget, and one copy of the building plans. Most building permit fees cost 15 cents per square foot.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><span class=\"h3\">Building Permit Fees*<br /></span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<table>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr class=\"tableheader\">\r\n<td>Project</td>\r\n<td>Cost</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Residential Construction</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; 15<span class=\"style3\">&cent;</span> per Square Foot ($100 Minimum)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Residential Additions</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; 15<span class=\"style3\">&cent;</span> per Square Foot (No Minimum)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Mobile Homes (Singlewides)</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; $50.00 Flat Fee</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Modular Homes</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; 15<span class=\"style3\">&cent;</span> per Square Foot ($100 Minimum)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Church Construction</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; 12<span class=\"style3\">&cent;</span> per Square Foot ($100 Minimum)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Church Additions</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; 12<span class=\"style3\">&cent;</span> per Square Foot (No Minimum)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Commercial or Industrial Construction</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; 12<span class=\"style3\">&cent;</span> per Square Foot ($150 Minimum)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Commercial or Industrial Additions</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; 12<span class=\"style3\">&cent;</span> per Square Foot (No Minimum)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Demolition</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; $30.00 per Building</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Cell Towers</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; 3% of Cost (Including Labor Cost)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Electric</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;&nbsp;$30.00</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Plumbing</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; $30.00&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Billboard &amp; Pole Signs</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; $15.00&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Roof &amp; Projecting Signs</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;&nbsp;$25.00</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Private Swimming Pools</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; $25.00</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Public Swimming Pools</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; $75.00</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Renovations</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; $6.00 per $1000 of Cost (Minimum $35)&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Underground Storage Tank Removal</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp; $35.00 per Tank&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"tabledata\">\r\n<td>Mechanical Inspections</td>\r\n<td>&nbsp;&nbsp;$30.00</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><strong>Certificate of Occupancy</strong></p>\r\n<p>A certificate of occupancy must also be obtained from the Building Inspector&rsquo;s Office:</p>\r\n<p>John Hess, Building Inspector<br />250 LeGrande Avenue, Suite A<br />P. O. Box 608<br />Charlotte Court House, VA 23923&nbsp;<br />Phone: (434) 542-5404</p>',2,'',105,'2017-07-23 15:41:18'),(122,'King and Queen County, VA Basement Remodeling Permits and Fees','Planning to start a project in King and Queen County? Here is a breakdown of the application and fees you need to know about with links!','King and Queen County, VA, Virginia, basement remodeling, basement renovation, building permit, building fee, building code, general contractor','king-and-queen-county-va-basement-remodeling-permits-and-fees','King and Queen County, VA Basement Remodeling Permits and Fees','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/122/fa503dfe81a0ef39a04b39458208ab82','','<p><strong>King and Queen County, VA Basement Remodeling Permits and Fees</strong></p>\r\n<p>You can obtain all of the necessary King and Queen County, VA permits for your next basement remodeling project by filling out just one form. This <a href=\"http://www.kingandqueenco.net/html/govt/bzondocs/epma_application.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">application</a> covers permits for electrical, plumbing, mechanical, demolition, gas, generators, building, and general alternations.</p>\r\n<p>Here is a breakdown of King and Queen County permit fees:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Building Permit &ndash; $0.20 per square foot</li>\r\n<li>Electrical Permit &ndash; $40 minimum ($50 per generator)</li>\r\n<li>Plumbing Permit &ndash; $40 minimum ($40 per additional structure)</li>\r\n<li>Mechanical Permit &ndash; 40 minimum ($40 per additional structure)</li>\r\n<li>Plan Review &ndash; $20.00</li>\r\n<li>Revisions &ndash; $50.00 each time</li>\r\n<li>Six-month Extension (Building Permit) &ndash; $25.00</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Feel free to look at the full list of <a href=\"http://www.kingandqueenco.net/html/govt/bzondocs/permfees.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">fees</a>.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Site Plans</strong></p>\r\n<p>Site plans are usually not required for residential basement remodeling projects, but inspections are. To see if you need to include site plans with your building permit application, check <a href=\"https://library.municode.com/va/king_and_queen_county/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=PTIIUNLAUSRE_CH3ZO_ART14SIPLRE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Section 3-311</a> of the Zoning laws.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Inspections</strong></p>\r\n<p>Inspections in King and Queen County, VA can be performed on the same day if they are requested before 9:30 a.m.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The basement walls must be inspected for drain tiles and waterproofing</li>\r\n<li>All pipes must provide at least 5 psi for moving water</li>\r\n<li>Ductwork, boots, returns, refrigerant and condensate lines are inspected.</li>\r\n<li>Gas lines require a minimum of 15 psi.</li>\r\n<li>All alarms must be wired and labeled for smoke or carbon</li>\r\n<li>You have until the final inspection to insulate any ceiling or floor areas</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>It costs $50 to re-inspect a basement remodeling project the first time, and $100.00 to re-inspect a basement project two times and more.</p>',2,'',106,'2017-07-16 15:41:29'),(123,'Is Having Silverfish in Your Basement a Problem?','If you find silverfish in your basement, it could be a sign of some structural problem in your basement. Find out here what to do in this case!','Silverfish, basement, basement remodeling, basement renovation, moisture','is-having-silverfish-in-your-basement-a-problem','Is Having Silverfish in Your Basement a Problem?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/123/30dc399c27b431d661e7beaf5194ea66','','<p><strong>Is Having Silverfish in Your Basement a Problem?</strong></p>\n<p>The short answer: maybe! Having <strong>silverfish in your basement</strong> is common in some parts of Maryland and Virginia, and it doesn&rsquo;t automatically mean that something major is wrong. Silverfish can become pests in numbers, but aside from looking gross, they don&rsquo;t spread diseases to humans. With that said, however, they can be a sign of a serious structural problem in your basement that may need to be addressed. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>What are Silverfish Doing in My Basement?</strong></p>\n<p>Silverfish are nocturnal bugs that spend their nights foraging for food. Sometimes their meals could be cardboard, and sometimes it could be old photographs (so they can become a menace to your precious scrapbook collection).</p>\n<p>Here&rsquo;s the thing that should concern you: silverfish love moisture, so if you see them in your basement, then it could be too damp. This could be weather-related, or it could be due to foundational problems and groundwater seeping in.</p>\n<p><strong>What to do if I Find Silverfish in My Basement?</strong></p>\n<p>If you are finding a large number of these creepy crawlers in your basement, then it could be time to contact the professionals. Before you call the exterminator though, you might want to contact a basement remodeling company instead. After all, if this is a structural problem that is causing the infestation, then the silverfish will probably return once the chemicals wear off.</p>\n<p>So before you &ldquo;bug bomb&rdquo; your entire basement, contact the professionals at Basement Masters (Maryland and Virginia only) and schedule an <a href=\"#\">appointment for inspection</a>. You&rsquo;ll find that the solution might be as easy as installing a dehumidifier, or even a simple caulk job. We&rsquo;re ready to inspect your basement and discuss permanent options to solve your silverfish problem today!</p>',3,'',107,'2017-07-16 15:41:39'),(124,'Montgomery County, MD Permits and Fees (Basement Remodeling)','This quick guide will show you where to find online Montgomery County, MD permit applications, as well as explaining the fees and other requirnements for your next basement remodeling project!','Montgomery Country, Maryland, MD, building permit, building fee, basement remodeling, general contractor','montgomery-county-md-permits-and-fees-basement-remodeling','Montgomery County, MD Permits and Fees (Basement Remodeling)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/124/761e24aeff2c66a5d9e392c53f108e3b','','<p><strong>Montgomery County, MD Permits and Fees (Basement Remodeling)</strong></p>\r\n<p>This quick guide will show you where to find online Montgomery County, MD permit applications, as well as explaining the fees and other requirnements for your next basement remodeling project.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Montgomery County, MD Building Permit</strong></p>\r\n<p>A permit is required prior to reconstruction or renovation to an existing structure other than repair or addition. A permit is not required for painting, wallpapering, replacing a faucet, installing countertops, installing hardwood floors or tiles or carpeting if no structural changes are performed. Reconstruction includes partial demolition (that does not require a demolition permit) and rebuilding a structure or building.</p>\r\n<p>If your construction project includes both alteration and addition to the structure you will receive an Add/Alter permit.<br /><br />If your project includes an accessory dwelling unit (ADU) such as accessory apartment, granny pod, backyard cottage or carriage house, among others, please read the <a href=\"https://www.montgomerycountymd.gov/DPS/Resources/Files/RCI/ADUGuidelines.pdf\">applicable requirements.&nbsp;</a></p>\r\n<p><strong>DPS is no longer accepting paper permit applications or plans. Information must be submitted using our eServices programs. For assistance with eServices please email DPS.eServices@montgomerycountymd.gov.</strong></p>\r\n<p>You must also include two sets of plans (including site plans). A set plan includes the following:</p>\r\n<p>Drainage Plans (2 Sets):</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Property lines</li>\r\n<li>Lot dimensions</li>\r\n<li>All existing drainage systems, devices, and &ldquo;other impervious structures&rdquo;</li>\r\n<li>Elevations of the basement floor</li>\r\n<li>Arrows pointing the drainage pattern on all current and proposed drainage systems</li>\r\n<li>A seal of approval from a Maryland-based engineer, survey or architect, including their date and official signature.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Architectural Plans (2 sets):</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>One floor plan should outline existing rooms and include the room&rsquo;s purpose, dimensions, materials, exit routes, and stairs, doors, and windows</li>\r\n<li>One floor plan should outline proposed rooms and include the same information.</li>\r\n<li>The gross square footage of the new space needs to be included</li>\r\n<li>Smoke and carbon monoxide alarms must be included</li>\r\n<li>Existing foundational structures must be included, and size, spacing, and material of all sheathing, rafters, trusses, joints, beams, and other &ldquo;framing elements&rdquo; must be outlined</li>\r\n<li>The proposed foundational structures must be included, and the same information about framing elements must be provided.</li>\r\n<li>Crawl space information</li>\r\n<li>Brace wall lines and braced wall panels</li>\r\n<li>Doors, windows, and other exterior exits must be shown</li>\r\n<li>Vertical dimensions (ceiling heights, ductwork clearances, window and door opening dimensions, etc.</li>\r\n<li>Thermal envelope</li>\r\n<li>Stairway materials and dimensions of all treads, risers, landings, winders, guards, handrails</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Check out the full list of Montgomery County, MD building permit <a href=\"http://permittingservices.montgomerycountymd.gov/DPS/pdf/GuidelinesForAdditionsAlterationsPlanSubmittal.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">plan requirements</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Most of the time, your building permit fee will be $0.681345 per SF</p>\r\n<p>.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Electrical Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>A Montgomery County, MD <a href=\"https://permittingservices.montgomerycountymd.gov/ApplyOnline/account/Login.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">electrical permit</a> is required for &ldquo;work that involves installing, relocating, repairing, or maintaining any electrical wiring or device designed for conducing, consuming or converting electrical current&rdquo; (no matter the amperage), and costs at least $90.00. &nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Mechanical Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>A <a href=\"http://permittingservices.montgomerycountymd.gov/DPS/pdf/ApplicationForMechanicalPermit.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mechanical permit</a> is needed for HVAC work, and cost a minimum of $65.00.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Septic System Approval</strong></p>\r\n<p>Almost every basement remodeling project must be reviewed by the state for septic system compliance. Read more <a href=\"http://permittingservices.montgomerycountymd.gov/DPS/wellseptic/SepticSystemsAndBuildingPermits.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">information</a>.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Fire Alarm Permit</strong></p>\r\n<p>Any installation, alteration, or modification of the fire alarm system requires a permit, including repairs. The fee depends on the number of fire alarms on the premises.</p>\r\n<p><strong>What is the Minimum Ceiling Clearance Requirement for Montgomery County, MD Basement Remodeling Projects?</strong></p>\r\n<p>Since there are conflicting laws in Montgomery County, MD for basement ceiling heights, the legal height of your basement ceiling depends on the year that the building permit was issued. If the permit was issued before October 2000, the minimal ceiling height is 6&rsquo;8, and 6&rsquo;4 when obstructions such as beams, columns, and ducts are present (they also have to be a minimum of 4&rdquo; on center). If the permit was issued after October 2000, then the minimal ceiling height is 7&ldquo;, with a minimum of 6&rsquo;6 in regards to beams and girders (again, they also have to be a minimum of 4&rdquo; on center).</p>\r\n<p>Read the <a href=\"http://permittingservices.montgomerycountymd.gov/DPS/pdf/BCP11-02BasementCeilingHeight.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">full explanation</a>.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Additional Permit Fees</strong></p>\r\n<p>If you need to resubmit your permit application for any reason, it usually costs $49.00 for each resubmission.</p>\r\n<p>If you would like us to handle your project from the permitting all the way to the final touches, click the link with your location below to get an online quote and schedule an in-home consultation.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"../../basement-finishing-area/md/montgomery/rockville\">Basement Finishing in Rockville, Maryland</a></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"../../basement-finishing-area/md/montgomery\">Basement Finishing in Montgomery County</a></p>',2,'',108,'2017-07-09 15:42:23'),(125,'How to Have a Successful Basement Remodeling Consultation','You are on your way to start your basement remodeling project, one of the crucial steps is to have a successful consultation with the contractor. Here are some tips to make sure it goes well!','basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, consultation, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','how-to-have-a-successful-basement-remodeling-consultation','How to Have a Successful Basement Remodeling Consultation','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/125/91e6a49ae122325d432ac4b90dd1dc00','','<p>You&rsquo;ve checked their insurance, references, and work history, and now you are ready to meet with a <strong>remodeling contractor</strong> at your home or place of business. The best remodeling contractors will make the consultation go as smoothly as the rest of the <strong>remodeling project</strong>, but there are still some things that you can on your end to make sure the <strong>remodeling consultation</strong> goes well. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>It&rsquo;s best to make sure that all members of the family or business team attend the meeting. This way, everyone gets the same information as well as plenty of opportunities to ask questions. &nbsp;Most consultations take anywhere an hour-and-a-half to two hours, so if this is a home consultation and you have young ones, then you might want to pop in a movie for them to watch.</p>\n<p>One of the most important aspects of the meeting is to establish design ideas for the basement remodeling. Having photographs from magazines or the internet of basements that you like is absolutely a good place to start. The more ideas you share, the more clearly the basement remodeling contractor will see your vision &ndash; and if you aren&rsquo;t sure what designs you like, ask for suggestions!</p>\n<p>Fleshing out the design details will help the remodeling contractor to establish a budget, which is the second major reason for a remodeling consultation. Try to have a budget in mind before the consultation begins. This will help the remodeling contractor choose different tiers of materials and design options available.</p>\n<p>The final step of a consultation is establishing a timeline. Your time is absolutely valuable, but avoid giving the remodeling contractor a deadline to complete the project. Instead, allow them to lead in this area and provide a timeline for you. Asking the remodeling contractor to explain the reasoning behind their timeline is a good idea, and try to get them to give deadlines for each major step as well.</p>',4,'',109,'2017-07-01 15:42:36'),(126,'Alexandria, VA Permits for Basement Remodeling','Here you will find a guide on how to obtain a building permit in Alexandria, VA with all the necessary links!','Alexandria VA Permits, Basement Remodeling, Basement renovation, general contractor, building permits, building fees','alexandria-va-permits-for-basement-remodeling','Alexandria, VA Permits for Basement Remodeling','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/126/54caccc393781e04fd361b463fa396a0','','<p><strong>Alexandria, VA Permits for Basement Remodeling</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Permit Center</strong> </p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Open to the public for in-person service Monday through Friday from 8:00am until 4:15pm.</li>\r\n<li>The City of Alexandria Permit Center is now located on the fourth floor, room 4200.</li>\r\n<li>Currently, we are asking for customers to only submit applications electronically through APEX.</li>\r\n<li>The Alexandria Permitting and Land Use System (<a href=\"https://apex.alexandriava.gov/EnerGov_Prod/SelfService\">APEX</a>) is available 24 hours a day from your computer or mobile device.</li>\r\n<li>Customer assistance is still available by email&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:Permit.Center@alexandriava.gov?subject=re%3A%20Permit%20Center\">Permit.Center@alexandriava.gov</a><a href=\"mailto:Permit.Center@alexandriava.gov?subject=re%3A%20Permit%20Center\">&nbsp;</a>or by calling 703.746.4200. A support team able to respond to inquiries within 24 hours or one business day.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>In order to obtain a building permit in Alexandria, VA, you must submit 5 site plans containing the following information:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The name of each room along with the window and door sizes</li>\r\n<li>Emergency escape openings (windows must be 24&rdquo; x 20&rdquo; with a 5 square foot minimum, and a 44&rdquo; maximum sill height</li>\r\n<li>The ceiling height must have a 7-foot minimum clearance</li>\r\n<li>A plumbing plan</li>\r\n<li>An electrical plan</li>\r\n<li>A mechanical plan</li>\r\n<li>The R-value of insulation</li>\r\n<li>Duct layout, sizes and ventilation rate (expressed in 3 cubic feet per minute)</li>\r\n<li>Ventilation locations (exhaust ducts and termination for the clothes dryer and toilet, for example)</li>\r\n<li>Smoke detectors</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Plans cannot be smaller than 8 &frac12; inches by 11 inches, and no larger than 24 inches by 36 inches. It costs $75.00 to have your site plans reviewed. For the full site plan requirements, please refer to this basement remodeling <a href=\"https://www.alexandriava.gov/uploadedFiles/Plan%20Submission%20Checklist%20-%20Finishing%20A%20Basement%20F-FIR-CO83%20REV%203.12.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">checklist</a>. &nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Permit Applications</strong></p>\r\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 4\">\r\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n<div class=\"column\">\r\n<p>Residential alterations and repairs are calculated at $0.30 per square foot of gross floor area; $18.00 per $1,000 of the total construction cost; or minimum permit fee; whichever is greater. The gross floor area shall be the floor area within the perimeter of the outside walls of the building or space under construction. The total construction cost shall include all involved labor and material valued at the current retail market value plus overhead and profit (total contract price).</p>\r\n<p>35% Deposit is required for plan review &ndash; based on estimated permit fee (Refer to&nbsp; <a class=\"coa-pdf-icon\" title=\"Department of Code Administration Fee Schedule (opens in new window)\" href=\"https://www.alexandriava.gov/uploadedFiles/2017%20Fee%20Schedule%20Res%20No%202769.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Department of Code Administration Fee Schedule</a><a title=\"(opens in new window) Department of Code Administration Fee Schedule&nbsp;\" href=\"https://www.alexandriava.gov/uploadedFiles/Fee%20Schedule%202015%20revised%20march%202014%20without%20change%20indicators%205%202014.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> </a>).</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>All permits cost at least $85.00 to obtain. Building, electrical, mechanical, plumbing, gas, demolition, and other permits are all filed online. To file for Alexandria, VA permits, please refer to the official government <a href=\"http://permits.alexandriava.gov/tm_bin/tmw_cmd.pl?tmw_cmd=UserHome&amp;tmw_current=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">online permit center</a>.</p>',2,'',110,'2017-06-25 15:42:46'),(127,'Here\'s What to do When Your Basement Floods','How do you handle a basement flood situation? What can you do to prevent it? Learn more here.','basement floods, basement flooding, waterproof basement,  basement remodeling, basement renovation, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','heres-what-to-do-when-your-basement-floods','Here\'s What to do When Your Basement Floods','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/127/f2afc6a1d0acb188f08edca15550d058','','<p>B<strong>asement flooding </strong>is a potentially dangerous situation if you do the wrong things. Here&rsquo;s exactly what to do the next time your <strong>basement floods </strong>so that you and your family stay safe.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Turn off the electricity and gas in the basement area. Do not touch the water if the power is still on. Call an electrician or a basement company if you aren&rsquo;t sure how to shut off power to these areas.</li>\n<li>If the basement flooding is due to bad weather, wait until the rain stops before taking action. Otherwise, you should react immediately.</li>\n<li>Wear boots and gloves to avoid electric shocks.</li>\n<li>If the water is coming in from a burst pipe, then shut off the water in the basement.</li>\n<li>Check the floor drain for clogs, if applicable.</li>\n<li>A wet vacuum, sump pump, or even a mop and bucket can be used to remove the water.</li>\n<li>Move any damaged belongings away from the basement and let them dry in an open area. Let them dry outside if it is sunny. Some items may take up to 48 hours to dry. If they are still wet, then you should through them away.</li>\n<li>Don&rsquo;t move any electrical appliances such as televisions or lamps. They can store a charge and cause a shock. Let them dry where they are and do not touch them for at least 48 hours.</li>\n<li>Any wet cardboard boxes should be thrown away or else bacteria can grow.</li>\n<li>The carpeting should be removed as soon as possible so that the basement floor can fully dry. Sometimes the carpet can be dried, but most of the time it simply mildews and lessens the air quality.</li>\n<li>Open the doors and windows (weather permitting) for several days. You can also put fans around the room and get a dehumidifier as well.</li>\n<li>Wash the floors and walls, and remove any wet drywall.</li>\n<li>Spray the floor and walls with an anti-mildew spray.</li>\n<li>If you have basement flooding insurance, then report the flood to your home insurance company.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>When to Call the Professionals</strong></h2>\n<p>If you see mold or mildew spreading, or if the water was more than 6 inches deep, then you should get a <a href=\"#\">professional opinion</a>. A basement waterproofing company can assess the basement flooding situation and come up with solutions to prevent it from happening again. They also can spot damage in areas that you may not know about (or want to crawl around in).</p>',3,'',111,'2017-06-24 15:42:55'),(128,'Loudoun County, VA Permits and Fees (Basement Remodeling)','Check out the breakdown of all the permits, applications and fees you need to go through to start your project in Loudoun County, VA! Link to official websites included!','Loudoun County, VA permits, basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor, building permits, building fees,  basemen finishingt','loudoun-county-va-permits-and-fees-basement-remodeling','Loudoun County, VA Permits and Fees (Basement Remodeling)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/128/4a5c68016bbc2664dcbfe3f4c0f84313','','<p><strong>Loudoun County, VA Permits and Fees (Basement Remodeling)</strong></p>\r\n<h1 id=\"versionHeadLine\" class=\"headline\">Permitting</h1>\r\n<div id=\"cc0ff074c7-ce0e-4b5e-82b5-ba08239f0fda\" class=\"pageContent cpGrid cpGrid24\" data-containerid=\"0ff074c7-ce0e-4b5e-82b5-ba08239f0fda\">\r\n<div class=\"row outer wide\">\r\n<div class=\"outer col col24 first last\" data-widgetcontainerid=\"0477ecd5-f98c-4642-9d39-8465dd95d1cc\">\r\n<div class=\"row nest first last wide\">\r\n<div class=\"inner col col24 first last ida3b3df9a-4836-4f63-9ec3-0f04c895c5f2\" data-widgetcontainerid=\"a3b3df9a-4836-4f63-9ec3-0f04c895c5f2\">\r\n<div id=\"divEditor7f7bc124-a889-4c14-bd15-e61c9c109b00\" class=\"widget editor pageStyles wide\" data-elementqueryclasses=\"{&quot;wide-narrow&quot;:&quot;min-width:25em&quot;}\">\r\n<div class=\"fr-view\">\r\n<p>Before beginning residential or commercial construction in Loudoun County, you must obtain permits from the appropriate county agencies and, if applicable, the appropriate agencies of the<a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/193/Incorporated-Towns\">&nbsp;incorporated towns</a>.</p>\r\n<div data-elementqueryclasses=\"&rsquo;&rsquo;&rsquo;&rsquo;&rsquo;{&quot;wide-narrow&quot;:&quot;min-width:25em&quot;}&rsquo;&rsquo;&rsquo;&rsquo;&rsquo;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Building permits are required for all new construction and remodeling projects.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Zoning permits are required for most construction projects.</li>\r\n<li>The Department of Building and Development issues building permits and grading permits for the entire county, and zoning permits &nbsp;for property which is located outside the incorporated towns.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 class=\"subhead1 \">Required Permits</h2>\r\n<p>The types of permits that may be required, depending on the complexity of the project, are as follows:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A building and zoning permit application is required for construction of architectural and structural elements, signed by the property owner.&nbsp;\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>If your property is located in an <a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/towns\">incorporated town</a> within Loudoun County, submit an approved zoning permit from the town with your application.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Trade permits:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>An electrical permit is required for all electrical installations.</li>\r\n<li>A gas permit is required for installations of all elements and appliances associated with gas piping systems.</li>\r\n<li>A mechanical permit is required when adding or extending ductwork.</li>\r\n<li>A plumbing permit is required for installations of all elements and appliances associated with plumbing systems.<a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/2904/Building-and-Zoning-Permit-Application-F\"><br /></a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/2904/Building-and-Zoning-Permit-Application-F\">Get the permit application forms here</a>.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>To obtain a building permit in Loudoun County, VA for your next basement remodeling project, you will need to submit a building permit <a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/DocumentCenter/View/117253\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">application</a> to the Building and Development Permit Counter, which can be found on the second floor of the Loudoun County Government Center (1 Harrison Street, S.E., Second Floor &ndash; Leesburg, Virginia, 20175). You must also submit three sets of plans that clearly show:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The name and intended purpose of each room.</li>\r\n<li>The stairs, furnace, water heater, and the electric panelboard.</li>\r\n<li>All smoke detectors</li>\r\n<li>The ceiling height (the minimal ceiling height in Loudoun, VA is 7 feet, with a 6&rsquo;6 minimum on any ceiling projections)</li>\r\n<li>Bedroom Egress Window Dimensions &ndash; All bedrooms need an emergency egress exit window with a minimum of 5 square feet of net clearance (opening height), 24-inch minimum clearance opening height, and 20-inch opening width.</li>\r\n<li>The height of the sill above the floor (after the floor is finished).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>If you are remodeling a residential basement, you can use the Loudoun County <a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/DocumentCenter/Home/View/897\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Suggested Standards</a> for Finishing Basements instead of site plans. However, this is only for residential projects that:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Include kitchens</li>\r\n<li>Alter load-bearing walls, exterior walls, or beams and columns (including posts)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Commercial projects (and certain residential projects) may require additional documentation. Call a county plan reviewer at (703) 777-0220) between 8:30 a.m. &ndash; 4:00 p.m., Monday through Friday to find out more. Loudoun County, VA building permits cost a minimum of $65.00.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Loudoun County, VA Electrical Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>Loudoun County, VA <a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/DocumentCenter/View/97963\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">electrical permits</a> are required for adding any electrical outlets and fixtures, and the cost depends on the equipment listed on the application.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Loudoun County, VA Plumbing Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>Loudoun County, VA <a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/DocumentCenter/View/97968\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">plumbing permits</a> are required for installing, setting or replacing any plumbing fixtures, and the price depends on the equipment listed on the application.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Loudoun County, VA Mechanical Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>Loudoun County, VA <a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/DocumentCenter/View/97967\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mechanical permits</a> are needed for any HVAC extensions or additions, and the cost depends on the equipment listed on the application.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Loudoun County, VA Gas Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>Loudoun County, VA <a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/DocumentCenter/View/97966\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gas permits</a> are needed for installing, moving or replacing all gas appliances, and the price depends on the type of equipment listed in the gas permit application.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Home Occupation Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>Most residential remodeling projects will require a <a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/DocumentCenter/View/117879\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">home occupation</a> permit if the homeowner or any other residents will be living in the home during remodeling.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Sign Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>You must submit, with your <a href=\"https://www.loudoun.gov/DocumentCenter/View/107540\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">sign permit</a> application, 3 copies of the sign drawings (8.5&rdquo; X 14&rdquo; maximum) that have the sign&rsquo;s dimensions, elevation view (from the building), and the actual text. An electric permit application must be sent if the sign is electric, along with 1 copy of the hookup drawings.</p>\r\n<p>Sign fees are as follows:</p>\r\n<p>Commercial &ndash; $235.00 for each sign</p>\r\n<p>Temporary or Residential &ndash; $10.00 for each sign</p>\r\n<p>Electrical Permit &ndash; $125.00 for each sign (where applicable)</p>',2,'',112,'2017-06-18 15:43:04'),(129,'What is Luxury Vinyl Tile (LVT) Flooring?','Learn all you need to know about Luxury Vinyl Tile, its benefits, and why it would be a great match for you!','LVT Flooring, basement remodeling, basement renovation, flooring, tile, laminated flooring, hardwood flooring, luxury vinyl tile, basement blog','what-is-luxury-vinyl-tile-lvt-flooring','What is Luxury Vinyl Tile (LVT) Flooring?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/129/3de81e2b184827bcc0d0e2dc0b827c9d','','<p><strong>What is Luxury Vinyl Tile (LVT) Flooring?</strong></p>\n<p>With its ability to realistically simulate many different textures, luxury vinyl tile (LVT) flooring is one of the most popular options for remodeling basement floors. Recent advances in 3D technology means that LVT flooring is now aesthetically identical to wood, ceramic, and other tones, giving you the same look and feel at a fraction of the price. &nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>What are the Benefits of LVT Flooring?</strong></p>\n<p>Aside from saving money, LVT flooring will also:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Save Time &ndash; Professionals can easily install LVT flooring using pre-fitted pieces that can be glued, taped, or clicked into place.</li>\n<li>Stay Current &ndash; As styles and trends change, you will be able to easily switch your floor to a different design on a whim.</li>\n<li>Stay Strong &ndash; LVT is much more scuff and scratch-resistant than most types of ceramic and wood (including laminated wood), giving you the same great appearance without the upkeep.</li>\n<li>Stay Clean &ndash; LVT flooring is naturally stain-resistant and does not need to be waxed or polished.</li>\n<li>Stay Comfortable &ndash; Even though your LVT flooring will look like it&rsquo;s made of stone, wood, or any other material, it will have much more bounce and generally feels better to walk across.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Questions About LVT Flooring?</strong></p>\n<p>If you have any questions about LVT flooring, our consultation experts want to speak with you! <a href=\"../../../../about-us/contact-us/\">Contact us</a> today to learn more about the benefits of installing LVT flooring in your basement area.</p>',1,'',113,'2017-06-17 15:43:16'),(130,'Overhead Lighting Guide (Basement Lighting Ideas)','Find out the most important  facts about different types of lighting you can pick for your basement, discover the advantages of each of those and find the right match for you!','overhead lighting, basement lighting ideas, basement remodeling, basement renovation, bulbs','overhead-lighting-guide-basement-lighting-ideas','Overhead Lighting Guide (Basement Lighting Ideas)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/130/fb498f77c5a6370f605078bec1654ea4','','<p><strong>Overhead Lighting Guide (Basement Lighting Ideas) </strong></p>\n<p>From the home office to the workout room, every area of your basement needs great overhead lighting. The basic idea is to evenly distribute the overhead lighting so that no area of the room looks brighter or darker, but there&rsquo;s a little more to it than that. Here are some different basement lighting ideas you can follow to get your downstairs looking just right. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Bulbs</strong></p>\n<p>Compact fluorescent lights (CFLs) and light emitting diodes (LEDs) are the two traditional choices. They are bright and use about one-quarter of the energy that incandescent bulbs. They also give off less heat, which will keep your wine at the right temperature, and will also keep you cooler during gym workouts.</p>\n<p><strong>Specs</strong></p>\n<p>Wattage is becoming less important as incandescent bulbs continue to be phased out. No matter which type of lightbulb you choose, you should focus on lumens, which is the measurement of a bulb&rsquo;s brightness, rather than wattage. A 32-watt fluorescent bulb is about 28000 lumens, while a 25-watt CFL is 1,600 lumens, and a 15-watt LED is 1,100 lumens. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You should also pay attention to the estimated yearly cost of your overhead lighting. Most basement lighting ideas will look just fine using a lower-wattage bulb. This is especially important if children leave the lights on in their playroom all night long &nbsp;An LED bulb typically lasts longer than CFLs.</p>\n<p><strong>Basement Lighting Ideas and CFLs</strong></p>\n<p>CFLs are not as good as LEDs when it comes to direct lighting. So for basement lighting ideas that need to cast direct light on countertops or artwork, CFLs might not be the right choice. This also eliminates them from most home theater basement lighting ideas.</p>',1,'',114,'2017-06-11 15:43:26'),(131,'Building Permits for St. Mary’s County, MD','If you are remodeling a basement in St, Mary\'s County, here you can find the useful information about how to apply for a permit and what to do to get one! Check out here!','basement remodeling, basement renovation, building permit, building fees, general contractor, building permit for ST. Mary\'s County, MD','building-permits-for-st.-marys-county-md','Building Permits for St. Mary’s County, MD','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/131/7fcb725d9f2e95b0943cc299c078ef8b','','<div class=\"html\">\r\n<p>If you are remodeling a basement in <strong>St. Mary&rsquo;s County, MD, building permits</strong> can be obtained in one of two ways &ndash; the traditional &ldquo;Drop Off&rdquo; process or the more streamlined &ldquo;on demand&rdquo; process. The on demand process can only be used if you don&rsquo;t plan to add new bedrooms in your basement.</p>\r\n<h2>St. Mary&rsquo;s County, MD On Demand Process</h2>\r\n<h1>Permits</h1>\r\n<p>The Permit Services Division&rsquo;s principal function is to process building and other permits including environmental (Critical Area and Floodplain), residential entrances, home occupations, family daycare, change of business occupants, and sign permits in accordance with the applicable regulations, such as the Building Code, Zoning Ordinance and Subdivision Regulations. The Permits staff must also coordinate the routing of permit information to other required agencies for their review and approval.</p>\r\n<h2>PERMIT COUNTER HOURS</h2>\r\n<p>All divisions are available to assist you from 8 am - 5 pm. Please note, however, permit applications are only accepted during the following hours:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Monday &amp; Thursday 8:30 AM - 2:00 PM</li>\r\n<li>Tuesday, Wednesday &amp; Friday 8:30 AM - 4:30 PM</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>APPLICATION FORMS</h2>\r\n<p>St. Mary&rsquo;s County, MD building permits have an application fee of $15:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Fill out a general <a href=\"http://www.stmarysmd.com/docs/Form5.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">permit application</a> and answer the questions as best you can.</li>\r\n<li>Submit written permission from the property owner and have them sign it.</li>\r\n<li>Show plans (drawn to scale) showing the boundaries, any &ldquo;existing and proposed structures&rdquo;, the location of the driveway, the location of the septic system (or well), easements, land disturbance estimations in square footage, and any surrounding woods.</li>\r\n<li>View the complete list of<a href=\"https://www.stmarysmd.com/it/formsanddocuments/\"> application forms</a>.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>St. Mary&rsquo;s County, MD Drop Off Process</h2>\r\n<p>St. Mary&rsquo;s County, MD building permits have an application fee of $15:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Fill out a general <a href=\"http://www.stmarysmd.com/docs/Form5.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">permit application</a> and answer the questions as best you can.</li>\r\n<li>Include contact information for whoever is in charge of the septic system requirements.</li>\r\n<li>Submit a recorded deed of the property.</li>\r\n<li>Submit written permission from the property owner and have them sign it.</li>\r\n<li>Show plans with boundaries, structures, driveway location, septic tank location, and other requirements as detailed in the previous section.</li>\r\n<li>Floorplans of each floor of the home, with clearly labeled rooms (does not have to be to scale).</li>\r\n<li>The Maryland Builder&rsquo;s Registration Number, or else the Home Improvement License Number.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>PERMIT STATUS</h2>\r\n<p>Have your application number? View your <a href=\"https://trakit-edge.stmarysmd.com/eTRAKiT/\">permit status online</a>. The status of the permit application will show \"Pending\" beside a required Agency so long as that Agency has not finished reviewing the application. If the status is listed as \"On Hold\", simply click on the words \"On Hold\" and specific comments will show why. When the status is listed as \"Approved\" please contact the Permit Office to check on the final details of the application before picking up the permit. This will allow our staff to verify that everything is in order and what total fees are due.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Check out the <a href=\"http://www.stmarysmd.com/docs/CAG2.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">full list</a> of potential review agencies and additional fees.</p>\r\n</div>',2,'',115,'2017-06-10 15:43:34'),(132,'5 Ways to Prevent a Wet Basement','A wet basement can serious cause mold and foundation problems, but here are 5 easy steps you can take to keep your basement nice and dry all year long.','wet basement, waterproof basement, basement remodeling, basement renovation','5-ways-to-prevent-a-wet-basement','5 Ways to Prevent a Wet Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/132/e06904bee107df9dadff660ab3ea193d','A wet basement can serious cause mold and foundation problems, but here are 5 easy steps you can take to keep your basement nice and dry all year long.','<p><strong>5 Ways to Prevent a Wet Basement </strong></p>\n<p>A wet basement can serious cause mold and foundation problems, but here are 5 easy steps you can take to keep your basement nice and dry all year long. &nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Clean Your Gutters &ndash; You might not expect anything that&rsquo;s on your roof to impact your basement, but cleaning your gutters and downspouts will keep water flowing away from your home&rsquo;s foundation.</li>\n<li>Epoxy &ndash; Minor foundation cracks can be sealed with epoxy, so be sure to inspect your exterior foundation along with the walls and floors of your basement.</li>\n<li>Dehumidifier &ndash; Summer&rsquo;s here, and humid weather is on the rise. Turning on a basement dehumidifier during extreme weather can help keep your basement&rsquo;s moisture levels under control.</li>\n<li>Sewer Maintenance &ndash; Keep your septic tank cleaned out or your sewer system routinely inspected so that your basement doesn&rsquo;t flood during heavy periods of rain.</li>\n<li>Sump Pump &ndash; If your home is surrounded by a higher water table, then a sump pump will pump water out of a sump pit and away from the property.</li>\n</ol>',3,'',116,'2017-06-04 15:44:10'),(133,'How to Choose the Right Colors for Your Basement','From a design standpoint, the color of your basement is one of the most important fashion decisions that you can make. Learn how to pick the best color for you!','basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, color, design, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','how-to-choose-the-right-colors-for-your-basement','How to Choose the Right Colors for Your Basement','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/133/d3af9595e6c571c7005e4c125f9aed8a','From a design standpoint, the color of your basement is one of the most important fashion decisions that you can make. It sets the tone of your downstairs area and it’s one of the first things that your guests will notice when they enter.','<p><strong>How to Choose the Right Colors for Your Basement</strong></p>\n<p>From a design standpoint, the color of your basement is one of the most important fashion decisions that you can make. It sets the tone of your downstairs area and it&rsquo;s one of the first things that your guests will notice when they enter. The right paintjob can entice guests to spend the night or send them running within the first hour, but how are you supposed to know which colors are best?</p>\n<p><strong>Natural Light</strong></p>\n<p>Natural lighting is the determining factor when choosing a paint color. If your basement receives a lot of natural light, then you can use light or dark colors. If your basement is dark to begin with, however, then using darker colors will make it look drab and depressing.</p>\n<p><strong>Stone and Cinderblock Walls</strong></p>\n<p>Any stone or cinderblock walls need to be considered when choosing a color scheme. These types of walls can cause an unsightly gray shadow to creep over any adjacent walls, so white walls must be avoided. Whenever cinderblocks or stone walls are involved, you are going to have to use saturated colors to hide the shadows.</p>\n<p><strong>Open Basements</strong></p>\n<p>Some basements lack dividing walls, and here is where colors can be creatively used to define different rooms and break up spaces. Not everything has to match, so don&rsquo;t be afraid to let the colors gently clash wherever necessary. All that really matters is that the areas are clearly defined.</p>',4,'',117,'2017-06-03 15:44:22'),(134,'Wicomico County, MD Building Permits and More','If you are remodeling a basement in Wicomico County, MD learn how to obtain a building permit right here!','Wicomico MD building permits, building fees, general contractor, basement remodeling, basement renovation, basement finishing','wicomico-county-md-building-permits-and-more','Wicomico County, MD Building Permits and More','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/134/47761bf3ab91e7c9f22e864aa9a625d8','If you are remodeling a basement in Wicomico County, MD building permits can be obtained by emailing this completed building permit form to permits@wicomicocounty.org or by mailing it to...','<p><strong>Wicomico County, MD Building Permits and More</strong></p>\r\n<p>If you are remodeling a basement in Wicomico County, MD building permits can be obtained by emailing this completed <a href=\"http://www.wicomicocounty.org/DocumentCenter/View/4379\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit form</a> to <a>permits@wicomicocounty.org</a> or by mailing it to:</p>\r\n<h2 class=\"subhead1\">Residential Building Permit</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.wicomicocounty.org/DocumentCenter/View/3883\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"Residential Building Permit Requirements Opens in new window\">Residential Building Permit Requirements</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.wicomicocounty.org/DocumentCenter/View/3888\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"Residential Building FAQs Opens in new window\">Residential Building FAQs</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.wicomicocounty.org/DocumentCenter/View/3879\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"Permit Fee Calculation Opens in new window\">Permit Fee Calculation</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"http://www.wicomicocounty.org/DocumentCenter/View/3887/Residential-Application-Form-Field-12-06-19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"Residential Permit Application Opens in new window\">Residential Permit Application</a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"mailto:permits@wicomicocounty.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"Submit Application by Email Opens in new window\">Submit Application by Email</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>125 N. Division Street<br />Room 201 Government Office Building<br />Salisbury, Maryland 21801</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;You&rsquo;ll need to include 2 site plans that have the following information:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The foundation plans</li>\r\n<li>All interior details including doors, windows and fixture locations</li>\r\n<li>Framing plans</li>\r\n<li>Cross sections</li>\r\n<li>Front, side and rear elevations</li>\r\n<li>Insulation R-values along with the size of the windows with U-factors and the solar heat gain coefficient (SGC)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The cost of the building permit can vary. In general, the estimated construction costs can be as low as $70 per square foot (up to 1,500 square feet) and as high as $100 per square foot (for 4,001 square feet and over). Check out the full list of estimations <a href=\"http://www.wicomicocounty.org/DocumentCenter/View/3879\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li><strong>Wicomico County, MD Electrical Permits</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>An <a href=\"http://www.wicomicocounty.org/DocumentCenter/View/2268\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">electrical permit</a> is required for any electrical work, no matter how large or small. These permits cost $25.00 and can be mailed or emailed to the same address that has handles building permits (this does not include inspection fees). They expire after one year.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Wicomico County, MD HVAC Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>In Wicomico County, an HVAC permit is not required to install HVAC systems. However, the contractor still must have the appropriate HVAC license.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Wicomico County, MD Health and Plumbing Permits</strong></p>\r\n<p>In most cases, a building permit as well as a plumbing permit cannot be obtained without first getting a health permit from the Health Department. If you are working on a well, then this department will also write a letter of approval (as required to obtain a Certificate of Occupancy and Use). Contact the Health Department at 410-546-4446 for all of the required steps to obtain a plumbing permit.</p>',2,'',118,'2017-05-28 15:44:57'),(135,'How to Choose the Right Basement Windows','There are many different types of basement windows to choose from, but it really depends on if you have a “daylight basement” or not.','basement windows, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','how-to-choose-the-right-basement-windows','How to Choose the Right Basement Windows','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/135/b212ed2047722e08b99c71b2ea0c5321','There are many different types of basement windows to choose from, but it really depends on if you have a “daylight basement” or not. A daylight basement is when...','<p><strong>How to Choose the Right Basement Windows</strong></p>\n<p>There are many different types of basement windows to choose from, but it really depends on if you have a &ldquo;daylight basement&rdquo; or not. A daylight basement is when your home rests on a slope and the front of the basement has one or more full-sized windows that are aboveground. If all of your basement is underground, then the basement windows are going to be wider than they are tall.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hopper Windows &ndash; A classic window that has a single piece of glass that opens by tilting inward or outward (unlike awning windows, which open from the bottom). These windows are ordinarily much wider than they are tall.</li>\n<li>Casement Windows &ndash; Since these windows are tall than they are wide, they are typically found in bathrooms or in daylight basements. They open like hopper windows.</li>\n<li>Slider Windows &ndash; These windows are popular for the section of the basement that faces the street. As the name implies, they slide open and are great for daylight basements.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Basement Window Materials</strong></p>\n<p>Try to avoid using wood around your basement windows because the window is low to the ground and can attract moisture, which in turn can promote shrinkage or rot. Vinyl-framed windows can be more easily cleaned, will not attract mold, and since they have become an industry standard for basements, they are easily replaceable. Aluminum is the second most popular choice for framing basement windows.</p>',4,'',119,'2017-05-27 15:45:12'),(136,'Queen Anne’s County Basement Remodeling Permits and Fees','This blog will show you everything you need to know to get all of the necessary Queen Anne’s County permits to complete your next basement remodeling project!','Queen Anne\'s County, Queen Anne\'s County permits, building permit, building fees, basement remodeling, basement finishing, general contractor, basement renovation','queen-annes-county-basement-remodeling-permits-and-fees','Queen Anne’s County Basement Remodeling Permits and Fees','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/136/fa1afb6f54289ec92c00468498df3fb1','This blog will show you everything you need to know to get all of the necessary Queen Anne’s County permits to complete your next basement remodeling project.','<p><strong>Queen Anne&rsquo;s County Basement Remodeling Permits and Fees</strong></p>\n<p>This blog will show you everything you need to know to get all of the necessary Queen Anne&rsquo;s County permits to complete your next basement remodeling project.</p>\n<p><strong>Queen Anne&rsquo;s County Building Permits</strong></p>\n<p>A <a href=\"http://www.qac.org/DocumentCenter/Home/View/313\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit</a> costs at least $90.00 minimum and takes about one or two weeks for approval. To get a Queen Anne&rsquo;s County building permit, you must first submit a site plan to the Zoning Office that includes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The property&rsquo;s address (including the 911 emergency address)and the owner&rsquo;s full name and contact information.</li>\n<li>The contractor&rsquo;s name and contact information, including license number. Any &ldquo;renovation, alternations, repairs or additions&rdquo; requires the contractor also have a Maryland Home Improvement license.</li>\n<li>All electrical, HVAC and plumbing contractor&rsquo;s names license numbers for Queen Anne&rsquo;s County.</li>\n<li>The county tax map and tax identification number (refer to your tax bill for this information).</li>\n<li>All dimensions, including the occupied and unoccupied areas, must be clearly outlined.</li>\n<li>The estimated value of the completed construction.</li>\n<li>The square footage of the property.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>When applying for a building permit, you must also include 4 plot plans that show the location of all of the roads and septic systems, along with the property lines and dimensions. You must also have 2 sets of building plans (blueprints) that have a floor plan showing the size of all doors and windows, the footer and foundational plans, cross sections and elevations.</p>\n<p>Orio to getting a building permit in Queen Anne&rsquo;s County, you must also have a sanitation permit from the Environmental Health Department (758-2281), and a plumbing and mechanical permits from the Plumbing Office at the Environmental Health Department (758-2281).</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>There is also a water connection fee of $25 and a sewer connection fee of $50 whenever applicable. For more information, contact the Sanitary Distract at 643-3535.</p>\n<p><strong>Plumbing Permits in Queen Anne&rsquo;s County</strong></p>\n<p>Queen Anne&rsquo;s County <a href=\"http://www.qac.org/DocumentCenter/Home/View/6543\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">plumbing permits</a> cost $10.00 (and also need an extra $50.00 for a gas permit, an extra $50.00 for public sewer, and an extra $50.00 for water or sewer alterations when applicable). It costs $50.00 for the first 5 fixtures or appliances, and $5.00 for each additional fixture or appliance after that.</p>\n<p><strong>Electrical Permits in Queen Anne&rsquo;s County</strong></p>\n<p>We will be explaining <a href=\"http://www.qac.org/DocumentCenter/Home/View/7119\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">residential permits</a>, though <a href=\"http://www.qac.org/DocumentCenter/Home/View/7120\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">commercial permits</a> are available as well. Both have a minimum fee of $50.00. HVAC connection fees range from $15.00 to $45.00, minor alterations and additions cost $60.00 for the first 25 outlets, and $30.00 for every 15 outlets past that amount. Construction service fees range from $65.00 (under 400 amps) to $90 (for over 400 amps), with possible service reconnection or upgrading fees of $45.00.</p>\n<p><strong>Mechanical Permits in Queen Anne&rsquo;s County</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"http://www.qac.org/DocumentCenter/Home/View/6542\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mechanical permits</a> have a base fee of $10.00. Each heating and cooling system is $50.00 for residential projects, and $25.00 for each additional unit. If you have a heating system only or an air conditioning system, it still costs the same amount ($50.00)</p>\n<p><strong>Other Fees For Queen Anne&rsquo;s County Basement Remodeling</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>New constructions and additions cost $12.00 per square foot, but renovations, alterations and repairs cost $7.00 per $1,000.00 of the overall estimated costs.</li>\n<li>Re-inspection fees typically cost $50.00 per visit.</li>\n<li>Most basement remodeling projects will have to pay a $50.00 fee to get a temporary certificate of occupancy</li>\n</ul>',2,'',120,'2017-05-21 15:45:28'),(137,'Warning Signs of Foundation Problems to Watch For','Aside from general home upkeep, you should keep an eye on your foundation for any potential problems. But what warning signs should you look for?','signs of foundation problems, warning signs, foundation problems, basement remodeling, basement finishing, foundation repair, remodel a basement, waterproof basement, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','warning-signs-of-foundation-problems-to-watch-for','Warning Signs of Foundation Problems to Watch For','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/137/07d393357fb23af63dceea38d9e42e51','Most homeowners keep good care of their home\'s exterior, but when did you last check your foundation for any warning signs?','<p>You keep the lawn green and the outside of your home nicely painted, but when was the last time you checked around your property for <strong>signs of foundation problems</strong>? Your foundation is the very structure on which your house was built upon, so you should regularly be on the lookout for any of these signs of foundation problems. Spotting them early on could indicate something serious that needs to be addressed right away.</p>\n<h2>Indoor Signs of Foundation Problems</h2>\n<p>Some of these warnings are pretty easy to overlook, so pay special attention to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Doors that jam instead of latching properly.</li>\n<li>Windows no longer open and close properly.</li>\n<li>Cracks in the walls, especially if they are over doors, windows, or where the floor intersects with the ceilings.</li>\n<li>Cracked tiles over concrete.</li>\n<li>Puddles in the basement.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Don&rsquo;t forget to check the posts and concrete supports under your basement if you have a crawlspace (or hire someone to do this for you).</p>\n<h2>Outdoor Signs of Foundation Problems</h2>\n<p>Walk outside to each corner of your house and visually check to see if the walls are even. Use a level to double check and make sure. If you see any bulges or curves in the foundation or on a concrete wall, then that is a strong sign that the soil is putting pressure on the walls by either expanding or contracting (due to moisture or heat).</p>\n<p>If you see any flaking or chipping in the concrete of your foundation, poke it with a screwdriver. If the screwdriver is able to take a chunk out of the concrete, then this is a sign that the concrete is wearing down and you need an inspection.</p>\n<h2>Do You Have Any of These Signs?</h2>\n<p>If so, contact Basement Masters now before it&rsquo;s too late. We have the knowledge and expertise to tell you how serious the situation is and what needs to be done next (if anything) to keep your home safe.</p>',4,'',121,'2017-05-20 15:45:48'),(138,'Dorchester County, MD Basement Remodeling Permits, Fees and Licenses','Find out here about Dorchester County, MD Building Permit Applications, Licensing and much more!','Dorchester County, MD, basement remodeling, basement renovation, building permits, building fees, building license, general contractor','dorchester-county-md-basement-remodeling-permits-fees-and-licenses','Dorchester County, MD Basement Remodeling Permits, Fees and Licenses','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/138/81cdb3d7ff78129c3d82beeb9f47c7e1','Dorchester County, MD Building Permit Applications and More','<p><strong>Dorchester County, MD Basement Remodeling Permits, Fees and Licenses </strong></p>\n<p>Building permit <a href=\"http://docogonet.com/index.php?page=site_plan_requirements\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">applications</a> in Dorchester County, MD require a site plan that outlines the following information:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2 sets of building plans drawn to scale with clearly labeled dimensions</li>\n<li>Each room of the basement must be outlined</li>\n<li>The number of families the household contains (if residential)</li>\n<li>Any nearby streams, wetlands, or bodies of water</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Basement remodeling projects for residential and commercial buildings cost $0.13 per square foot (<a href=\"http://docogonet.com/uploads/File/Planning%20and%20Zoning/FY15%20Fee%20Schedule%20-%20approved.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOURCE</a>).</p>\n<p><strong>Electrician&rsquo;s License for Dorchester County, MD</strong></p>\n<p>An electrician&rsquo;s license ranges anywhere from $80.00 (limited license) to $150.00 (master electrician). To apply for an electrician&rsquo;s license in Dorchester County, MD, fill out this <a href=\"http://docogonet.com/uploads/File/Planning%20and%20Zoning/Forms/License%20of%20Reciprocity%20Application.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">form</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Plumber&rsquo;s License for Dorchester County, MD</strong></p>\n<p>A plumber&rsquo;s license costs $75.00. To apply for an plumber&rsquo;s license in Dorchester County, MD, fill out this <a href=\"http://docogonet.com/uploads/File/Planning%20and%20Zoning/Forms/Plumbing%20License%20Application%202016%20-17.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">form</a>.</p>',2,'',122,'2017-05-14 15:46:06'),(139,'We Remodel Luxury Basements in Maryland','Basement Masters is a local business that has been designing hundreds of luxury basements in Maryland ever since 2006.','luxury basements in Maryland, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','we-remodel-luxury-basements-in-maryland','We Remodel Luxury Basements in Maryland','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/139/ea79694d67662c3aec9cb70240c1964c','Basement Masters is a local business that has been designing hundreds of luxury basements in Maryland ever since 2006.','<p><strong>We Remodel Luxury Basements in Maryland</strong></p>\n<p>Basement Masters is a local business that has been designing hundreds of luxury basements in Maryland ever since 2006. From construction to design, we specialize only in creating the finest luxury basements in Maryland to date and seeing them through to completion. In fact, your downstairs is the only area of the property that we will work on.</p>\n<p>Our expert basement remodeling team can easily translate your fanciest basement ideas into actual working schematics and 3D models. You&rsquo;ll have total creative control as we transform your basement into how you&rsquo;ve always envisioned it, right down to the final interior touches like paintjobs and flooring (at no extra charge).</p>\n<p>Commercial or residential, no project is too large for our professional team. We can deploy multiple architects and engineers to a site as needed, and securing the appropriate permits according to your county&rsquo;s law is a both a necessity and our specialty. In addition, every project has a 1-year labor warranty, with additional basement protection plans available. We also are insured at a minimum of $1 million for every project we work on.</p>\n<p>Basement Masters understands that reputation means everything. Aside from hundreds of positive reviews online, we have a long list of satisfied clients and partners who will gladly share their experiences with you. For a full list of references, please email us at <a>contacts@basementmasters.com</a>.</p>',5,'',123,'2017-05-13 15:46:36'),(140,'Garret County, Maryland Permits and Fees','Let’s look at the rest of the permits you’ll need to finish your next Garret County, MD basement remodeling project.','Gatter County, Maryland, MD, Permits, building permits, building fees, basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor, basement finishing','garret-county-maryland-permits-and-fees','Garret County, Maryland Permits and Fees','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/140/e54434677fc83d08c2f9ca15d3a5dad7','Let’s look at the rest of the permits you’ll need to finish your next Garret County, MD basement remodeling project.','<p>Our last blog post focused on <strong>Garret County, MD building permits</strong>. Now let&rsquo;s look at the rest of the permits you&rsquo;ll need to finish your next Garret County, MD basement remodeling project. &nbsp;</p>\n<h2>How Much Does a Plumbing Permit Cost in Garret County, MD?</h2>\n<p>Plumbing permits cost $10 in Garret County, MD. If you are going to do anything other than fix a leak or replace a fixture in Garret County, MD, then you are going to need a plumbing permit. When you are filling out Garret County, Maryland <a href=\"https://www.garrettcounty.org/resources/permits-inspections/pdf/Plumbing%20%26%20Electric/Plumbing%20Permit%20blank%20form.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">plumbing permit application</a>, you will need to include basic information like the type of structure and the number of baths, and it must be signed off by the master plumber, or the homeowner themselves.</p>\n<h2>How Much Does an Electrical Permit Cost in Garret County, MD?</h2>\n<p>Electrical permits cost $10 in Garret County, MD. If you are performing anything beyond &ldquo;minor repair work&rdquo;, chances are you need to <a href=\"https://www.garrettcounty.org/resources/permits-inspections/pdf/Plumbing%20%26%20Electric/Electrical%20Permit%20blank%20form.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">apply for a permit</a>. The application form will ask for the name of the electric company, and the name of the master electrician along with their license number. The license must be signed by either the master electrician or the homeowner. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',2,'',124,'2017-05-07 15:47:22'),(141,'Garret County, MD Building Permits for Basement Remodeling','Looking to pick up a building permit in Garret County, MD for a basement remodeling project? Here\'s what you need to know.','Garret County, MD, Garret County, Maryland, Garret County building permits, basement permits, building permits, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement remodeling permits, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement contractor','garret-county-md-building-permits-for-basement-remodeling','Garret County, MD Building Permits for Basement Remodeling','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/141/ebc2fede28d0900ebdf2e0f21bd9072b','Everything you need to know to get a building permit in Garret County, MD','<p>To apply for a <strong>Garrett County, MD building permit</strong>, you must apply in-person at the Permits and Inspections Services office between Monday and Friday, 8:30a.m. to 4:30p.m.</p>\n<p>You\'ll need to give them two copies of floor plans or drawings that clearly outlines the dimensions and square footage of the home, as well as what each room is for, and the locations and sizes of all windows and doors (all to scale &ldquo;whenever possible&rdquo; according to their website, though dimensions must be exact). You must also show what the house is made of, how many baths and fireplaces are in it, and the type of heating and air conditioning it has. You must include the names of all contractors, electricians and plumbers along with their license numbers, and if the house has had more than one owner in the last year, then their names and specific dates of transfer must be included.</p>\n<p>After the building permit has been granted, construction must begin within one year or else the permit is nullified. Permits are also void if work ceases for six months.</p>\n<h2>How Much do Garret County, MD Building Permits Cost?</h2>\n<p>The cost of building permits for a basement in Garret County, Maryland depends on the square footage of the new addition. Additions cost $0.10 per square foot with a $100 minimum, plus a $15 use and occupancy fee.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;The <a href=\"https://www.garrettcounty.org/resources/permits-inspections/pdf/Building/2015-BuildingCode.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Garret County Building Code</a> adheres to the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2015 International Building Code</li>\n<li>2015 International Residential Code</li>\n<li>2015 Energy Conservation Code</li>\n</ul>',2,'',125,'2017-05-06 15:47:33'),(142,'5 Basement Wet Bar Design Trends for 2017','Looking for the best basement wet bar design trends of 2017? Here are 5 things that we’ve noticed as the basement bar scene continues to evolve.','wet bar design, basement remodeling, basement renovation, interior design, home bar, basement bar, basement finishing, basement design trends, basement wet bar designs, 2017 wet bar design trends, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','5-basement-wet-bar-design-trends-for-2017','5 Basement Wet Bar Design Trends for 2017','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/142/32c4c6a8c92f9c3e29123ac86bee3501','What new wet bar design trends has 2017 brought us so far?','<p>2017 is bringing about a lot of new and unique basement designs, ideas, and trends. Here are 5 of the most interesting<strong> basement wet bar design trends</strong> we\'ve seen so far this year.</p>\n<h2>1. Wine Fridges</h2>\n<p>The days of single cabinet wine storage are gone. Modern wet bar design now calls for wine refrigerators to keep the chilled drinks flowing. Smaller wine fridge models seem to be more popular. &nbsp;</p>\n<h2>2. Go All Out</h2>\n<p>Modest &ldquo;den&rdquo; wet bar design ideas are outdated as high-end granite countertops and expensive wooden floors take the lead. The second most popular look is minimalist chic that has an emphasis on base cabinets and neutral color schemes</p>\n<h2>3.&nbsp;Say it With Mosaics</h2>\n<p>Your wet bar design could include a mosaic accent wall for a bold and artistic look that simply screams &ldquo;stand here and chat&rdquo;. Tiled flooring is also now an excellent method to subtly delineate the wet bar space from the rest of the room.</p>\n<h2>4.&nbsp;Recreational Focus</h2>\n<p>Installing a wall-mounted HDTV and adding a surround sound system is one of the most practical trends for 2017. If real bars can do it, why can&rsquo;t you? It&rsquo;s perfect for playing soft music or watching the big game.</p>\n<h2>5. A Family Space</h2>\n<p>A wet bar can easily become a family-friendly area when not entertaining guests. Many homeowners have lowered countertops and a microwave for popcorn. Why not keep a few board games in the cabinet for rainy day?</p>\n<h2>Need More Basements Wet Bar Design Ideas?</h2>\n<p>Check out our wet bar <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/spaces/wet-bars/\">ideas section</a> for all of the latest <strong>wet bar design trends</strong>! &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',1,'',126,'2017-04-30 15:47:44'),(143,'A Guide to Cecil County Permits for Maryland Basement Remodeling','Searching for what permits you\'ll need for your next Cecil County, Maryland basement remodeling project? Here\'s everything you need.','Cecil County permits, Cecil County building permit, Cecil County MD, Cecil County Maryland, building permit, basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor, basement finishing, basement building permits, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','a-guide-to-cecil-county-permits-for-maryland-basement-remodeling','A Guide to Cecil County Permits for Maryland Basement Remodeling','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/143/0433e399e4f635531218c11890ced652','Here\'s all the relevant information you need concerning basement remodeling permits in Cecil County, Maryland.','<p>Need Cecil County permits for your next Maryland basement remodeling project? Let&rsquo;s go over them all.</p>\n<p>All applications for <strong>Cecil County building permits </strong>must be submitted in person by the contractor or a representative of the property owners, and must contain the following information:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Two building plan copies (three copies if it&rsquo;s for Charlestown or Port Deposit)</li>\n<li>Three copies of the site plan, which has the project&rsquo;s location and any other structures (such as the well or septic system)</li>\n<li>A completed Residential Energy Efficiency Form (depending on project type)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Prior to applying for a building permit, you will also need to obtain special permission if your project falls within the town limits of:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"http://www.ceciltonmd.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cecilton</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://www.chesapeakecity-md.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Chesapeake City</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://charlestownmd.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Charlestown</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://northeastmd.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">North East</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://www.perryvillemd.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Perryville</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://portdeposit.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Port Deposit</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Here is the Cecil County building permit <a href=\"http://www.ccgov.org/home/showdocument?id=21284\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">application form</a> for commercial projects, and here is the Cecil County building permit <a href=\"http://www.ccgov.org/home/showdocument?id=19421\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">application form</a> for residential projects. Both of them cost $30.00 to apply for, and additional feels may apply when paying with a credit card, so use cash, check, or a money order!</p>\n<h2>Cecil County Permits (HVAC)</h2>\n<p>An HVAC permit application can be found <a href=\"http://www.ccgov.org/home/showdocument?id=708\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>. It&rsquo;s important to note that if you are going to be working with gas pipes, you&rsquo;ll need a plumbing permit, not an HVAC one. For more information as to what does and does not need an HVAC permit in Cecil County, consult this brief <a href=\"http://www.ccgov.org/home/showdocument?id=21036\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">city guide</a>.</p>\n<h2>Cecil County Permits (Electrical)</h2>\n<p>You must be a Master or Limited electrician to perform work in Cecil County, and you must also be registered (click <a href=\"http://www.ccgov.org/home/showdocument?id=714\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a> to apply for registration). You can apply for an electrical permit <a href=\"http://www.ccgov.org/home/showdocument?id=700\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>. If the system is 50 volts or less, no permit is required.</p>\n<h2>Cecil County Permits (Plumbing)</h2>\n<p>Only registered Master plumbers can do authorized work in Cecil County. Click <a href=\"http://www.ccgov.org/home/showdocument?id=21034\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a> to apply for a county license. Prior to applying, you must also show your license and proof of liability insurance to the Maryland State Board of Plumbing. Otherwise, click <a href=\"http://www.ccgov.org/home/showdocument?id=718\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a> to apply for a plumbing permit in Cecil County, MD.</p>\n<h2>Passing Cecil County, MD Basement Inspections</h2>\n<p>For a general timeline of building, plumbing, HVAC and electrical inspections, refer to this helpful Cecil County <a href=\"http://www.ccgov.org/government/land-use-development-services/permits-and-inspections-division/required-inspections\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">inspection guide</a>.</p>',2,'',127,'2017-04-29 15:47:44'),(144,'How Much Are Basement Permits in Harford County, Maryland','Wondering how much you\'ll have to spend on fees for basement permits in Harford County, MD? Here’s everything you need to know.','Harford County, Maryland, MD, Building permit, basement permit, building fee, basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement remodeling blog, basement remodeling permits','how-much-are-basement-permits-in-harford-county-maryland','How Much Are Basement Permits in Harford County, Maryland','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/144/fdfbb2a2007d4e317be1ba986dd94adc','A complete guide to permit fees so you\'re prepared for your next basement project in Harford County, Maryland!','<p>Here&rsquo;s everything you need to know to estimate <strong>basement permit fees</strong> for your next construction, remodeling, or finishing project in <strong>Harford County, Maryland</strong>!</p>\n<h2>How Much do Building Permits Cost in Harford County, Maryland?</h2>\n<p>Building permits fees can vary in Harford County, Maryland depending on the structure.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Harford County, MD building permit fees range from $65-$235, depending on the type of building (this includes the $10 Certificate of Occupancy fee)</li>\n<li>There is also a fee of 5-12 cents per square foot.</li>\n<li>Refer to this easy <a href=\"http://www.harfordcountymd.gov/DocumentCenter/View/319\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">chart</a> to see how much building permits will cost for your project</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How Much do Other Permits Cost in Harford County, MD?</h2>\n<p>Harford County, MD Plumbing Permits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>$30 for the first fixture (new installation), $5 for subsequent ones</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Harford County, MD Mechanical Permits</p>\n<ul>\n<li>$70 for each heating and air conditioning system</li>\n<li>$55 if heating only</li>\n<li>$55 if air conditioning only</li>\n<li>$30 is this is a replacement system</li>\n</ul>\n<p>NOTE: Fees for commercial building installations are estimated based on the labor, equipment and work materials used. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>Harford County, MD Electrical Permits</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Can cost anywhere from $60 (under 600 amps) to $125 (800 to 1,000 amps)</li>\n<li>This flat rate applies to townhomes, condominium units, and apartment buildings</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Registration Fees in Harford County, Maryland</h2>\n<p>Electricians:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Anywhere from $5 (apprentice) to $45 (Master Electrician)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Plumbers:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Anywhere from $15 (journeyman) to $45 (Master Plumber)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Mechanical Workers:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Anywhere from $5 (apprentice) to $45 (Master)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How Much Are Permit Violations in Harford County, MD?</h2>\n<p>General Violations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Re-inspection fee of $50</li>\n<li>$100 fee for county investigations</li>\n<li>$250 for &ldquo;first occurrence&rdquo; violations, with $50 increase for subsequent offenses</li>\n<li>Administrative hearings may be required for multiple offenses</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Mechanical Violations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>$50 re-inspection fee</li>\n<li>$250 for &ldquo;first occurrence&rdquo;, with $50 increases for subsequent violations</li>\n<li>$60 per hour to review plans</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Additional Mechanical Fees:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>$25 for any changes to the permit</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Specific Plumbing Violations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>$30 if plumbing fixture is not listed on permit, $5 for each one after</li>\n<li>$60 per hour for additional plan reviews</li>\n</ul>\n<p>General Plumbing Violations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>$250 for &ldquo;first occurrence&rdquo;, with $50 increase each time</li>\n<li>Administrative hearing after third warning</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Electrical Violations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Re-inspection fee of $50</li>\n<li>$100 fee for county investigations</li>\n<li>$250 for &ldquo;first occurrence&rdquo; violations, with $50 increase for subsequent offenses</li>\n<li>Administrative hearings may be required for multiple offenses</li>\n</ul>',2,'',128,'2017-04-23 15:48:08'),(145,'Why Do Basements Flood?','Your basement can flood at practically any time, even during dry weather. But why exactly do basements flood?','Why do basements flood, basement flooding, basement flood, moisture, basement remodeling, basement renovation, waterproof basement, basement waterproofing, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','why-do-basements-flood','Why Do Basements Flood?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/145/f48e0c8fdd7d7408f88b1e4eedd44d02','Why exactly do basements flood? Is there a specific reason?','<div class=\"html\">\n<p><strong>Basement flooding</strong> can happen at any time &ndash; even if the weather is dry, and even if it&rsquo;s never happened before. So why do basements flood? &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Groundwater &ndash; Sometimes the groundwater level can become higher than the level of the basement foundation. Basement flooding can occur if there are any cracks in the walls or the floor. This problem is compounded if your land slopes towards the house, which keeps the groundwater from moving away.</li>\n<li>Sewers &ndash; Why do basements flood in warm weather? Sometimes a sewer system (storm and sanitary alike) can be above the basement floor level. Like groundwater, cracks in the foundation or the walls can cause basement flooding. If the sewer system itself is clogged, then this can cause basement flooding as well.</li>\n<li>Plumbing problems &ndash; If the weather is dry, then perhaps the water supply-line or hot water tank is the source of your basement flooding.</li>\n<li>Foundation Drainage &ndash; Your foundation&rsquo;s drainage system itself may be malfunctioning. The weeping tile may have deteriorated and cause water to come out of the sump pump.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>BasementRemodeling.com Solves Basement Flooding</h2>\n<p>We are the leaders in residential and commercial basement waterproofing for the Maryland, Virginia, and Washington D.C.. If you want a licensed expert to solve your basement flooding situation, then schedule an <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">appointment</a> with us today. Preventative maintenance is key, so even if you are not experiencing any basement flooding at the moment, contact BasementRemodeling.com! &nbsp;</p>\n</div>',3,'',129,'2017-04-23 15:48:21'),(146,'A Summary of Worcester County, Maryland Permits and Inspections','Obtaining permits and passing inspections in Worcester County, MD doesn\'t have to be difficult—you simply need to know what rules to follow.','Worcester County MD, Worcester County MD Permits, Worcester MD Inspections, building permit, basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor, basement finishing, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','a-summary-of-worcester-county-maryland-permits-and-inspections','A Summary of Worcester County, Maryland Permits and Inspections','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/146/2535e083811aa25837221fa035c2e8ad','What permits do you need for basement remodeling or finishing in Worcester County, MD? How complex are inspections? Here\'s what you need to know.','<p>Obtaining <strong>Worcester County, MD permits</strong> and passing inspections can be a painless process if you know what steps to take. Here is what you need to know to get Worcester County, MD permits for a <strong>basement remodeling job</strong>.</p>\n<h2>Applying for Worcester County, Maryland Permits (Residential Construction)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>To apply, you&rsquo;ll need to submit 3 &ldquo;stick built&rdquo; construction plans, and 4 modular ones (view the <a href=\"https://www.co.worcester.md.us/sites/default/files/Building-Plan-Permit-Application-required-info-062615-residential.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">full requirements</a>).</li>\n<li>You must also include all of the appropriate information for the main contractor, including license number, so that it can be checked with the Maryland database.</li>\n<li>For electrical, HVAC, and building contractors, license verification comes later.</li>\n<li>If the house is not new, then sprinkler systems are not required in the plans (but they could be required later by the Fire Marshall, so you will have to schedule an inspection).</li>\n<li>Foundation dimensions, thickness, framing, joist size, and spacing details are all needed.</li>\n<li>A completed Worcester County 2015 IECC Energy Code form.</li>\n<li>Documentation for insulation, windows and doors, and HVAC systems.</li>\n<li>The airflow for ducts and doors must be performed by an approved county contractor.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How to Pass Worcester County, MD Inspections</h2>\n<p>In order to pass Worcester County, MD inspections, you must have the following checked:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Insulation (done by a Worcester County Inspector)</li>\n<li>Air leakage (performed by a certified contractor or inspector)</li>\n<li>Certificate of Compliance &ndash; this includes HVAC controls, hot water controls, duct insulation, duct and piping sealing, ventilation, sizing, and lighting equipment (inspected at the final stage by Worcester officials).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Specific zoning issues, certificates, and building code requirements can vary from project to project and will be reviewed by the building inspector. For more information of Worcester County, MD inspections, read the <a href=\"http://www.worcesterma.gov/e-services/faqs/building-permits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">official FAQ</a>.</p>',2,'',130,'2017-04-16 15:48:33'),(147,'How to Hire a Contractor (Everything You Must Ask)','How do you hire a contractor? Are there any specific questions you should ask? There\'s a lot you need to know first.','how to hire a contractor, hiring a contractor, basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor, basement masters, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas','how-to-hire-a-contractor-everything-you-must-ask','How to Hire a Contractor (Everything You Must Ask)','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/147/4840af9d81507e32e1e989946046f496','What questions should you ask contractors before hiring them?','<p>There&rsquo;s a lot of things to consider when your business is <strong>hiring a contractor</strong>. The competition is stiff, and everyone is making themselves sound like the best possible option. If you want to know how to hire a contractor the right way, here are 10 simple questions that will tell you everything you need to know straight away.</p>\n<h2>How to Hire a Contractor</h2>\n<h3>1. Licensing</h3>\n<p>Don&rsquo;t be afraid to ask for proof that the contractor is properly licensed.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>As a state, Maryland does not require a Contractors License, but contractors must still be properly licensed to perform electrical, plumbing, or HVAC work.</li>\n<li>Virginia, on the other hand, <a href=\"http://www.dpor.virginia.gov/Boards/Contractors/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">requires multiple licenses</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. Insurance</h3>\n<p>Contractors must have:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Workers&rsquo; compensation insurance</li>\n<li>Property damage and liability insurance</li>\n<li>Commercial auto insurance</li>\n<li>Rental equipment insurance</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. Business History</h3>\n<p>Before hiring a contractor, you want to find out the following information:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Legal history (lawsuits)</li>\n<li>Financial history (such as bankruptcies)</li>\n<li>Any accredited associations they are a part of (such as the BBB)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Be sure to request a list of references for similar projects that they have worked on, and follow through by contacting them and investigating their legitimacy.</p>\n<h3>4. General Procedures</h3>\n<p>Ask them who will be at the site, and how the site will be supervised. More specifically:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>How much time will be spent at the site each work?</li>\n<li>How many other projects is the contractor currently handling?</li>\n<li>What permits need to be pulled?</li>\n<li>What materials will be used?</li>\n<li>Is the contractor performing labor themselves or supervising?</li>\n<li>What is their clean-up procedure?</li>\n<li>When is the start date and completion date?</li>\n<li>Do they have itemized price estimates?</li>\n<li>What is their payment schedule?</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>5. Payments</h3>\n<p>Be sure to ask how &ldquo;surprise&rdquo; expenses will be handled, and agree upon a reasonable down payment. Remember: a stable contractor won&rsquo;t need much money upfront, so if you are hiring a contractor and one of them asks for a huge advance, then it should be taken as a major red flag.</p>\n<p>Also, make sure that you are paying a company and not an individual. If you are cutting checks to an individual who owns a business license, then it could mean they aren&rsquo;t going to declare this on their taxes (again, not a good sign).</p>\n<p>Most importantly, if you want to know how to hire a contractor properly, then don&rsquo;t ever pay cash! You want to use a method of payment with a paper trail in case anything is ever disputed in the future.</p>\n<h2>How to Hire a Contractor While Doing Your Own Research</h2>\n<p>Asking the contractor about permits and licenses is a good idea, but don&rsquo;t rely solely on their word. Do your own research and learn what the rules are in your area. There are plenty of resources to figure out exactly which permits are required for your area, whether you live in Maryland or Virginia.</p>',4,'',131,'2017-04-14 15:48:45'),(148,'Anne Arundel County Permits and Fees','Planning a basement remodeling project in Anne Arundel County, MD? This guide explains all of the different types of permits you’ll need.','basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor, Anne Arundel County, MD, building permits, permits, Maryland, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','anne-arundel-county-permits-and-fees','Anne Arundel County Permits and Fees','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/148/1dceb8e3d675d5c931f86bf6c7244ff1','What permits do you need for a basement remodeling project in Anne Arundel County, Maryland?','<p>This helpful guide will explain all of the different types of <strong>Anne Arundel County permits</strong> you&rsquo;ll need for a Maryland basement remodeling job, exactly what is considered a finished basement in Anne Arundel County, and how to pass county inspections. Let&rsquo;s start with the basics!</p>\n<h2>What Kind of Anne Arundel County Permits do I Need for Basement Remodeling?</h2>\n<p>If you are waterproofing a basement, all you need is a simple building permit. However, if you are finishing a basement in Anne Arundel, MD, you are going to need the following permits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Building Permit</li>\n<li>Electrical Permit</li>\n<li>Plumbing Permit</li>\n<li>Mechanical Permit (this covers all HVAC work)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What Information Do I Need to Get a Anne Arundel County Building Permit?</h2>\n<p>When applying for a <a href=\"http://www.aacounty.org/departments/inspections-and-permits/permit-center/forms-and-publications/BuildPermAppl.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">building permit</a> (Anne Arundel County, MD), you are going to need to submit one copy of a site plan and three copies of the construction plan.</p>\n<p>The site plan:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Must be drawn to scale by professional engineering standards</li>\n<li>Must show the &ldquo;location, configuration, and dimensions&rdquo; of your work.</li>\n<li>Must show easements, property lines, private wells or septic systems, and a grinder pump (if any).</li>\n<li>Only one site plan copy is needed.</li>\n<li>If the basement does not have a private well or septic system, no site plan is required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Construction plans:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Must use an official architectural scale</li>\n<li>Must show all room dimensions</li>\n<li>Must show what kind of materials will be used</li>\n<li>Must outline the actual construction process</li>\n<li>Three copies are needed.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How Much do Anne Arundel County Permits Cost?</h2>\n<p>Electrical, building, and mechanical permits all come with a $25 application fee (plumbing does not).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Building Permits &ndash; Depending on the value of the property, these permits can cost anywhere from $50 to $140. Check out the <a href=\"http://www.aacounty.org/departments/inspections-and-permits/permit-center/IP_Permits/Building-Permit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">official price chart</a>.</li>\n<li>Electrical Permits &ndash; Depending on the total amps and property type, these permits range from $20 to $190. Check out the <a href=\"http://www.aacounty.org/departments/inspections-and-permits/permit-center/IP_Permits/Electrical-Permit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">full chart</a>.</li>\n<li>Mechanical Permits &ndash; These permits range from $30 all the way to $75, depending on the type of system and the type of property. Check out the <a href=\"http://www.aacounty.org/departments/inspections-and-permits/permit-center/IP_Permits/Mechanical-Permit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">full list</a>.</li>\n<li>Plumbing Permits &ndash; Although these types of permits can be expensive, a permit to reconstruct existing plumbing is much cheaper than normal, averaging about $30. Check out the <a href=\"http://www.aacounty.org/departments/inspections-and-permits/permit-center/IP_Permits/Plumbing-Permit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">full table</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What is Considered a Finished Basement in Anne Arundel County, Maryland?</h2>\n<p>A finished basement in Anne Arundel County, Maryland needs to have the proper measurements. Here&rsquo;s an <a href=\"http://www.aacounty.org/departments/inspections-and-permits/permit-center/forms-and-publications/Resources/FinishBasementCodeRequirements.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">official checklist</a> containing the most crucial measurements you&rsquo;ll need to remember:</p>\n<p>Habitable Rooms &ndash; Any room that is going to be inhabited must have a minimum area of 70 square feet, and a minimum horizontal dimension of 7 feet.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A minimum horizontal dimension means the largest circular diameter within the confines of a room.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Bedroom Windows &ndash; Each bedroom must have at least one bedroom window that has:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A minimum &ldquo;clear opening&rdquo; of 5.7 square feet (this allows a fireman who is wearing breathing apparatus to fit through the door).</li>\n<li>24 inches for minimum opening height.</li>\n<li>20 inches for minimum opening width.</li>\n<li>A sill height no more than 44 inches.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ceiling Height &ndash; The minimum height of the ceiling depends on the type of room.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Habitable Rooms must be 7 feet tall.</li>\n<li>All other areas must be at least 6&rsquo;8 feet tall, but 6&rsquo;4 feet tall if under beams or ductwork.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Hallways &ndash; All hallways must have a minimum width of 36 inches.</p>\n<p>Stairways &nbsp;-- All stairways must be at least 36 inches wide and have at least 6&rsquo;8 feet of headroom. The stair tread itself must be 10 inches wide, and the stairs themselves must rise no more than 7-3/4 inches.</p>\n<p>Bathrooms &ndash; The shower or bathtub area must use a &ldquo;non-absorbent surface&rdquo;.</p>\n<p>Stud Walls &ndash; Stud walls must use 2 x 4 inch studs, with the center of each stud placed at 16-inch intervals. Pressure-treated sole plates must be used.</p>\n<p>Warm Air Furnaces &ndash; May not be installed in closets, or bedrooms, or bathrooms.</p>\n<p>Fuse Boxes &ndash; May not be installed in clothing closets.</p>\n<h2>How to Pass Anne Arundel County Inspections</h2>\n<p>Simply getting Anne Arundel County permits isn&rsquo;t enough. To pass Anne Arundel County inspections, your basement must be up to Anne Arundel County, Maryland basement remodeling <a href=\"http://www.aacounty.org/departments/inspections-and-permits/permit-center/building-codes/residential-code-requirements/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Code</a>. For residential properties, an Anne Arundel County inspections officer will be checking the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows and doorways must use double studs and double headers, and the headers have to be set on the studs, on edge.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>A finished basement in Anne Arundel, Maryland must have two separate exits.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>A basement wall must utilize R-10 (for belowground) or R-13 insulation (for stud walls).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Check out the <a href=\"http://www.aacounty.org/departments/inspections-and-permits/permit-center/building-codes/residential-code-requirements/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Residential Code</a> for more information on design loads, framework requirements, foundation walls, and everything else you need to pass Anne Arundel County inspections!</p>\n<p>If you would like us to handle permitting, as well as all other aspects of your project, select your location below and schedule your free in-home consultation today!</p>\n<p><a href=\"../../../../basement-finishing-area/md/anne-arundel/annapolis\">Annapolis</a>, <a href=\"../../../../basement-finishing-area/md/anne-arundel/crofton\">&nbsp;Crofton</a>, <a href=\"../../../../basement-finishing-area/md/anne-arundel/glen-burnie\">Glen-Burnie</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"../../../../basement-finishing-area/md/anne-arundel/severn\">Severn</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"../../../../basement-finishing-area/md/anne-arundel/severna-park\">Severna-Park</a>, <a href=\"../../../../basement-finishing-area/md/anne-arundel\">Anne Arundel County</a></p>',2,'',132,'2017-04-09 15:48:59'),(149,'Maryland Basement Remodeling: Caroll County Permits','Thinking about doing some basement remodeling in Caroll County, Maryland? You\'ll need permits! Learn more here with this helpful permit guide.','Caroll County MD permits, Caroll County permits, Maryland basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor, basement finishing, permits, building permits, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','maryland-basement-remodeling-caroll-county-permits','Maryland Basement Remodeling: Caroll County Permits','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/149/510a1446881107ccab84208d8c5854d4','Don\'t try any basement work in Carroll County, MD without first consulting our permits guide!','<p>Planning on doing some basement remodeling in <strong>Caroll County, Maryland</strong>? Permits are required! But in order to apply for <a href=\"https://ccgovernment.carr.org/ccg/permits/Basement.aspx?ver=con\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Caroll County MD permits</a>, you must submit with your application two sets of construction plans that show the following information:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Labeled rooms</li>\n<li>The square footage of finished and unfinished basement remodeling areas</li>\n<li>Door, window and ceiling measurements (both existing and proposed)</li>\n<li>Clearly-marked exits</li>\n<li>Any proposed partition walls</li>\n<li>The type of material that will be used for wall framing and spacing (wood or metal)</li>\n<li>Smoke detector locations</li>\n<li>A sprinkler system (optional, but if one is not one in place, you must make it clear)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How Long Does it Take to Get Caroll County MD Permits?</h2>\n<p>Going forward with <strong>Maryland basement remodeling</strong> in Caroll County is easy. If everything is in order, Caroll County MD permits can be issued within 10-15 business days.</p>\n<h2>Caroll County MD Permits &amp; Inspections</h2>\n<p>So now that you have all of your <strong>Caroll County permits</strong> and you&rsquo;re ready to build, here is what you need to know to pass inspections:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The minimum ceiling height for an unfinished basement is 6&rsquo;8 (unless under beams, at which point it&rsquo;s 6&rsquo;4).</li>\n<li>For finished basements, at least 50% of all &ldquo;habitable rooms&rdquo; must be at least 7 feet.</li>\n<li>All sill plates must utilize pressure treated wood or wood that is naturally durable.</li>\n<li>Non-bearing walls can be constructed using 2 X 3 studs spaced 16 or 24 inches from the center (an appropriate wall finish is still required). 2 X 4 or 2 x 6 walls are permitted so long as they have the correct wall finish according to Caroll County MD permit <a href=\"http://www.ccgovernment.carr.org/ccg/permits/Codes.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Code</a>.</li>\n<li>Every &ldquo;sleeping room&rdquo; needs to have either a door or an exit window that has a &ldquo;net clear opening&rdquo; of 5&rsquo;7 sq. feet and an opening width of at least 20 inches, and a minimum opening height of 24 inches. Be aware that the minimum opening width and the minimum opening height is not enough to reach the net clear opening of 5&rsquo;7 sq. feet.</li>\n<li>The glazing in the basement should be 2% of the total finished basement floor area. So if the basement is 1,000 sq. ft., then the area of basement with glass windows or doors must be no less than 20 sq. ft.</li>\n<li>If you are glazing a &ldquo;habitable room&rdquo;, then this percentage jumps up to 8%.</li>\n<li>If your basement has an existing sprinkler system, it may need to be redesigned in accordance to the State Fire Marshall&rsquo;s specifications.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Check out an important summary of the <a href=\"http://ccgovernment.carr.org/ccg/permits/doc/Residential/ResidentialCodeComplianceGuidelinesBasement.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">code compliance guidelines</a>.</p>\n<h2>Any More Questions About Obtaining Caroll County MD Permits?</h2>\n<p>Drop a question in the comments below! We&rsquo;ve remodeled countless basements in Caroll County, MD and we know the permit process inside and out, and we&rsquo;re ready to help.</p>',2,'',133,'2017-04-03 15:49:12'),(150,'6 Need-to-Know Basement Finishing Regulations in Maryland','Are you sure your finished basement is truly finished in they eyes of the state? Find out here if your finished basement is up to Maryland code!','basement finishing, basement finishing regulations, finished basement, basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor, Maryland regulations, MD finished basement regulations, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','6-need-to-know-basement-finishing-regulations-in-maryland','6 Need-to-Know Basement Finishing Regulations in Maryland','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/150/b81ba57186de309cb531907ee8c42ccd','You might think you have a finished basement, but are you positive?','<p>You might think you have a finished basement, but are you positive? Each county has its own specific rules, but here are 6 general <strong>basement finishing regulations in Maryland </strong>that you have to follow in order to have a legally finished basement.</p>\n<h2>Maryland Finished Basement Regulations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Minimum Height</strong> &ndash; The minimum ceiling height is 6&rsquo;8, but 6&rsquo;4 under bulkheads.<br /><br /></li>\n<li><strong>Smoke Detectors </strong>&ndash; A smoke detector/carbon monoxide detector must be near the stairs, and also within 15 feet of any bedroom entrances<strong>.<br /><br /></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Safe Exits </strong>&ndash; Most counties require at least two exits leading directly from the finished basement to outside of the home, though sometimes only one exit is necessary.<br /><br /></li>\n<li><strong>Blower Door Test &ndash; </strong>If the finished basement required new ductwork or major changes to the walls or ceiling, then the airflow of your home or business might <a href=\"http://energy.maryland.gov/Documents/YourHomeandtheEnergyCode.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">need to be tested</a> by a device called a blower door.<br /><br /></li>\n<li><strong>Insulation </strong>&ndash; All &ldquo;continuous insulation&rdquo; (a special type of heat-retaining insulation) that&rsquo;s below ground must be R-10, but insulation must be R-13 for stud walls. In general, when we have continuous insulation installed by the builder (which is another code requirement), we frame the walls next to it without compressing the pre-attached insulation. When you compress it, it loses thermal resistance.<br /><br /></li>\n<li><strong>Energy Efficiency Certification </strong>&ndash; Someone involved in the remodeling process (builder, contractor, or<br />designer) must provide documentation showing that the building materials and various systems are compliant with the <a href=\"http://dhcd.maryland.gov/Codes/Documents/BuildingCodes/2016,%20MBPS%20-%20List%20of%20Applicable%20Codes%20and%20Standards.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">International Energy Conservation Code</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Do you have any finished basement questions? If so, drop a comment below. We want to answer them!</p>',2,'',134,'2017-03-29 15:49:24'),(151,'Can You Include Basement Remodeling Deductions for Taxes?','If you’ve done some basement remodeling recently, you may be able to write some or all of it off on your taxes! Learn more here.','taxes, deductions for taxes, basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor, basement finishing, taxation, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','can-you-include-basement-remodeling-deductions-for-taxes','Can You Include Basement Remodeling Deductions for Taxes?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/151/36aea396b7e0800114d35d54169f4bc2','Check through our list and see how many potential basement remodeling tax deductions apply to you!','<p>The tax man is here again, but before you groan too loudly, know that there are some things you can write off on your taxes if you&rsquo;ve had some basement remodeling done lately. Check through our list and see how many potential <strong>basement remodeling tax&nbsp;deductions</strong>&nbsp;apply to you!</p>\n<h2>Office Space Deductions For Taxes</h2>\n<p>If you added a home office last year, the remodeling expenses may be one of the things you can write off on your taxes. In order to do this, you typically (but not always) <a href=\"https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/home-office-deduction\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">have to prove</a> that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You are self-employed</li>\n<li>The home office basement remodeling was essential for your business operations</li>\n<li>You only use this space for business</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Figuring out your office space deductions for taxes can be tricky. We are not accountants, but you need to somehow figure out the percentage of home space that is being used for an office, and deduct that exact amount. Sometimes you can even write off a portion of your utilities and insurance costs.</p>\n<h2>Disability Tax Write Offs</h2>\n<p>Basement remodeling costs that were made specifically to <a href=\"https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-pdf/p907.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">accommodate a disability</a> are sometimes things you can write off on your taxes, providing that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You, your spouse, or someone you claim as &ldquo;dependent&rdquo; on taxes has the disability.</li>\n<li>The person with the disability also lives on the property</li>\n</ul>\n<p>There are certain limitations to how much you can claim, especially if the improvements increase the overall value of the property. Cosmetic improvements do not count. The improvements must be a medical necessity to qualify.</p>\n<h2>Energy Efficiency Write Offs</h2>\n<p>Most of the <a href=\"https://www.energystar.gov/about/2016_federal_tax_credits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">federal energy efficiency tax credits</a> have long since expired, but you might be able to qualify for deductions for taxes if you choose an energy-efficient furnace or water heater. At the very least, utility companies have been known to sometimes give you credits for doing this, if not the IRS.</p>',2,'',135,'2017-03-22 15:49:36'),(152,'3 Great Design Benefits of a Basement Tray Ceiling','Wondering why a basement tray ceiling still remains a popular design choice over the years? It\'s primarily because of these three benefits.','basement remodeling, basement renovation, ceiling, drop ceiling, tray ceiling, design, basement tray ceiling, ceiling designs, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas','3-great-design-benefits-of-a-basement-tray-ceiling','3 Great Design Benefits of a Basement Tray Ceiling','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/152/cea5783458231004c4828a9b07f28c76','Basement tray ceilings are a continuously popular ceiling design choice, but what are some of the benefits?','<p><strong>Basement tray ceilings</strong> have remained quite popular for years now, and 2017 shows no signs of slowing down. A basement tray ceiling means that the center of the ceiling is raised and layered, bringing a dramatic look to any room.</p>\n<h2>Adding basement tray ceilings will:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Increase Height </strong>&ndash; Basements can tend to look small, but even an average-sized basement will look very tall with tray ceilings thanks to the added depth.</li>\n<li><strong>Add Volume </strong>&ndash; Basement tray ceilings will make a room look wider. In fact, homeowners sometimes buy too much furniture because the room looks much larger (fortunately, our decorators will keep you from making this mistake).</li>\n<li><strong>Offer Unlimited Design Possibilities</strong> <strong>&ndash; </strong>When it comes to decorating, a basement tray ceiling lets you add different colors, borders, and even hidden LED lights.</li>\n</ul>',1,'',136,'2017-03-19 15:49:53'),(153,'How to Prevent Mold in Your Basement: 5 Tips','Mold is a necessary part of nature, but it doesn’t have to be a part of your basement! Read more here on how to prevent mold in your basement.','Mold, moisture, waterproof basement, prevent basement mold, mold prevention, tips to prevent mold, basement renovation, basement remodeling, mold removal, mold inspection, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas','how-to-prevent-mold-in-your-basement-5-tips','How to Prevent Mold in Your Basement: 5 Tips','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/153/5f29721734c91ebc6f1fd19edb9a0e73','Are you doing all you can to prevent mold from growing in your basement?','<p>Mold&mdash;it might be a part of nature, but it definitely shouldn\'t be a part of your basement! The experts at BasementRemodeling.com know how to stop mold from growing into a bigger problem, so read on to find out <strong>how to prevent mold </strong>in your basement...before it&rsquo;s too late!</p>\n<h2>Tip #1: Identify Problem Areas</h2>\n<p>You can&rsquo;t <strong>stop mold from growing </strong>until you&rsquo;ve located the source of the moisture, so take a look around. Is water coming from a leaky pipe, cracks in the foundation, or from the edges of a window? Keep an eye on these areas, and look for any discoloration on the walls or ceiling.</p>\n<h2>Tip #2: Dry the Basement Out</h2>\n<p>Any wet areas need to be dried within 24 to 48 hours, and this includes everything from rainwater seepage to minor spills. Installing a good ventilation system is absolutely necessary because, above all else, keeping your basement free of moisture is the best way we know how to prevent mold.</p>\n<h2>Tip #3: Try to Keep Your Basement Tidy</h2>\n<p>Good news: if you&rsquo;re a tidy person, then you already know how to prevent mold for the most part. Never leave wet items such as used towels lying on the basement floor, and be extra sure to dry the floors and walls after showering or taking a bath. &nbsp;</p>\n<h2>Tip #4: Install a Humidity Monitor</h2>\n<p>You can stop mold from growing by controlling your basement environment and keeping conditions unfavorable for mold. This <a href=\"https://www.epa.gov/mold/mold-course-chapter-2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EPA guide</a> suggests keeping the humidity level between 30 and 50 percent, which will also keep bugs out of your basement as well.</p>\n<h2>Tip #5: Hire A Waterproofing Contractor</h2>\n<p>A professional waterproofing team has the necessary equipment and expertise to analyze your basement and come up with a customized solution to keep moisture out of your home. They will examine your basement walls for cracks, your pipes for leaks, your drainage system, and more. If you are experiencing a mold problem in the Maryland or Virginia areas, you can <a href=\"http://www.basementmasterswaterproofing.com/basement-waterproofing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">request a free inspection</a> and get the help you need. We&rsquo;ll show you how to prevent mold in your basement once and for all.</p>',3,'',137,'2017-03-14 15:50:09'),(154,'5 Common Basement Remodeling Mistakes','Read about these most common errors people make during basement remodeling. Are you sure you are not committing any of these?','common basement remodeling mistakes, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish, basement remodeling blog, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas','5-common-basement-remodeling-mistakes','5 Common Basement Remodeling Mistakes','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/154/cb792872eda98212df563ba327e1624e','Are you committing any of these 5 basement blunders?','<p>Remodeling your basement is a complex process with many factors to consider. Fortunately, we have years of expertise and are here to help! Here are 5 <strong>common basement remodeling mistakes</strong> to avoid when taking on your next project.</p>\n<h2>Don&rsquo;t Put Small Rooms Everywhere</h2>\n<p>A common basement remodeling mistake is to try and make your downstairs look exactly like the first floor. However, breaking your basement into too many different rooms will most likely make it feel claustrophobic instead of inviting. Rather than closing your basement off, open it up with cabinets, glass doors and archways.</p>\n<p>You can delineate different spaces by tastefully using different flooring, decorative columns or half-walls. All of these options can give off a much warmer impression than fully closing the room off.</p>\n<h2>Not Waterproofing</h2>\n<p>Depending on where you live, basement floods can be a common or rare occurrence &ndash; but eventually, it&rsquo;s almost bound to happen. Planning a drainage or dehumidifying system now will save you from expensive repairs in the future. Also, be sure to check your foundation for cracks early on and seal them accordingly.</p>\n<h2>Using The Wrong Materials for the Job</h2>\n<p>Hardwood floors look nice, but if your basement floods regularly, then you might want to choose a different building material such as LVT. Similarly, you have to make sure to use the correct insulation when building interior walls. Using the incorrect insulation will cause moisture retention and other problems over time.</p>\n<h2>Not Updating the Stairway</h2>\n<p>If you are going to go through the effort of remodeling your basement, you should pay special attention to the entrance staircase because an updated basement with an out-of-date staircase will clash noticeably. Iron wrought railings, half-walls, and fancy banisters may better match your new d&eacute;cor.</p>\n<h2>Not Hiring a Contractor</h2>\n<p>Basements are oftentimes the hardest area of the house to remodel. Unless you have years of experience, it&rsquo;s best to leave basement remodeling up to the professionals. Otherwise, you could very well end up hiring one anyway to fix your mistakes, costing you more money and time in the long run!</p>',1,'',138,'2017-03-10 15:50:26'),(155,'How Much Does Basement Waterproofing Cost?','Waterproofing your basement is essential to the longevity of your home and health, but how much does it cost? Here\'s what you need to know.','waterproof basement, cost, how much does waterproof basement cost, basement renovation, basement remodeling, basement waterproofing cost, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','how-much-does-basement-waterproofing-cost','How Much Does Basement Waterproofing Cost?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/155/7f29b8bef2eea9fbe44c1fe246dd502c','Waterproofing your basement is necessary to keep your family healthy and your home in good condition, but how much does it cost?','<p>You&rsquo;ve found water in your basement, and now you logically want to know,&nbsp;<strong>how much does basement waterproofing cost?</strong>&nbsp;Before you can figure out exactly how much waterproofing a basement will cost, you need to take many different factors into consideration.</p>\n<h2>Interior Versus Exterior Basement Waterproofing</h2>\n<p>How much does basement waterproofing cost? Well, that depends on the source of the problem. If high humidity is the problem, then a good dehumidifier system could be all you need. If you have damp soil around your foundation, then the basement walls themselves might need to be waterproofed.</p>\n<p>In general, it is cheaper to waterproof your interior walls, but it can be more effective to waterproof your exterior walls in the long run. Having a professional inspection will let you know which one you need for sure.</p>\n<h2>Waterproofing Methods</h2>\n<p>The second factor when determining basement waterproofing cost is choosing the right method for the job. Not all basement waterproofing costs the same. There are all sorts of different waterproofing sealers and coatings that are meant to handle different types of leaks, and the key is to find the cheapest solution that will give you the longest-lasting results.</p>\n<h2>Leave it to the Professionals</h2>\n<p>This is where we come in! At <a href=\"../../../../how-it-works/basement-tips/\">BasementRemodeling.com</a>, we have years of experience identifying sources of basement leaks and solving them with speed and accuracy. We only use the most appropriate basement waterproofing solutions for you and your home or place of business &ndash; no surprises, no up-charges. Just quality results!</p>',3,'',139,'2017-03-08 15:50:38'),(156,'Types of Insurance That Every Independent Contractor Needs','Before starting a basement project, an independent contractor needs to have a variety of insurance coverage. But why? and which types? Find out here.','Building permit, basement remodeling, basement renovation, general contractor, insurance, liability insurance, basement remodeling blog, basement blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas, independent contractor, types of insurance','types-of-insurance-that-every-independent-contractor-needs','Types of Insurance That Every Independent Contractor Needs','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/156/94695fbaa54e318240b78f963a453550','There are a ton of insurance types every homeowner or independent contractor should consider using before starting a basement project, but what are they? Which types are unnecessary and which aren\'t?','<p>Many <strong>different types of insurance</strong> need to be considered when an <strong>independent contractor</strong> enters the home or place of business to work on a basement. Whether you are a homeowner reading this to better understand the process, or you are an independent contractor yourself, this blog will clearly explain the different types of insurance both parties need to get the job done. &nbsp;</p>\n<h2>What is General Liability Insurance?</h2>\n<p>What is General Liability Insurance? In one word, essential! This insurance is mainly designed to cover expenses stemming from any job-related accidents and injuries.</p>\n<p>How it works:</p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">You purchase a General Liability Insurance plan.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">An independent contractor causes injury or damages property.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">The insurance company will cover it (up to a certain amount) under general liability insurance.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Having said this, every independent contractor, homeowner, and place of business should have some form of general liability insurance before the project begins. Although General Liability Insurance is not always mandatory, ask yourself, &ldquo;what is General Liability Insurance compared to the cost of an actual lawsuit?&rdquo; Leading companies such as Basement Masters will always have strong General Liability Insurance &ndash; in fact, most people won&rsquo;t do business with basement remodeling companies unless they have it!</p>\n<h2>What is Umbrella Insurance?</h2>\n<p>Umbrella insurance is one of the many different types of insurance that&rsquo;s designed to protect you from a major lawsuit. It is basically an upgrade your existing policy so that you have will more coverage than the standard liability deduction. In other words, if you get in more financial trouble than a standard policy covers, then the umbrella insurance policy will usually kick in (at least with most cases).</p>\n<p>Essentially, you pay more to the insurance company now in exchange for having them pay higher settlements later. If you are a homeowner or own a place of business, then an Umbrella insurance policy could be a wise investment. If you are an independent contractor, it is also a good idea, but not nearly as important (because most circumstances in Umbrella policies relate to the property owner).</p>\n<p>There is, however, a second reason for contractors to have Umbrella insurance. Your company might take on a big project with a contract requiring an increase in your current General Liability Insurance coverage. Adding an Umbrella insurance policy to your existing General Liability Insurance plan is an easy way to do this (doing this is sometimes called Excess Liability Insurance). Basically, almost any basement remodeling company looking to expand to bigger projects will eventually need Umbrella insurance!&nbsp;</p>\n<h2>What is Workers Compensation Insurance?&nbsp;</h2>\n<p>Workers Compensation Insurance is a crucial way to make sure employers reasonably take care of their workers. It has two purposes: first, it guarantees workers will get reimbursed for lost income and medical expenses in the event of an emergency. Second, it mostly prevents the employer from being sued for negligence (though not always).</p>\n<p>Exactly what is workers compensation varies from state to state. Your state will have its own set of laws that determine payouts, layouts, and whether such insurance is mandatory or not. Some states, for example, will require you to buy Workers Compensation Insurance after your company grows to a certain number of employees. Check with your state&rsquo;s local website to find out more about your area.</p>\n<p>If you are the one having your basement worked on, you don&rsquo;t need Workers Compensation Insurance. If you are a contractor, however, it is absolutely in your best interest to have Workers Compensation Insurance (and oftentimes mandatory).</p>\n<h2>What is Commercial Auto Insurance?&nbsp;</h2>\n<p>Commercial Auto Insurance only applies to contractors. This form of insurance covers vehicle repairs, and many different types of expenses stemming from automobile accidents.</p>\n<p>If one of your employees gets into an auto accident &ndash; even in their own personal vehicle &ndash; you could be held responsible. Commercial Auto Insurance kicks in whenever an employee&rsquo;s personal insurance is not enough to cover damages. It can also cover professional tools and other work equipment inside of the vehicle. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<h2>What is Rental Equipment Insurance?&nbsp;</h2>\n<p>Again, this is one of the different types of insurance that only the contractors have to worry about. Here&rsquo;s how it works:</p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Many independent contractors will rent the necessary tools and equipment to get the job done.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">The rental companies make them sign waivers saying that they take full legal responsibility for the rental equipment and will not sue in the case of an accident.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Contractors buy Rental Equipment Insurance to cover themselves in the event of an accident that occurred while using the equipment, or to cover the cost if the equipment is stolen or otherwise damaged.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Which Types of Insurance Are Most Important?</h2>\n<p>&nbsp;At BasementRemodeling.com, we are far from legal consultants, so choosing from the different types of insurance is ultimately up to you. However, we can say that the more insurance you have, the more secure your projects will be, and that&rsquo;s never a bad thing!</p>',2,'',140,'2017-03-03 15:50:58'),(157,'Can a Finished Basement Add Value to Your Home or Business?','Does having a finished basement add any extra value to your home? Is it worth your time to finish an unfinished basement? Find out here!','basement remodeling, added value, price of house, cost, basement renovation, general contractor, MD, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas, finished basement ideas, finished basements','can-a-finished-basement-add-value-to-your-home-or-business','Can a Finished Basement Add Value to Your Home or Business?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/157/8c01e7180e5a4d2a255c0bd280e7144d','Will finishing your basement add value to your home? If so, exactly how much value will it add?','<p>Does a <strong>basement add value</strong> to a home (or business)? Put simply&mdash;yes, almost always. Of course, the immediate follow-up question is &ldquo;how <em>much</em> value can a <strong>finished basement</strong> add to your home?&rdquo;, and that&rsquo;s where things can get confusing for some. Fortunately, BasementRemodeling.com is here to clear everything up.</p>\n<h2>How Does a Finished Basement Add Value to Your Home?</h2>\n<p>When you are getting your home appraised, your aboveground floor space is valued differently than the basement area. Basically, everything belowground is worth slightly less per square foot, and its dimensions aren&rsquo;t included in the total square footage. However, when the appraiser is figuring out the total value of each square foot of the aboveground space, a finished basement is factored into the mathematical formula and makes everything worth more.</p>\n<h2>Why is it Like This?</h2>\n<p>Real estate agents created this unique appraisal system because they don&rsquo;t want basements to overinflate the price of the home. If aboveground space was considered to be the same worth as belowground space, then a small home with a large basement would be way too expensive. Unfinished basements are scored differently as well, offering less value. So, finishing your basement now can make a huge difference come listing time.</p>\n<h2>Are You Ready to Improve the Value of Your Home or Business?</h2>\n<p>Finishing your basement now is a great way to improve the overall value of your home per square foot, and BasementRemodeling.com is ready to help. When you are ready for a beautiful finished basement in your downstairs area, give us a call at (301) 798-4444 for a free estimate or get an <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">online quote</a> today! &nbsp;</p>',2,'',141,'2017-03-02 15:51:11'),(158,'5 Common Basement Bugs in Maryland that Could Indicate a Water Problem','What the most common basement bugs in Maryland? Do any of them indicate a water problem? Find out here.','bugs, termites, silverfish, basement remodeling, basement renovation, bee, cockroach, common basement bugs, water problems, basement waterproofing, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas','5-common-basement-bugs-in-maryland-that-could-indicate-a-water-problem','5 Common Basement Bugs in Maryland that Could Indicate a Water Problem','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/158/d915a4cfadf1af832d07aa46827ab873','What are these 5 common basement bugs telling you about your business or home?','<p>Do you have bugs living in your basement? Almost undoubtedly so. While most<strong> common basement bugs in Maryland </strong>are essentially harmless, there are 5 in particular that could indicate a serious water problem in your basement that needs to be addressed.</p>\n<h2>1. Silverfish</h2>\n<p>These grey bugs are about an inch in length and only come out at night. They will eat small holes into many items that people keep in their basement for storage such as books and photographs, and even cotton clothing, making them potential pests in your downstairs dwelling.</p>\n<p>These common basement bugs in Maryland also like to feast on mold, which means that they are good indicators of a leaky basement. If you see a suddenly influx of silverfish in your basement, you might want to see if there is a leak nearby that is attracting them.</p>\n<h2>2. Centipedes</h2>\n<p>Did you know that a single centipede can live for up to 6 years? This makes them quite the persistent pests if left unchecked. They like to lay their eggs in moist soil, and they prefer to live in damp places in general. Therefore, if you see lots of centipedes in your basement, it could mean that a water problem is making the conditions damp enough for them to move in.</p>\n<h2>3. Mold Mites</h2>\n<p>As their name suggests, mold mites like to go wherever mold is. So if you see them cropping up around your basement, then some sort of fungus most likely isn&rsquo;t far behind. And behind every case of basement mold is a source of water, which means a leaky pipe, foundational cracks, or something similar could be to blame.</p>\n<h2>4. Earwigs</h2>\n<p>Though one of the least common basement bugs in Maryland, you will occasionally hear of earwigs in a basement from time to time. These nocturnal insects prefer to hang out in damp soil and tree stumps outside, so if you do see some in your basement, chances are you have a bad water problem. Although these bugs do not cause much damage to a home per se, they are a good indication that something could be wrong.</p>\n<h2>5. Pillbugs</h2>\n<p>Pillbugs in the basement means that a water problem may be to blame. These pillbugs prefer soft and damp soil, so if you see them in your basement, it could mean that the surrounding soil is oversaturated, which could lead to cracks in the foundation (and other problems).</p>\n<h2>Are You Experiencing Any of These Common Maryland Bugs In Your Basement?</h2>\n<p>If so, you may have a water problem that BasementRemodeling.com can help with. Learn more about <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/waterproofing/\">waterproofing your basement</a>&nbsp;so that you can keep pests, moisture and mold out of your home or business once and for all!</p>',3,'',142,'2017-03-01 15:51:23'),(159,'Basement Masters is Expanding!','From now on, Basement Masters will be making even more basements! Are you in need of a basement remodeling service in MD, DC, VA? Call us now!','basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','basement-masters-is-expanding','Basement Masters is Expanding!','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/159/cf18b6233c8f92f99fdc79ca6dde8355','What big changes are in store for Basement Masters?','<div class=\"html\">\n<p><strong>Basement Masters is Expanding!</strong></p>\n<p>Good news! We are currently expanding our business so that we can work on even more basements beyond the borders of Maryland, D.C., and Virginia. Stay tuned as we unveil exciting new plans and multiple partnerships. We can&rsquo;t wait to share the full story with you soon.</p>\n<p>For now, what we can say is that 2017 is shaping up to be a great year for basements everywhere!</p>\n<p>&nbsp;<strong>Are you in need of basement remodeling in Maryland, D.C., or Virginia?</strong></p>\n<p>If so, Basement Masters wants to help. Give us a call at (301) 798-4444 to speak to a friendly and experienced in-house team member, or get a free quote online by filling out our quick and easy <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">form</a>. We can&rsquo;t wait to hear from you!</p>\n</div>',5,'',143,'2017-02-28 15:51:37'),(160,'Do I Really Need a Building Permit for Basement Remodeling (Marylanders Must Read)?','Discover here how it is important to get  a permit if you are planning to start a basement remodeling project in MD!','basement remodeling, basement renovation, building permit, building fees, general contractor, building permit for MD, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas','do-i-really-need-a-building-permit-for-basement-remodeling-marylanders-must-read','Do I Really Need a Building Permit for Basement Remodeling (Marylanders Must Read)?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/160/518dda7dc1d4c2abdaa2d7382b18039f','How important are permits when it comes to basement remodeling?','<p>No matter which state you are in, whether it be Maryland, D.C., Virginia, or anywhere else, basement remodeling needs to be done with a permit to be considered legal. If you try any basement remodeling without one, then serious trouble can follow. So if you&rsquo;re asking yourself, &ldquo;do I really need a building permit for basement remodeling?&rdquo;, Maryland law says you do.</p>\n<h2>What happens if I perform basement remodeling (Maryland residence) without a permit?</h2>\n<p>The obvious answer is that you can face steep fines and even jail time, but there are other reasons, too. Permits are in place as a way to protect the consumer from harm or fraud. This is why some permits require an inspection before they can be approved. Skipping these inspections opens you up to all sorts of legal and moral problems should anybody get hurt later on.</p>\n<p>If you are caught without a permit while performing basement remodeling, Maryland authorities can do more than just fine or jail you. They will almost undoubtedly require you to remove any of the unauthorized work, which will only set you back even further. So even though you were trying to take a shortcut, it ended up costing you even more in the long run.</p>\n<h2>&ldquo;Do I really need a building permit?&rdquo; Yes, you really do.</h2>\n<p>Or better yet, why not skip all of the hassle and have the professionals at Basement Masters do it for you? We have years of experience . . . and all the permits needed to get the job done!</p>',2,'',144,'2017-02-27 15:51:48'),(161,'Basement Remodeling Costs: Splurge or Save?','There are a lot of different ways to spend money on basement remodeling costs, but spending smart is the key to a successful project.','basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing , costs, remodel a basement, , basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas','basement-remodeling-costs-splurge-or-save','Basement Remodeling Costs: Splurge or Save?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/161/296b8aca98787db84c618ffa01d0c9d2','Basement remodeling projects can vary wildly in cost, from reasonable to extremely expensive. But where should you try to save money? Where can you splurge?','<p>There are a lot of different ways to spend money on basement remodeling costs, but spending smart is the key to a successful project. Basement remodeling can be a pleasure for future guests and your wallet if you follow these tips to keep basement remodeling costs low.</p>\n<h2><strong>Open Rooms Versus Separate Rooms</strong></h2>\n<p>Unless you prefer privacy, having an open space is usually cheaper than separate rooms. Basement remodeling costs can go up in terms of additional drywall, studs and designer doors once the floorplans call for separate rooms.</p>\n<h2>Use LVT Where Possible</h2>\n<p>Luxury vinyl tiles (LVT) are impressive-looking, relatively inexpensive, and can be manufactured to look like many different building materials, including hardwood floors and even marble. They are also scuff-and-scratch-resistant, meaning you usually also save additional money on maintenance in the long run.</p>\n<h2>Ask the Professionals</h2>\n<p>If you are already straining your budget with a basement remodeling project, then there is nothing wrong with leaving a few ideas out. The best basement remodeling companies (like Basement Masters) will offer you a personal consultant who can draft excellent ideas that still fall within your basement remodeling costs.</p>\n<h2>What to Spend On</h2>\n<p>Now that we\'ve told you a few ways to save on basement remodeling costs, let\'s talk about areas that should absolutely be focused on every time.</p>\n<h3>The Wet Bar</h3>\n<p>If you plan on entertaining guests, you have to have a place to really &ldquo;wow&rdquo; them. Putting extra money into a customized ceiling and columns are two great ways to create a friendly gathering space.</p>\n<h3>Lighting</h3>\n<p>The right lighting is a way to make all of your architectural upgrades really pop out. Windows can be a great way to let natural let in, but they can also be hard to come by in basements sometimes. Custom lighting is a great way to create a warm atmosphere for you and guests.</p>\n<h3>Ceiling Insulation</h3>\n<p>For most basement remodeling projects, ceiling insulation is not a good area to skimp out on. A properly insulated basement will keep noise from reaching other rooms from upstairs, which is especially important if you have a theater or home office. It\'s better to insulate your basement than to let loud footsteps from above put a damper on your next social gathering!</p>\n<h2><strong>Want More Great Ideas to Save on Basement Remodeling Costs?</strong></h2>\n<p>At BasementRemodeling.com, it\'s what we love to talk about all day long! Give us a call at <strong>(301) 798-444 </strong>or visit our website to receive a <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">free online quote</a> within 24 hours!</p>',4,'',145,'2017-02-26 15:52:02'),(162,'Basement Remodeling Vs Renovation: What\'s the Difference?','What exactly is the different between renovating your basement and remodeling it? Learn the difference between renovation and remodeling here!','basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish','basement-remodeling-vs-renovation-whats-the-difference','Basement Remodeling Vs Renovation: What\'s the Difference?','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/162/8c1d06a019e739bdeed1c9b2208a56a3','Knowing the difference can save you time and hassle in the long run.','<p>Here\'s a common question that we get quite often: &ldquo;what\'s the difference between basement remodeling and basement renovations?&rdquo; These two terms are not interchangeable, though people tend to confuse the two sometimes. There is, as it turns out, a big difference!</p>\n<h2><strong>What\'s involved in Basement Renovation?</strong></h2>\n<p>Renovations tend to involve a basement that is currently in a state of disrepair. It is basically taking an old basement with lots of damage and making it looks new again. The term &ldquo;basement renovations&rdquo; typically applies to cosmetic adjustments (sink faucets, counters, cabinet knobs, and paint are all good examples) that does not dramatically alter the basement\'s original design.</p>\n<p>In other words, a basement renovation typically updates the look of the basement without altering the basement\'s overall structure.</p>\n<h2><strong>What is Basement Remodeling?</strong></h2>\n<p>Remodeling a basement means that you are focusing more on the layout of the basement rather than cosmetic changes. Adding a different ceiling to your basement or additional rooms are considered remodels, for example. Electrical work, plumbing, and other &ldquo;behind-the-scenes&rdquo; upgrades are all considered basement remodels.</p>\n<p>An example of a basement remodel is combining a kitchen-like wet bar with the family room, or installing an island in your kitchen-like wet bar. In both of these examples, you are altering the basement\'s floor plans.</p>\n<h2><strong>Why Know The Difference Between Basement Remodeling and Renovation?</strong></h2>\n<p>Understanding the difference between these two terms will help the remodeling process go smoothly as you closely communicate with contractors. If you ever list your home for sale, knowing whether you have a remodeled basement or a renovated one will attract the right kind of buyer.</p>\n<h2><strong>BasementRemodeling.com: Masters of the Basement</strong></h2>\n<p>Do you have any other basement terms that you need to have cleared up? BasementRemodeling.com wants to talk basements with you. Give us a call at at 301-798-4444 or go online for a free <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">basement remodeling quote</a>!</p>',4,'',146,'2017-02-25 15:52:15'),(163,'10 Professional Basement Remodeling Tips','Coming up with a proper strategy for basement remodeling is never easy. Fortunately, BasementRemodeling.com is here to give you 10 tips!','basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas','10-professional-basement-remodeling-tips','10 Professional Basement Remodeling Tips','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/163/2dfd674646f3bcf4d2c237b213d16a75','10 great basement remodeling tips from BasementRemodeling.com!','<p>When you deal with as many basements as we do (hundreds upon hundreds), you are bound to learn a few <strong>basement remodeling tips</strong> along the way. Here are 10 basement remodeling tips that will leave your basement looking as good as the rest of your home!</p>\n<h2>1.) Family Rooms Are a Must</h2>\n<p>Your basement is the perfect place for your family to gather and socialize. A kids&rsquo; playroom or family room with an HDTV and an oversized couch is practically a traditional basement staple when remodeling. Putting a family room in the center of the basement can make your downstairs area feel as warm and inviting as the main floor.</p>\n<h2>2.) Consider Guest Spaces</h2>\n<p>The basement can be a great spot for guests or teenagers. Basement remodeling tips for the guest rooms include considering the size of the room before choosing an appropriate mattress size, and making sure your basement bedroom is up to code by having emergency exits (and other requirements).</p>\n<h2>3.) Use Your Basement to Entertain Others</h2>\n<p>The basement makes for the perfect retreat during unfavorable weather or for low-key gatherings. Transform your basement into the ultimate entertainment center with a kitchen-like wet bar and recreational game room (with ping pong, pool, and more). Here are some basement remodeling tips for a home theater setup: go with a tray ceiling with movie lighting and a built-in sound system! &nbsp;</p>\n<h2>4.) Make it a Multi-Purpose Downstairs</h2>\n<p>A practical basement can make life much easier. Remodeling your laundry room with the proper shelving and sink can make it twice as convenient as before. If you are looking to improve yourself, installing a home gym gives you absolutely no excuse not to work out this week (or every day)!</p>\n<h2>5.) Stairs Matter</h2>\n<p>Stairs are usually the way to get in and out of your newly remodeled basement, and therefore, they also make the first impression.</p>\n<p>Basement remodeling tips to make your stairs better:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Go with classic iron wrought bars (if they match your home)</li>\n<li>Take advantage of storage with under-the-stairs closets.</li>\n<li>For the ultimate in designer entrance, go with a <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/engeneering-features/walk-outs/\">walk-out</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>6.) Finish the Walls</h2>\n<p>The concrete foundation walls in your basement may reinforce your home, but they also can be an eyesore. If you want to make your downstairs look as nice as the rest of your home, then here are some basement remodeling tips for hiding the foundation.</p>\n<p>Cover the concrete with:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Drywall</li>\n<li>Paneling</li>\n<li>Mosaic tiles</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>7.) Finish the Ceilings</h2>\n<p>Nothing kills the ambiance of a basement more than an open ceiling. You need to hide the pipes and ductwork with a ceiling that&rsquo;s dropped or suspended. Hollow ceiling beams can give your basement a cottage feel without costing as much as one.</p>\n<h2>8.) Choose the Right Flooring</h2>\n<p>With LVT, your basement floors can be practical and durable without sacrificing aesthetics. Carpet can help delineate different rooms without putting up additional walls.</p>\n<h2>9.) &nbsp;The Right Lighting for the Right Feel</h2>\n<p>Strong lighting is necessary to both give a welcoming vibe and to showcase all of your other great basement features. Basement remodeling tips for lighting:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Recessed lights are great for areas where you&rsquo;ll be at work or at play (such as the office or kids&rsquo; playroom).</li>\n<li>Table lamps are perfect for keeping corners well-lit and not shadowy.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>10.) Windows and Door Planning</h2>\n<p>Speaking of lighting, you might want to enlarge your current basement windows to let more natural light come through. Adding exterior doors and window wells are two great ways that will help further ventilate your basement (but should always be left to the professionals).</p>\n<h2><strong>Want More Great Basement Remodeling Tips?</strong></h2>\n<p>Basement Masters has plenty of them! We have been remodeling hundreds of basements for years, and we want to take a look at yours. Check out more <a href=\"../../../../basement-ideas/features/\">basement remodeling tips</a> and then head on over to our main page to find out how we can make them happen in your basement!</p>',4,'',147,'2017-02-24 15:52:27'),(164,'Top 3 Hottest Basement Design Trends for 2017','Discover what basement design were in trend in 2017. Browse the former best options for your basement today!','basement remodeling, design, trend, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish, basement blog, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog, basement design ideas','top-3-hottest-basement-design-trends-for-2017','Top 3 Hottest Basement Design Trends for 2017','https://basementremodeling.com/public/upload/tips/164/dee9bf74024fdc8588f802fb3cbfe8d3','Find out what’s in-style for 2017.','<p><strong>Basement design trends</strong> are constantly changing, and one of our many jobs at BasementRemodeling.com is to keep an eye on the latest emerging <strong>basement design fashions</strong>. So far, 2017 is shaping up to be a huge year for basement design trends. Here&rsquo;s what&rsquo;s going to be in-style this year for sure.</p>\n<h2>Basement Design Trends #1: Modern Meets Retro</h2>\n<p>This year, mixing old and new design concepts is going to be way &ldquo;in&rdquo;. This is already happening in the Washington-Bethesda area, which is deeply rooted in American history and incorporates many traditional styles into its interior designs. Retro trends and vintage looks will resurface and merge with contemporary furnishings and building materials in the ultimate cultural fusion.</p>\n<h2>Basement Design Trends #2: Go Mosaic!</h2>\n<p>2016 was a good year for mosaic tiling, and 2017 will continue this basement design fashion in full force. Mosaic tiles are so trendy right now that they may soon replace regular bathroom tiles in overall popularity. Designer patterned tiles will power past the bathroom and extend to virtually every other room imaginable in 2017.</p>\n<h2>Basement Design Trends #3: All White is Out</h2>\n<p>This final interior basement design fashion our personal favorite. The standard and long-favored traditional white is being replaced by more dramatic colors, both bright and dark. Striking greens and purples are becoming the norm instead of being reserved for the occasional accent wall.</p>\n<p>We have been doing this for some time and it always creates a well-received response. Here are two examples: <a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-and-remodeling-ashton-md-16-01\">first</a>, and <a href=\"../../../../portfolio/basement-finishing-remodeling-bowie-maryland\">second</a>.</p>\n<h2>Want More Great Basement Design Fashions?</h2>\n<p>If you are looking for pictures of new basement design fashions, then check out our <a href=\"../../../../portfolio/\">full portfolio</a> for more great ideas. Better yet, contact us for a <a href=\"../../../../instant-quote/\">free quote</a>!</p>',1,'',148,'2017-02-23 15:52:38'),(165,'The Best Basement Remodeling & Finishing Blog Around!','Check out BasementRemodeling.com blog for all of the latest in basement remodeling and finishing tips, advice, and everything else you need to know!','basement masters, basement remodeling, basement finishing, basement finishing company, remodel a basement, basement contractor, basement renovation, finished basement, basement refinish, basement blog, basement design ideas, basement remodeling blog, basement finishing blog','the-best-basement-remodeling--finishing-blog-around','The Best Basement Remodeling & Finishing Blog Around!',NULL,'This basement remodeling and finishing blog covers everything you could possibly need to know about basements—design ideas, tips, advice, trends, and much more!','<p>Welcome to the best basement blog on the internet! We post weekly articles and blogs covering basement ideas, designs, projects, tips, tricks, advice, news, trends, and more!</p>\n<h2>Who we are</h2>\n<p>When it comes to <strong>basement remodeling</strong>, Maryland, D.C., and Virginia businesses and residents alike have been well-served by Basement Masters for years. First established in 2006, our expert team of <strong>basement remodeling contractors </strong>have successfully completed well over 500 basement projects in just ten years&rsquo; time, and have a combined workforce experience of over 250 years! If you&rsquo;re in need of basement remodeling (Maryland, D.C., or Virginia), or if you simply need your basement finished the right way, then we&rsquo;re ready to do a perfect job for a competitive price.</p>\n<p>Led by engineering genius Pavel Abaev, BasementRemodeling.com (formerly Basement Masters) has secured a sterling reputation as one of the best basement remodeling contractors on the entire East Coast. <a href=\"http://www.houzz.com/pro/mastersofmd/basement-masters\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Houzz</a> recently awarded us with the &ldquo;Best of Houzz Service 2016 Award&rdquo; for our exceptional basement remodeling techniques, and we also won the &ldquo;Best of Houzz Customer Service 2015 Award&rdquo; for keeping clients as happy with the overall process as they are with the finished results.</p>\n<h2>Why Choose Us?</h2>\n<p>When you choose BasementRemodeling.com, you are choosing local basement modeling contractors who will give a detailed timeline and follow through with professional results. Pavel will consult with you personally so that no price point is left in question before construction begins, and he will be there every step of the way. You&rsquo;ll also have experienced personal advisers helping you every day. Every permit will be present, and every inspection will be aced. It&rsquo;s simply our way of business.</p>\n<p>To find out more about our basement remodeling and finishing process, or to find an estimate for your home or business, please check out our <a href=\"../../../../\">webpage</a> or give us a call today (301-798-4444)!</p>',5,'',149,'2017-02-21 15:52:50');
